{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2300998.zip::R2-2300998 Rel17-RemoteSynchronization.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"F","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-17","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-16(Release 16)Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)Rel-19(Release 19)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"At RAN2#120 it was agreed to add a NOTE that “When sl-SyncPriority in SIB12 is set to gnbEnb, the choice of synchronisation source for an out of coverage L2 U2N Remote UE is left to UE implementation” ","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This NOTE contradicts to the concept of the previous normative specifications where there are clear rules how the UE selects the synchronization source for SL. Moreover, we should also consider that if the Remote UE has received SIB12 via a Relay UE, then it should be synchronized already from some source.","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The NOTE 1 in clause 5.8.6.2 is revised in the following way: “When an out of coverage L2 U2N Remote UE receives SIB12 with sl-SyncPriority set to gnbEnb, the L2 U2N Remote UE continues using the current synchronization source (GNSS or SyncRef UE) until higher priority synchronization source is found or the current synchronization source becomes unreliable.”","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impact analysis","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impacted functionality: SL Relay functionality","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inter-operability: ","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Implementation of this CR by a Release 17 UE will not cause compatibility issues.","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"0950c947c7225bfbbc13b523c879813ad3af901538962efda3538350a2957b9d","original_member_sha256":"2b04455bf0b88c447b792444a829043734e8fd9ca21a419a61b3728d0ffad2d3","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e4ea5591218aa96d0cd407936b651eb165fb4c75e229dab64ec9de6be991cb96","2d00e3b1a82065155328ddd802c3d4a8ebff11f4a0d6da9ecf9b1e34dc8ebfc8","635d19d0d12b0713c739366094067ed6737ba425cccfc618b3946b6b65dbbe4a","761fa4d36b282591b5f5bb5ee554c6086f6eb9d5925f257d405f142f9e3a17e1","9ee3a8ef1b4d8b5d23ae68c79878f83d9a7ffdf02ec93cff53f7b1de6029f4d6","ab4db6ad122cf5d1483b1c473508f97205e077ce063f7ad357feaf27ffcc1f65","b08252b53f111fda758564f01d6aeb287a86cee