nates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3ae7382fac5a05fbdfcee0ce7ffa40cab8c9106486f09469eabd3ee9af9676d5","original_member_sha256":"22956335148b7a5c16c2b5dda19d49a29d30d34a1f02b6918ba645f49922cb03","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c2960a19bb692d01d1f9862af5c1a8442b20f38930214e0f9afa316ae3b1980e","6532cdbdc42cb2b6c71151736bc4b84fb04c65c51f00d6e7764b50ea505de2c9","1a94f06f703028be2fdc6de76571d3801cfccb90ed864ed20338841a7a2439ff","b9e913aad0e497a4b57fdac8f957c6c2493f619fdfe60b36f24de74f303518ac","11dd8f4b3f581b5049896fd422642101c8f0c133a9a14d9d6337090a814dc162","f4a12e438cccd3d02b52885b1a23f122fe0d6bedad4ec7ef81d9f7a5f436c453","0c53d31d54edd66a7999e48174a7e1f4e5aade1189f7753e39e4a7c817fb5686","ffbdd6ee2badb01742654f97a1f3458d5fa35df335ef162b84c06af2e8bf2395","4b13c76efbaebc188ee9d1783b856c98b591082ec768e4c219f6665bf94f0c23","c1ac0d5c49af445f42e7ba2bacb03b66075a1ff7356880bb1295dcd8c0134066","eac692708b4d366b52c4d935eb2b0c378a6d054b57c12e937d77424fba36db8e","7e4af7cbd43f75ea6e9cd0fa26f3aafc1045ce43804f8160f46ef3dad788ec7d","41f55f019718923165acc7ad17f34ea49591ec0d5d6ef7b15dc6fe584102c851","d5c8d2b51376a7ba7dde3fcd6454d166d7f8906335e34c8c32bc5eb4f71c12fe","3e89e1c90c5b775f00e55a574438645dea87b9940a8b65a5b962a366ee8bbf9b","e17f84074e7a3f1111292fe5a6be9a9da97285ba2031a31622c57ed1628621a1","576c662217d7d850b9f75ff37289a910cad2fcda1133dc7d51a456bebab9084b","59f612609a943bac005342d0d0f285f1818ac0431181b125e2d60c717828df1b","62a384efeab935efaff06400021ea98060317a5bb0d6ed3bdee973933714ef00","cbf1a42f74965296bbb7cd8d44a9f2594f445719d0f1a214eac7b0ad6a461502","3628301294184f1c9d5fa330a9c6f82496bfbe5a721ffab37d72cf7dbfe0712f","06c33f1c918a43353fefad321aa610eebaa81c77ec52218d724198a4dcca5403","7b8a8a4b1c9e40094e642dcf8bc7bb052cc5f94bb3e89bab54eb64784d4120b6","e7dd3a08f495ff589b0439e307bfccc476290fcf0e854fee912b78c4dadda582"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[24,47],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2301167.zip::R2-2301167 - CR3872 Correction for receiving PC5 link release during path switching.docx:p24"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2301167.zip::R2-2301167 - CR3872 Correction for receiving PC5 link release during path switching.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"F","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-17","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-15(Release 15)Rel-16(Release 16)Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When UE receives RRCReconfiguration message for path switching from indirect to direct path, UE performs random access and starts T304. For the source inirect path, the timing to execute source link release is up to UE implementation. In addition, the RRCReconfiguration message to the L2 U2N Relay UE can be sent any time after transmitting RRCReconfiguration message to the remote UE based on gNB implementation (see TS38.300, 16.12.6.1). That means the remote UE still can receive NotificationMessageSidelink message or PC5 unicast link release due to e.g RLF from the source relay UE. ","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"According to 5.3.7.2 of TS38.331, upon PC5 unicast link release indicated by upper layer, the U2N Remote UE in RRC_CONNECTED shall initiate the RRC connection re-establishment procedure.","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"It is obious that the remote UE does not initiate the RRC connection re-establishment procedure during path switching upon receiving PC5 unicast link release from the source relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Regarding NotificationMessageSidelink, there is a ‘NOTE 2’ in 5.8.9.10.4 to ensure that re-establishment procedure will not be triggered if UE receives NotificationMessageSidelink and T304 is running. ","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:The L2 U2N Remote UE may ignore the NotificationMessageSidelink if it does not release the PC5 unicast link in source side yet during an indirect-to-direct path switch, i.e. T304 is running.","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Therefore, the above case associated with PC5 unicast link release should be avoided. One NOTE also can be introduced to address it.","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In section 5.3.7.2, one NOTE is added.","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"3ae7382fac5a05fbdfcee0ce7ffa40cab8c9106486f09469eabd3ee9af9676d5","original_member_sha256":"2295633