{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2301431.zip::R2-2301431 Orbit and Tropo.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Beginning of Changes","paragraph_zero_based":144},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6.5.2.2GNSS Assistance Data Elements","paragraph_zero_based":145},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–GNSS-ReferenceTime","paragraph_zero_based":146},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"<Skip Unmodified Changes>","paragraph_zero_based":147},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–GNSS-SSR-OrbitCorrections","paragraph_zero_based":148},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE GNSS-SSR-OrbitCorrections is used by the location server to provide radial, along-track and cross-track orbit corrections. The target device may use the SSR-OrbitCorrectionList to compute a satellite position correction to be combined with the satellite position calculated from broadcast ephemeris.","paragraph_zero_based":149},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The parameters provided in IE GNSS-SSR-OrbitCorrections are used as specified for SSR Clock Messages (e.g., message type 1057 and 1063) in [30] and apply to all GNSSs.","paragraph_zero_based":150},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":151},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GNSS-SSR-OrbitCorrections-r15 ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"epochTime-r15GNSS-SystemTime,","paragraph_zero_based":154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ssrUpdateInterval-r15INTEGER (0..15),","paragraph_zero_based":155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"satelliteReferenceDatum-r15ENUMERATED { itrf, regional, ... },","paragraph_zero_based":156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"iod-ssr-r15INTEGER (0..15),","paragraph_zero_based":157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ssr-OrbitCorrectionList-r15SSR-OrbitCorrectionList-r15,","paragraph_zero_based":158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"...","paragraph_zero_based":159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SSR-OrbitCorrectionList-r15 ::= SEQUENCE (SIZE(1..64)) OF SSR-OrbitCorrectionSatelliteElement-r15","paragraph_zero_based":162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SSR-OrbitCorrectionSatelliteElement-r15 ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"svID-r15SV-ID,","paragraph_zero_based":165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"iod-r15BIT STRING (SIZE(11)),","paragraph_zero_based":166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"delta-radial-r15INTEGER (-2097152..2097151),","paragraph_zero_based":167}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"402880a9d8f08f91fe24b048856b9780e089d79cd12536aba800d266be1e632a","original_member_sha256":"7cb6fb3149876999a30042fc450d0b566e79a928f6263bf65b46f1ac1a712180","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["20e33cc5bdf126e4a81b9f210df64a2ac632883f5f621f522f83c08e2065f893","f0626185323d22f72f4c44a23c5aec736baa7c8b53290d01925443b33fa3681a","bbebf73b0c96bf4f88a2ce9f2d40dd155988ff83d183d09ff365211c402982d4","f448509b4ac0ff94e9407df7ecd948c2fd891fd52f1e4d6d9a3dc8c3a3423965","aeec7ca75639196bd5055b304287520a45e0867fc4a4cca3f1ec3260bee994f8","fba1ef28ba5a0617d4abc83f3f4e4dd49f12ee69a4b87fd29e67f8f36afe469e","0e54a2738a0049e8d13b2c14084d7e6b72c10562fbbf3dcbd56adc1c29d1ba58","c590366378d992ec0bc9ec2433b6e48bddac6186be3e7d43bd5d8a5b91c76d82","5daa375a41e3e7a5e71ffac3f9c7333000d8394cca48125189d9af6d152074bb","d65ce906af80c5cb1f5c70cec7a310319af0580284d26271a945974e71cd0c57","88af64c029fae2a92e0467f53e0fc8c5b885050aedd19e9604b3167077ade69e","c9457959a94dfca9c249163861b04e0a35c1f7efb03e175390232fea4080803a","cf24ed163e2e9b4333666769050b1d369a9bab68a4d631dbf954bafebae0beac","0ba1f767fd833857414785e82bc70967b9764cfe714ca4dd5b0665e76f3e2aac","f58b1143ae5d89ff855bf5b95f0944152151261cce6fa755d21ffc5128cc9812","f4ac59e2ff71861ee37668c0c4756adc981b156faabb01f00d81b6cdedc94521","55f5457a1239955f1ca72d6b6152a424f4a46a690c9dec78e9e34ad987ce48f8","7a0c849f3effc0a88b706e2957ae53bee55e89302ba001a3549548fd5136b920","13590fca3ad928c815c77074fe24665fdad785c801991ef377fae15e0bda9415","298b933b85f079466cf0f2d5ec20a4ce9b8b6d3a24eb6fdad3c510eabaade96a","824c5caa3a1161da89ee9f6bcd8b54695e0f2a793837273315fa4e856e8e9d36","ad3ae10cd69e003c956c3217dda270eeb32c4a2665e0c73500ea10450d28347d","7bd5d7d2f156be4cdb83c93329397d5f91fa48bd012f35bfff279429c1778fcb","dd70e03b649ef0b20b9058d9e822a01a8926d78a1a3127fdd27bbdc9bdad2018"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[144,167],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2301431.zip::R2-2301431 Orbit and Tropo.docx:p144"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2301431.zip::R2-2301431 Orbit and Tropo.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"delta-AlongTrack-r15INTEGER (-524288..524287),","paragraph_zero_based":168},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"delta-CrossTrack-r15INTEGER (-524288..524287),","paragraph_zero_based":169},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dot-delta-radial-r15INTEGER (-1048576..1048575)OPTIONAL, -- Need ON","paragraph_zero_based":170},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dot-delta-AlongTrack-r15INTEGER (-262144..262143) OPTIONAL, -- Need ON","paragraph_zero_based":171},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dot-delta-CrossTrack-r15INTEGER (-262144..262143) OPTIONAL, -- Need ON","paragraph_zero_based":172},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"...","paragraph_zero_based":173},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":174},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":175},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":176},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":177},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":178},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GNSS-SSR-OrbitCorrections field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":179},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"epochTime","paragraph_zero_based":180},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the epoch time of the orbit corrections. The gnss-TimeID in GNSS-SystemTime shall be the same as the GNSS-ID in IE GNSS-GenericAssistDataElement. ","paragraph_zero_based":181},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ssrUpdateInterval","paragraph_zero_based":182},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the SSR Update Interval. The SSR Update Intervals for all SSR parameters start at time 00:00:00 of the GPS time scale. A change of the SSR Update Interval during the transmission of SSR data should ensure consistent data for a target device. See table Value of ssrUpdateInterval to SSR Update Interval relation below. NOTE 1.","paragraph_zero_based":183},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"satelliteReferenceDatum","paragraph_zero_based":184},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the satellite refence datum for the orbit corrections.","paragraph_zero_based":185},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"iod-ssr","paragraph_zero_based":186},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the Issue of Data number for the SSR data. A change of iod-ssr is used to indicate a change in the SSR generating configuration. ","paragraph_zero_based":187},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"svID","paragraph_zero_based":188},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the satellite for which the orbit corrections are provided.","paragraph_zero_based":189},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"iod","paragraph_zero_based":190},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the IOD value of the broadcast ephemeris for which the orbit corrections are valid (see IE GNSSNavigationModel). NOTE 2.","paragraph_zero_based":191}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"402880a9d8f08f91fe24b048856b9780e089d79cd12536aba800d266be1e632a","original_member_sha256":"7cb6fb3149876999a30042fc450d0b566e79a928f6263bf65b46f1ac1a712180","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["a76a4d7ab877615539ce8f0d8d9384645b5f4af494cf96659b17499458d123ec","dc03fa7eea1fc4fa350dc0d5ae8511c7854c00a3fe62fc3c42675999bea7ccf4","00096cc46369cc15cfff0dcf9d8803e85a731451fd8e2b9fe5ef982ba356eb82","db1bc8e19e3431f3d6d92e23548c08a72496ce37b2365b7a7a72ada1c36ca077","2b756511b94739d75ecaa4deeda591d8c4cccc51a5eddd060d7c681045b004b0","032216c018f8f100f5f7233adc42b9d668ba2764bd70938f3bd65ad6d6021a24","06b67b2c9a1b0894ea837fd4af21255a39da10ba502b7ba47a9194a3a2d7d04c","9ee1d0d625b60f942ab2becf07cfa223c4b27090e4f0df1fa766d186f6c656ca","e717c086823958438e892ac4de9820ab142cbdcc75b4286232eaf87714faa27e","24df16c33a6929bce7c1355ffe8f126dd7c7225280c61db1fce49d59ab10e408","f8f6e54b1f8e5293c520e05a57afd31b6c1c72ddb969a7d72a6c9a094a027860","1ee710519d7a926a774bef7bc7821f55287ec60e9f07a6d9666e3d5359a46c35","8fd2018253dfc485ccb8b59f37cf5b0fbe7a0c311b11542e72a4393ccc07726f","b2aabaacfad2113a90196201a77887b0f3f8aba18bf19ea7980c051d2126df6a","c2d3938dc3f402550a6cf77b21b0d1c8f42115070f14099bfc2d0bca96c33897","13e680659fbe77c49beb68d01e6b6ba499fbf9447df14934441ddd5e73881812","c6db88ef17b1a3c3893b14cad49c265f129a74a980d09804412df30434bb09f9","f03a43ca270ef1f407f5e8514b2a192b17d3c77d9abafd3d248f33830fe0f6e2","1f950ee5a475fb7432fe001aa2f7567f0f4d816d4936b0992022a357f72f6a9d","af0dafbbc803b4e236c2cdfe3a82e0b69668a9e87c90868f59e39ebe31155543","47b1d398cbdc921e1c8bd05cb8fb895e17192c96304eafd3e1bb15d131c4b50f","813da9109a71148953435095f7c7e58608934df6338cae629aaf839b134bcd36","ae23c5eac50b89f5477dd3d51e1210474d7738bbec4873a7078e2de64c40b443","ed0265f37e574b77c5467d375b34b3da87d4fa16efee10db036cbefca3a59832"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[168,191],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2301431.zip::R2-2301431 Orbit and Tropo.docx:p168"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2301431.zip::R2-2301431 Orbit and Tropo.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"delta-radial","paragraph_zero_based":192},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the radial orbit correction for broadcast ephemeris. NOTE 3.","paragraph_zero_based":193},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scale factor 0.1 mm; range ±209.7151 m.","paragraph_zero_based":194},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"delta-AlongTrack","paragraph_zero_based":195},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the along-track orbit correction for broadcast ephemeris. NOTE 3.","paragraph_zero_based":196},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scale factor 0.4 mm; range ±209.7148 m.","paragraph_zero_based":197},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"delta-CrossTrack","paragraph_zero_based":198},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the cross-track orbit correction for broadcast ephemeris. NOTE 3.","paragraph_zero_based":199},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scale factor 0.4 mm; range ±209.7148 m.","paragraph_zero_based":200},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dot-delta-radial","paragraph_zero_based":201},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the velocity of radial orbit correction for broadcast ephemeris. NOTE 3.","paragraph_zero_based":202},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scale factor 0.001 mm/s; range ±1.048575 m/s.","paragraph_zero_based":203},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dot-delta-AlongTrack","paragraph_zero_based":204},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the velocity of along-track orbit correction for broadcast ephemeris. NOTE 3.","paragraph_zero_based":205},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scale factor 0.004 mm/s; range ±1.048572 m/s.","paragraph_zero_based":206},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dot-delta-CrossTrack","paragraph_zero_based":207},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the velocity of cross-track orbit correction for broadcast ephemeris. NOTE 3.","paragraph_zero_based":208},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scale factor 0.004 mm/s; range ±1.048572 m/s.","paragraph_zero_based":209},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":210},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1: The update intervals are aligned to the GPS time scale for all GNSSs in order to allow synchronous operation for multiple GNSS services. This means that the update intervals may not be aligned to the beginning of the day for another GNSS. Due to the leap seconds, this is generally the case for GLONASS.","paragraph_zero_based":211},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:In the cases that gnss-ID indicates 'gps',  'qzss', galileo, the iod refers to the specific broadcast ephemeris (GPS L1 C/A,  QZSS L1 C/A, Galileo I/NAV, respectively, in table GNSS to iod Bit String(11) relation in IE GNSSNavigationModel).","paragraph_zero_based":212},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 3: The reference time t0 is epochTime + ½ × ssrUpdateInterval. The reference time t0 for ssrUpdateInterval '0' is epochTime.","paragraph_zero_based":213},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value of ssrUpdateInterval to SSR Update Interval relation","paragraph_zero_based":214},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value of ssrUpdateInterval","paragraph_zero_based":215}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"402880a9d8f08f91fe24b048856b9780e089d79cd12536aba800d266be1e632a","original_member_sha256":"7cb6fb3149876999a30042fc450d0b566e79a928f6263bf65b46f1ac1a712180","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["52e6a2776b436de2c2e63665acd06eeeb52d6e3ddc7e48535fec5e5b5abac0ed","c1b0b1b141bf8c2f7963cf94ee80d045eaae47997c355ca38ef4a6ebd0d9e917","02cef0e64a5c9ed2a7ae0997a7bc2a30a9be3a0641cccdb2110a1ba980e009ab","b53df85d22d6bd51870278214b77c06381eb0cfc19e263984b785e6087063bcd","270055fa5cd9b50211ed71f002f890b3b58cbb