etation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2301433.zip::R2-2301433 Orbit and Tropo.docx:p24"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2301433.zip::R2-2301433 Orbit and Tropo.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-17","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-16(Release 16)Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)Rel-19(Release 19)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The SSR orbit corrections are relative to broadcasted Ephemeris and should be provided for GNSS Type Galileo to ensure that there is no ambiguity with the clock correction reference, since Galileo has both F/NAV and I/NAV messages. ","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For the SSR clock correction, the following is specified:","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The target device may use the SSR-ClockCorrectionList to compute a clock correction to be applied to the broadcast satellite clock parameters, identified by iod of corresponding GNSS-SSR-OrbitCorrections.","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Therefore, the Note 2 for GNSS-SSR-OrbitCorrections has to sort of the ambiguity for Galileo.","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Note 2 for GNSS-SSR-OrbitCorrections have been updated to include Galileo I/NAV","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"fb8ec76fc8fff2631a54eea3056fb58660493df02c08adfc8f87a29b6647ca9c","original_member_sha256":"c372cd2cebbb02ac4d53a8ac60ad70ed83b67917bcef75f23e4950c4d4dce8c5","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e4ea5591218aa96d0cd407936b651eb165fb4c75e229dab64ec9de6be991cb96","2d00e3b1a82065155328ddd802c3d4a8ebff11f4a0d6da9ecf9b1e34dc8ebfc8","213d6c23000a0aad58355fcaa739a7677e7e097ea7c7468368ad7f5271af234a","761fa4d36b282591b5f5bb5ee554c6086f6eb9d5925f257d405f142f9e3a17e1","9ee3a8ef1b4d8b5d23ae68c79878f83d9a7ffdf02ec93cff53f7b1de6029f4d6","cac273bd4e7f81367e55cd1db6a4902cb162182d88d6b93948ca914cf110d2da","b08252b53f111fda758564f01d6aeb287a86ceee9730eba0ca5fcf7c7dadb00e","5397ebe3cc2afa3393b897343a62f60e5b485315d8236802a715ec930f5cc336","275fd5f28330e81a71bc0f424bdb9e870b94721e1fbac96c6b96ce5232317404","1257bef6de0d6fbcb35da4ad9e5d1d2efb40539d216438a199be822d1e60e855","16c8d70f7d429c511b56c375317337c5d5c75b5a185ec91bf088b77069963fb7","acd6206245de4b9556a4853ff1b8b41875944834aa76df6c7d72af763f365262","3c4c80e1e1104