{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2301433.zip::R2-2301433 Orbit and Tropo.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the satellite for which the orbit corrections are provided.","paragraph_zero_based":192},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"iod","paragraph_zero_based":193},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the IOD value of the broadcast ephemeris for which the orbit corrections are valid (see IE GNSSNavigationModel). NOTE 2.","paragraph_zero_based":194},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"delta-radial","paragraph_zero_based":195},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the radial orbit correction for broadcast ephemeris. NOTE 3.","paragraph_zero_based":196},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scale factor 0.1 mm; range ±209.7151 m.","paragraph_zero_based":197},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"delta-AlongTrack","paragraph_zero_based":198},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the along-track orbit correction for broadcast ephemeris. NOTE 3.","paragraph_zero_based":199},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scale factor 0.4 mm; range ±209.7148 m.","paragraph_zero_based":200},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"delta-CrossTrack","paragraph_zero_based":201},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the cross-track orbit correction for broadcast ephemeris. NOTE 3.","paragraph_zero_based":202},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scale factor 0.4 mm; range ±209.7148 m.","paragraph_zero_based":203},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dot-delta-radial","paragraph_zero_based":204},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the velocity of radial orbit correction for broadcast ephemeris. NOTE 3.","paragraph_zero_based":205},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scale factor 0.001 mm/s; range ±1.048575 m/s.","paragraph_zero_based":206},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dot-delta-AlongTrack","paragraph_zero_based":207},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the velocity of along-track orbit correction for broadcast ephemeris. NOTE 3.","paragraph_zero_based":208},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scale factor 0.004 mm/s; range ±1.048572 m/s.","paragraph_zero_based":209},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dot-delta-CrossTrack","paragraph_zero_based":210},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the velocity of cross-track orbit correction for broadcast ephemeris. NOTE 3.","paragraph_zero_based":211},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Scale factor 0.004 mm/s; range ±1.048572 m/s.","paragraph_zero_based":212},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":213},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1: The update intervals are aligned to the GPS time scale for all GNSSs in order to allow synchronous operation for multiple GNSS services. This means that the update intervals may not be aligned to the beginning of the day for another GNSS. Due to the leap seconds, this is generally the case for GLONASS.","paragraph_zero_based":214},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:In the cases that gnss-ID indicates 'gps',  'qzss', galileo, the iod refers to the specific broadcast ephemeris (GPS L1 C/A,  QZSS L1 C/A, Galileo I/NAV, respectively, in table GNSS to iod Bit String(11) relation in IE GNSSNavigationModel).","paragraph_zero_based":215}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"fb8ec76fc8fff2631a54eea3056fb58660493df02c08adfc8f87a29b6647ca9c","original_member_sha256":"c372cd2cebbb02ac4d53a8ac60ad70ed83b67917bcef75f23e4950c4d4dce8c5","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["813da9109a71148953435095f7c7e58608934df6338cae629aaf839b134bcd36","ae23c5eac50b89f5477dd3d51e1210474d7738bbec4873a7078e2de64c40b443","ed0265f37e574b77c5467d375b34b3da87d4fa16efee10db036cbefca3a59832","52e6a2776b436de2c2e63665acd06eeeb52d6e3ddc7e48535fec5e5b5abac0ed","c1b0b1b141bf8c2f7963cf94ee8