coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"5acf77e0c3f4b05a52d04a20ae928b42a5fa643e6677c3d314b652a4309cde06","original_member_sha256":"18536e53a580a3c3e340d54874eeb9406a7cf49faf8633e5de53d7de7c7fa610","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["5bddd5039a10346bcbccb2616a1c7e3880107ecffb27271f383c9385e917fe65","2dee114c0f0bd9ef0ba301f381c7d93047a8f6c5a3de6e73f4a64b1e578a81a7","4d083632cc30485618cfbf46ee9c2fe7f412ab5aa2bfe99317440517e03f9818","397a1c52f37550186c52f17c76f8ace403b8942cd5f0a74dd23436f9243c1e97","5b732b23a7e4a66e6298e8fe6e97ce03f04c6d438d5ffbf7a04614d0a8e9f2ce","358e0906dde987ae3d9f58cf0182e4a4688c5489b7284328fd23242b2b4f341d","5eba849f58c6b50baa5c001db53fe471e61f552412ec5c104534e93d53a2dac4","ebd8b1a7df30d471311b2f0736c9a0506b3259968f6dcea3911e464ef44aa73e","9bcb7d761bd511fdddcccc3372e7984d5ea86c54f54184515afa7bf00709d4c0","e521728909feef103bfcd106046e3e8182fbd76fa2c35d5af12ea0014d5c40cf","5803ca1f87eef8dd2cb2895b4c1be8f5fa86b68b48aac6a2f99e3fd5f350052e","d3925a22997db7836b1bb0d4e35265f3c03bf084fb60f4e29815437be9f34b55","0e523b814924d87ba4df8d4d401e59c98b9fd7f1f4976b24dacb90868309bdbf","231841d20406cf1c257e8be72d6e381441669fef130c9a986ad74cb65cf1bcf8","0e19b81f87d3bdc2ef8b647396cef0b654a0980685f47da385dbf025b72d6b3a","a9c53bdfdd39f8e6ca97cd76d19167c48157f0677c11978d12e4c36116d72d0a","5344855e0fe3fa7f07b6e9f317481cc9b7dfd6f4dd34d3babe988ed5122da228","a2f6639e81b0b309dc2818dc9d799155d7eacc71f419342dc03b98db169b2da1","0fbc15aca88709f6e0bf1a4ad3b9408ba17eba977f695f93b785cfcbd249c3c5","e0d334f23360a49063cb320b71d49e2def0fe9a5e62366582f2ae3c702804472","2f93927e419275c53b47819922013b596f9af8fb5cd8adcc2fa9fe352596b09b","37af868d797143f2f4c78d0430a28d61e696204a98d6d30cc71e31b834542543","f0c962faa7eb7da162ce4cc0907bfe475042520891e2dbb21a8ee1ffdab2d682","7e85ce478e209d0d2c158e5a9941ab2af0d3f96791ae3375ba35acfb2035094a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[96,119],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2302839.zip::R2-2302839 - 38300_CR0649_Rel-17_Correction to 38.300 on IUC Terminologies.docx:p96"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2302839.zip::R2-2302839 - 38300_CR0649_Rel-17_Correction to 38.300 on IUC Terminologies.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TS/TR ... CR ... ","paragraph_zero_based":120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Other comments:","paragraph_zero_based":123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This CR's revision history:","paragraph_zero_based":127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"START OF CHANGE","paragraph_zero_based":134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"16.9.8Inter-UE Coordination (IUC)","paragraph_zero_based":135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The SL UE can support inter-UE coordination (IUC) in Mode 2, whereby a UE sends information about resources to a peer UE, which the peer UE then uses for resource (re)selection. The following schemes of inter-UE coordination are supported:","paragraph_zero_based":136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-IUC scheme 1, where the IUC information sent from a UE to a peer UE is the preferred or non-preferred resources for the peer UE's transmission, and","paragraph_zero_based":137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-IUC scheme 2, where the IUC information sent from a UE to a peer UE is the presence of expected/potential resource conflict on the resources indicated by the peer UE's SCI.","paragraph_zero_based":138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In scheme 1, the transmission of IUC information from a UE can be triggered by a condition at this UE, or by an explicit request from a peer UE. The UE determines the set of resources reserved by other UEs or slots where the UE, when it is the intended receiver of the peer UE, does not expect to perform SL reception from the peer UE due to half-duplex operation. The UE uses these resources as the set of non-preferred resources, or excludes these resources to determine a set of preferred resources and sends the preferred/non-preferred resources to the peer UE. Regarding the IUC information received from the UE, the peer UE's resources for resource (re)selection can be based on both the peer UE's sensing results (if available) and the IUC information, or it can be based only on the IUC information. For scheme 1, MAC CE and second-stage SCI or MAC CE only can be used to send IUC information. For transmission of the explicit request and reporting for IUC information in unicast manner is supported. For IUC information transmission triggered by a condition other than the explicit request, the IUC information indicating preferred resource set is transmitted in unicast manner, and the IUC information indicating non-preferred resource set is transmitted in unicast, groupcast or broadcast manner.","paragraph_zero_based":139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In scheme 2, a UE determines the expected/potential resource conflict within the resources indicated by a peer UE's SCI as either resources reserved by other UEs and identified by the UE as fully/partially overlapping with the resources indicated by the peer UE's SCI, or as slots where the UE is the intended receiver of the peer UE and does not expect to perform SL reception on those slots due to half-duplex operation. The peer UE uses the conflicting resources to determine the resources to be reselected and exclude the conflicting resources from the reselected resources. For scheme 2, PSFCH is used to send IUC information.","paragraph_zero_based":140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"END OF CHANGE","paragraph_zero_based":141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":142}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"5acf77e0c3f4b05a52d04a20ae928b42a5fa643e6677c3d314b652a4309cde06","original_member_sha256":"18536e53a580a3c3e340d54874eeb9406a7cf49faf8633e5de53d7de7c7fa610","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ffbb247ee065aee728a9425d0566548b22fb77f21ba1ee91c1bbdf65a25d33d9","83c7c63b7e064386d69c2724cd6cf1b784e8809b9a5f5530e0cb97c705f27633","08eed9f3d3c0d7b5ad9be1268595ad2385e4e52065f3b7cf1b63e31e7a945772","5088cc15e2280550796b212be9e2cb84ba7be08e5e8ef8357a7987518a9b92db","ccf3e542702790e906a6e62672ded541e15cf1844698454a407440a6d9bd3bf9","15c688de34899defee20bf40d5bf07ec6e66c5369a7f00a115b509170ca43ab4","e127f5f36047df71a523d9fc7438651c56df8ee54afb27eb5796b70c202318b0","73e61e81b73c1707d43cde5a184477ca2042f4c4701ef35e50c63924c61e4f29","49069048e641b79dbced68ded3190a3fb952b6c2769342d89bbcfc02dc29b02c","e5a540b784baac4e7e88e4749d98f4312b0928d04870520da544cce2e21619f3","81418ac13d85402c9609f527f5640ca56502a6f0ef578ded0b8a21a026eb4f72","f48fb27a6a89fdde9d50d486328dbedc0705c4f368208c3078020ab08174b22c","6045ba58047ee2d19433a64a819ca03b42f5a1436272df37f327d6352bbacebf","19fb35ad82bf85e0f78ea6847fdbecc85570aab93d5ef0c13402c8c03a71df8c","172d9a54c2ebed122b168abe78b6b4b72d1be2b8ea124a0aa67ad957185a04ed","3ac6591eba8f96ea7d65ddb6c62522553875ded40e039faab348e3f1d1ca9a51","f478e63c0fe886db51063305e259f4c2098c7aeeecec5da1ed664572bccfea96","54bf355feb25a0a46c6e8da5da34958c9339b48b47f7f52a92e9a185a88ec6d4","93c5806c506f84c160afdb11362070e17e8c654608af7b0fedb2939c63789c26","b158f9d255a0557dd3aa40ae53e202ce8342698931d93b8e89708f847fb6930b","daa1e10a04d7e466361d5e89f2cf