":{"document_XML_sha256":"5fa410a7ffa3e1f88caffede2551dc13218dfb2ab5374b280cff93ae9eeefce3","original_member_sha256":"f6d595631cb9621be67c9ac13fbd053acf174052ca516ce2a9467ec42d9bb9cf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e66b66bc5025c53ae14cb11e5c9c2a12d29ff2114d6bf973d066ea236a83c887","38d3bb4b00ecac42900cb3687ad3de962a36cc9f5e49712f2fd70195394d9fbf","7eb9d663a3709818cb5ea6bd1dd6f0c105b505b069d2fdb0e540c03ee2a02c8c","e670f754660b81878a17e39940f866e13bae160ba5fe699af1678173b6f4b827","bc177da58e1099897dbed84ac36757d325cbb0f418d13d2b83119deb63862493","1f1cba165083321edb79d5a2624c715da1fad481c44b42bde2a70f967f808961","7fd7bc1d8a223c9118950f65de306072f19e83b7968408a8c93be386daf8c20f","d267c787c3eb48ae10fe33cb46c08ba4267aee6a8c09b29e822fde8c804c77e9","5d0a52bbe070c80e35455cb60bef44a10c63fa12688be4fd058de912350eb595","302af39fa4e14c995b6657ed86c370ce8f49ecb91b56851265bb7cecbdee72fe","b1a2a57b139eca1cacb902149eba500eb57f8376aa52d4d6fa201f55ba580bb0","7aebca719754320b4fe745337e680f1d5c5905fc949dd2525a842ff2c27c4eaf","8b1a7a996783bc2588d16157b553cb178fc9e0bf5de7641c8abb98092c328090","88980f2035c7ae21fb9935709ca78844ad5d99bb085bd785ae2b84ff80f18ec4","5a897923e9bea20ec6fcf5df8ce7559bb2144f5938a16a1f878b9575786f37c6","7e96d23bc2fb80fd6d80ae4cd3d1ffd010bccd25e310b9603dcdd3fefea8c1b6","3ad7d8054396d343050261d1948ac3298756b970c6749bad8712e5d8f001a0ee","bcc431018803f0c5054e89294297d3675ea64625666c0e368b6638a3ad98aed0","94e9c80b27cd3707c7f8a342deb86d399f941c375fea31061054d18c893a87c6","f03e1538b3578bc1869e71cf38be3bbc33858dcaec58d45167cfaf75d1d70712","f5c695f359b03d536753dfaf0f2e927f79b58d6fb7f2f268c8cc1b55367fb323","4a6ffd05d3b03bb7c3f19783849e70405ee36c83688c3aae489900f795cad1f9","8ef65c44b635c0080cb6f96cd22ad6495c1035658cf6cd8cc08502a9c89fad98","8b2fedeaa5869e4a946b455052a34e145b9c2a53f52a384d8f8bdb64f3adca37"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[96,119],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2302840.zip::R2-2302840 - 38300_C0650_Rel-17_Correction to 38.300 on IUC cast type.docx:p96"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2302840.zip::R2-2302840 - 38300_C0650_Rel-17_Correction to 38.300 on IUC cast type.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Other comments:","paragraph_zero_based":120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This CR's revision history:","paragraph_zero_based":124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FIRST CHANGE","paragraph_zero_based":129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"16Verticals Support","paragraph_zero_based":130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"16.9Sidelink","paragraph_zero_based":131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"<<<<Skipped>>>>","paragraph_zero_based":132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"16.9.8Inter-UE Coordination (IUC)","paragraph_zero_based":134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The SL UE can support inter-UE coordination (IUC) in Mode 2, whereby a UE-A sends information about resources to UE-B, which UE-B then uses for resource (re)selection. The following schemes of inter-UE coordination are supported:","paragraph_zero_based":135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-IUC scheme 1, where the IUC information sent from a UE-A to a UE-B is the preferred or non-preferred resources for UE-B's transmission, and","paragraph_zero_based":136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-IUC scheme 2, where the IUC information sent from a UE-A to a UE-B is the presence of expected/potential resource conflict on the resources indicated by UE-B's SCI.","paragraph_zero_based":137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In scheme 1, the transmission of IUC information from UE-A can be triggered by an explicit request from UE-B, or by a condition at UE-A. UE-A determines the set of resources reserved by other UEs or slots where UE-A, when it is the intended receiver of UE-B, does not expect to perform SL reception from UE-B due to half-duplex operation. UE-A uses these resources as the set of non-preferred resources, or excludes these resources to determine a set of preferred resources and sends the preferred/non-preferred resources to UE-B. UE-B's resources for resource (re)selection can be based on both UE-B's sensing results (if available) and the IUC information received from UE-A, or it can be based only on IUC information received from UE-A. For scheme 1, MAC CE and second-stage SCI or MAC CE only can be used to send IUC information. For IUC information transmission triggered by an explicit request, both the explicit request and the IUC information are transmitted in unicast manner. For IUC information transmission triggered by a condition other than the explicit request, the IUC information indicating preferred resource set is transmitted in unicast manner, and the IUC information indicating non-preferred resource set is transmitted in unicast, groupcast or broadcast manner.","paragraph_zero_based":138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In scheme 2, UE-A determines the expected/potential resource conflict within the resources indicated by UE-B's SCI as either resources reserved by other UEs and identified by UE-A as fully/partially overlapping with the resources indicated by UE-B's SCI, or as slots where UE-A is the intended receiver of UE-B and does not expect to perform SL reception on those slots due to half-duplex operation. UE-B uses the conflicting resources to determine the resources to be reselected and exclude the conflicting resources from the reselected resources. For scheme 2, PSFCH is used to send IUC information.","paragraph_zero_based":139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"END OF FIRST CHANGE","paragraph_zero_based":142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":143}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"5fa410a7ffa3e1f88caffede2551dc13218dfb2ab5374b280cff93ae9eeefce3","original_member_sha256":"f6d595631cb9621be67c9ac13fbd053acf174052ca516ce2a9467ec42d9bb9cf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["bf0e19b6352bd184dd78c6284a87d71324334937397dc2aad472e453cb29449e","580b88d6d21cacdceda658d0453136c16a3dda9bc53411e948e7ccdcfd6d991b","0f22df788cca7de53c6f0d5fd70a5628cd806d1fca9940ffede47fb52e2645b1","4c699106d705b3220b7d3d876a0fe9b312413b758d7ffd51c6f369775e31282b","338d51da5790e58016b7fe4e3beb9889e41e072eb1ff55160a546bcd87e925a7","527546f15e39d4b12112c780992fc25e5863da972e3359bd21421fce25d8468e","b69619039db8daa7bc42d3339870fbebbc643f3a67509349cfaa1d8c85925ebc","08c136329adf2210b9a0cb227778d1ad4a75e2b85b24521cb8417f393a12e92e","468fd9ccfd5e1a77ab11ac081431bb3549dac235669963a8e6809e3f3c776d0b","0c7cf3a0447e7b1fd5c5c2004829c6a7149ee46db2520f948e9ba42fbc0f9bbc","fdc2c8e85f98282ae3900055d43b302d7b774e35136ccb2e892ec89057c4952e","40403b38f7b8b46e434bf1dd5420bb6a2ccdf5bc834a9025d78f73da2fdd596b","25ba682b4ecddd2e3b16ca3f59003c42c8f2836f51e0d3a021f9b5f2b3862aed","698c54dcc05081e54da46a369a3955832e8ec43336c6280151dc4009dc6b400c","4010ccbdabbf22c42d9e365bb1914bfe977d9f76313e561a9a2b752a3089704e","8e0f04153934a4c97c1c7c3b3e5f6e85d2603d6971e4850970eaa4bf876c5040","796e9661efeba46ff1464cdc5d151065becccd60f72cd7671ff632bdae8f4bfe","e8beac508129d4773218e19f47c4ee20c202bed89579f3ec9586e455f8f73e90","c4ef69bf019dab685693fe7093c0cb5ad2933276f1206b765d51c60b9ade45b8","38f58e47d10faef01a1322be0a8d2c119cd943c327917382cc25a9dbb3aa455c","13eeefcbf1615a5f