{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2303215.zip::R2-2303215 Correction on the usage of default CBR values for NR sidelink.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"F","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-17","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-15(Release 15)Rel-16(Release 16)Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"     Rel-19(Release 19)","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In RAN2#119bis meeting, RAN2 further discussed the different use cases of R16/17 default CBR parameters, and reached the following agreement.","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Case 1: partial sensing, R17 normal pool, R17 default CBR – partial","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Case 2a: random selection, R17 normal pool, R17 default CBR – random","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Case 2b: random selection, R16/17 exceptional pool, R16 default CBR","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Case 3: full sensing, R16/17 normal pool, R16 default CBR or invalid case?","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Case 1, 2a, 2b are confirmed. Case 3 will be revisited next meeting.","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In RAN2#120 meeting, RAN2 sent LS to RAN1 to ask if case 3 is a valid case or not. RAN1 replied in R1-2302174 that:","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RAN1 reply to Q1:","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"From RAN1 perspective, whether case 3 is valid or not is the same in Rel-16 as in Rel-17, and therefore RAN1 recommends to RAN2 that the usage of default CBR configuration for full sensing case in R17 is unchanged compared to R16","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"7415921573891a3b422a70566bf834f34997fbf688c6bbe9a6822a18366f7dc6","original_member_sha256":"fb9a2ae736bd47dbee922f41b02070f91d504cf37a31fe0a2639ea321127534f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["6c14188b935b71c193d6e88beab856351147c70ff8d4348a6e87fcd8c73e7fb9","b0a809ef3d489b75d5885f0fd106c2212f09a2f99dc066d4f6f3a4e7a42a5f14","b492eae2f5f89dd7af65044b9c03a7dda795334fd0cebbbbf8e4456e6938838f","b10cc07f5fd694b129fbbc5076893a354db3ef9208ec057f546d2901bf4c71e8","6800356d20b56d6e56cd4bc8f075b32b66392d20291e93fb5b543d9ff25e3528","7ea33120eaa33c256662eda67c055565e1877b94ad96a6c6390c1a6223c7f914","224417853c2536e2e9a02f1beb0ac2155a24bb8e4b9bcb45112811525a765a67","639705040e6190bacfc3a72dc66b5ec316f4e7c57b6dae323c7f42ff6d2263bd","2778d2f78f1b80d9f28ff0a902f4dd45de598fce5e9b0ff8efbf7354afca2937","49193f0680870b23ee68f45f6ebde151d353198122730dc52f031120fcb76ddb","20ece7df4fcc561e6207ff53152a190af027fc33b1abcb0ccb58d347a8e43ee4","b9bc6977f1abedcd15b18b762ea84d40304107eba31a1727be490b4c2b061c04","10dddf03bf6a9eb1ac12a281a941a328b81d01279928a7469aa9d025e7c671c2","d91f7f26bf6342647586c7ce2c38f0895d71be2eef20adddd59f3d5267fa0ecb","e4a5902338551ae46485bd4c5c2d1caabaa0aaa97e55f956bb57969b8b0ecffb","2a9aed28241951b510721dab165bd373edfda64ad792c1d3102e3e919066eb14","de3b6c59031c00bfcfe3ac072c066dc032c5aaa1ec30c009b719037052d557ec","3d9bd1c99a48f82818b21b5476d1c2e37692ebe27bedf1061cf85c1d1e2d8e2e","abef57673e12a11ff4c037b833f7cd379fcc9c5b646064dc1bf74b1516b948fb","d9bd297ad3a5b7970ef4620793bb6314f7500b912d96f3fe40012ce4262b655a","cf130cb63b369263ded0d04dd303afd59064e018861a13928b1fb347450ddff5","858c77957f4318c4e7b2228dff98d178d2cb54d17b7670d9345136f0cd3563eb","e50949ddfb4109b8b912c49fc1db9784d4651325efcc23f818933c6888527410","cda066b4a873d116249cee899053c2caa939c3eae6dfa650c3a1fdd39666143f"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[48,71],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2303215.zip::R2-2303215 Correction on the usage of default CBR values for NR sidelink.docx:p48"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2303215.zip::R2-2303215 Correction on the usage of default CBR values for NR sidelink.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Based on current R16 specification, when UE performs full sensing in R16 normal pool, if there is no CBR measurement result, UE relies on R16 default CBR value. Therefore, to follow the instruction from RAN1 reply, when UE performs full sensing in R17 normal pool, if there is no CBR measurement result, UE should use R16 default CBR value. In addition, corresponding description should be added to support the other cases, i.e., case 1, 2a and 2b.","paragraph_zero_based":72},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":73},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":74},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":75},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In section 5.22.1.1, clarify how to determine the CBR value when CBR measurement result is not available under different cases.","paragraph_zero_based":76},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impact analysis","paragraph_zero_based":77},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impacted 5G architecture options: ","paragraph_zero_based":78},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"  NR SA, NR-DC, NE-DC, (NG)EN-DC","paragraph_zero_based":79},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":80},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impacted functionality","paragraph_zero_based":81},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Resource (re)selection","paragraph_zero_based":82},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inter-operability: ","paragraph_zero_based":83},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the network is implemented according to this CR while the UE is not, there is no inter-operability issue.","paragraph_zero_based":84},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the UE is implemented according to this CR while the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue.","paragraph_zero_based":85},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If one UE is implemented according to this CR while the other UE is not, there is no inter-operability issue.","paragraph_zero_based":86},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":87},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":88},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Consequences if not approved:","paragraph_zero_based":89},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"It remains unclear how to determine the CBR value when CBR measurement results are not available under different cases.","paragraph_zero_based":90},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":91},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":92},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Clauses affected:","paragraph_zero_based":93},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.22.1.1","paragraph_zero_based":94},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":95}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"7415921573891a3b422a70566bf834f34997fbf688c6bbe9a6822a18366f7dc6","original_member_sha256":"fb9a2ae736bd47dbee922f41b02070f91d504cf37a31fe0a2639ea321127534f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["d2c9305ab33633c34e2f1437e49fa5f8d00e38a1d701ebcf142761783d10c52d","0c050a72c03e8c896afb0566ebf23a69a75f9ea82c9a8cf6ec4991968bcffb9e","4d77ec1a9866eb8f55adce89a3212e7e79d1b8b2ac27b65d68da4b06e9a25c09","e9ba8b5ee3aaeba52b6fbf51ab4594ff5db9a5b99ffac93673c4b196f0aa2135","0a0b92b15811244d5d310f643373dc0b9f6f23dd72cf2c917fc37f9b95d75950","1b43373d331ddd6a04598df2c94b98a75ecfd707e35d55b7e75e2e18dc415a8a","5dc4a25513b8c3ee36dedd9bea5275be8af58ce45b84950f7541bbb9a66668c7","a84774b8a435d796a1c015a54b54d29f48cc7ba89e1cc4d77caba0a073508074","b38eecfe58bcee2cce7bc898016c814166283b7daf930f09fa514b48d60315f5","55f79e90c6e923a31e3020d0736291f1466a02d9b8f41ae6556535a0789ee374","7984d5cdc126bfed2255ab371183a97d227f9326875a