{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2304803.zip::R2-2304803 Correction to PosSRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"F","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-17","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-16(Release 16)Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)Rel-19(Release 19)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Issue1: The current spec mentions that the UE shall transmit periodic SRS or semi-persistent SRS when the validation for the SRS has passed. However, the semi-persistent SRS is still subject to the activation/deactivation command from the network and is not solely dependent on the validation for SRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE. This needs to be clarified in the spec.","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Issue2: UE can request Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request using MAC CE only if Scheduling Request Configuration has been configured by RRC layer.  In MAC specification, in section 5.25 it mentions to trigger a Scheduling Request for Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request MAC CE. However, it is unclear as what configurations UE shall check before triggering the SR; since;","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"There are two ways to send SR from the UE to the network (a) by PUCCH resource and (b) by RACH procedure","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For (a), a UE can only send the SR on PUCCH with RRC configuration ","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"While for (a), when there is no SR configuration corresponding to the triggered SR, the UE would trigger SR on PRACH, according to the clause specified in 5.4.4.","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Thus, in section 5.25; the reference for section 5.4.4 should be provided where it says The MAC entitity Shall  “trigger a Scheduling Request for Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request MAC CE.”, so that it is clear as how UE can send the SR from the UE to the NW for intended positioning measurement gap activation/deactivation.","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Issue3: There is a typo in the section for SP positoning SRS activation/deactivation MAC CE","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"95b5452dcdc46b87411657002095bc67fd93f084654e53f76beb747cb0df61f4","original_member_sha256":"a570081078373