{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2304803.zip::R2-2304803 Correction to PosSRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":72},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":73},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":74},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1/ Add reference to the section for SP positioning SRS activation/deactivation for the transmission of SP posSRS in RRC_INACTIVE","paragraph_zero_based":75},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2/ In section 5.25  for “Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request” a reference to section 5.4.4 has been added.","paragraph_zero_based":76},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3/ Change the word ‘withn’  to ‘within’.","paragraph_zero_based":77},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":78},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":79},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Consequences if not approved:","paragraph_zero_based":80},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Change1: SP posSRS can be transmitted without SP posSRS activation, which is wrong","paragraph_zero_based":81},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":82},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impact analysis","paragraph_zero_based":83},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impacted functionality:","paragraph_zero_based":84},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Positioning SRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE","paragraph_zero_based":85},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inter-operability:","paragraph_zero_based":86},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the UE is implemented according to the CR while the network is not, there is no inter-operability issue since the network wouldn’t expect the UE to transmit SRS and thus would not attempt to receive SRS","paragraph_zero_based":87},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the network is implemented according to the CR while the UE is not, the netowrk would not receive SP SRS transmission and which would cause SRS measurement failure.","paragraph_zero_based":88},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":89},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Chagne2: In section 5.25  for “Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request” a reference to section 5.4.4 has been added.","paragraph_zero_based":90},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":91},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impact analysis","paragraph_zero_based":92},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Impacted functionality:","paragraph_zero_based":93},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request ","paragraph_zero_based":94},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Interoperability Issue:","paragraph_zero_based":95}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"95b5452dcdc46b87411657002095bc67fd93f084654e53f76beb747cb0df61f4","original_member_sha256":"a5700810783730dc819152118c725930196bfe57c3f7e171d8317425bb53ec2f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["2baeb447d42f4fbdcf91a657b2c46883c5f78bd67151cd4ef33a787701eadc66","b8c1197f002287c97d8903fe47794bbab160a66324c7df10d0d2ed01e72698ec","fcb16d8564a1d9e436033a00834763357c6288a090fd41e1182a7d2eaa1bfe09","aa3c17fbd547d1918b959b3dc6e2ba5fc2bac88617fb120ebdaea9437f55775c","6c1b39df005aa60e401c1e8096fe8167653ab18a707b06fc19b73c9865258c5f","866e12c0c82dd3134e0d2c9927ece90c8a9200ba8f7e74438fd4958e5afd8d5a","3fddc6627f11f494b43fa07fa0036bd329f467763fab733ab293ef5ef3052af4","18a7ce0ef1ef71f58b80667e1b2f2656a812011d7533cf89f2abb06d70f3f61e","791e969a1cfa4a6a13ebeb9dd0479078a256a61b8edefc41d47eca30bf7099b9","ec87a6a8f59819dea1b94a98f4b24a16d7ef3570d9429a0b1ba33958e5af8b7d","890c8dcdb4299fcae17832566c72e8b5da1b09fa729f524ae02d3c21c4136a27","388b0e3f733eab63ecd6d303a0e5d4be884672ff638137274d1160beb7ba0fec","d