{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2304803.zip::R2-2304803 Correction to PosSRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TS/TR ... CR ... ","paragraph_zero_based":120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"affected:","paragraph_zero_based":121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"X","paragraph_zero_based":123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":" Test specifications","paragraph_zero_based":124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TS/TR ... CR ... ","paragraph_zero_based":125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"(show related CRs)","paragraph_zero_based":126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"X","paragraph_zero_based":128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":" O&M Specifications","paragraph_zero_based":129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TS/TR ... CR ... ","paragraph_zero_based":130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Other comments:","paragraph_zero_based":133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This CR's revision history:","paragraph_zero_based":137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Ver0 in RAN2#122: R2-2304803","paragraph_zero_based":138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"==================================CHANGE BEGINS===================================","paragraph_zero_based":141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.25Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request","paragraph_zero_based":142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the UE is configured with pre-configured positioning measurement gap and the request of the activation/deactivation of the positioning measurement gap by UL MAC CE, the UE may request the network to activate or deactivate the Positioning measurement gap with UL MAC CE for Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request in clause 6.1.3.40.","paragraph_zero_based":143}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"95b5452dcdc46b87411657002095bc67fd93f084654e53f76beb747cb0df61f4","original_member_sha256":"a5700810783730dc819152118c725930196bfe57c3f7e171d8317425bb53ec2f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["4649ab77f104ded5ec8d1d29bcb3a693818ea166cf0aed57e2a3a15c73da602e","4234a517f694029993908bbd3d106e658396d52b256e4b2e0f72005fd3dbd111","effffdb51b2be0894d3bf0ef3a15bbda14eceb6c6dc216775ce54ab1a20317f1","c500083d4903865a085e45118dfa29a960b2b59f050b98f2c04630273f893fe7","0eb12ccec2c016e1494a0c2bcb3931c69da7b6e25ad1fb8d7443477ebb2f9f3d","7d71ec15ca419be631c3ad8e625bcd7f5108e93f936731372dc1e482999b0bb6","d966b4773be33c51de2dd8183a5b3f38bff3bbeb54c8497c2e1360de6b5fbefd","441be3364cf689a1dbb64a3c58958b2063d123df85f8fe1f9b96153b93f750af","2daab1825bc13530715a7b76e2b553585da87e93509af5a0e65a1415db14cd77","3100e00407b0d3ed1fb81eda093b48086118f4edb36ed73fd73fc9926f2f9c20","702b762ce6ad472e2df68dac167bd97ce5ddaeb58ace84487f44c1f17e2d4519","c8b6e0f7faaa81840fcdb143b5cb70324b762094eacbf069e5d689b8db1b754d","bb387edbf67af04ad1a34e348a4ae73cec33c4bae613b9f0004617e11fd21ba9","99b68ccc26fa71d62765a580ae7330e28ca3a5a5e5ef7afe58c2a8d9655f1cdc","bb81fefa9e0bf549cc05e6b0254a44dcd8ea9da31ff2c65d332789ee25f7311f","987650e1bc810d2c24d10a823054b29ae888cd89a4d131e2589d5925c5dcba8f","47e082545a32adecc92d8fd072fcc8f2480cb03db21b24d74a85eaf388b1cd5b","0377fd80acc06533ccf7639a329086e6f3063bd02cfcba1527e8f0a01bf15f1e","ba73d5bd5a819e40d15150f4869aa2bdb9372572e2c68affca8fdd1704efb2ff","6cedbc991448bb85aeb2055492b31dcfb4d42872f0a4c0e41f85eac3a7157e3b","5e6e78c509901ae3936d881dd0c9b12c94a02c1a5b9226ba72b61bcdd6bc46b1","2f6571028be5d5692f485da63534bcd2446fcf98ce61f146ec558cf4a6e7f41a","9f9d869084689e03c4401d051b9815a1e81848e158fa4732d349ce7bee40f265","3e90c181e4dcbc5394354b7666c2f82011ceb272e12c37bd3ea5ca914a5a754c"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[120,143],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2304803.zip::R2-2304803 Correction to PosSRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE.docx:p120"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2304803.zip::R2-2304803 Correction to PosSRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The MAC entity shall, when triggered by the upper layer to send Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request, cancel the triggered Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request, if any and trigger another Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request according to the upper layer's request.","paragraph_zero_based":144},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The MAC entity shall,","paragraph_zero_based":145},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request MAC CE has been triggered, and not cancelled:","paragraph_zero_based":146},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if indication from upper layer has been received that the triggered Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request MAC CE should be cancelled; or","paragraph_zero_based":147},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the pre-configured measurement gap indicated in the Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request MAC CE has already been activated/deactivated according to clause 5.18.20:","paragraph_zero_based":148},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>cancel the triggered Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request MAC CE.","paragraph_zero_based":149},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if UL-SCH resources are available for a new transmission and these UL-SCH resources can accommodate the Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request MAC CE plus its subheader as a result of logical channel prioritization:","paragraph_zero_based":150},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>instruct the Multiplexing and Assembly procedure to generate the Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request MAC CE according to the upper layer's request;","paragraph_zero_based":151},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>cancel triggered Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request MAC CE.","paragraph_zero_based":152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>trigger a Scheduling Request for Positioning Measurement Gap Activation/Deactivation Request MAC CE as specified in clause 5.4.4.","paragraph_zero_based":154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"================================NEXT CHANGE========================================","paragraph_zero_based":155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.26Positioning SRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE","paragraph_zero_based":156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.26.1General","paragraph_zero_based":157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Periodic and semi-persistent Positioning SRS can be configured for Positioning SRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE.","paragraph_zero_based":158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The MAC entity shall, if the TA of the configured Positioning SRS is valid according to clause 5.26.2, and the conditions for positioning SRS transmission in clause 7.3.1 of TS 38.213 [6] and clause 6.2.1.4 of TS 38.214 [7] are satisfied:","paragraph_zero_based":159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-instruct to the lower layer according to TS 38.214 [7] to transmit Positioning Periodic SRS or activated Semi-Persistent SRS according to clause 5.18.17,.","paragraph_zero_based":160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"====================================NEXT CHANGE===================================","paragraph_zero_based":161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6.1.3.36SP Positioning SRS Activation/Deactivation MAC CE","paragraph_zero_based":162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The SP Positioning SRS Activation/Deactivation MAC CE is identified by a MAC subheader with eLCID as specified in Table 6.2.1-1b. It has a variable size with following fields:","paragraph_zero_based":163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-A/D: This field indicates whether to activate or deactivate indicated SP Positioning SRS resource set. The field is set to 1 to indicate activation, otherwise it indicates deactivation;","paragraph_zero_based":164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Positioning SRS Resource Set's Cell ID: This field indicates the identity of the Serving Cell, which contains activated/deactivated SP Positioning SRS Resource Set. If the C field is set to 0, this field also indicates the identity of the Serving Cell which contains all resources indicated by the Spatial Relation for Resource IDi fields, if present. The length of the field is 5 bits;","paragraph_zero_based":165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Positioning SRS Resource Set's BWP ID: This field indicates a UL BWP as the codepoint of the DCI bandwidth part indicator field as specified in TS 38.212 [9], which contains activated/deactivated SP Positioning SRS Resource Set. If the C field is set to 0, this field also indicates the identity of the BWP which contains all resources indicated by the Spatial Relation for Resource IDi fields, if present. The length of the field is 2 bits;","paragraph_zero_based":166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-C: This field indicates whether the octets containing Resource Serving Cell ID field(s) and Resource BWP ID field(s) within the field Spatial Relation for Resource ID i are present, except for Spatial Relation Resource IDi with DL-PRS or SSB. When A/D is set to 1, if this field is set to 1, the octets containing Resource Serving Cell ID field(s) and Resource BWP ID field(s) in the field Spatial Relation for Resource IDi are present, otherwise if this field is set to 0, they are not present. When A/D is set to 0, this field is always set to 0 that they are not present;","paragraph_zero_based":167}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"95b5452dcdc46b87411657002095bc67fd93f084654e53f76beb747cb0df61f4","original_member_sha256":"a5700810783730dc819152118c725930196bfe57c3f7e171d8317425bb53ec2f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["eb63141cb8a6f6d13437bcf68fcf9d1fe016f0dcc89eb7e687e856f43bb9310b","dcdcf5da8b7bd57f57f5a61abbbd8e17cf99851110a77ba908847c3a0293fbc7","a2270c5e5c12c742a3381d7d74fb9c63f4bf062b51b42629b8b0f94b43fc1892","5f0e4472eea4655650f71ed8ca696939eab84faeb4a54bf6c3e8953ee224c3b4","5d674bb261bb82dc0833ac8bb0fcf827aa95b0231c69190f021e5e185ec24f2d","ebcde51af90958dac02557a4559cd5ec192b8df1e9ca0fd0ecc2cc2b8661dae4","691944b9dce602c74fd9c8ce1c177cb44675af3f91746ff2df3236b02dac64df","b48fa170bfddb9e17f45b9aa965e583c03c6db0f2cd765ea62b69d453102b0d4","8ad44112d5d0eefd0289ead6f41af25eadd0c4d7551b2cd8b101bf3f48d2f225","99ed4fd2bbd6e1bccfb359b8d76c241a2c83041503463f7054b48754517b9ef8","393cf4869e654bed65df44a126fbd9054a29b8c58b5f7232c38e59518db63df0","b0b3ed513778a0e884873a6715d714c7e2eeb5bad891a1151a95ea3e59986809","8d3385aeee6f0da7387bc7fd50b48fcd44c9f022ede425bc74575c3f89c86c65","9316dcfcbeb3df597cde33e536bf2c17416313be20fca1d79ed9871e4ef81e6c","5e1cba02d561701b0c0ebb6ce0aeec3fa29660233ddb23adebf36fe44f4d2cb1","9c853bc1c06ce8833672d08ef8101bf5cfc10f45837d9f0b296cf5c76de2fb4c","9bd324c44d39fd408e9367e5d8da5f7ff70175a619b84885bc4f0c4a3c0297d4","db040a39339ac868f37f277bb2c6544ca5e627e6224fa5869b316cb96c9b0c2f","15e426877d31cc9044b5f402c779240e345ade6e1126d5e452f0c99c7e33961c","df1821fef6fec175e9e38b8ae96b759fba623822908e9428ac416d7ff7ff733d","89e26f1bd0ad307d4a92c8d8a7ad49d3693f7831c870b64c02e96cfaa18626e8","81b5da29a3be8a180127158747c812d0e04a5d007ae6b164b28acab112d415ed","3662524a8ed07773d4a4e2862aee75c4177885d27abdb23c49ea2c2cef6c906c","902e89169a774765a4c702524bb05e1b7c8996cb3115e0cbd80d57cf2fd189f5"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[144,167],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2304803.zip::R2-2304803 Correction to PosSRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE.docx:p144"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2304803.zip::R2-2304803 Correction to PosSRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SUL: This field indicates whether the MAC CE applies to the NUL carrier or SUL carrier configuration. This field is set to 1 to indicate that it applies to the SUL carrier configuration, and it is set to 0 to indicate that it applies to the NUL carrier configuration;","paragraph_zero_based":168},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Positoining SRS Resource Set ID: This field indicates the SP Positioning SRS Resource Set identified by SRS-PosResourceSetId as specified in TS 38.331 [5], which is to be activated or deactivated. The length of the field is 4 bits;","paragraph_zero_based":169},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Spatial Relation for Resource IDi: The field Spatial Relation for Resource IDi is only present if MAC CE is used for activation, i.e. the A/D field is set to 1. M is the total number of Positioning SRS resource(s) configured under the SP Positioning SRS resource set indicated by the field Positioning SRS Resource Set ID. There are 4 types of Spatial Relation for Resource IDi, which is indicated by the F (F0 and F1) field within. The fields within Spatial Relation for Resource IDi are shown in Figures 6.1.3.36-2 to 6.1.3.36-5 for the 4 types of Spatial Relations for Resource IDi;","paragraph_zero_based":170},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-S: This field indicates whether the fields Spatial Relation for Resource IDi for the positioning SRS resource i within the positioning SRS resource set are present. If the field is set to 1, the fields Spatial Relation for Resource IDi are present; otherwise, they are absent;","paragraph_zero_based":171},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-R: Reserved bit, set to 0.","paragraph_zero_based":172},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":173},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 6.1.3.36-1: SP Positioning SRS Activation/Deactivation MAC CE","paragraph_zero_based":174},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":175},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 6.1.3.36-2: Spatial Relation for Resource IDi with NZP CSI-RS","paragraph_zero_based":176},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":177},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 6.1.3.36-3: Spatial Relation for Resource IDi with SSB","paragraph_zero_based":178},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":179},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 6.1.3.36-4: Spatial Relation for Resource IDi with SRS","paragraph_zero_based":180},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":181},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 6.1.3.36-5: Spatial Relation for Resource IDi with DL-PRS","paragraph_zero_based":182},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field Spatial Relation for Resource IDi consists of the following fields:","paragraph_zero_based":183},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-F0: This field indicates the type of a resource used as a spatial relation for the ith Positioning SRS resource within the Positioning SRS Resource Set indicated with the field Positioning SRS Resource Set ID. The field is set to 00 to indicate NZP CSI-RS resource index is used; it is set to 01 to indicate SSB index is used; it is set to 10 to indicate SRS resource index is used; it is set to 11 to indicate DL-PRS index is used. The length of the field is 2 bits;","paragraph_zero_based":184},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-F1: This field indicates the type of SRS resource used as spatial relation for the ith Positioning SRS resource within the SP Positioning SRS Resource Set indicated with the field Positioning SRS Resource Set ID when F0 is set to 10. The field is set to 0 to indicate SRS resource index SRS-ResourceId as defined in TS 38.331 [5] is used; the field is set to 1 to indicate Positioning SRS resource index SRS-PosResourceId as defined in TS 38.331 [5] is used;","paragraph_zero_based":185},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-NZP CSI-RS Resource ID: This field contains an index of NZP-CSI-RS-ResourceID, as specified in TS 38.331 [5], indicating the NZP CSI-RS resource, which is used to derive the spatial relation for the positioning SRS. The length of the field is 8 bits;","paragraph_zero_based":186},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SSB index: This field contains an index of SSB SSB-Index as specified in TS 38.331 [5] and/or TS 37.355 [23]. The length of the field is 6 bits;","paragraph_zero_based":187},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-PCI: This field contains physical cell identity PhysCellId as specified in TS 38.331 [5] and/or TS 37.355 [23]. The length of the field is 10 bits;","paragraph_zero_based":188},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SRS resource ID: When F1 is set to 0, the field indicates an index for SRS resource SRS-ResourceId as defined in TS 38.331 [5]; When F1 is set to 1, the field indicates an index for Positioning SRS resource SRS-PosResourceId as defined in TS 38.331 [5]. The length of the field is 5 bits representing the index from 0 to 31;","paragraph_zero_based":189},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-E: This field indicates the extension of SRS resource ID as the MSB of SRS resource ID. The total length of the extended SRS resource ID is 6 bits. If E bit is set to 1, the SRS resource ID value is 5-bit SRS resource ID field + 32;","paragraph_zero_based":190},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-DL-PRS Resource Set ID: This field contains an index for DL-PRS Resource Set nr-DL-PRS-ResourceSetId as defined in TS 37.355 [23]. The length of the field is 3 bits;","paragraph_zero_based":191}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"95b5452dcdc46b87411657002095bc67fd93f084654e53f76beb747cb0df61f4","original_member_sha256":"a5700810783730dc819152118c725930196bfe57c3f7e171d8317425bb53ec2f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["65a8ef6d95773fdb68e4ef8417df7c7b0475c708591d3d2c5eccee4d2616d1c9","f4bcbfbd298932418f1a521ad8f80f491ca8fa2c330ea2e936ace6a5e550256b","e1ccd0f484d8851f5b6f1ab1d03ab15910ee0a552defc8c90a87edf7fdd6a59a","2b277abd94bf2d2241b72468e2fec154c0a7bf3e966df1ed0d463b9f5fd55f4f","5822fe0fba6234f10353c0ca30118726e95ab2ceab7d2c1b705f56a35b7388af","cb23ed6bcd3d626086af2439d20cf29ed397ca8c8994b6bce008b1b57d43ab67","a3c0648aa1a3be24a7ee69cbba389d27356ea15f9aa89777c2ab9622c4be4990","d59350752bb8e1849f2e3cc4e02f3e1eac11859d067f69524e2182d3e3096ec4","57af52e8c46e55e926a822e552112e92b4ce69b17abc271696cfb4f14729e653","130762b037deedcecea1a789ce37dc711115cb6c78b93362105277f4616b7ae7","e8715168802c6a1a4875b5f95d740dc4247725727b0cf75933410b713dfe9807","c97c6f6879b6328d572e5cb7ce7e42386ed441251211ebe923a7fc7d8c916195","2c2260f9c68909f7c00e24be7bf59d9de4414d6c253fd0a409d5cb4aebf6214b","40ca4fd5d4225d70daaa700852566adf18ee563e0b29cd441804ddfe09610aec","6e69cbc271f45f9a0cedeef3e57d51d11ed6b83b851299a73c958a55c6a40450","ef11fd9315472c53121cb5ea6011ba2da5ec2e14f00279901664772a7e8d2200","75081a3178f982b099123b11d4fa463e606f70df65531ace1b24335249e8025c","356264239c4b768babdd53fa32bef593a15b39b578c84200e21238d50410e1e8","dd0474d87c11cf9f31a09f7384d6112aa10a7c8b80a52bd1fd93e5aa86aebbc8","0e20adea9c25254a7bd1414855b11fa1ee5b9f920f9190f5528d2d6b2ea6de7a","ba4fe880408ae8ad35c88cd9355a54c48763d4503799f2412c27138553e52844","ec392b85a17d573c7265ac83b4936105805d7a7cb834c39bbf8cf288ffd8e708","b860c07838d8f57a74f8f53e2bd6061b674889c7224ea96b1b343ebe3ade149d","3c06848f549792dd44bc30ad08692208e9f522d2048ca7f414ac26ee11fdfacd"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[168,191],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2304803.zip::R2-2304803 Correction to PosSRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE.docx:p168"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2304803.zip::R2-2304803 Correction to PosSRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-DL-PRS Resource ID: This field contains an index for DL-PRS resource nr-DL-PRS-Resource-Id as defined in TS 37.355 [23]. The length of the field is 6 bits;","paragraph_zero_based":192},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-DL-PRS ID: This field contains an identity for DL-PRS resource dl-PRS-ID as defined in TS 37.355 [23]. The length of the field is 8 bits;","paragraph_zero_based":193},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-PI: This field indicates whether the field DL-PRS resource ID is present within the Spatial Relation for Resource IDi with DL-PRS. If the field is set to 1, the octet containing the field DL-PRS resource ID is present; otherwise, the octet is omitted;","paragraph_zero_based":194},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SI: This field indicates whether the field SSB index is present within the Spatial Relation for Resource IDi with SSB. If the field is set to 1, the octet containing the field SSB index is present; otherwise, the octet is omitted;","paragraph_zero_based":195},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Resource Serving Cell IDi: This field indicates the identity of the Serving Cell on which the resource used for spatial relationship derivation for the ith Positioning SRS resource is located. The length of the field is 5 bits;","paragraph_zero_based":196},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Resource BWP IDi: This field indicates a UL BWP as the codepoint of the DCI bandwidth part indicator field as specified in TS 38.212 [9], on which the resource used for spatial relationship derivation for the ith Positioning SRS resource is located. The length of the field is 2 bits.","paragraph_zero_based":197},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":198},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"==================================END OF CHANGES==================================","paragraph_zero_based":199},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":200}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"95b5452dcdc46b87411657002095bc67fd93f084654e53f76beb747cb0df61f4","original_member_sha256":"a5700810783730dc819152118c725930196bfe57c3f7e171d8317425bb53ec2f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["a5e3046c21e4c4448d142891e46fac5fe7acb6cb427fe56559f5019b166fcd8b","7d9e85785cfc5e4cacb00264eaa72df2337ada14a0b9d020ee689001ea4a77b8","369da0d74d76a212780e23d780380dbc5f110a362906d363f4b96aaf29b6c64c","c926651da554db22593743ce66b07fda2095493b6543356cab689d8f92d03cca","2f468833771ef066b993db7680b0a6abb19404824fb9ce91ee432fc24219de60","e2e08fe3297f8fe3ffee62739afad8d5fece08df85ed84031d844ac502be2d31","dcf92fa48abe716b5d0adef93fb3f0f94da069966346fad4cb46105b37653d8d","56861f60d0bed566c06c67d4c445a340c9bd996017543b5a5302a7588a6b2a05","63006fecee8fc25bbb86877bd20f2d193f5a6dea8c48cf450341e702728abab0"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[192,200],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2304803.zip::R2-2304803 Correction to PosSRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE.docx:p192"}
