ow":"R2-2305363.zip::R2-2305363 Correction on PosSRS-RRC-Inactive-OutsideInitialUL-BWP.docx:p24"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2305363.zip::R2-2305363 Correction on PosSRS-RRC-Inactive-OutsideInitialUL-BWP.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"F","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-17","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-16(Release 16)Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)Rel-19(Release 19)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For IE PosSRS-RRC-Inactive-OutsideInitialUL-BWP in the current TS 38.331, the meaning of the enumerated values for IE maxSRSposBandwidthForEachSCS-withinCC-FR1-r17 and maxSRSposBandwidthForEachSCS-withinCC-FR2-r17 are ambiguous. For example, what does bwX mean (X MHz or X RBs)? According to the definition in TS 38.306, it should be interpreted as X MHz. ","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"posSRS-RRC-Inactive-OutsideInitialUL-BWP-r17","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates support of Positioning SRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE state configured outside initial UL BWP. The capability signalling comprises the following parameters:","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxSRSposBandwidthForEachSCS-withinCC-FR1-r17 Indicates the maximum SRS bandwidth supported for each SCS that UE supports within a single CC for FR1;","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxSRSposBandwidthForEachSCS-withinCC-FR2-r17 indicates the maximum SRS bandwidth supported for each SCS that UE supports within a single CC for FR2;","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For the correct understanding of the values within the above IEs, corresponding correction should be made, i.e., change “bwX” to “mhzX”.","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For IE maxSRSposBandwidthForEachSCS-withinCC-FR1-r17 and maxSRSposBandwidthForEachSCS-withinCC-FR2-r17, change the enumerated values “bwX” to “mhzX” to clarify the meaning of the enumerated values.","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"24273b4ef99b5a2d0758d9b8e3ad1f745d80c24ed85e18922d59df74d935fbfe","original_member_sha256":"797e2b62538c09f6c1b2b2e6eef304c2e4c50fe5f5092a2af009507d16bc66db","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e4ea5591218aa96d0cd407936b651eb165fb4c75e229dab64ec9de6be991cb96","2d00e3b1a82065155328ddd802c3d4a8ebff11f4a0d6da9ecf9b1e34dc8ebfc8","8bb13f99acb223c5eba6fed86da1bb6a30ac61eb5c9c12af4d63bc738065819c","761fa4d36b282591b5f5bb5ee554c6086f6eb9d59