{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2305891.zip::R2-2305891_(LPP CR on local coordinates)_v01.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"...","paragraph_zero_based":2664},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":2665},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":2666},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":2667},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":2668},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR-SSB-Config field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":2669},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"nr-ARFCN","paragraph_zero_based":2670},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the ARFCN of the first RE of SSB's RB#10.","paragraph_zero_based":2671},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ss-PBCH-BlockPower","paragraph_zero_based":2672},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Average EPRE of the resources elements that carry secondary synchronization signals in dBm that the NW used for SSB transmission, see TS 38.213 [48], clause 7.","paragraph_zero_based":2673},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"halfFrameIndex","paragraph_zero_based":2674},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the 5 msec offset of the SSB within a 10 msec system frame.","paragraph_zero_based":2675},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ssb-periodicity","paragraph_zero_based":2676},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The SSB periodicity in ms for the rate matching purpose.","paragraph_zero_based":2677},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ssb-PositionsInBurst","paragraph_zero_based":2678},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the time domain positions of the transmitted SS-blocks in a half frame with SS/PBCH blocks as defined in TS 38.213 [48], clause 4.1. The first/leftmost bit corresponds to SS/PBCH block index 0, the second bit corresponds to SS/PBCH block index 1, and so on. Value 0 in the bitmap indicates that the corresponding SS/PBCH block is not transmitted while value 1 indicates that the corresponding SS/PBCH block is transmitted. ","paragraph_zero_based":2679},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ssb-SubcarrierSpacing","paragraph_zero_based":2680},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Subcarrier spacing of SSB. Only the values 15 kHz or 30 kHz (FR1), and 120 kHz or 240 kHz (FR2) are applicable.","paragraph_zero_based":2681},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sfn-SSB-Offset","paragraph_zero_based":2682},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the 10 msec system frame offset of the SSB within the SSB periodicity. Value 0 indicates that the SSB is transmitted in the first system frame; 1 indicates that the SSB is transmitted in the second system frame and so on. This field shall be configured according to the field ssb-Periodicity and the indicated system frame shall not exceed the configured SSB periodicity.","paragraph_zero_based":2683},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":2684},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–NR-TimeStamp","paragraph_zero_based":2685},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE NR-TimeStamp defines the UE measurement associated time stamp.","paragraph_zero_based":2686},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":2687}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ad5861da0dccef1291129531d32d787af0fd13713ef27f554120fd6d7dfa3c8b","original_member_sha256":"85e43ed4cce9951e9169dd51891e9ea74001bd66e886c9b8fd4a0c481e900934","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["4d96be7e2e3fb91bf6c0d2e17931e576f86b875aef63dd19cc0a22b3eb5f744f","830ab9f5e6914451fc6d672e180a610309e0d812cdcb6e4b534d780e75370a08","e3c133a287a770632327777dcba5d2bb8820125df69d9e11e92c3aa0a365a725","29ec7d6313e49749243887c8c2a8b74317f765ae064b5c3c61b2d197e98369fe","2956a5cbfab16ca199394e96047990123470dcc4d31c47791a25ea7dc7bc1664","56f838b69bb4ab8c1fdcc7ffadbb9a6c5ba365c6e70ad9796fa4138bd3b2b4b7","21ec7