n the first entry of the NR-TRP-LocationInfoPerFreqLayer list; otherwise it is optionally present, need OP.","paragraph_zero_based":2901},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":2902},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR-TRP-LocationInfo field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":2903}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ad5861da0dccef1291129531d32d787af0fd13713ef27f554120fd6d7dfa3c8b","original_member_sha256":"85e43ed4cce9951e9169dd51891e9ea74001bd66e886c9b8fd4a0c481e900934","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e8abbd6f969aa448770c949deed08f07a7bb2abc9f086204dda0cb9501174edb","6d61e5218c93ae079a19c54974e2bbae60d7ee146c21b90c778ae094a1799396","fa9aacb163518e9689958345c615567b918f0b8bd5b757441d2dd5d832f302e3","fdeb37e9f830b2583e7066619f1018a24ca26f5aac0e87c07d1ade73293e267c","36ab7402e5ffdfee0699ebd5c6d3a714ee770a3b234a6a57c0d62501c0b703f7","4b9a20ee7a3e2368baa82049e05690fda52e185f8166949d060bedb2e6e5c9d0","776cc802783211c1a89f4b462a729603ebb2a4772f7e10ae6849d08686448d50","e551026c5935175e224424c1670988dad743ca1ae0e86119eb71534f57dc65e6","6667f777ed79a238d60ff4e10732957ec5281c2e1e69fa2334e7513a4fcf4ce1","642a8a47eec93c88e55d66dcce131df400d366115c8a8026f729f138aa5e1254","76e1e0969ad9e0a7e6b702a21500e25288f21fc17c2c2cc65ac639546a5752d3","6257562cc345dd82ea6ca0fa7b6743dba73175945ce1cf007c3766b35e0490a0","3a937ed8a970339089a4a0ded817fc6682e1a959d6fa1b6f512c34df1832f6bd","1b964a41c8119e7763700c32c06270cf91cd76cd042e7db6ed66e5598a7fdf24","97950827bb16dadf16a5a0589fecce20fe6c3f2e02084780426cdd836aed83ea","099cf55c8ecc28e60a7a35f012dcf4763e2b18ebd224a4d801c1128bbb4634b3","e3a6364f71fff7abccaeedb617fb226c60607a496218b5dd5fb4a7d5da08b2ca","d249e72d6a5f9219c00b8c02bc0c8c8d4c712b805fc00af61131eba37abfe8ca","80a6b49efbf5eeddf8bed30d4a36d5e1420526902e628f5d27c66ff967882efb","1544e073949f435b664e4039d1ea80475bc3101bd17a8b41f07badcaef1dde01","abc90bcdf44e4c6c5deb55b5b4898a055fc4e09ad20ea3877fd60633726d903f","eddad6767e8f8f113b1b60bb1a0bc575b0f33226944478ddcb79554d118e190b","eb2ad664bc3bed113ce7a108edeb43730531e43bf522068735e6870e269d2187","1376b5d88d999ee115a6f632f193be3aa7758d55569a550948cdcec85af024b9"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[2880,2903],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2305891.zip::R2-2305891_(LPP CR on local coordinates)_v01.docx:p2880"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2305891.zip::R2-2305891_(LPP CR on local coordinates)_v01.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"referencePoint","paragraph_zero_based":2904},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field specifies the reference point used to define the TRP location in the trp-LocationInfoList. If this field is absent, the reference point is the same as in the previous entry of the NR-TRP-LocationInfoPerFreqLayer list.","paragraph_zero_based":2905},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"trp-LocationInfoList","paragraph_zero_based":2906},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field provides the antenna reference point locations of the DL-PRS Resources for the TRPs and comprises the following sub-fields:","paragraph_zero_based":2907},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-dl-PRS-ID: This field is used along with a DL-PRS Resource Set ID and a DL-PRS Resources ID to uniquely identify a DL-PRS Resource, and is associated to a single TRP.","paragraph_zero_based":2908},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-nr-PhysCellID: This field specifies the physical cell identity of the associated TRP.","paragraph_zero_based":2909},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-nr-CellGlobalID: This field specifies the NCGI, the globally unique identity of a cell in NR, of the associated TRP.","paragraph_zero_based":2910},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-nr-ARFCN: This field specifies the NR-ARFCN of the TRP's CD-SSB (as defined in TS 38.300 [47]) corresponding to nr-PhysCellID.","paragraph_zero_based":2911},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-associated-DL-PRS-ID: This field, if present, specifies the dl-PRS-ID of the associated TRP from which the trp-location or trp-LocationCartesian information is adopted. If the field is present, the field trp-Location and trp-LocationCartesian shall be absent.","paragraph_zero_based":2912},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-trp-Location, trp-LocationCartesian: This field provides the location of the TRP relative to the referencePoint location either in geodetic coordinates (trp-Location) or local Cartesian coordinates (trp-LocationCartesian). If this field is absent the TRP location coincides with the referencePoint location, unless the field associated-dl-PRS-ID is present, in which case the trp-Location or trp-LocationCartesian is adopted from the associated TRP indicated by associated-dl-PRS-ID.","paragraph_zero_based":2913},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"- trp-DL-PRS-ResourceSets: This field provides the antenna reference point location(s) of the DL-PRS Resource Set(s) associated with this TRP. If this field is absent, the antenna reference point location(s) of the DL-PRS Resource Set(s) coincides with the trp-Location/trp-LocationCartesian location. This field comprises the following sub-fields:","paragraph_zero_based":2914},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-dl-PRS-ResourceSetARP, dl-PRS-ResourceSetARP-Cartesian: This field provides the antenna reference point location of the DL-PRS Resource Set relative to the trp-Location or trp-LocationCartesian location. If this field is absent, the antenna reference point location of this DL-PRS Resource Set coincides with the trp-Location or trp-LocationCartesian location.","paragraph_zero_based":2915},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-dl-PRS-Resource-ARP-List: This field provides the antenna reference point location(s) of the DL-PRS Resource(s) associated with this Resource Set of the TRP. If this field is absent, the antenna reference point location(s) of the DL-PRS Resources coincides with the dl-PRS-ResourceSetARP or dl-PRS-ResourceSetARP-Cartesian location. This field comprises the following sub-fields:","paragraph_zero_based":2916},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-dl-PRS-Resource-ARP-location, dl-PRS-Resource-ARP-locationCartesian: This field provides the antenna reference point location of the DL-PRS Resource associated with the DL-PRS Resource Set of the TRP relative to the dl-PRS-ResourceSetARP/dl-PRS-ResourceSetARP-Cartesian location. If this field is absent, the antenna reference point location of this DL-PRS Resource coincides with the dl-PRS-ResourceSetARP location or dl-PRS-Resource-ARP-locationCartesian.","paragraph_zero_based":2917},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":2918},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE: The locations may be provided in either geodetic coordinates (RelativeLocation) or local Cartesian coordinates (RelativeCartesianLocation), but not both.","paragraph_zero_based":2919},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–NR-UE-TEG-Capability","paragraph_zero_based":2920},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE NR-UE-TEG-Capability defines the TEG capability of the target device.","paragraph_zero_based":2921},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":2922},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":2923},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR-UE-TEG-Capability-r17 ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":2924},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"nr-UE-TEG-ID-CapabilityBandList-r17SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..nrMaxBands-r16)) OF","paragraph_zero_based":2925},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR-UE-TEG-ID-CapabilityPerBand-r17OPTIONAL,","paragraph_zero_based":2926},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"...","paragraph_zero_based":2927}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ad5861da0dccef1291129531d32d787af0fd13713ef27f554120fd6d7dfa3c8b","original_member_sha256":"85e43ed4cce9951e9169dd51891e9ea74001bd66e886c9b8fd4a0c481e900934","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["448c3385d2b40aa2c3b62bf91cd0ff9901790d218c141fc19d9cf1d795b57526","e0246420e3b3b045d8c35c8c88c8cdf2f2dcdda21159c8f1ff727bc1307b8c88","cbd0c2ca57cb485b6cebd8903f50932163d805158dc8b787dd77fedeeac93ce9","1861e2f7d46dcadac23d65c53fcc7e05eb89c945cc6e858564a1f4034b7a645f","810db7417f259387148cce5b6b2b4a4429dbfbab869832efcdb