{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2305891.zip::R2-2305891_(LPP CR on local coordinates)_v01.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"OPTIONAL,","paragraph_zero_based":3072},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"...","paragraph_zero_based":3073},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":3074},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":3075},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":3076},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":3077},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR-UL-SRS-Capability field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":3078},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-PosResourceConfigCA-BandList","paragraph_zero_based":3079},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the number of SRS for positioning resources supported by the target device. The target device includes this field for each band for the current configured CA band combination. The capability signalling comprises the following parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":3080},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-freqBandIndicatorNR indicates the current configured NR band of the target device.","paragraph_zero_based":3081},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumberSRS-PosResourceSetsPerBWP indicates the maximum number of SRS Resource Sets for positioning supported by the target device per BWP. Enumerated values n1, n2, n4, n8, n12, n16 correspond to 1, 2, 4, 8, 12, 16 SRS Resource Sets for positioning, respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":3082},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumberSRS-PosResourcesPerBWP indicates the maximum number of periodic, semi-persistent, and aperiodic SRS Resources for positioning supported by the target device per BWP. Enumerated values n1, n2, n4, n8, n16, n32, n64 correspond to 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64 SRS Resources for positioning, respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":3083},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumberPeriodicSRS-PosResourcesPerBWP indicates the maximum number of periodic SRS Resources for positioning supported by the target device per BWP. Enumerated values n1, n2, n4, n8, n16, n32, n64 correspond to 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64 periodic SRS Resources for positioning, respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":3084},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumberAP-SRS-PosResourcesPerBWP indicates the maximum number of aperiodic SRS Resources for positioning supported by the target device per BWP. Enumerated values n1, n2, n4, n8, n16, n32, n64 correspond to 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64 aperiodic SRS Resources for positioning, respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":3085},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumberSP-SRS-PosResourcesPerBWP indicates the maximum number of semi-persistent SRS Resources for positioning supported by the target device per BWP. Enumerated values n1, n2, n4, n8, n16, n32, n64 correspond to 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64 semi-persistent SRS Resources for positioning, respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":3086},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"maxNumberSRS-PosPathLossEstimateAllServingCells","paragraph_zero_based":3087},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the maximum number of pathloss estimates that the UE can simultaneously maintain for all the SRS resource sets for positioning across all cells in addition to the up to four pathloss estimates that the UE maintains per serving cell for the PUSCH/PUCCH/SRS transmissions. The UE shall include this field if the UE supports any of olpc-SRS-PosBasedOnPRS-Serving, olpc-SRS-PosBasedOnSSB-Neigh and olpc-SRS-PosBasedOnPRS-Neigh. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3088},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"maxNumberSRS-PosSpatialRelationsAllServingCells","paragraph_zero_based":3089},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"indicates the maximum number of maintained spatial relations for all the SRS resource sets for positioning across all serving cells in addition to the spatial relations maintained spatial relations per serving cell for the PUSCH/PUCCH/SRS transmissions. It is only applied for FR2. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports any of spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnSSB-Serving, spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnCSI-RS-Serving, spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnPRS-Serving, spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnSSB-Neigh or spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnPRS-Neigh. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3090},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"olpc-SRS-Pos","paragraph_zero_based":3091},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the UE supports open-loop power control for SRS for positioning. The capability signalling comprises the following parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":3092},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-olpc-SRS-PosBasedOnPRS-Serving indicates whether the UE supports OLPC for SRS for positioning based on PRS from the serving cell in the same band. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports NR-DL-PRS-ProcessingCapability and srs-PosResources TS38.331 [35] Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3093},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-olpc-SRS-PosBasedOnSSB-Neigh indicates whether the UE supports OLPC for SRS for positioning based on SSB from the neighbouring cell in the same band. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports srs-PosResources TS 38.331 [35]. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3094},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-olpc-SRS-PosBasedOnPRS-Neigh indicates whether the UE supports OLPC for SRS for positioning based on PRS from the neighbouring cell in the same band. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports olpc-SRS-PosBasedOnPRS-Serving. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3095}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ad5861da0dccef1291129531d32d787af0fd13713ef27f554120fd6d7dfa3c8b","original_member_sha256":"85e43ed4cce9951e9169dd51891e9ea74001bd66e886c9b8fd4a0c481e900934","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["9074754a947e7896bec60dabd9613d999572e36f204766aa0965f515af9c563e","459270aa7719c57b9617f198548ee92c0d79b2d19cc72dc28f1b202c8ffee70d","409cafb15ec46b33393ae44648c930e01a4635f3d803a031a22c41ded78a8859","d3a3490eea05292d55230a8f0e9f2eec4234377330e5cdeee32e19de65fff181","f84aa880c48fcbdca016d7f0a0c1e26080d157201a5b3c8559ffa88569cd135f","66e4dcaec0631929310c1635e300482abc7be52374abd31688eb37783051994a","53c22e2b8e6609e1bb4fe63270961c2d87897582e83929d9c931d56b86eb2af3","001ce025a327e886cbadcdfede78320575cdad2a3bf20a57840c4bef6ef2dd24","19b5f3a06c9a0fdf906749b9113859dbee827600f81da09ba37665f6fea77528","7bdb67de78dff310e33aab7b94065b16484de315ef12b8df0ec1147f5722d6ed","5711d115cd8612ec2913978cdb67c77c63d62bd57d118b31da7a0b5df7d94d44","759fc2eb0199395dc1c2bed128dbe41efc0c48b12314d6c0fa65a337f6d2c06d","d6ef5908ee904bf35c69d4a3f616ce091def1873a2ed3f1c4a21a8ad4b8f0bab","711755e6ac8e073785476dd637d4becdec273e9cf6b232419df724ed3a37b96a","dcd480faa7c4be5cff52e14230c046caa0f25b89b33005e214190f2ea25ce7c5","d772a500bce958216d70eb61f1f439c351f12d78d6e27a60dca17e06572dcb89","12ee53834ad1cb74601ab83827d0e843eed2d0a227120673b661935db488aaae","a8a8121ee93b992930f0cc306128ce2d20897e7c0feb9fec7895e811717e6bd5","e7853dafbbe4d8a827dd8eb8e4d3e5c03c3a3c6d51522a404c0fe40cb30e3313","321d7795401679d208de4898c519ac232a9aaa6538f836412864527ee83fc3dc","99a9757fa48c448316e584b2683825ec7764364a7dcc186a75f7915b0092545e","49b35219b69d5328bb9d280113dcb78e8803af8c82182bfbd610e1e913da5f1c","e66b5ca492e14a60c64a0bb2521a6f03165beeae85203d9692463645efc103bd","f18047ed2409b0427d8ee6e31a87d43ac5b8841459d498452b0ea2321708ea39"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[3072,3095],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2305891.zip::R2-2305891_(LPP 