{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2305891.zip::R2-2305891_(LPP CR on local coordinates)_v01.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Note:A PRS from a PRS-only TP is treated as PRS from a non-serving cell.","paragraph_zero_based":3096},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumberPathLossEstimatePerServing indicates the maximum number of pathloss estimates that the UE can simultaneously maintain for all the SRS resource sets for positioning per serving cell in addition to the up to four pathloss estimates that the UE maintains per serving cell for the PUSCH/PUCCH/SRS transmissions. The UE shall include this field if the UE supports any of olpc-SRS-PosBasedOnPRS-Serving, olpc-SRS-PosBasedOnSSB-Neigh and olpc-SRS-PosBasedOnPRS-Neigh. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3097},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"spatialRelationsSRS-Pos","paragraph_zero_based":3098},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the UE supports spatial relations for SRS for positioning. It is only applicable for FR2. The capability signalling comprises the following parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":3099},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnSSB-Serving indicates whether the UE supports spatial relation for SRS for positioning based on SSB from the serving cell in the same band. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports srs-PosResources TS 38.331 [35]. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3100},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnCSI-RS-Serving indicates whether the UE supports spatial relation for SRS for positioning based on CSI-RS from the serving cell in the same band. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnSSB-Serving. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3101},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnPRS-Serving indicates whether the UE supports spatial relation for SRS for positioning based on PRS from the serving cell in the same band. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports any of DL-PRS Resources for DL-AoD, DL-PRS Resources for DL-TDOA or DL-PRS Resources for Multi-RTT, or srs-PosResources TS 38.331 [35]. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3102},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnSRS indicates whether the UE supports spatial relation for SRS for positioning based on SRS in the same band. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports srs-PosResources TS 38.331 [35]. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3103},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnSSB-Neigh indicates whether the UE supports spatial relation for SRS for positioning based on SSB from the neighbouring cell in the same band. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnSSB-Serving. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3104},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnPRS-Neigh indicates whether the UE supports spatial relation for SRS for positioning based on PRS from the neighbouring cell in the same band. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports spatialRelation-SRS-PosBasedOnPRS-Serving. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3105},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Note:A PRS from a PRS-only TP is treated as PRS from a non-serving cell.","paragraph_zero_based":3106},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"posSRS-RRC-Inactive-InInitialUL-BWP","paragraph_zero_based":3107},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the UE supports positioning SRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE state for initial UL BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":3108},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfSRSposResourceSets indicates the maximum number of SRS Resource Sets for positioning supported by the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":3109},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfPeriodicAndSemiPeristentSRSposResources indicates the maximum number of periodic and semi-persistent SRS Resources for positioning supported by the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":3110},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfPeriodicAndSemiPeristentSRSposResourcesPerSlot indicates the maximum number of periodic and semi-persistent SRS Resources for positioning per slot supported by the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":3111},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfPeriodicSRSposResources indicates the maximum number of periodic SRS Resources for positioning supported by the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":3112},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfPeriodicSRSposResourcesPerSlot indicates the maximum number of periodic SRS Resources for positioning per slot supported by the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":3113},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfSemiPersistentSRSposResources indicates the maximum number of semi-persistent SRS Resources for positioning supported by the UE. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports posSRS-RRC-Inactive-InInitialUL-BWP. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3114},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfSemiPersistentSRSposResourcesPerSlot indicates the maximum number of semi-persistent SRS Resources for positioning per slot supported by the UE. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports posSRS-RRC-Inactive-InInitialUL-BWP. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3115},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"posSRS-RRC-Inactive-OutsideInitialUL-BWP","paragraph_zero_based":3116},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the UE supports positioning SRS transmission in RRC_INACTIVE state outside initial UL BWP. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports posSRS-RRC-Inactive-InInitialUL-BWP. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3117},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxSRSposBandwidthForEachSCS-withinCC-FR1 indicates the maximum SRS bandwidth supported for each SCS that UE supports within a single CC for FR1.","paragraph_zero_based":3118},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxSRSposBandwidthForEachSCS-withinCC-FR2 indicates the maximum SRS bandwidth supported for each SCS that UE supports within a single CC for FR2.","paragraph_zero_based":3119}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ad5861da0dccef1291129531d32d787af0fd13713ef27f554120fd6d7dfa3c8b","original_member_sha256":"85e43ed4cce9951e9169dd51891e9ea74001bd66e886c9b8fd4a0c481e900934","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["8f320a69a2f963dfd27d20dd9227016288dc4cc9bd08dc59559f312ad8515ea5","2e5c0f06869e5365170ef5aae5642594f40a8143ed38aef99f114c51fe26bd0b","47f8074908e6253c916677d358d0e06ee9c04b048017a8626d49e257fbd828e2","becf3c03a5607eb76992f02741671ed059731e03d8afce58ae7fd3b182340391","b14ccb1d508682b733594f0f5561b5c1cd502d6b614a9237b8bc739bcf00a415","1b20cb3d7da2891b1ae9462d6d502ae90dffb0e16bc392e3982374973d46ab75","ae227db283edc3d08deca6e02ec3781d52cbf428b6bb965ef6e1ada3568877b7","1ef4b5b0f003b8c8016ced6e5ec24699dbafc9eba750218456e7d942278d6ec3","9f277d168f03ae4f46b49abb72626eb654e5fde7d9a8117dfff47b9fbfa81409","dc73a5aae583268b91b93a8bbd7ac5fdb0d1ac4767736db7533ef53dd83e084c","6e4349c62892e2ac6e86811a197c5b822fe4fb2c20f2f2c96ebd688e78edf4cf","43b467464e2138c2543d8e7496851b497616878e6f8cce58bbff77a605b76eca","ee3fdb915d788f03fc7e70fb1cc31840c0fe6ff9e94f546173bc439f2d1de42e","c76f5392d5a7619996250940cfa6e19739c357f4e61def43ec3765a6a0e67de7","40687dcb8f11ca43a8d90b9d3d7efc980b1a107d75a69e0fa44764dd2452214b","f696628e3a9d6983414e4e422fb56a4dc506af876b995d99d31ecd71a5dfb302","d61d4525fc9c188d1df94be311f2ecdfb4ad5276a96982dc8b409f97f3dd730a","8c614bfbf812edc85b89ac72024cf9991d07216512b60d856859757e2860195e","c604194f8d0edfc3d54f2d4c32b539a43b77ec63c2e681195fe0c4b40bddeed0","e8892edd6fcadd1236323e0a9cfc43efc54da36f2c9e0f9f04f96c64f5a5d1ed","72459d7264f062c6913cd766a4aa8e86ab1a5fe0d9aa44d7de55a169ea0a9fd7","5a3bdddd86d043f9b3b51ac99971bb7e22a9e3e8deefbb6cd7450d9dad47e1b0","8015473ff0703c8d466b43d32121b75b80ba06dbf8242c1460b1ddaa4a956349","e1288a9037c7ce00137dff8f4847da48dda626c9e1523413583806aa582273da"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[3096,3119],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2305891.zip::R2-2305891_(LPP CR on local coordinates)_v01.docx:p3096"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2305891.zip::R2-2305891_(LPP CR on local coordinates)_v01.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfSRSposResourceSets indicates the maximum number of SRS Resource Sets for positioning supported by the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":3120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfPeriodicSRSposResources indicates the maximum number of periodic SRS Resources for positioning supported by the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":3121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfPeriodicSRSposResourcesPerSlot indicates the maximum number of periodic SRS Resources for positioning per slot supported by the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":3122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-differentNumerologyBetweenSRSposAndInitialBWP indicates whether different numerology between the SRS and the initial UL BWP is supported by the UE. If the field is absent, the UE only supports same numerology between the SRS and the initial UL BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":3123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-srsPosWithoutRestrictionOnBWP indicates whether SRS operation without restriction on the BW is supported by the UE; BW of the SRS may not include BW of the CORESET#0 and SSB. If the field is absent, the UE supports only SRS BW that include the BW of the CORESET #0 and SSB.","paragraph_zero_based":3124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfPeriodicAndSemiPeristentSRSposResources indicates the maximum number of periodic and semi-persistent SRS Resources for positioning supported by the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":3125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfPeriodicAndSemiPeristentSRSposResourcesPerSlot indicates the maximum number of periodic and semi-persistent SRS Resources for positioning per slot supported by the UE.","paragraph_zero_based":3126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-differentCenterFreqBetweenSRSposAndInitialBWP indicates whether different center frequenecy between the SRS for positioning and the initial UL BWP is supported by the UE. If the field is absent, the UE only supports same center frequency between the SRS for positioning and initial UL BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":3127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfSemiPersistentSRSposResources indicates the maximum number of semi-persistent SRS Resources for positioning supported by the UE. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports posSRS-RRC-Inactive-InInitialUL-BWP. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-maxNumOfSemiPersistentSRSposResourcesPerSlot indicates the maximum number of semi-persistent SRS Resources for positioning per slot supported by the UE. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports posSRS-RRC-Inactive-InInitialUL-BWP. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-switchingTimeSRS-TX-OtherTX indicates the switching time between SRS Tx and other Tx in initial UL BWP or Rx in initial DL-BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":3130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"olpc-SRS-PosRRC-Inactive","paragraph_zero_based":3131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the UE supports open-loop power control for SRS for positioning in RRC_INACTIVE state. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports posSRS-RRC-Inactive-InInitialUL-BWP. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"spatialRelationsSRS-PosRRC-Inactive","paragraph_zero_based":3133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the UE supports spatial relations for SRS for positioning in RRC_INACTIVE state on FR2. The UE can include this field only if the UE supports posSRS-RRC-Inactive-InInitialUL-BWP. Otherwise, the UE does not include this field.","paragraph_zero_based":3134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":3135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–ReferencePoint","paragraph_zero_based":3136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE ReferencePoint provides a well-defined location relative to which other locations may be defined.","paragraph_zero_based":3137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":3138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":3139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ReferencePoint-r16 ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":3140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"referencePointGeographicLocation-r16 CHOICE {","paragraph_zero_based":3141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"location3D-r16 EllipsoidPointWithAltitudeAndUncertaintyEllipsoid,","paragraph_zero_based":3142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ha-location3D-r16 HighAccuracyEllipsoidPointWithAltitudeAndUncertaintyEllipsoid-r15,","paragraph_zero_based":3143}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ad5861da0dccef1291129531d32d787af0fd13713ef27f554120fd6d7dfa3c8b","original_member_sha256":"85e43ed4cce9951e9169dd51891e9ea74001bd66e886c9b8fd4a0c481e900934","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["0cd2692787fab35ad82e81ba309248faf972ad04d46ac60d8e86f97471ebe6bc","214215568e2bd74c404c980a433c6b9c09fff5bdd9f36609b4045dc8311d4aac","280bb3c41011905e0cb24ef5fbb2dc32a6332c12807e52c9b0ed4e996e50c2ed","a14553656d93920bbc2dddd95d90ea16a076ba31cd2f64adea4931b68028ff8f","4b06c605698bb7a25ef6b76b31cbfacd37409db0585722b2e5d2cfa12f889357","ed2fb996577006bc723dcf6cb9da5ccb2e8c5233ca823b8fa311dcbf08d127b3","95cce93eaf4e182689ed0c009a236d45cd0bad35ff8b5a8f97897348d4a32b8d","bdbef99a02276f11700d2d7c24faa8d07fc15bcb16b2181a7c6dc6a3b7597e83","4fa5dd25ebf4d340977d9a6e706f8972782dbbdd04a8bc8ff66abfed7b464c62","c8733bb2392406741cb3d272f25dbc91c2c56b5dedceb43ec6f7ee85ef96f60e","878aba1a913b9d66d19147d551ffb02afdfa4b2734f7e29a3475534d97307673","902e6aa33d787e088074643aa81aa6d153b9f000c6cd8fa8872395174cf495c2","a1