{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2306676.zip::R2-2306676_(Misc LPP corrections).docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–GNSS-NavigationModel","paragraph_zero_based":720},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE GNSS-NavigationModel is used by the location server to provide precise navigation data to the GNSS capable target device. In response to a request from a target device for GNSS Assistance Data, the location server determines whether to send the navigation model for a particular satellite to a target device based upon factors like the T-Toe limit specified by the target device and any request from the target device for DGNSS (see also GNSS-DifferentialCorrections). GNSS Orbit Model can be given in Keplerian parameters or as state vector in Earth-Centered Earth-Fixed coordinates, dependent on the GNSS-ID and the target device capabilities. The meaning of these parameters is defined in relevant ICDs of the particular GNSS and GNSS specific interpretations apply. For example, GPS and QZSS use the same model parameters but some parameters have a different interpretation [7].","paragraph_zero_based":721},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":722},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":723},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GNSS-NavigationModel ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":724},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"nonBroadcastIndFlagINTEGER (0..1),","paragraph_zero_based":725},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"gnss-SatelliteListGNSS-NavModelSatelliteList,","paragraph_zero_based":726},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"...","paragraph_zero_based":727},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":728},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":729},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GNSS-NavModelSatelliteList ::= SEQUENCE (SIZE(1..64)) OF GNSS-NavModelSatelliteElement","paragraph_zero_based":730},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":731},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GNSS-NavModelSatelliteElement ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":732},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"svIDSV-ID,","paragraph_zero_based":733},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"svHealthBIT STRING (SIZE(8)),","paragraph_zero_based":734},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"iodBIT STRING (SIZE(11)),","paragraph_zero_based":735},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"gnss-ClockModelGNSS-ClockModel,","paragraph_zero_based":736},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"gnss-OrbitModelGNSS-OrbitModel,","paragraph_zero_based":737},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"...,","paragraph_zero_based":738},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[[svHealthExt-v1240 BIT STRING (SIZE(4))OPTIONAL-- Need ON","paragraph_zero_based":739},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"]]","paragraph_zero_based":740},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":741},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":742},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GNSS-ClockModel ::= CHOICE {","paragraph_zero_based":743}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e4e44ee677ed4051201972f11f51bb54396e91b31bb2136139e5ab06d90870d5","original_member_sha256":"7e17bac3b5b722159fad6bbbdc973ced135f72f2a32bb2bedf6473afad53255e","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["48937f7efba35c9c2a6dbb19cca329879a0c204ecccfaacff15c14db2e003c49","5c6b436d12c3561e0d0dd786df7166fa4c50db19735c20bf4db5d3ce8b7d6174","70c945b56ea1bf7ba25c9b90f4de3fbcf36ed03967a7a886fb68b3ecad917437","c072f4f0c91f1ac879fa1bad622e30be13548baf5e22678744016d8bc341fc26","d640264b9a62a9433c105d9a5a9982458bd6fa5cf72aa58245a038283f565bac","fc5980801f87bffb93a9f2127928cc58e22f831293b8b20f997522fb7e1c7c4d","a9bf18e34a725a6b141716ab0322bd599d265a553a87166136ea093d39f0f5ab","47a736148732790c6a9ac269e844d62dfc7e09bbe10e5241b94e4c80bf417b21","9084cf31033dd7a5794fa116395fedef6191cb8