d":116},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If it is experiencing internal overheating;","paragraph_zero_based":117},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If it prefers certain DRX parameter values, and/or a reduced maximum number of secondary component carriers, and/or a reduced maximum aggregated bandwidth and/or a reduced maximum number of MIMO layers and/or minimum scheduling offsets K0 and K2 for power saving purpose;","paragraph_zero_based":118},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If it expects not to send or receive any more data in the near future, and in this case, it can provide its preference to transition out of RRC_CONNECTED where this indication may express its preferred RRC state, or alternately, it may cancel an earlier indicated preference to transition out of RRC_CONNECTED;","paragraph_zero_based":119}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"2e092a6a9eb9b2fed0eb36b6d5a7399f4cb8b54518eaef74fdb89ef1caf55545","original_member_sha256":"d015739bbaeb4ebff6cd0d986206dd1c31170696065b7d767d69f35a7c813674","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["3f35077488e12dc06f895840db1356d1325c923ee35ad231c8f853329d337e31","7c067ace4ff3d5b6cf2d08a07e2b7bdae23c45b4d0a3d3a4ea00a360bb4cf1f3","d2ffe82feea279162744adfa718b96e17180c6c94c7b73992ff9e87c099891b8","79448ed1210e065de3cd86a93afb4dd7351f78b9841094f07ca1ef2bc908972e","fba855cade31bc9efec5969782ad9b219ae66da22566db83a58f60af4f90d410","946857079461c338b369995da4d6cecd9e85fb2d2be6fae34860a16cc00aaf62","6580267f9f1fc67e2438af5271a0a2627ebd2580f63f5f0b5abdd660b418d497","faf92c80d83218cc2992a48b9fb9b91f20a208d7e05f9ad018d7bafee83014ef","1569d7938cb20e5f9c225ea91ac2d564bd7f3ce117a213d179a17f4dfe5f9abd","d1a69153843ba5c02bdf44f7c614cbbf4c3014b254f2af070b6377316871c237","ffc83312a4178a9b10e1be744f0178bfc57b38ab6a3a227fcbe624a335d731f3","c0224b22eaf5f4c0635f522d0d38d85684f612dc1d7c70eb944eaae6cc4417c5","9ece041b20bbf90620a38b80d89910c95dddcc951044c741fb82a5aae0d3d6a5","3a61907a954adb10fd5e0e169694f2478eb02144ca7cfd92b412f03dec571c74","f974391919cbafd4029340c0c8df8a239055e0b09b4bf249ba8655f856ad9bd9","9fe8ebf318536e3098f5fb8750abe60b4b75279c23f21a8209a03655b59db1e9","c61d65c9f9d80ddadef82d5348b94875154eee7270c5c3bc3256ab693da8c91b","1be3094abc69e6f35f2465653a8b113b7a917e7268fdfddc39affc22c737c38e","7f08f0a499654a81e5eb0c7b5e203f8caac724c0b6a549e72456d14fd2a4ba16","cba7b47a019f37ad91e9c51c921b05faa752f98741663c33f474f05a4e146c12","738aa43ea18ea629d7018dd81f64deee184934f90ff7f3d29d6473b8bfddc4fa","2edc771f80e960c25a98b35e0f48c6f477f0095df6c4b5b446d738d747d12538","995ad612ffe39825884a28235dedb7717df24cc7f96f68ba891ed2a445e89c19","5833cb455efcbdb70a0c2617c762b72ae19466b87e9b4d7a5a036aaf41b29b8e"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[96,119],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2306923.zip::R2-2306923 38.300 running CR for IDC Enhancements.docx:p96"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2306923.zip::R2-2306923 38.300 running CR for IDC Enhancements.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If it prefers (not) to be provisioned with reference time information;","paragraph_zero_based":120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If it prefers to transition out of RRC_CONNECTED state for MUSIM operation and its preferred RRC state after transition;","paragraph_zero_based":121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If it wants to include assistance information for setup or release of gaps for MUSIM operation;","paragraph_zero_based":122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-When affected by IDC problems that it cannot solve by itself:","paragraph_zero_based":123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The list of frequencies affected by IDC problems (see clause 23.4 of TS 36.300 [2]); or","paragraph_zero_based":124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The list of frequency ranges/frequency range combinations affected by the IDC problems; and","paragraph_zero_based":125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-TDM assistance information;","paragraph_zero_based":126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Its RRM measurement relaxation status indicating whether RRM measurement relaxation criteria are met or not;","paragraph_zero_based":127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Its RLM measurement relaxation status indicating whether the UE is applying RLM measurements relaxation;","paragraph_zero_based":128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Its BFD measurement relaxation status indicating whether the UE is applying BFD measurements relaxation.","paragraph_zero_based":129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:The requirements on RRM/RLM/CSI measurements in different phases of IDC interference defined in TS 36.300 [2] are applicable except that for NR serving cell, the requirements in TS 38.133 [13] and TS 38.101-1 [18], TS 38.101-2 [35], TS 38.101-3 [36] apply.","paragraph_zero_based":130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In the second case, the UE can express a preference for temporarily reducing the number of maximum secondary component carriers, the maximum aggregated bandwidth and the number of maximum MIMO layers. In all cases, it is up to the gNB whether to accommodate the request.","paragraph_zero_based":131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For sidelink, the UE can report SL traffic pattern(s) to NG-RAN, for periodic traffic.","paragraph_zero_based":132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"End of 1st change","paragraph_zero_based":133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Start of 2nd change","paragraph_zero_based":135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"10Scheduling","paragraph_zero_based":136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"10. x    Autonomous Denial for IDC","paragraph_zero_based":137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The network may configure a long-term denial rate by dedicated RRC signalling to limit the amount of NR UL autonomous denials. Once configured by the network, the UE can autonomously deny NR UL transmission. Otherwise, the UE shall not perform any NR UL autonomous denials for IDC.","paragraph_zero_based":138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"End of 2nd change","paragraph_zero_based":139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":143}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"2e092a6a9eb9b2fed0eb36b6d5a7399f4cb8b54518eaef74fdb89ef1caf55545","original_member_sha256":"d015739bbaeb4ebff6cd0d986206dd1c31170696065b7d767d69f35a7c813674","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["81f39168102b94f7223d30aa49b8b4a733331e860aef0f159ef2dfa12d72fe7f","186b93c