38"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[96,119],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311924.zip::R2-2311924_Introduction of BWP_Wor in TS38.300.docx:p96"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311924.zip::R2-2311924_Introduction of BWP_Wor in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Start of change","paragraph_zero_based":121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3.2Definitions","paragraph_zero_based":122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For the purposes of the present document, the terms and definitions given in TR 21.905 [1], in TS 36.300 [2] and the following apply. A term defined in the present document takes precedence over the definition of the same term, if any, in TR 21.905 [1] and TS 36.300 [2].","paragraph_zero_based":123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"BH RLC channel: an RLC channel between two nodes, which is used to transport backhaul packets.","paragraph_zero_based":124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Boundary IAB-node: as defined in TS 38.401 [4].","paragraph_zero_based":125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Broadcast MRB: A radio bearer configured for MBS broadcast delivery.","paragraph_zero_based":126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CAG Cell: a PLMN cell broadcasting at least one Closed Access Group identity.","paragraph_zero_based":127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CAG Member Cell: for a UE, a CAG cell broadcasting the identity of the selected PLMN, registered PLMN or equivalent PLMN, and for that PLMN, a CAG identifier belonging to the Allowed CAG list of the UE for that PLMN.","paragraph_zero_based":128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CAG-only cell: a CAG cell that is only available for normal service for CAG UEs.","paragraph_zero_based":129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Cell-Defining SSB: an SSB with an RMSI associated.","paragraph_zero_based":130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Child node: IAB-DU's and IAB-donor-DU's next hop neighbour node; the child node is also an IAB-node.","paragraph_zero_based":131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Handover (CHO): a handover procedure that is executed only when execution condition(s) are met.","paragraph_zero_based":132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CORESET#0: the control resource set for at least SIB1 scheduling, can be configured either via MIB or via dedicated RRC signalling.","paragraph_zero_based":133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DAPS Handover: a handover procedure that maintains the source gNB connection after reception of RRC message for handover and until releasing the source cell after successful random access to the target gNB.","paragraph_zero_based":134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Direct Path: a type of UE-to-Network transmission path, where data is transmitted between a UE and the network without sidelink relaying.","paragraph_zero_based":135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Downstream: direction toward child node or UE in IAB-topology.","paragraph_zero_based":136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Early Data Forwarding: data forwarding that is initiated before the UE executes the handover.","paragraph_zero_based":137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Earth-centered, earth-fixed: a global geodetic reference system for the Earth intended for practical applications of mapping, charting, geopositioning and navigation, as specified in NIMA TR 8350.2 [51].","paragraph_zero_based":138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Feeder link: wireless link between the NTN Gateway and the NTN payload.","paragraph_zero_based":139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Geosynchronous Orbit: earth-centered orbit at approximately 35786 kilometres above Earth's surface and synchronised with Earth's rotation. A geostationary orbit is a non-inclined geosynchronous orbit, i.e. in the Earth's equator plane.","paragraph_zero_based":140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Group ID for Network Selection: an identifier used during SNPN selection to enhance the likelihood of selecting a preferred SNPN that supports a Default Credentials Server or a Credentials Holder, as specified in TS 23.501 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"gNB: node providing NR user plane and control plane protocol terminations towards the UE, and connected via the NG interface to the 5GC.","paragraph_zero_based":142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"High Altitude Platform Station: airborne vehicle embarking the NTN payload placed at an altitude between 8 and 50 km.","paragraph_zero_based":143}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"5beccf2c4f7bc5ba3600d747955377cdba92a80fa413985f5bae4049b3acb775","original_member_sha256":"d98a639b7aa49723a0879cdea4b6917ea304cb84ec0d9c26e2a2bc33ee4c3d9f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["988da09017f4000bfd02eca7f05d2df3e2234f33fe7a64830e298594650234cc","207671f6cd5b02dbe4aee1ed91a7f4c00aac4f6d9de38b900e3ff118fdb6caf1","ed8409c0b98b900fa6e8833592c4787f67909aaf66363ba989f03d0d6ad5322b","d4d8634d01123de23dbbec9486cf61a1593e3e4b912008a3ef29f6bcb1d6c8e6","62b2d90b7a3c3223feff5ec4eff2f1d4145570005d90a2ec53d67f47f1d06796","491b1c670c190c1481f572cd054ded299e830b91fa1ab6bc24a131686ea0b93c","302fc50e7ca57fac9727015e13d63070bb34f9d697ce5f252f10cb571ea3a0a6","00e70da633fcf023796add2034e2ee4f80bf3177fe4f853301b10bcb9785236d","430754402fb01ecca13f1bf8cdd77b81f9aba0c65dcdab4d98dc465c35901bdd","0ea300aa6ffb45c723279b4372ddb111123032c1307607b85b4293172c065e64","339ac71cf2add25b2b01b386493b85399edeb300b82f97c6a6820d51ff318d2f","1db1e356a45aecfe9e1d8e84dc090f5364c7956271938aea2594ff7f339a8fc2","68ce99fddd7bf7051993cd5a1997f66e627c6a35eac5bae6a24433eaa920926f","ba0b8a335c93d717f53a837209e385d3a25f3347f75712a80e06a711db523818","6877bb36627c1645a1f90bedf9bc08d9d4023b6005dc8b160ad9a61c0a3659a0","409443ea161d6225c7861ede6b17e504bbde791de14ed005e70e7419a30b4b8d","c6bd97734a94b7f315b117b68259c64b08050814491f85d5fad878554a4e0e8b","8697c5cf2cffd0083ea4971ccfa95b82c3b525bbb2786c5c00dbbddbef54bf36","e30dc94cde030b1e4e1b91cd3c7e448e21210cfa26b32c6688af7968e106070e","c49b3815d06a7f68f2c25cb736842cf37fcc9322170d7d7c41a657d641ed12fc","6695c9aec063b909c23d8fa1476db4da7dedc9b020c1c31413dd4852d60243d1","d0f1364b625d23f0513b0891c36a7064c3cc4db470d817a8e86462371464080a","84fa465fe5eb7a6ea3409418508a41136b6a60a7217159a3f240cef0a36948e5","0e5ce3b2c80fa3e6bbb4c61e378b76da96bd750ab09ece72c89cf96348f34c22"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[120,143],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311924.zip::R2-2311924_Introduction of BWP_Wor in TS38.300.docx:p120"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311924.zip::R2-2311924_Introduction of BWP_Wor in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB-donor: gNB that provides network access to UEs via a network of backhaul and access links.","paragraph_zero_based":144},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB-donor-CU: as defined in TS 38.401 [4].","paragraph_zero_based":145},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB-donor-DU: as defined in TS 38.401 [4].","paragraph_zero_based":146},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB-DU: gNB-DU functionality supported by the IAB-node to terminate the NR access interface to UEs and next-hop IAB-nodes, and to terminate the F1 protocol to the gNB-CU functionality, as defined in TS 38.401 [4], on the IAB-donor.","paragraph_zero_based":147},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB-MT: IAB-node function that terminates the Uu interface to the parent node using the procedures and behaviours specified for UEs unless stated otherwise. IAB-MT function used in 38-series of 3GPP Specifications corresponds to IAB-UE function defined in TS 23.501 [3].","paragraph_zero_based":148},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB-node: RAN node that supports NR access links to UEs and NR backhaul links to parent nodes and child nodes. The IAB-node does not support backhauling via LTE.","paragraph_zero_based":149},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"IAB topology: the unison of all IAB-nodes and IAB-donor-DUs whose F1 and/or RRC connections are terminated at the same IAB-donor-CU.","paragraph_zero_based":150},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indirect Path: a type of UE-to-Network transmission path, where data is forwarded via a U2N Relay UE between a U2N Remote UE and the network.","paragraph_zero_based":151},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inter-donor partial migration: migration of an IAB-MT to a parent node underneath a different IAB-donor-CU while the collocated IAB-DU and its descendant IAB-node(s), if any, are terminated at the initial IAB-donor-CU. The procedure renders the said IAB-node as a boundary IAB-node.","paragraph_zero_based":152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Intra-system Handover: handover that does not involve a CN change (EPC or 5GC).","paragraph_zero_based":153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Inter-system Handover: handover that involves a CN change (EPC or 5GC).","paragraph_zero_based":154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Late Data Forwarding: data forwarding that is initiated after the source NG-RAN node knows that the UE has successfully accessed a target NG-RAN node.","paragraph_zero_based":155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Mapped Cell ID: in NTN, it corresponds to a fixed geographical area.","paragraph_zero_based":156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MBS Radio Bearer: A radio bearer configured for MBS delivery.","paragraph_zero_based":157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MSG1: preamble transmission of the random access procedure for 4-step random access (RA) type.","paragraph_zero_based":158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MSG3: first scheduled transmission of the random access procedure.","paragraph_zero_based":159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MSGA: preamble and payload transmissions of the random access procedure for 2-step RA type.","paragraph_zero_based":160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MSGB: response to MSGA in the 2-step random access procedure. MSGB may consist of response(s) for contention resolution, fallback indication(s), and backoff indication.","paragraph_zero_based":161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Multicast/Broadcast Service: A point-to-multipoint service as defined in TS 23.247 [45].","paragraph_zero_based":162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Multicast MRB: A radio bearer configured for MBS multicast delivery.","paragraph_zero_based":163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Multi-hop backhauling: using a chain of NR backhaul links between an IAB-node and an IAB-donor.","paragraph_zero_based":164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ng-eNB: node providing E-UTRA user plane and control plane protocol terminations towards the UE, and connected via the NG interface to the 5GC.","paragraph_zero_based":165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NG-C: control plane interface between NG-RAN and 5GC.","paragraph_zero_based":166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NG-U: user plane interface between NG-RAN and 5GC.","paragraph_zero_based":167}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"5beccf2c4f7bc5ba3600d747955377cdba92a80fa413985f5bae4049b3acb775","original_member_sha256":"d98a639b7aa49723a0879cdea4b6917ea304cb84ec0d9c26e2a2bc33ee4c3d9f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["6c18b31032aac11feb16f568e62e6d1121f3a21ed934dbf9a6cfc6d5f7a33ec5","c51e33b1c3c703c6e7e3f45bcc544865b6ef9a00233f4ab980d39d571f8062c2","fa62aa007e781d48b17c0be9837851e9fe31d3ad7d3135369fb33fb89c7f54f7","96787c95ff599c31bf80dbb1443ee0e9a3d48f77c3f0cc90dbe68ea6db9ce141","437994b7fdad7a8033c6af9bd46dc63178fee7f794633e8e605d54dd9a239e80","8e277c6c30e07389481979751bc4a833bde0024c44e913dd540e6288abe88df0","07567b7aee718b639af35cd546f694cc3fe6ce9c254d8a33108200f73b323a76","065b67e5e9fd836dea0820f439d30d9bd23eeca351a9438ff23b2c147f195682","c12d40a0b9e2e6b38622e6a675c1768b2c969afad3b774a841ee02fc72fbd00c","34601fe5f173addb891a60ec34f20caaf7d8073ee5cb4fc515518589dbbb778e","8e66c19f203bf1b0fceb3bbf9757c6cd43da54ad292eca160622eab980ec8646","009296f5af7de2b4c410fa4da93f8334759a58923eacf23563174c8bcde206d1","a81dbe7c3382abd4b42d06854259d6858d5b7a5aa68574d4c89347ffb67a6271","065a01b7e0602944b242a594b065427280a094a1f99e73a7f0c4a73f100154cd","8f286d8b48c16942622cccfbd3e92aa3a4d40b5766163b4adaa101d728651e38","e6d872683ea4eacf8f2db4073ebdf3dc9f0d40d167d0455e564c104947613bdf","11c448cd42005436307c564f0d923b47f132fb1295f619621ab5cb6b984bd71b","85e2a043822053a05d03795e17f766f2ffd085c276e33c05e0f70eb6629c8082","9189aec4c01a939272fe612f2b8423dabef52723daed1b21cd0265cdc1907a0b","536bdf0d1e1dcdccec95ef9657291ac99780ed50ef4e8a418af43d20fc0b7fb3","1aed2ee3d51d82a61ba67590f37dfa78ace3ebc2abd0c4176803ab5c19e7e60f","ebff9b3baa5d0954866e85a87ec1be2e65ca59313b4645c209fd489a0a9bb6e3","c5019f9687af9a4636a638ae28859bfeb6fbc5b97459e42fab481a7004b85876","19c1693f90e2324e0a2c862c78b1b605ae04c077e363c9329ba746fb09d2e9ae"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[144,167],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311924.zip::R2-2311924_Introduction of BWP_Wor in TS38.300.docx:p144"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311924.zip::R2-2311924_Introduction of BWP_Wor in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NG-RAN node: either a gNB or an ng-eNB.","paragraph_zero_based":168},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Non-CAG Cell: a PLMN cell which does not broadcast any Closed Access Group identity.","paragraph_zero_based":169},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Non-Cell Defining SSB: an SSB without an RMSI associated.","paragraph_zero_based":170},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Non-Geosynchronous orbit: earth-centered orbit with an orbital period that does not match Earth's rotation on its axis. This includes Low and Medium Earth Orbit (LEO and MEO). LEO operates at altitudes between 300 km and 1500 km and MEO at altitudes between 7000 km and 25000 km, approximately.","paragraph_zero_based":171},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Non-terrestrial network: an NG-RAN consisting of gNBs, which provide non-terrestrial NR access to UEs by means of an NTN payload embarked on an airborne or space-borne NTN vehicle and an NTN Gateway.","paragraph_zero_based":172},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR backhaul link: NR link used for backhauling between an IAB-node and an IAB-donor, and between IAB-nodes in case of a multi-hop backhauling.","paragraph_zero_based":173},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR sidelink communication: AS functionality enabling at least V2X communication as defined in TS 23.287 [40] and the ProSe communication (including ProSe non-Relay and UE-to-Network Relay communication) as defined in TS 23.304 [48], between two or more nearby UEs, using NR technology but not traversing any network node.","paragraph_zero_based":174},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR sidelink discovery: AS functionality enabling ProSe non-Relay Discovery and ProSe UE-to-Network Relay discovery for Proximity based Services as defined in TS 23.304 [48] between two or more nearby UEs, using NR technology but not traversing any network node.","paragraph_zero_based":175},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NTN Gateway: an earth station located at the surface of the earth, providing connectivity to the NTN payload using the feeder link. An NTN Gateway is a TNL node.","paragraph_zero_based":176},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NTN payload: a network node, embarked on board a satellite or high altitude platform station, providing connectivity functions, between the service link and the feeder link. In the current version of this specification, the NTN payload is a TNL node.","paragraph_zero_based":177},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Numerology: corresponds to one subcarrier spacing in the frequency domain. By scaling a reference subcarrier spacing by an integer N, different numerologies can be defined.","paragraph_zero_based":178},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parent node: IAB-MT's next hop neighbour node; the parent node can be IAB-node or IAB-donor-DU","paragraph_zero_based":179},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PC5 Relay RLC channel: an RLC channel between L2 U2N Remote UE and L2 U2N Relay UE, which is used to transport packets over PC5 for L2 UE-to-Network Relay.","paragraph_zero_based":180},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PLMN Cell: a cell of the PLMN.","paragraph_zero_based":181},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RedCap UE: a UE with reduced capabilities as specified in clause 4.2.21.1 in TS 38.306 [11].","paragraph_zero_based":182},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Relay discovery: AS functionality enabling 5G ProSe UE-to-Network Relay Discovery as defined in TS 23.304 [48], using NR technology but not traversing any network node.","paragraph_zero_based":183},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Satellite: a space-borne vehicle orbiting the Earth embarking the NTN payload.","paragraph_zero_based":184},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Service link: wireless link between the NTN payload and UE.","paragraph_zero_based":185},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Sidelink Discovery RSRP: RSRP measurements on PC5 link related to NR sidelink discovery.","paragraph_zero_based":186},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Sidelink RSRP: RSRP measurements on PC5 link related to NR sidelink communication.","paragraph_zero_based":187},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SNPN Access Mode: mode of operation whereby a UE only accesses SNPNs.","paragraph_zero_based":188},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SNPN-only cell: a cell that is only available for normal service for SNPN subscribers.","paragraph_zero_based":189},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SNPN Identity: the identity of Stand-alone NPN defined by the pair (PLMN ID, NID).","paragraph_zero_based":190},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Transmit/Receive Point: part of the gNB transmitting and receiving radio signals to/from UE according to physical layer properties and parameters inherent to that element.","paragraph_zero_based":191}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"5beccf2c4f7bc5ba3600d747955377cdba92a80fa413985f5bae4049b3acb775","original_member_sha256":"d98a639b7aa49723a0879cdea4b6917ea304cb84ec0d9c26e2a2bc33ee4c3d9f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ab964e607a7dc388fbdf28aa6d8e1b1e2ecff1ab9598b7e7c0fdfee11b15f001","b713e1457e45ddba3087b7eaa981b1791cc78c19afee67a123410f3233101137","37b02945e1d0b0be58b77dc0b1a3a66b047e4761c5647968ac6d12b8bbacc495","a86a8397cbfa261a5f15289c64e79bc6130842f238fdd07924bf67ad366bd7fe","9b1a3ff2dd73cfa7247ca5f6ee16743a2533de6c3bc71ebc93a58a90ded82edc","6b6ca3df2badadea80f3fe019f91fb07659f67f094d44982d9320c32d3ea7b48","e11653d56ed97ce5602b1c2df0c090d4df134d54f593452825c1a8facd2b2d4d","812ff29189d3ab0c65f0709e976147e71038a314445dd0c6777a9b33bc30f7ef","b25ea3acd947f971916c1296dafdab167f3d44527833a7bffba9f4b9846657be","42018d3996783f87344f84167353954935c04da74f1fea957fd6753dbb73a430","b0ec513bf4be018babe5593fd5deff3db56f590b65ee0948dc3cf880c0734adf","6db70c85e1e5a0e2d7e5e49afe72e4f3e1b9cd6dd717db60e022e7b58933a251","43c04d7779f1383c1ca1b0494bfa9f581151493d2a38ae0d69deefbd806811c0","81aa6c0c403adcf4a80d172d8b761012dc99266b75170c97babc829c71601fb1","cb5aa9a52649197f239118f2ea428824477b4a8f7d7545a9b4b58e1174c5e6da","51a0fa21467465d927f98bf7d4e758263e967a6598830f54a3cbcec37c037484","24b6fae618ea9870b7291e44dd1f6b23d2df0a13ab38a1d53a8027bb94e45229","1056d5d8568e712ee10d2e92188a09e57a359b9823358dcf1c04697081e533dc","9d4f6d2640e0225cbc64b1c7677e7d963fbd65a3b698535bfbe19e4f81857850","a307b78af7bac57d94e4fdc057b961338b63957eb51b1367fbd64d3b316ccc93","6e06688c9f144aec4f4f2269fe5c1159e4160528392def22a492669d54661c75","a66f46b8e2265b80d9e16855ea629cb009f2984d3b361bfde335f610b83a60d7","606fbfe04c19774e184271589dbd0d80ac1ff75b1b7224d6f6b622d1e679a9b2","72f22df1b4cbde1ada6253d5223f78c7e3e7d14d464bcf8da300c759e582a43a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[168,191],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311924.zip::R2-2311924_Introduction of BWP_Wor in TS38.300.docx:p168"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311924.zip::R2-2311924_Introduction of BWP_Wor in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"U2N Relay UE: a UE that provides functionality to support connectivity to the network for U2N Remote UE(s).","paragraph_zero_based":192},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"U2N Remote UE: a UE that communicates with the network via a U2N Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":193},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upstream: direction toward parent node in IAB-topology.","paragraph_zero_based":194},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Uu Relay RLC channel: an RLC channel between L2 U2N Relay UE and gNB, which is used to transport packets over Uu for L2 UE-to-Network Relay.","paragraph_zero_based":195},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"V2X sidelink communication: AS functionality enabling V2X communication as defined in TS 23.285 [41], between nearby UEs, using E-UTRA technology but not traversing any network node.","paragraph_zero_based":196},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Xn: network interface between NG-RAN nodes.","paragraph_zero_based":197},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":198},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":199},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":200},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.2.4Synchronization signal and PBCH block","paragraph_zero_based":201},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The Synchronization Signal and PBCH block (SSB) consists of primary and secondary synchronization signals (PSS, SSS), each occupying 1 symbol and 127 subcarriers, and PBCH spanning across 3 OFDM symbols and 240 subcarriers, but on one symbol leaving an unused part in the middle for SSS as show in Figure 5.2.4-1. The possible time locations of SSBs within a half-frame are determined by sub-carrier spacing and the periodicity of the half-frames where SSBs are transmitted is configured by the network. During a half-frame, different SSBs may be transmitted in different spatial directions (i.e. using different beams, spanning the coverage area of a cell).","paragraph_zero_based":202},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Within the frequency span of a carrier, multiple SSBs can be transmitted. The PCIs of SSBs transmitted in different frequency locations do not have to be unique, i.e. different SSBs in the frequency domain can have different PCIs. However, when an SSB is associated with an RMSI, the SSB is referred to as a Cell-Defining SSB (CD-SSB). A PCell is always associated to a CD-SSB located on the synchronization raster. When an SSB is not associated with an RMSI, the SSB is referred to as a non-Cell Defining SSB (NCD-SSB), which can be used to perform RLM, BFD, and RRM measurements and measurements for RA resource selection inside the active DL BWP when the active BWP does not contain the CD-SSB. A non-cell defining SSB may also be configured for RedCap UEs in RRC_INACTIVE to perform SDT. A UE may be configured with multiple SSBs provided that each BWP is configured with at most one SSB (CD-SSB or NCD-SSB).","paragraph_zero_based":203},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":204},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.2.4-1: Time-frequency structure of SSB","paragraph_zero_based":205},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Polar coding is used for PBCH.","paragraph_zero_based":206},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE may assume a band-specific sub-carrier spacing for the SSB unless a network has configured the UE to assume a different sub-carrier spacing.","paragraph_zero_based":207},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PBCH symbols carry its own frequency-multiplexed DMRS.","paragraph_zero_based":208},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"QPSK modulation is used for PBCH.","paragraph_zero_based":209},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The PBCH physical layer model is described in TS 38.202 [20].","paragraph_zero_based":210},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":211},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":212},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":213},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.2.3Mobility in RRC_CONNECTED","paragraph_zero_based":214},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.2.3.1Overview","paragraph_zero_based":215}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"5beccf2c4f7bc5ba3600d747955377cdba92a80fa413985f5bae4049b3acb775","original_member_sha256":"d98a639b7aa49723a0879cdea4b6917ea304cb84ec0d9c26e2a2bc33ee4c3d9f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["fafe6d933d28bd58ba7e2c499267cce38684bd2472e072c0b0582671bc5c4142","75f2c86a1c602838fa4c709295cf79b42b35918d94861b7dae9dfd117ac52fd9","fb3f99c96518ebda1fedd6a425105ec9f723d8c45cb6e6ed38668ca6373b4e3e","551cc2ab5dc03641f5c093e3038eb4a9d14e8b3c5b9d6e2198218350a70e149d","a6879c20266588f89cc79fc6524f2d4ef583043b642fd2b0346939b4c18f5842","bc94e8630b63cee43e66797e19fe9daca6868a66aba9a9cfbbf769e416ac22ca","517dc90565e68d9b83c6b1c9b7a108889d0bf1b9ab2130e6dcdb642b914eb97c","6950977a5ee71098961de7d7578b95ec80888a33d7587fd653f68803af29fad9","3c54021f010992660a7414a5ec34209ebae8f81c20eb737e3b31e6bc78e5157d","a8bbbdc65c84349c4fc734ff25ca94cddd8d76a496833302b0e69799bfe2155f","c27e9792c0792692b3f127f96c5b5f03cd971adc17b329d979160c470fcdd539","4ee363137421374e6e78ff83a76c67e099eeb4f39ac944ab4ea5e041c04f5a13","ef581ad45e765584c67676c1364b0bd86ae9170dc0d900f03a3dfc6dbaa4c68e","3d4fca33d6e63157dbf23cb5fd13cc254e6dc3d9b720631f282574b2d1f29210","298c188d8aea38bc716bd2f89477930546e717f311716942b1d430b21cfeeb45","601d205aabb38c6fd6c8312d0155f31c931b6d9ba7d735187e7fc5803abe8997","9c9f7ebad141d81d3244cae1e03fd1ae947523f8fc2baf8880e5d23bba7b58fd","b56f0285ae2d7ed0a87b89240cdf4ccb1206421db108a79795f7c68a6271cda7","b8eb5d6028c71003bed8ec10d80daf2375b50afee76f4fcb3342e587632f3ff0","46b979c4d61b9c9a74214442c2b09dc9a8e3f4e176ba1ed3ae015752c2e7cb4d","599af6cacc3f2a73246ea3c06b6c40847cef81cd889bfdca8dfe2bc9c3fb0211","cf4292d120de33b3e17cbba2b68729d8cbd0246b2bb39f0da0355b8fa46ced0a","7244bb22710cafdf9b93bb7e28f67906507df544954b43729d1208c8197b62ce","792ab52544a23ef5ee88e6e0295cb1b271c1bae4ca36aa4e12b6eeac101e2766"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[192,215],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311924.zip::R2-2311924_Introduction of BWP_Wor in TS38.300.docx:p192"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311924.zip::R2-2311924_Introduction of BWP_Wor in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":216},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[unchanged text omitted]","paragraph_zero_based":217},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Beam Level Mobility does not require explicit RRC signalling to be triggered. Beam level mobility can be within a cell, or between cells, the latter is referred to as inter-cell beam management (ICBM). For ICBM, a UE can receive or transmit UE dedicated channels/signals via a TRP associated with a PCI different from the PCI of a serving cell, while non-UE-dedicated channels/signals can only be received via a TRP associated with a PCI of the serving cell. The gNB provides via RRC signalling the UE with measurement configuration containing configurations of SSB/CSI resources and resource sets, reports and trigger states for triggering channel and interference measurements and reports. In case of ICBM, a measurement configuration includes SSB resources associated with PCIs different from the PCI of a serving cell. Beam Level Mobility is then dealt with at lower layers by means of physical layer and MAC layer control signalling, and RRC is not required to know which beam is being used at a given point in time.","paragraph_zero_based":218},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SSB-based Beam Level Mobility is based on the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP and can be configured for the initial DL BWPs, for DL BWPs containing the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP, and if supported, for DL BWPs not containing the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP. SSB-based Beam Level Mobility can be also performed based on a non-cell defining SSB, if configured for the active DL BWP. For other DL BWPs, Beam Level Mobility can only be performed based on CSI-RS, if configured for the active DL BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":219},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":220},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[unchanged text omitted]","paragraph_zero_based":221},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":222},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":223},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.2.4Measurements","paragraph_zero_based":224},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[unchanged text omitted]","paragraph_zero_based":225},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Intra-frequency neighbour (cell) measurements and inter-frequency neighbour (cell) measurements are defined as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":226},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SSB based intra-frequency measurement: a measurement is defined as an SSB based intra-frequency measurement provided the center frequency of the SSB of the serving cell and the center frequency of the SSB of the neighbour cell are the same, and the subcarrier spacing of the two SSBs is also the same.","paragraph_zero_based":227},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SSB based inter-frequency measurement: a measurement is defined as an SSB based inter-frequency measurement provided the center frequency of the SSB of the serving cell and the center frequency of the SSB of the neighbour cell are different, or the subcarrier spacing of the two SSBs is different.","paragraph_zero_based":228},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:For SSB based measurements, one measurement object corresponds to one SSB and the UE considers different SSBs as different cells.","paragraph_zero_based":229},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2a:If a UE is configured to perform serving cell measurements based on an NCD-SSB configured in its active BWP, this NCD-SSB is considered as the SSB of the serving cell in the definition of intra-frequency and inter-frequency measurements as above.","paragraph_zero_based":230},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":231},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[unchanged text omitted]","paragraph_zero_based":232},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Whether a measurement is non-gap-assisted or gap-assisted depends on the capability of the UE, the active BWP of the UE and the current operating frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":233},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For SSB based inter-frequency measurement, if the measurement gap requirement information is reported by the UE, a measurement gap configuration may be provided according to the information. Otherwise, a measurement gap configuration is always provided in the following cases:","paragraph_zero_based":234},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE only supports per-UE measurement gaps;","paragraph_zero_based":235},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If the UE supports per-FR measurement gaps and any of the serving cells are in the same frequency range of the measurement object.","paragraph_zero_based":236},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For SSB based intra-frequency measurement, if the measurement gap requirement information is reported by the UE, a measurement gap configuration may be provided according to the information. Otherwise, a measurement gap configuration is always provided in the following case:","paragraph_zero_based":237},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Other than the initial BWP, if any of the UE configured BWPs do not contain the frequency domain resources of the SSB associated to the initial DL BWP, and are not configured with NCD-SSB for serving cell measurement.","paragraph_zero_based":238},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In non-gap-assisted scenarios, the UE shall be able to carry out such measurements without measurement gaps. In gap-assisted scenarios, the UE cannot be assumed to be able to carry out such measurements without measurement gaps.","paragraph_zero_based":239}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"5beccf2c4f7bc5ba3600d747955377cdba92a80fa413985f5bae4049b3acb775","original_member_sha256":"d98a639b7aa49723a0879cdea4b6917ea304cb84ec0d9c26e2a2bc33ee4c3d9f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["60114ddd828ccfd07cc20ec3ecbf42621875d3fe58c36bfe880589002db8caa9","1cb111399d212eaae37bb456728794f8ea962326f7528cd28e62491f2a542658","ba449f8b1d235786c82b95d1f3ee8850303f7bc3f07f230d326e26ec78fd4761","650ea3f7d1ab751c914f97e57809afbde0ebd0a94984f9150d7a3fa5136c5f73","67432221b6f4aa58f2bddc65808d9d86733391d64c7bf8d703fe5a91d603030c","d3d30471c45b8a6d7caf2db18535651155290f3d7fffefe94390830420dc115c","f4f236b8754d46f9c5d0870d67894782c5b580351deb681d69a62fa4ff7ec058","8b5485c3d5225289df5c6a70e4c590ac1988b423c0628d3443483e982255a124","2dbd21a50ff8c23b2a0bbd4b6347f127ef06f285ad4e31066aa1c536248705ec","3e9e500116712e1d1bbab252db4edb40553726afba62dee01529b352cf65cbd4","a0ec663a423a1bf23616ecaef34dc24ae9556ebd43800198386fbcdcfd11182b","53bcad57e3c196a15454d93fb4cd4d23c3e8ca844afa1ab654425adda7a67341","8794b3f1e52b501e0fec1d9d19479d4e2d884e001131846557f38b36d1866bb2","ae2624591ba718fae03f9074e6f8a2c93534f995f8d2e7dfd6de3abab9c59a0e","82fc584561ebe76e211a514a9d27d26f7dd8f3f4ffac87f39cf8ead195502def","b5de0889367bafd4848e55f9c8746f8e49f77bd8cddc06a3b6d0f3d93b1a9927","85f9923ddde440521cea50161116b25fe6cd2bc2e7631c10a015f0dc269937ec","3f8212b641398af7c77c15fb77e6a0978904a55e620172d95ea9d8d7567fcf5a","a77f1384806faf4e6c0d1aef826048cc00275878f873893c31e9e15f9da3a09d","303b1a2615a3e4b1e1eee70f1ee5a4d693b92a9fb837cd2251ba5796e05bf922","3869f25897172a729ea454f99803323f961e93746e2485069e5a532ec5055e12","236d9c74aaf549f711c17e25a427e10e2e43998daa6b1399a98c66f58005d955","405eb2b91872d7acae000c30a0862b4038a414e1a41069b2b539c8cb0ae1f15e","8ba10ade0e69897ceca10e86d58e98753b51328d950b16914d5b6b55edfa560d"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[216,239],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311924.zip::R2-2311924_Introduction of BWP_Wor in TS38.300.docx:p216"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311924.zip::R2-2311924_Introduction of BWP_Wor in TS38.300.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":240},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[unchanged text omitted]","paragraph_zero_based":241},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":242},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":243},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.2.7Radio Link Failure","paragraph_zero_based":244},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In RRC_CONNECTED, the UE performs Radio Link Monitoring (RLM) in the active BWP based on reference signals (SSB/CSI-RS) and signal quality thresholds configured by the network. SSB-based RLM is based on the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP and can be configured for the initial DL BWP, for DL BWPs containing the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP, and, if supported, for DL BWPs not containing the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP. Besides, SSB-based RLM can be also performed based on a non-cell defining SSB, if configured for the active DL BWP. For other DL BWPs, RLM can only be performed based on CSI-RS, if configured for the active DL BWP. In case of DAPS handover, the UE continues the detection of radio link failure at the source cell until the successful completion of the random access procedure to the target cell.","paragraph_zero_based":245},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":246},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[unchanged text omitted]","paragraph_zero_based":247},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":248},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":249},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"9.2.8Beam failure detection and recovery","paragraph_zero_based":250},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For beam failure detection, the gNB configures the UE with beam failure detection reference signals (SSB or CSI-RS) and the UE declares beam failure when the number of beam failure instance indications from the physical layer reaches a configured threshold before a configured timer expires. For beam failure detection in multi-TRP operation, the gNB configures the UE with two sets of beam failure detection reference signals, and the UE declares beam failure for a TRP / BFD-RS set when the number of beam failure instance indications associated with the corresponding set of beam failure detection reference signals from the physical layer reaches a configured threshold before a configured timer expires.","paragraph_zero_based":251},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SSB-based Beam Failure Detection is based on the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP and can be configured for the initial DL BWPs, for DL BWPs containing the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP, and, if supported, for DL BWPs not containing the CD-SSB associated to the initial DL BWP. Besides, SSB-based Beam Failure Detection can be also performed based on a non-cell defining SSB, if configured for the active DL BWP. For other DL BWPs, Beam Failure Detection can only be performed based on CSI-RS, if configured for the active DL BWP.","paragraph_zero_based":252},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":253},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[unchanged text omitted]","paragraph_zero_based":254},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":255},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Next change","paragraph_zero_based":256},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":257},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"16.13.5BWP operation","paragraph_zero_based":258},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A RedCap UE in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE monitors paging only in an initial BWP (default or RedCap specific) associated with CD-SSB and performs cell (re-)selection and related measurements on the CD-SSB. If a RedCap-specific initial UL BWP is configured and NUL is selected, RedCap UEs in RRC_IDLE and RRC_INACTIVE shall use only the RedCap-specific initial UL BWP to perform RACH.","paragraph_zero_based":259},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":260},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"End of change","paragraph_zero_based":261},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":262}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"5beccf2c4f7bc5ba3600d747955377cdba92a80fa413985f5bae4049b3acb775","original_member_sha256":"d98a639b7aa49723a0879cdea4b6917ea304cb84ec0d9c26e2a2bc33ee4c3d9f","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["6bbf640e6f69aaabe6c69a2ced11e20e4b9eedf6f660a5d1dfcad51b0bce3856","3e8b357ae3f32385588b06868947628b616df4fbd0434c423a43aaa6f07c3e45","7fb5365dd042a074ee0c2d2161bcdb924973204b95a3adec809b0e34e198e79e","b5351ecf189b92182033f2f2066d8d1768389b02ea3b88e075333530c6b488c0","fe6c905882ed15f0f4346cf25e045474da0ab847b73a935e356f7776d264c2d5","5e5959493c7727fcd29909c5b334074c17c2953efc9d54741cf17f77a26ba903","97e8ff9a77ff2834cf1e108ac99a7e3f6f1bf456abfdb9d5312757bdd1923a19","982221cd50f0150f923f8fb0bde855ee5c5a6697a2e1fb9dfc2ad21cc4743cfb","fb65608c281b60540832ea9bcbe758ba6ed78ecaa6da614c5a64eed992aaa95e","e97322a9f2b1fa45e845d4d795d4d67bfaedc4441314cb5b57603a601bc7e730","bdf0d8d5754692ef3ab3ca11d83d38d189d8ee99a5a9f730fa9d9e1f7668cf3f","8115b2b081b03abc42879aa0e6c36a9dfcaf04e5e726b0822bf3a796b4787aa5","c1343d46b212e9ddc0e48e632fd201d7b3874b8f73d0b5968a8eecd9190c3a28","eb37c771b8f8106078663baa324583884f15530cc8e04dcddae9b6657f635db2","e835602fe07fce23cbe9e5dba1beab6e65d56ca999be49ef963904777597fb57","5dbc0b1096bea66ce4bfda754ac06244471218b0ddeef1fe845f68453ed7e7b7","ae0bc5217e0267ca7286332e69667618ce8fc712881887ed306bb16a392cc9c8","65bcd2c1c5a21e51e5bbf24d3855d9434815407689d96ed5ccb314f3a0225522","502eb44a806fb7c9c86cb224156f19b08d4b03bcec6766403203080f21b902e6","00f19a25d7470e7d566ae60d08e9a7d74a4590eb0e229f8f6694b7f97