{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"VRVirtual Reality","paragraph_zero_based":408},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":409},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In the ASN.1, lower case may be used for some (parts) of the above abbreviations e.g. c-RNTI.","paragraph_zero_based":410},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4General","paragraph_zero_based":411},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.1Introduction","paragraph_zero_based":412},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This specification is organised as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":413},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-clause 4.2 describes the RRC protocol model;","paragraph_zero_based":414},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-clause 4.3 specifies the services provided to upper layers as well as the services expected from lower layers;","paragraph_zero_based":415},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-clause 4.4 lists the RRC functions;","paragraph_zero_based":416},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-clause 5 specifies RRC procedures, including UE state transitions;","paragraph_zero_based":417},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-clause 6 specifies the RRC messages in ASN.1 and description;","paragraph_zero_based":418},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-clause 7 specifies the variables (including protocol timers and constants) and counters to be used by the UE;","paragraph_zero_based":419},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-clause 8 specifies the encoding of the RRC messages;","paragraph_zero_based":420},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-clause 9 specifies the specified and default radio configurations;","paragraph_zero_based":421},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-clause 10 specifies generic error handling;","paragraph_zero_based":422},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-clause 11 specifies the RRC messages transferred across network nodes;","paragraph_zero_based":423},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-clause 12 specifies the UE capability related constraints and performance requirements.","paragraph_zero_based":424},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.2Architecture","paragraph_zero_based":425},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.2.1UE states and state transitions including inter RAT","paragraph_zero_based":426},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE is either in RRC_CONNECTED state or in RRC_INACTIVE state when an RRC connection has been established. If this is not the case, i.e. no RRC connection is established, the UE is in RRC_IDLE state. The RRC states can further be characterised as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":427},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-RRC_IDLE:","paragraph_zero_based":428},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-A UE specific DRX may be configured by upper layers;","paragraph_zero_based":429},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-At lower layers, the UE may be configured with a DRX for PTM transmission of MBS broadcast;","paragraph_zero_based":430},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-UE controlled mobility based on network configuration;","paragraph_zero_based":431}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["70e02da3966b422d134f2269e3cfee63acf14e660689961f131c9f922fa76c84","84b7f52e48a61775f9f5492133c4e6f500dbc7998bec5f8216964e7a9e684b52","09a96f23c3ea03db3a6753746418bb538e7f68e9354dc5535f477407c78e7417","f057546642a497ceb18ec7ca4b65db8a1a1ac41d8e8fe7b01d4b96deb005ab21","072d901868035a3743aaaa3dc46de0d496de008143cce57846e97b5c929adf66","46374db42f032ab5b4a585da604f06d0d26543f6843e353777fcaace5d326f0e","87734f446176093c123064aae03c448400ef491ed73967ebc067cc38a2e64b46","d0aac57db7ee39fb34f04323411a471dc09391ae92f816e2c501807acba9664d","d60bc9f7eb72ea24d237427492f9491cfeeb257a52e9f68d9aa3a3553303b3b5","f58bd81c5f187f8e0f41237049beca197c340a77e988de58c8ee25cc1365df95","c39c96d8d1c89cc6bfef21c8987b94efff83d14c25c053a0af1bc52a9e17d79c","8f3d3a679f246eaa0cd147a6bd38b60ef13f48ed1b40c8e4a8a622190e05fcad","c04009c6308a3781ae938fdb82c467e85dca8e76667a85f01911daae94495611","aae313cbee4932bd2dadf9c7082acec02985cfbd65fb014ee3a65c44c0153eaf","6b5b32b3cb6f784c4055ae16c418bef98b4b7525f6bef467b44085efea8693aa","77aca7343bc07c8862c88d0b488493dcd4b9b3000b7ce293c40c340d4d084a9c","d7e63f590ee2c8a617ade31f77be7411a2ad5b63947e6c5a7a27394295dfe624","56c8124c4b26b283ffcc0cf239fa8a7e42a1d6c243d65c4973914e2eb42d31bb","3791127584d77dab476ac90a31b332f010afd49ba7f2ec3aacf56d947e48f56e","b63b8e4ea4a92b1bcf7cb27699031e18f1a91855c6b353f829fe0da487e46d43","e796037bd3d59ca8aefafed0fac7824f48e1029b3e26c677ab2d3060a56ca4b3","e70dfd728c9023a669583cbbac0407fedf9fcfd6e7438cc0648d9cffa46ab0b5","b584e53df8ef85b151a559598384ee8279a6432b6b9b21e0e8f790d4d25a0aa7","7e4348c70056dfc55dd347b1b5431d2144b557eeaa25a07d38024e4e901bd8d4"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[408,431],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p408"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The UE:","paragraph_zero_based":432},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Monitors Short Messages transmitted with P-RNTI over DCI (see clause 6.5);","paragraph_zero_based":433},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Monitors a Paging channel for CN paging using 5G-S-TMSI, except if the UE is acting as a L2 U2N Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":434},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If configured by upper layers for MBS multicast reception, monitors a Paging channel for CN paging using TMGI;","paragraph_zero_based":435},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Performs neighbouring cell measurements and cell (re-)selection;","paragraph_zero_based":436},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Acquires system information and can send SI request (if configured);","paragraph_zero_based":437},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Performs logging of available measurements together with location and time for logged measurement configured UEs;","paragraph_zero_based":438},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Performs idle/inactive measurements for idle/inactive measurement configured UEs;","paragraph_zero_based":439},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If configured by upper layers for MBS broadcast reception, acquires MCCH change notification and MBS broadcast control information and data.","paragraph_zero_based":440},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-RRC_INACTIVE:","paragraph_zero_based":441},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-A UE specific DRX may be configured by upper layers or by RRC layer;","paragraph_zero_based":442},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-At lower layers, the UE may be configured with a DRX for PTM transmission of MBS broadcast;","paragraph_zero_based":443},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-UE controlled mobility based on network configuration;","paragraph_zero_based":444},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The UE stores the UE Inactive AS context;","paragraph_zero_based":445},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-A RAN-based notification area is configured by RRC layer;","paragraph_zero_based":446},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Transfer of unicast data and/or signalling to/from UE over radio bearers configured for SDT.","paragraph_zero_based":447},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE:","paragraph_zero_based":448},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Monitors Short Messages transmitted with P-RNTI over DCI (see clause 6.5);","paragraph_zero_based":449},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-During SDT procedure, monitors control channels associated with the shared data channel to determine if data is scheduled for it;","paragraph_zero_based":450},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-While SDT procedure is not ongoing, monitors a Paging channel for CN paging using 5G-S-TMSI and RAN paging using fullI-RNTI, except if the UE is acting as a L2 U2N Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":451},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If configured by upper layers for MBS multicast reception, while SDT procedure is not ongoing, monitors a Paging channel for paging using TMGI;","paragraph_zero_based":452},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Performs neighbouring cell measurements and cell (re-)selection;","paragraph_zero_based":453},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Performs RAN-based notification area updates periodically and when moving outside the configured RAN-based notification area;","paragraph_zero_based":454},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Acquires system information, while SDT procedure is not ongoing, and can send SI request (if configured);","paragraph_zero_based":455}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["415c7b0ca1cd10cf5548bc0469f1edb22840fc65446991b068a2bd64c0d5aa6c","168cd523c58fd2495092f75b339cf3c2e21394fff1740b36ac8a76b3ba1feb6f","354aa178204e3766044ec37c8bb1d84e70c21f5b778eeb9e9c850c6e2accbae3","9d97c3a7ada6811b4751411d21a76046c9b5cbbc256788eec34ac2862f3aa752","ab08a5ab07da2b576aff766bc8cba832d546cca2de5e5263f32639ac2ebc58c5","28df756c9c4e76e2daa497108ff90c1857e6243477f08d295f7aabe48cf6bdd3","e01dab96a5a440c945c393ee5fde265eef83a2eba88b6cb156bb5d6b14dbae7e","77a467eca9821d0d2d4916646d5bebbbc217c7652ae3537b404cff2e44f2c980","896773afcb73aee5e7a8716f83a37cf37a9699025bc4272ce62ffda225faa49d","2e48af91209391dcbf035d1842423e580e4f4024d8d28757a43c1c5296053ff8","7421dc5b7f5b5fc4ff5228df08da72d03b8e0210a91f8aeddd49c59e40626625","7c966aca121fedb5019814a6bb3cafda7bb1b410f794b68a27219e9d4db1a6ff","3cc187dc88f8e209f9d52cce9d6c5d16faadc544eb3f7881c210c4a095fa56cf","40b7ba5b10edb6d45c1ba5814539d486c68250a83cc4c6f34d9be78b918414f5","d57eb8a759498e5a09a8c4c518de6c3837250913a47bf0663e18a25ec5e8e694","8fd1f677174c006bf0338f2b5f3484edfb7abe861874be8fdd448e802b4fa670","109e7d9dbcc40362337baed0c80f14c37b2716571d5e26282c7d0d89e914e24f","3dbae91a7e7d68c4148adf5584dc5374a9943127bf479ea9a2ca64bf00a5c09e","f266cf170197d9d79debb17fc2faa0003dd2746fe0cdff630ae1113baeb9e030","5bd376ded247ea2cc0087f077ca4293925951628f3db228cd37d17b190651650","128a3dec8cf3872b0c16d56ba08e948262037b38c2a0821e955f37798379e102","cbb67b096501b754ad62096da2ca7f876b183c750519390c2d4c5eed5988118d","4b12db8b86952cac3e456dbb2f7ff3771991f989caff738ea544cf33b71cd558","e88b9e0faaac64fd59e51c79bcf3f1b84eb1b241e58413b25a20a98ea58bf727"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[432,455],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p432"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-While SDT procedure is not ongoing, performs logging of available measurements together with location and time for logged measurement configured UEs;","paragraph_zero_based":456},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-While SDT procedure is not ongoing, performs idle/inactive measurements for idle/inactive measurement configured UEs;","paragraph_zero_based":457},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If configured by upper layers for MBS broadcast reception, acquires MCCH change notification and MBS broadcast control information and data;","paragraph_zero_based":458},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Transmits SRS for Positioning.","paragraph_zero_based":459},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-RRC_CONNECTED:","paragraph_zero_based":460},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The UE stores the AS context;","paragraph_zero_based":461},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Transfer of unicast data to/from UE;","paragraph_zero_based":462},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Transfer of MBS multicast data to UE;","paragraph_zero_based":463},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-At lower layers, the UE may be configured with a UE specific DRX;","paragraph_zero_based":464},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-At lower layers, the UE may be configured with a DRX for PTM transmission of MBS broadcast and/or a DRX for MBS multicast;","paragraph_zero_based":465},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For UEs supporting CA, use of one or more SCells, aggregated with the SpCell, for increased bandwidth;","paragraph_zero_based":466},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For UEs supporting DC, use of one SCG, aggregated with the MCG, for increased bandwidth;","paragraph_zero_based":467},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Network controlled mobility within NR, to/from E-UTRA, and to UTRA-FDD;","paragraph_zero_based":468},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Network controlled mobility (path switch) between a serving cell and a L2 U2N Relay UE, or vice versa.","paragraph_zero_based":469},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-The UE:","paragraph_zero_based":470},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Monitors Short Messages transmitted with P-RNTI over DCI (see clause 6.5), if configured;","paragraph_zero_based":471},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Monitors control channels associated with the shared data channel to determine if data is scheduled for it;","paragraph_zero_based":472},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Provides channel quality and feedback information;","paragraph_zero_based":473},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Performs neighbouring cell measurements and measurement reporting;","paragraph_zero_based":474},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Acquires system information;","paragraph_zero_based":475},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Performs immediate MDT measurement together with available location reporting;","paragraph_zero_based":476},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-If configured by upper layers for MBS broadcast reception, acquires MCCH change notification and MBS broadcast control information and data.","paragraph_zero_based":477},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 4.2.1-1 illustrates an overview of UE RRC state machine and state transitions in NR. A UE has only one RRC state in NR at one time.","paragraph_zero_based":478},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":479}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["90a1a2a7d88b9884c78bcc54370dd01e27a2d15eb1239ae4a510137ca8564239","34795d3054b37ae17fcd724b7b9fc8bc294ae94590ddf11c4c103c4343a45bc1","f57d463e6fbbd4c4a3643a0e9582664217aa41b2eee6a3f1b39fbececce6fef9","e023fd7365258ada2a3645e76bf2a573e4fbbd63e2e91713015dd8b5b9baafc4","1547e6e717b1f669a0ee80b88b2e0f555903260bcefa3425e8732294ae5c5977","bb86bdf2511a3292037587bf52bcdc4e78d47af54a9decfde0d162b25e37f24f","b7dc43d9c40c3cd46f98d4001bdbe680d3da37ef3fd024dfbd1213278410c90b","3d068043c1b11ba012622dba6f2b279e281afeb468867c6543f2751ddf79f104","f0bc90c17a26b4dd736ea371a02bdb19acbe049faac1b80df25ad9e6920cb0b4","f6708aeb773ce4f9d1099fa21502745111a5e47db8eb361a62d43d6757624f5b","a3535087b4232694bc0c4cc39f6639b035f4807da42bb55f47843144f3e0989b","3ea43ccb4a77f68c0ae8272eefe4ff01b14c6c35c4aead907f2616f4f601c264","9e6b9f2ef35a53316ed2bd918134b3fa0f6b0e19b1c79d91dc4d0bbeb7b5682d","6411d7524b4d358a95af669bc882698a109126079077156eed2b2d20e0897f36","2c3a6b1329a600f25fe38a805ed5986d424cdeacc4644aee46257b30e80d7bb5","881ce4215449c63905631cf81a5490d1331c713b3b50c76b1dfc7d1bccd31ee6","9d76becac3087c2c700343efb497a395a859866e9fd4f7a205bef37ec229ef9e","459b90eb0b0e8c761414f782c71e4233bc4d913897e5bd0643551f898b5a3304","43c4eceac7c303d70312e8785bfe0574427b0c58b975f562efcf0c8111e772b1","1eec72b498e1679b743788a25c9c9eafa8e35798d10349cd8cb47baedfbe8cee","af4a4716a43e947d08315f156c99d4849e87be32347b06fb81a5797eb7a05fc3","8e8f5e5249f1df61c12c1e9d17639bb64812f410261d7aab4422a6c8451fb6d7","f017407799fb3370ea28a0c8b57060eb0c75ff45104953d72e27de981934d1d5","be1c0f0cc86ffe0076f18e202080758e70996ce2678f75d9ab0ad55410f3ee00"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[456,479],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p456"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 4.2.1-1:UE state machine and state transitions in NR","paragraph_zero_based":480},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 4.2.1-2 illustrates an overview of UE state machine and state transitions in NR as well as the mobility procedures supported between NR/5GC, E-UTRA/EPC and E-UTRA/5GC.","paragraph_zero_based":481},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":482},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 4.2.1-2:UE state machine and state transitions between NR/5GC, E-UTRA/EPC and E-UTRA/5GC","paragraph_zero_based":483},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 4.2.1-3 illustrates the mobility procedure supported between NR/5GC and UTRA-FDD.","paragraph_zero_based":484},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":485},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 4.2.1-3:Mobility procedure supported between NR/5GC and UTRA-FDD","paragraph_zero_based":486},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":487},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.2.2Signalling radio bearers","paragraph_zero_based":488},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"\"Signalling Radio Bearers\" (SRBs) are defined as Radio Bearers (RBs) that are used only for the transmission of RRC and NAS messages. More specifically, the following SRBs are defined:","paragraph_zero_based":489},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SRB0 is for RRC messages using the CCCH logical channel;","paragraph_zero_based":490},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SRB1 is for RRC messages (which may include a piggybacked NAS message) as well as for NAS messages prior to the establishment of SRB2, all using DCCH logical channel;","paragraph_zero_based":491},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SRB2 is for NAS messages and for RRC messages which include logged measurement information, all using DCCH logical channel. SRB2 has a lower priority than SRB1 and may be configured by the network after AS security activation;","paragraph_zero_based":492},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SRB3 is for specific RRC messages when UE is in (NG)EN-DC or NR-DC, all using DCCH logical channel;","paragraph_zero_based":493},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SRB4 is for RRC messages which include application layer measurement report information, all using DCCH logical channel. SRB4 has a lower priority than SRB1 and can only be configured by the network after AS security activation.","paragraph_zero_based":494},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In downlink, piggybacking of NAS messages is used only for one dependant (i.e. with joint success/failure) procedure: bearer establishment/modification/release. In uplink piggybacking of NAS message is used only for transferring the initial NAS message during connection setup and connection resume.","paragraph_zero_based":495},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:The NAS messages transferred via SRB2 are also contained in RRC messages, which however do not include any RRC protocol control information.","paragraph_zero_based":496},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Once AS security is activated, all RRC messages on SRB1, SRB2, SRB3 and SRB4, including those containing NAS messages, are integrity protected and ciphered by PDCP. NAS independently applies integrity protection and ciphering to the NAS messages, see TS 24.501 [23].","paragraph_zero_based":497},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Split SRB is supported for all the MR-DC options in both SRB1 and SRB2 (split SRB is not supported for SRB0, SRB3 and SRB4).","paragraph_zero_based":498},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For operation with shared spectrum channel access in FR1, SRB0, SRB1 and SRB3 are assigned with the highest priority Channel Access Priority Class (CAPC), (i.e. CAPC = 1) while CAPC for SRB2 is configurable.","paragraph_zero_based":499},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.3Services","paragraph_zero_based":500},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.3.1Services provided to upper layers","paragraph_zero_based":501},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The RRC protocol offers the following services to upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":502},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Broadcast of common control information;","paragraph_zero_based":503}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["43b6aa99eac5d65e5131b44fa5e31a6b812a005dd54998cc2c7ef06dd2012cc8","d8ccb12899390aa2dcce463d1992237cc6b191fc8fea80c95f31c97ab99e405c","21db476eeed2fedb894477f81b4c943f9230dd236857aa65d3d461fd70c3cd64","2c320ba21b572e3b3ba622f62d4bb165f5e53813a0cf6a2d5c8b3744e608ca3b","c405e7dacd488d1b3569131e9f43b3244ace030a58e1294e7112f1eb43d3deb3","d1ec70a402d2784924875a612a5cd64563956f27992fcf39d7358708afe28c34","b766d989a7a91f1e80c385c6880fa50c5f367f82282dec938124e9f77ca5ef18","c563cae76505982585ee8a16c5aee99c91e5ac3e59204367ea1dc219041ec496","a7fa77094953ac68498b2b22715ae7ffad3c2da850fdbdedc69aa4ae2ecb953d","a2bd328a4a1d74ec7f70d9520020ddf704c3b25b1c285f172eab9f941d72657f","172765d1b1e7d5760f55d77181e452f782ed3588855f90ac6b28fbaff288adaf","70475f50cb000f14761d92a40a2a8bfe8b6eb773ddbb7be9baaa9c167a070e0d","dfcc48dd890b0da88eaf59cc08751bad0cf3884cd2256cb2d0ad09186f7a8137","e696889179f335e8739717712e42c7d516dd4b1ed5aa8a9f1deae98dbd1437ad","9b39293229935025be21ebd52814518e483160f2f53bd30523a5b60f2e2ce208","7ed7d10c14879ff498f2b34cba1f62f5c1b458af31670756d0cbf6fa8789c64b","c89bcf229c2e877a3b5c3e5c028e812cac3380740b8bd32a0cf2dea3f3713a89","32623ed6db7ff8a6b54a8d3261912355e387a9f4cd4bd24dae6505555fa04e22","5061695cf91cfb95110c6ee96bea196b9ef0b789cf7843b83104bdb6f544387c","5899b6ef26be2d861540068e694068dbdecc73343ce523d9612ebf372c89c3f0","8816ef1bfb3da2a24b9746e0f70eb58dacf8322c0028d1de1dc63220e3be03e8","468a6315f7cf6341385465c75783c424cf9fab4b33f649d1cbdcacba8002693e","925bfeac56c83bc7288525179e8832d6a7190ca0820b7da14f3a4efa82818a2e","bedc16c6c56f1c1d720499fa27a45f73a4d91bb03c4ee6785161d9208fcf84a4"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[480,503],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p480"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Notification of UEs in RRC_IDLE, e.g. about a mobile terminating call;","paragraph_zero_based":504},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Notification of UEs about ETWS and/or CMAS;","paragraph_zero_based":505},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Transfer of dedicated signalling;","paragraph_zero_based":506},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Broadcast of positioning assistance data;","paragraph_zero_based":507},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Transfer of application layer measurement configuration and reporting.","paragraph_zero_based":508},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.3.2Services expected from lower layers","paragraph_zero_based":509},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In brief, the following are the main services that RRC expects from lower layers:","paragraph_zero_based":510},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Integrity protection, ciphering and loss-less in-sequence delivery of information without duplication;","paragraph_zero_based":511},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.4Functions","paragraph_zero_based":512},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The RRC protocol includes the following main functions:","paragraph_zero_based":513},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Broadcast of system information:","paragraph_zero_based":514},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Including NAS common information;","paragraph_zero_based":515},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Information applicable for UEs in RRC_IDLE and RRC_INACTIVE (e.g. cell (re-)selection parameters, neighbouring cell information) and information (also) applicable for UEs in RRC_CONNECTED (e.g. common channel configuration information);","paragraph_zero_based":516},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Including ETWS notification, CMAS notification;","paragraph_zero_based":517},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Including positioning assistance data.","paragraph_zero_based":518},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-RRC connection control:","paragraph_zero_based":519},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Paging;","paragraph_zero_based":520},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Establishment/modification/suspension/resumption/release of RRC connection, including e.g. assignment/modification of UE identity (C-RNTI, fullI-RNTI, etc.), establishment/modification/suspension/resumption/release of SRBs (except for SRB0);","paragraph_zero_based":521},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Access barring;","paragraph_zero_based":522},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Initial AS security activation, i.e. initial configuration of AS integrity protection (SRBs, DRBs) and AS ciphering (SRBs, DRBs);","paragraph_zero_based":523},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-RRC connection mobility including e.g. intra-frequency and inter-frequency handover, path switch from a PCell to a target L2 U2N Relay UE or from a L2 U2N Relay UE to a target PCell, associated AS security handling, i.e. key/algorithm change, specification of RRC context information transferred between network nodes;","paragraph_zero_based":524},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Establishment/modification/suspension/resumption/release of RBs carrying user data (DRBs/MRBs);","paragraph_zero_based":525},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Radio configuration control including e.g. assignment/modification of ARQ configuration, HARQ configuration, DRX configuration;","paragraph_zero_based":526},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-In case of DC, cell management including e.g. change of PSCell, addition/modification/release of SCG cell(s);","paragraph_zero_based":527}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["14d607662dd691427b0e5fb72f3a6d222472d8a43918b9920730825dad71736e","322e7c4409ec2a9521ee0cccbca1b6763df06ddab2b4718a0e590e6aa1c4e14d","adbc2da8ba397c5af92915ce29a58efb141f9ff6f18ab2fe7160f419c1a5e020","506eb10177b6ee420639523c022eb8e191ec7499a274294dd0314ef7119f4f26","ad956bfcff01e81fc21aa30a695bf8c6fd83aa2214c3aada8ed494f5635ae511","52ed194fe9a146cf19354a2b92c4c22cd117f5e140ae00b661a1884628c5b237","2b365b7b3e91e17d1fe2ad93bb753ec0cc7135e4ef9c234222133e50e39d500b","e3dbe77de351f88aefabbebc53746dcb798f93e5e5de0cae03c5dc26c0d27901","8f3db76cd243da08b08e11f9c05894670a3a6f4e928ccc78912a3460f0089726","bda49cc76913060bc33867330567a9dbaba254dcb70696a59f5f66e6e9b031a9","5f40b433fe2ada3668e28e0ad9f10f530eb8e0cc11b9f9a8dc7e90bf188ee06d","f3ae15bea5b874fc9a47c3f2605919016b6b3a5fa5d3384ba5042f61d1ec1697","996d735e1e45914278abf9627c90d0275b6a7f0f9ab05b868f1892265cdfd5ee","078397ccec1bbf42548b25ea1a9c00bad39291ff8e24652614c86e610dba6d47","f0181edcc519ea4909ea828008efda6f500b98eb2b21a533ae96959c32afb7f9","dc8e01fc1b9a6e3a070c2a32cc9c4fb00da486bec4d2b03c0bcefc63080e76e2","00df35a547e3fb25c76e5213dc95b339e51f1034f135556256b40b9cdd004e96","be04d04ca3914a677c98a1f73b02c33dbdc9879fe57dc09e0d9b11d597e9ec3d","078b523731494206de734aba30cfcde0ecf84321e66bc9dad41fa5601b5f27c7","7b85608094a880634e7e6aba0aa62c8b0f2de75321ecc4580325c9a24800344b","2920750cbfb041aa2a51ee52620af1f3d23048f7cbefd5266a4caad47fb0d37a","652ca24a3140464d0c95cb19efa82fd911db1415e347fe4c028c82d01b12f40f","dc48c01f0c11421e03b84ae43ec710a77c469e3f8550422cb5f3fc64c5760f65","c54f110b5bca52b7d4b0fb9bbfa8d3c45f19e5dc64b808127776535fd75bd6ab"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[504,527],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p504"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-In case of CA, cell management including e.g. addition/modification/release of SCell(s);","paragraph_zero_based":528},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-QoS control including assignment/ modification of semi-persistent scheduling (SPS) configuration and configured grant configuration for DL and UL respectively, assignment/ modification of parameters for UL rate control in the UE, i.e. allocation of a priority and a prioritised bit rate (PBR) for each RB of UE and logical channel of IAB-MT.","paragraph_zero_based":529},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Recovery from radio link failure.","paragraph_zero_based":530},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Inter-RAT mobility including e.g. AS security activation, transfer of RRC context information;","paragraph_zero_based":531},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Measurement configuration and reporting:","paragraph_zero_based":532},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Establishment/modification/release of measurement configuration (e.g. intra-frequency, inter-frequency and inter- RAT measurements);","paragraph_zero_based":533},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Setup and release of measurement gaps;","paragraph_zero_based":534},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Measurement reporting.","paragraph_zero_based":535},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Configuration of BAP entity and BH RLC channels for the support of IAB-node.","paragraph_zero_based":536},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Other functions including e.g. generic protocol error handling, transfer of dedicated NAS information, transfer of UE radio access capability information.","paragraph_zero_based":537},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Support of self-configuration and self-optimisation.","paragraph_zero_based":538},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Support of measurement logging and reporting for network performance optimisation, as specified in TS 37.320 [61];","paragraph_zero_based":539},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Support of transfer of application layer measurement configuration and reporting.","paragraph_zero_based":540},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5Procedures","paragraph_zero_based":541},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"<<Skip Unchanged>>","paragraph_zero_based":542},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.5.3.2Layer 3 filtering","paragraph_zero_based":543},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":544},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each cell measurement quantity, each beam measurement quantity, each sidelink measurement quantity as needed in clause 5.8.10, for each CLI measurement quantity that the UE performs measurements according to 5.5.3.1, and for each candidate L2 U2N Relay UE or candidate U2U Relay UE measurement quantity according to 5.5.3.4:","paragraph_zero_based":545},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>filter the measured result, before using for evaluation of reporting criteria, for measurement reporting or for U2U Relay (re)selection evaluation, by the following formula:","paragraph_zero_based":546},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Fn = (1 – a)*Fn-1 + a*Mn","paragraph_zero_based":547},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"where","paragraph_zero_based":548},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Mn is the latest received measurement result from the physical layer;","paragraph_zero_based":549},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Fn is the updated filtered measurement result, that is used for evaluation of reporting criteria,  for measurement reporting or for U2U Relay (re)selection evaluation;","paragraph_zero_based":550},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Fn-1 is the old filtered measurement result, where F0 is set to M1 when the first measurement result from the physical layer is received; and for MeasObjectNR, a = 1/2(ki/4), where ki is the filterCoefficient for the corresponding measurement quantity of the i:th QuantityConfigNR in quantityConfigNR-List, and i is indicated by quantityConfigIndex in MeasObjectNR; for other measurements, a = 1/2(k/4), where k is the filterCoefficient for the corresponding measurement quantity received by the quantityConfig; for UTRA-FDD, a = 1/2(k/4), where k is the filterCoefficient for the corresponding measurement quantity received by quantityConfigUTRA-FDD in the QuantityConfig;","paragraph_zero_based":551}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["063cd05c3208f0c98381cc9fd7190ad246395770d5fbc5d2a35fe5ed3f8db796","f51987fcf53edebc27b0916c3f63225d3bed4ae38efcab9dcc38c40d6c856c43","0939b7fe90052a4cc0da4239363cae781dc5e8d6e3f51e16cb15d1cd113f5104","205101d32ad4c681c6e535d0611fd3972c1b1b8b28b50f07597a44e081bd918f","433cf86c046045c80ddd83e6df942645baf82c3c4a1e4223f9a2e3fbaa585f7f","7ff2fff47fb8a1836d6e6140ac180a06537e5eecf6fa91279c5c3d1eb1e94289","58258eb5f06f0e62a35df001ee47b352cd38e741b20f2e1aec1ab2d5569f9b1f","e14c7d57c2cc0d6ba6f33433d404313b11e317852bb96c8f5f60213227cd4a55","d480e02ab50e71fdfbce704eacc6e19f9970d2e1e34657199358dadd15d86c61","5adde2b2e95b1ff0b95d07120452ca6a53d6017b275efd4201b3f77d1bf1fead","a27ba3ea50a9afed89716ac5802141505dc467c39d5411697c0cbaf46abcc44a","6f106f52a4e51585fec6b924706041d64b5e7aa96e3775731c0bb8f1d978c928","296f7e633bf576e74978bda48b6dd39a08d08173edeb6ffaeba1aab1a4b27282","7bfb1b9dd37f9ea027face6bbde8d22112471a5f15f02b29ee159588b2f0cb3b","23f1a515398296c411dc951526ba32c9ca614e58e70487665db78500d1e7f924","9622d556d6c00064a3ab5f027ae0e1383f94f3077de8ec06962c251d9c694a11","7e8982a0d5ed6aee9b4e28073472d118056c81971a8d62d3defedeb3fc2fd869","adb5ce855fd2254a039fb66b33b53941dca61b238a476fced29a6a4b91354834","46e3a484f37dc523eb721a2db21ea75f17988eb28248a87f50311c388dc168b2","86c9bcf19b2ea135357b19018f7e0d8d00c97a1a07e351cdb497a13d9763711f","1ea18dcf4e86fb49484d833a8fdb5d95bb542649cf087b68706017760f78b836","61996d87b8b87110486159e8bc932896b0ca01143e0f0ec78e4cc8944ba5aa07","2a522e8844888b5918565561aad977550411f8fe1a6744b3995b23203cee43fd","f462e591221703b4814a4830ed382843ee529c82b58d80c14c144d7c94298d7a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[528,551],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p528"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>adapt the filter such that the time characteristics of the filter are preserved at different input rates, observing that the filterCoefficient k assumes a sample rate equal to X ms; The value of X is equivalent to one intra-frequency L1 measurement period as defined in TS 38.133 [14] assuming non-DRX operation, and depends on frequency range.","paragraph_zero_based":552},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:If k is set to 0, no layer 3 filtering is applicable.","paragraph_zero_based":553},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:The filtering is performed in the same domain as used for evaluation of reporting criteria or for measurement reporting, i.e., logarithmic filtering for logarithmic measurements.","paragraph_zero_based":554},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 3:The filter input rate is implementation dependent, to fulfil the performance requirements set in TS 38.133 [14]. For further details about the physical layer measurements, see TS 38.133 [14].","paragraph_zero_based":555},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 4:For CLI-RSSI measurement, it is up to UE implementation whether to reset filtering upon BWP switch.","paragraph_zero_based":556},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.5.3.3Derivation of cell measurement results","paragraph_zero_based":557},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The network may configure the UE in RRC_CONNECTED to derive RSRP, RSRQ and SINR measurement results per cell associated to NR measurement objects based on parameters configured in the measObject (e.g. maximum number of beams to be averaged and beam consolidation thresholds) and in the reportConfig (rsType to be measured, SS/PBCH block or CSI-RS).","paragraph_zero_based":558},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The network may configure the UE in RRC_IDLE or in RRC_INACTIVE to derive RSRP and RSRQ measurement results per cell associated to NR carriers based on parameters configured in measIdleCarrierListNR within VarMeasIdleConfig for measurements performed according to 5.7.8.2a.","paragraph_zero_based":559},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":560},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each cell measurement quantity to be derived based on SS/PBCH block:","paragraph_zero_based":561},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if nrofSS-BlocksToAverage is not configured in the associated measObject in RRC_CONNECTED or in the associated entry in measIdleCarrierListNR within VarMeasIdleConfig in RRC_IDLE/RRC_INACTIVE; or","paragraph_zero_based":562},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if absThreshSS-BlocksConsolidation is not configured in the associated measObject in RRC_CONNECTED or in the associated entry in measIdleCarrierListNR within VarMeasIdleConfig in RRC_IDLE/RRC_INACTIVE; or","paragraph_zero_based":563},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the highest beam measurement quantity value is below or equal to absThreshSS-BlocksConsolidation:","paragraph_zero_based":564},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>derive each cell measurement quantity based on SS/PBCH block as the highest beam measurement quantity value, where each beam measurement quantity is described in TS 38.215 [9];","paragraph_zero_based":565},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":566},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>derive each cell measurement quantity based on SS/PBCH block as the linear power scale average of the highest beam measurement quantity values above absThreshSS-BlocksConsolidation where the total number of averaged beams shall not exceed nrofSS-BlocksToAverage, and where each beam measurement quantity is described in TS 38.215 [9];","paragraph_zero_based":567},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if in RRC_CONNECTED, apply layer 3 cell filtering as described in 5.5.3.2;","paragraph_zero_based":568},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each cell measurement quantity to be derived based on CSI-RS:","paragraph_zero_based":569},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>consider a CSI-RS resource to be applicable for deriving cell measurements when the concerned CSI-RS resource is included in the csi-rs-CellMobility including the physCellId of the cell in theCSI-RS-ResourceConfigMobility in the associated measObject;","paragraph_zero_based":570},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if nrofCSI-RS-ResourcesToAverage in the associated measObject is not configured; or","paragraph_zero_based":571},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if absThreshCSI-RS-Consolidation in the associated measObject is not configured; or","paragraph_zero_based":572},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the highest beam measurement quantity value is below or equal to absThreshCSI-RS-Consolidation:","paragraph_zero_based":573},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>derive each cell measurement quantity based on applicable CSI-RS resources for the cell as the highest beam measurement quantity value, where each beam measurement quantity is described in TS 38.215 [9];","paragraph_zero_based":574},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":575}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["6d7b76044fda178c872200cdfd73ac6122b060d9db8efa760ba1c0ee6d5c5a2d","26fec5b9d12b83b2a18ce86735ea65a32b429f58e2cde313c79fdc6814e29d83","ecb0c1ce683b2995f1bdf91f89e1200174606ce06f5956a7137e64696a5a2a96","f33a4e0eb65827b36d7b50f576f50e34db7c995b358576d620b3bc399cb73462","c7ac421d77893d4b54bd9c74e094c245e486b3eda209bcacbe6a5704b802a8a8","2d36c8afa3969f3d2ff746dec51f36a993d67afaf1ff45ecc6b1847da4de2ab2","69e553800d852d66d1c036deb9723f372a85fa75669e58c391513da80f41f985","f2784d703289a0ccc3a8a04bafbd06c0b52ce47082bdaaa40115701e0bc48273","b70694312ec11f3ab3edf8116962b5732d1c01e3ce9f3d0f0a3c406b9b550afa","ec35cfb40281da834ab54254801834f92e2dfdd36c3c7087f49675cbe5dbce0e","8ac0cc37a9f776c356674dbda156f189b0e51d2a0082e7a10478c7003ec5ce76","9502578f09ec438327f353d76b6034cac052fd6fe3b93f6fd7582336043a9da9","51f702d384096a1d60fd0d496492ebc7fa61b481852a6b511951ae20c2b58cdd","ca819d9afd348653de312e7e2a9189f780ce2524965a3526e9b1d21b6f5520d8","c4917799923be8f32abe5385327b37983719da4389a430833ffd01b28a582b9c","143fa14b30789e83d4b6d86d456829779cf67fa0d7439546350a87e2542b9149","ffa2a1db1900e606bd30859ac5a2325a88d3d188f8b719295ed9d526db155539","88cb1bf067452a332710be312f278bb4c71a40775e5372460b7af9124417c3d7","86519461a889aa7f3f9fcbd4f634691e77993074443a778749c814dbb392e8a1","e9930c53e50087e48d749f9fcc1806d3d3f0bd12e1d8738f7c95d03555e5f1fb","97d4480b98e28e57e32902c3ca03bed92f9287818287168bb9926b3b2b6201e0","a7393c8fa8c1acaaa12e97e9745892c09ea4e177c3410af7e4ce82e91cc9fe77","ef2a1678789192481686fd141d36026596cc3f9e39bf62df49573fcf0ec8882a","fef6e82fce6f76d1b7c7e96f479d32897e2448c8afe637f24572818273ceb16d"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[552,575],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p552"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>derive each cell measurement quantity based on CSI-RS as the linear power scale average of the highest beam measurement quantity values above absThreshCSI-RS-Consolidation where the total number of averaged beams shall not exceed nrofCSI-RS-ResourcesToAverage;","paragraph_zero_based":576},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>apply layer 3 cell filtering as described in 5.5.3.2.","paragraph_zero_based":577},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.5.3.3aDerivation of layer 3 beam filtered measurement","paragraph_zero_based":578},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":579},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each layer 3 beam filtered measurement quantity to be derived based on SS/PBCH block;","paragraph_zero_based":580},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>derive each configured beam measurement quantity based on SS/PBCH block as described in TS 38.215[9], and apply layer 3 beam filtering as described in 5.5.3.2;","paragraph_zero_based":581},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each layer 3 beam filtered measurement quantity to be derived based on CSI-RS;","paragraph_zero_based":582},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>derive each configured beam measurement quantity based on CSI-RS as described in TS 38.215 [9], and apply layer 3 beam filtering as described in 5.5.3.2.","paragraph_zero_based":583},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.5.3.4Derivation of L2 U2N Relay UE measurement results","paragraph_zero_based":584},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE may be configured by network to derive NR sidelink measurement results of serving L2 U2N Relay UE or candidate L2 U2N Relay UEs associated to the measurement objects configured in the measObjectRelay.","paragraph_zero_based":585},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":586},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each L2 U2N Relay UE measurement quantity to be derived:","paragraph_zero_based":587},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>derive the corresponding measurement quantity based on DMRS as described in TS 38.215 [9];","paragraph_zero_based":588},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>apply layer 3 filtering as described in 5.5.3.2;","paragraph_zero_based":589},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"<<Skip Unchanged>>","paragraph_zero_based":590},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8Sidelink","paragraph_zero_based":591},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.1General","paragraph_zero_based":592},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR sidelink communication consists of unicast, groupcast and broadcast. For unicast, the PC5-RRC connection is a logical connection between a pair of a Source Layer-2 ID and a Destination Layer-2 ID in the AS. The PC5-RRC signalling, as specified in clause 5.8.9, can be initiated after its corresponding PC5 unicast link establishment (TS 23.287 [55]). The PC5-RRC connection and the corresponding sidelink SRBs and sidelink DRB(s) are released when the PC5 unicast link is released as indicated by upper layers.","paragraph_zero_based":593},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For each PC5-RRC connection of unicast, one sidelink SRB (i.e. SL-SRB0) is used to transmit the PC5-S message(s) before the PC5-S security has been established. One sidelink SRB (i.e. SL-SRB1) is used to transmit the PC5-S messages to establish the PC5-S security. One sidelink SRB (i.e. SL-SRB2) is used to transmit the PC5-S messages after the PC5-S security has been established, which is protected. One sidelink SRB (i.e. SL-SRB3) is used to transmit the PC5-RRC signalling, which is protected and only sent after the PC5-S security has been established. One sidelink SRB (i.e. SL-SRB4) is used to transmit/receive the NR sidelink discovery messages.","paragraph_zero_based":594},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For unicast of NR sidelink communication, AS security comprises of integrity protection of PC5 signalling (SL-SRB1, SL-SRB2 and SL-SRB3) and user data (SL-DRBs), and it further comprises of ciphering of PC5 signaling (SL-SRB1 only for the Direct Link Security Mode Complete message as specified in TS 24.587 [57] for V2X service or TS 24.554 [72] for Proximity-services, SL-SRB2 and SL-SRB3) and user data (SL-DRBs). The ciphering and integrity protection algorithms and parameters for a PC5 unicast link are exchanged by PC5-S messages in the upper layers as specified in TS 33.536 [60], and apply to the corresponding PC5-RRC connection in the AS. Once AS security is activated for a PC5 unicast link in the upper layers as specified in TS 33.536 [60], all messages on SL-SRB2 and SL-SRB3 and/or user data on SL-DRBs of the corresponding PC5-RRC connection are integrity protected and/or ciphered by the PDCP.","paragraph_zero_based":595},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For unicast of NR sidelink communication, if the change of the key is indicated by the upper layers as specified in TS 24.587 [57] or TS 24.554 [72], UE re-establishes the PDCP entity of the SL-SRB1, SL-SRB2, SL-SRB3 and SL-DRBs on the corresponding PC5-RRC connection.","paragraph_zero_based":596},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:In case the configurations for NR sidelink communication are acquired via the E-UTRA, the configurations for NR sidelink communication in SIB12 and sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration used in clause 5.8 are provided by the configurations in SystemInformationBlockType28 and sl-ConfigDedicatedForNR within RRCConnectionReconfiguration as specified in TS 36.331 [10], respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":597},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:In this release, there is one-to-one correspondence between the PC5-RRC connection and the PC5 unicast link as specified in TS 38.300[2].","paragraph_zero_based":598},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 3:All SL-DRBs related to the same PC5-RRC connection have the same activation/deactivation setting for ciphering and the same activation/deactivation setting for integrity protection as specified in TS 33.536 [60].","paragraph_zero_based":599}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["50f4360817c92f28f73af3d62902d08dc5c4944eb77a2244b3a8a05c4acf14e3","7a6671c70112cdea72e7ff31a32f71ae9d2d41650712b1c7b6f9daada283514d","7db06047c222203546c51423faf50268fd685b0862571e58a95a3d1ab5a9d2c3","15f2bfcb16ce31e75911d28dfd0168821685afc7ff48b92e0304af50e1a1e175","7c186013a836a72af50a570715e34d75f27e83adaa495a39bb2894536ce5fd82","b11719577ece28d803ba774b206f64b9108a8e1069fadc12f52d305a61256d53","4c4e905258c3b80854ef96f7e802d6a99c13f658f73855fe44b4b58cdd81bd18","586f94f0efe162dc4a0a74483cefcb88c56e2fafec58807ee71077ae43a2cc11","7576d95f8e54d0dff451528d57303fb9bdb87acae124caeeb51666bbabcc94f3","86a737d840399d7204a7d43be1b807180cb7e96f9a54f77ea67b4859908491ea","8ba6d0c48fc55b819306a17a68257db9fe8b7f6da863a1686648faeb5ed48bb2","acbe959b5e9e1755e0c7b6269bb9bd45203052f8dc0335daa3c367284c5997eb","02c07aa256c07bddcaf17341144e62772f85c70e49ac10725cf3a023bcd9a7d2","49b260cd38d578ef75fdba4c420521c424cef4193f4f8a6b604d266b146a54eb","7da773f83df2fb2ded3689ba457cf57fce1bc1b291805e2ac66f0f1e8bad0b78","e20187db5325a7ef742a4923bf34016c2aec81d307fa9e2d1f027fbfd7582e63","1f5385da0563ee3192839a1ef27ccc70c5cb411d38e3d9e7352f4b10ad78f59c","065facd5ed6cf647c7993370cc3c81a6d972a25de3a7d30645f9035212301fd8","4872f5284ef43b7c2a39cc74bf0a2676b0c644dad2a002f8cde8f74ff5085bf2","7dec34f48ee5eee89b72658d4223223485c5096e10cbbeb197bc5971d96734ae","05161900fbb9d957d9745e48151997c85b39773c993bdd1f32ce94322bef6deb","f6956ef2ed6f992837a2326109b4e2de2e2fe4756c85336b7ac1fe677e65e099","18df289c58e2a889f60669a5543192c8c0c1ff54a4d584fb629b00ff85f0afc6","b1e05dfb2fe28e26ba6be2aaea2a8ca1d5cf04e6750d80e35e3f76cb44fab557"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[576,599],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p576"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 4:When integrity check failure concerning SL-SRB1 for a specific destination is detected, the UE sends an indication to the upper layers [57].","paragraph_zero_based":600},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 5:The selection of NULL algorithms means that the PC5 messages are considered protected for the purposes of being allowed to be sent or received.","paragraph_zero_based":601},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.2Conditions for NR sidelink communication/discovery operation","paragraph_zero_based":602},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall perform NR sidelink communication operation only if the conditions defined in this clause are met:","paragraph_zero_based":603},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE's serving cell is suitable (RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE or RRC_CONNECTED); and if either the selected cell on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery operation belongs to the registered or equivalent PLMN as specified in TS 24.587 [57] or TS 24.554 [72] or the UE is out of coverage on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery operation as defined in TS 38.304 [20] and TS 36.304 [27]; or","paragraph_zero_based":604},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE's serving cell (RRC_IDLE or RRC_CONNECTED) fulfils the conditions to support NR sidelink communication/discovery in limited service state as specified in TS 23.287 [55]; and if either the serving cell is on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery operation or the UE is out of coverage on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery operation as defined in TS 38.304 [20] and TS 36.304 [27]; or","paragraph_zero_based":605},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE has no serving cell (RRC_IDLE).","paragraph_zero_based":606},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.3Sidelink UE information for NR sidelink communication/discovery","paragraph_zero_based":607},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.3.1General","paragraph_zero_based":608},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":609},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.3.1-1: Sidelink UE information for NR sidelink communication/discovery","paragraph_zero_based":610},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to inform the network that the UE:","paragraph_zero_based":611},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is interested or no longer interested to receive or transmit NR sidelink communication/discovery,","paragraph_zero_based":612},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is requesting assignment or release of transmission resource for NR sidelink communication/discovery,","paragraph_zero_based":613},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting QoS parameters and QoS profile(s) related to NR sidelink communication,","paragraph_zero_based":614},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting that a sidelink radio link failure or sidelink RRC reconfiguration failure has been detected,","paragraph_zero_based":615},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting the sidelink UE capability information of the associated peer UE for unicast communication,","paragraph_zero_based":616},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting the RLC mode information of the sidelink data radio bearer(s) received from the associated peer UE for unicast communication,","paragraph_zero_based":617},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting the accepted sidelink DRX configuration received from the associated peer UE for NR sidelink unicast reception,","paragraph_zero_based":618},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting the sidelink DRX assistance information received from the associated peer UE for NR sidelink unicast transmission, when the UE is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig,","paragraph_zero_based":619},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting, for NR sidelink groupcast transmission, the sidelink DRX on/off indication for the associated Destination Layer-2 ID, when the UE is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig,","paragraph_zero_based":620},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting, for NR sidelink groupcast or broadcast reception, the Destination Layer-2 ID and QoS profile(s) associated with its interested services to which sidelink DRX is applied,","paragraph_zero_based":621},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting DRX configuration reject information from its associated peer UE for NR sidelink unicast transmission, when the UE is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig,","paragraph_zero_based":622},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-is reporting parameters related to U2N relay operation,","paragraph_zero_based":623}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["a86deec051bfc2651df1aa74f35f0e4632087088f12eb4e2db190b54d3346e51","6604c79bd92c4ef9b5b0ae4d76bdefa94757d0eac5a2f1a88d7629f2f604d6f1","72fdb223696087a1849ae73d3dbe610d35e7fe1fbf2d4a8c77cc960d690d0b55","55a503cb657b35282096c35b4e6a57dfffb2efc87d50a4edcd202acd47f14b30","03eebb9ece53bf5cbcacbd6b39930693476a92053a4b8ad35a3e41c28c60eef5","4b21890c34fb703cacf55ce88d259682558d39e1f1cc37a4463ef152e3c3358b","740eff43fd0e3561eda049029a6baa916ce8ec16369656ce5cc406c33e3f836e","04380cb8a43145338ea408f811845c0bb52f24875398321cc83e707274b0af86","e9ef315d9d415a2c76e60e5aabc737ff664b7576d15c8ef068ab9f5b36e78746","e7f8fb195275a4aaec1d17bbd2802f96fdd1ba0b2eab780c70c7a28f65d77426","c5730adf89573e05741ea1a18e4217d57a407ccb1735c5abf137ff603102affc","6d90229b4878ab05bd235432843d17210b7ba6f262244c7d32c883db1d3a9b6e","0c6534cf857ddd9113107ae6b6b279be5b364167e99e51e746051b19199dbb42","ef06a948810ba7836f6f73a515fe1012eeb5a87b296dacf8c4e725acb4354bfa","06178d77806138ee3a8ef19f8319b14ece47e8054deee26230308978b35c7e59","451ca15cb689161e6c8d4a5320373438550378dff2e9eb7b48a4940c4e8596a3","d11e621f7b6c3a1546de543ee299a5d370036c397453adeaad7b656f99f7b831","668806fa8950044236705288ec568f12933d246b2046976add059686541df54c","ed50c23a99be88f951504c3965aa61035ac05b171972b62b17a27cc207d114e1","caa6d2cadfac45ce01f7155ee981e5f7056f1eda1407b5d4408df55306581a31","ed7daea178331e17025f3db1e1df6ea1d0553761f2b0a6e0a1923e57642bade6","8491d3ee2b699fabe91217d0bc804090193f31d169ea683e24b09ec29ffd3d8e","e17844528f0f90946821b478a54aa2b28bdfba37ce0830b0182f45c9af80e3cf","741ccea4d461ed8fc9e6213374a33b715ae40e77c62220c7c50be0a70014179a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[600,623],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p600"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Editor Note:FFS stage 3 impact to message formats (e.g., additional fields) for an RRC_CONNECTED U2U relay/remote UE.","paragraph_zero_based":624},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.3.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":625},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink communication or NR sidelink discovery or NR sidelink U2N relay operation that is in RRC_CONNECTED may initiate the procedure to indicate it is (interested in) receiving or transmitting NR sidelink communication or NR sidelink discovery or NR sidelink U2N relay operation in several cases including upon successful connection establishment or resuming, upon change of interest, upon changing QoS profile(s), upon receiving UECapabilityInformationSidelink from the associated peer UE, upon RLC mode information updated from the associated peer UE or upon change to a PCell providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR. A UE capable of NR sidelink communication may initiate the procedure to request assignment of dedicated sidelink DRB configuration and transmission resources for NR sidelink communication transmission. A UE capable of NR sidelink communication may initiate the procedure to report to the network that a sidelink radio link failure or sidelink RRC reconfiguration failure has been declared. A UE capable of NR sidelink discovery may initiate the procedure to request assignment of dedicated resources for NR sidelink discovery transmission or NR sidelink discovery reception. A UE capable of U2N relay operation may initiate the procedure to report/update parameters for acting as U2N Relay UE or U2N Remote UE (including L2 Remote UE's source L2 ID).","paragraph_zero_based":626},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink operation that is in RRC_CONNECTED may initiate the procedure to report the sidelink DRX configuration received from the associated peer UE for NR sidelink unicast reception, upon accepting the sidelink DRX configuration from the associated peer UE. A UE capable of NR sidelink communication that is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig and is performing sidelink unicast transmission may initiate the procedure to report the sidelink DRX assistance information or the sidelink DRX configuration reject information received from the associated peer UE, upon receiving either of them from the associated peer UE. A UE capable of NR sidelink communication that is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig and is performing sidelink groupcast transmission may initiate the procedure to report the sidelink DRX on/off indication for the associated Destination Layer-2 ID.","paragraph_zero_based":627},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink operation that is in RRC_CONNECTED may initiate the procedure to report the Destination Layer-2 ID and QoS profile(s) associated with its interested service(s) that sidelink DRX is applied, for NR sidelink groupcast or broadcast reception.","paragraph_zero_based":628},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon initiating this procedure, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":629},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR is provided by the PCell:","paragraph_zero_based":630},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>ensure having a valid version of SIB12 for the PCell;","paragraph_zero_based":631},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layers to receive NR sidelink communication on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell:","paragraph_zero_based":632},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE did not transmit a SidelinkUEInformationNR message since last entering RRC_CONNECTED state; or","paragraph_zero_based":633},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if since the last time the UE transmitted a SidelinkUEInformationNR message the UE connected to a PCell not providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR; or","paragraph_zero_based":634},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message did not include sl-RxInterestedFreqList; or if the frequency configured by upper layers to receive NR sidelink communication on has changed since the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message:","paragraph_zero_based":635},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate the NR sidelink communication reception frequency of interest in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":636},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":637},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message included sl-RxInterestedFreqList:","paragraph_zero_based":638},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate it is no longer interested in NR sidelink communication reception in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":639},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layers to transmit non-relay NR sidelink communication on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell:","paragraph_zero_based":640},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE did not transmit a SidelinkUEInformationNR message since last entering RRC_CONNECTED state; or","paragraph_zero_based":641},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if since the last time the UE transmitted a SidelinkUEInformationNR message the UE connected to a PCell not providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR; or","paragraph_zero_based":642},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message did not include sl-TxResourceReqList; or if the information carried by the sl-TxResourceReqList has changed since the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message:","paragraph_zero_based":643},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate the NR sidelink communication transmission resources required by the UE in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":644},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":645},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message included sl-TxResourceReqList:","paragraph_zero_based":646},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate it no longer requires NR sidelink communication transmission resources in accordance with 5.8.3.3.","paragraph_zero_based":647}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["b5870f3d39ef62e331b144e07fbf5dc8164265232dbacea7d1693e23e5f0e0bc","82344baadd46254e59e290fa5633b6c4f0b6eebd92a4b9a69bcd9a8c68938399","411b94b546507beaa964d02f62d2702d919fee8600e3d162bc53e7319fb07a35","55c3933604a578c64af7e8343e4bd07f400e791b6a4f315c3f9bd6c35f894244","058b82e231339eff0c59faeb42e99b0e3b7ce462bb00549b7f34952d2a05776b","3c0515a23c11945d0e710362ce6fefad9dc56940cfdcc96ccc784d0efd41c5ad","eca80206215980834afaecd8ad22356f3a9717268160d1b650410ac0584234a4","e4cfc68b7c5ef69d289bb10880e1957fe5a51813058efe94eff2e3935ce6bf89","3b09da209ec6567383adb43816aacb0a52080bad64685fcde3c28d10d3fc07b3","a70e06568fd29cb03764aa396a07b28e43417360413714a9633e363399c592ce","5702d8b9ec3766d94a19fe7e04b49a62c25faf68547d998039dcfd42f2cf584a","9174630cf780d8285622cbfd388e7a1a4858ea7197f9ed5f3f54e3a1f96c4a25","126dfeddbf41c79dfc831c2f233a4604bba316ffd7c82c3266be019b526a249a","4225594d25935d2b065009c36679a863e71dc0ffb144892f2aa5c2f4621dcee3","5548c11bb7076d5aab394a5e407a6de07d25a5a3966811d875a5a2e7b38cbdfc","f6b88185859373cbbcbe1d83820c2d66b95bcee131c49877eeee2d590ff6eb3a","592088572b558e944dff65858e3c0b95a84f4041761db83069fa9e436250dfa3","18ab3f33018c4123d7a825995a9181d2c8981d67bcd510f6bbce3f81eb9736de","d33148c53e6dbb6a77bc4090096c01a86fdc1c38441ee743763db763d207612a","c40a5660d78c7d9ffc257efef6b8db995d674551e8530f57e26a912c159eb6b2","7b566abdb2d10d37e5566b3a9d81063ff01b236ac13ba83f5e1f10fd2579c641","9545f2c2c67f73bcb90ed303321cc46997ff601b904085628c4482914bdaadbb","4c7a0555d10c775b776708d980c5fc5477f6ff1f9aac5ffdb4582a8f725a0aa4","cf970025a758b2a2c80686dccacccb9961d94e8274ddb01b5e43aedb4ad95453"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[624,647],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p624"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layer to receive NR sidelink non-relay discovery messages on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell including sl-NonRelayDiscovery:","paragraph_zero_based":648},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE did not transmit a SidelinkUEInformationNR message since last entering RRC_CONNECTED state; or","paragraph_zero_based":649},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if since the last time the UE transmitted a SidelinkUEInformationNR message the UE connected to a PCell not providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR or connected to a PCell providing SIB12 but not including sl-NonRelayDiscovery; or","paragraph_zero_based":650},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message did not include sl-RxInterestedFreqListDisc; or if the frequency configured by upper layers to receive NR sidelink non-relay discovery messages on has changed since the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message:","paragraph_zero_based":651},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate the NR sidelink discovery reception frequency of interest in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":652},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":653},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message included sl-RxInterestedFreqListDisc:","paragraph_zero_based":654},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate it is no longer interested in NR sidelink non-relay discovery messages reception in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":655},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layer to receive NR sidelink L2 U2N relay discovery messages on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell including sl-L2U2N-Relay; or if configured by upper layer to receive NR sidelink L3 U2N relay discovery messages on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell including sl-L3U2N-RelayDiscovery:","paragraph_zero_based":656},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE did not transmit a SidelinkUEInformationNR message since last entering RRC_CONNECTED state; or","paragraph_zero_based":657},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if since the last time the UE transmitted a SidelinkUEInformationNR message the UE connected to a PCell not providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR; or connected to a PCell providing SIB12 but not including sl-L2U2N-Relay in case of L2 U2N relay operation; or connected to a PCell providing SIB12 but not including sl-L3U2N-RelayDiscovery in case of L3 U2N relay operation; or","paragraph_zero_based":658},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message did not include sl-RxInterestedFreqListDisc; or if the frequency configured by upper layers to receive NR sidelink discovery messages on has changed since the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message:","paragraph_zero_based":659},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the UE is capable of U2N Relay UE, and if SIB12 includes sl-RelayUE-ConfigCommon; or","paragraph_zero_based":660},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the UE is selecting a U2N Relay UE / has a selected U2N Relay UE / configured with measurement object associated to L2 U2N Relay UEs, and if SIB12 includes sl-RemoteUE-ConfigCommon:","paragraph_zero_based":661},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate the NR relay sidelink discovery reception frequency of interest in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":662},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":663},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message included sl-RxInterestedFreqListDisc:","paragraph_zero_based":664},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate it is no longer interested in NR relay sidelink discovery messages reception in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":665},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if configured by upper layer to transmit NR sidelink non-relay discovery messages on the frequency included in sl-FreqInfoList in SIB12 of the PCell including sl-NonRelayDiscovery:","paragraph_zero_based":666},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE did not transmit a SidelinkUEInformationNR message since last entering RRC_CONNECTED state; or","paragraph_zero_based":667},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if since the last time the UE transmitted a SidelinkUEInformationNR message the UE connected to a PCell not providing SIB12 including sl-ConfigCommonNR or connected to a PCell providing SIB12 but not including sl-NonRelayDiscovery; or","paragraph_zero_based":668},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message did not include sl-TxResourceReqListDisc; or if the information carried by the sl-TxResourceReqListDisc has changed since the last transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message:","paragraph_zero_based":669},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to indicate the NR sidelink non-relay discovery messages resources required by the UE in accordance with 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":670},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":671}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c