{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-DestinationIdentityL2U2N to the destination identity configured by upper layer for NR sidelink L2 U2N relay communication transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":768},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-TxInterestedFreqListL2U2N to indicate the frequency of the associated destination for NR sidelink L2 U2N relay communication transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":769},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-TypeTxSyncListL2U2N to the current synchronization reference type used on the associated sl-InterestedFreqListL2U2N for NR sidelink L2 U2N relay communication transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":770},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-LocalID-Request to request local ID for L2 U2N Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":771},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-PagingIdentityRemoteUE to the paging UE ID received from peer L2 U2N Remote UE, if it is not released as in 5.8.9.8.3;","paragraph_zero_based":772},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-CapabilityInformationSidelink to include UECapabilityInformationSidelink message, if any, received from peer UE.","paragraph_zero_based":773},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>include ue-Type and set it to relayUE;","paragraph_zero_based":774},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if SIB12 including sl-L2U2N-Relay and if configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink L2 U2N relay communication and the UE has a selected L2 U2N Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":775},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>include sl-TxResourceReqL2U2N-Relay in sl-TxResourceReqListCommRelay and set its fields (if needed) as follows to request network to assign NR sidelink L2 U2N relay communication resource:","paragraph_zero_based":776},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-TxInterestedFreqListL2U2N to indicate the frequency of the associated destination for NR sidelink L2 U2N relay communication transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":777},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-TypeTxSyncListL2U2N to the current synchronization reference type used on the associated sl-InterestedFreqListL2U2N for NR sidelink L2 U2N relay communication transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":778},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-CapabilityInformationSidelink to include UECapabilityInformationSidelink message, if any, received from peer UE.","paragraph_zero_based":779},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>include ue-Type and set it to remoteUE;","paragraph_zero_based":780},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if SIB12 including sl-L3U2N-RelayDiscovery and if configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication:","paragraph_zero_based":781},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>include sl-TxResourceReqL3U2N-Relay in sl-TxResourceReqListCommRelay and set its fields (if needed) as follows for each destination for which it requests network to assign NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication resource:","paragraph_zero_based":782},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-DestinationIdentity to the destination identity configured by upper layer for NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":783},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-CastType to the cast type of the associated destination identity configured by the upper layer for the NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":784},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-RLC-ModeIndication to include the RLC mode(s) and optionally QoS profile(s) of the sidelink QoS flow(s) of the associated RLC mode(s), if the associated bi-directional sidelink DRB has been established due to the configuration by RRCReconfigurationSidelink;","paragraph_zero_based":785},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-QoS-InfoList to include QoS profile(s) of the sidelink QoS flow(s) of the associated destination configured by the upper layer for the NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":786},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-TxInterestedFreqList to indicate the frequency of the associated destination for NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":787},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-TypeTxSyncList to the current synchronization reference type used on the associated sl-InterestedFreqList for NR sidelink L3 U2N relay communication transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":788},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>set sl-CapabilityInformationSidelink to include UECapabilityInformationSidelink message, if any, received from peer UE.","paragraph_zero_based":789},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>include ue-Type and set it to relayUE if the UE is acting as NR sidelink L3 U2N Relay UE or to remoteUE otherwise;","paragraph_zero_based":790},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if sl-DRX-ConfigCommonGC-BC is included in SIB12-IEs:","paragraph_zero_based":791}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["24b6a3b622f51416071263517c678e0aafba6ff7605ee69ae5f0e4a5aa4d54eb","37bcd3e4315fd16bc26f764892daf26be6d21a0d39827fdf8309c37b5c66f80f","3a0d78c1faf937af4d2fddbfac4af5f82371c6f98461d8ca00f2d6e8622feec6","f981d189a58f012915df09c000db69368c71aa3af31bebdb3be22f0d896bc6ae","f18b8daec5048f20b041ddb42877dd6138400409696a493563326c0424ce9313","25cdcab5cd169d5dfd464102ebd31256558946fd635f8a0db000f31d7cac85e2","8148b09987ad7dfe76c800aa21705ce1715caae0160f832c705805ac07dee0ff","9ba638d5bdc47c925097e8b5b048d80cdb506df7c6092df52a792cdfb5fee7b7","bb1757c1d7d6c5a2a24bf8ae4fe0b1b30dbaf5b84bdc4b578d487af9f5b0cf8e","a768a404dc8e84e3690fb6e3c1ac8dd37394f021c02741acd19a4abd729a14ed","a4a504b3623bb32d5f0973cfde5e8b8809ee48ea00f0c0cb3c308e5361abb210","7b04450cbdb72e2ebedfc25a6e465f376ce65d5fdf70db1e8e2bca0ac52301dd","3095c1591a55d348be22ecf525b053a909d983553a31248444e27c4a5afd2955","06f50738aca14927fb64b6791d09ad1e7a137e50550758d43ff964b4252ad438","fb32af6facab5d5c2810e9d6a1eeb683115920bc74374a98fc8c61ecadd4c6fd","7a01b79ddbac1bcf3ac246689feb4c388454f5983144f54eb7a2300a8e1ea8d4","0a4a2928f3d89d83a4669560442c2b044a1b52efc32a3c4f4e8fe0b649a0027d","c4c7708eeebf746760956349fd6b158ae3281e340a1bbb2c75565b8acfb72876","025e689dce46e27667274d4e8ce9d11df67e469589b4f3b3cb5da20939dac01b","c4a9d0001ff849e7d700d8c23802f6bdc87e7b6ccfa1e0c2c8d5434477bc1597","1c8e80734def8546946cb1ca1c4d1e3377b5d9d840c5e80bb8855355d8a4e0b4","1e6ff76e4192fda9b8be3da6fa97f73f5f785fc37c8d6304eaa4a395123e7295","57707c27debe55bfe062b71e0d05e0f8c29b4e857f8f50d15af6d3330dcdfb9d","ac562bf139342ed8b6dcd05b756c03844eec7c114abe508a3a60b04b78874173"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[768,791],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p768"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if configured by upper layers to perform NR sidelink reception:","paragraph_zero_based":792},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>include sl-RxDRX-ReportList and set its fields (if needed) as follows for each destination for which it reports to network:","paragraph_zero_based":793},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>set sl-DRX-ConfigFromTx to include the accepted sidelink DRX configuration of the associated destination for NR sidelink unicast communication, if received from the associated peer UE;","paragraph_zero_based":794},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>include sl-RxInterestedGC-BC-DestList and set its fields (if needed) as follows for each Destination Layer-2 ID for which it reports to network:","paragraph_zero_based":795},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>set sl-RxInterestedQoS-InfoList to include the QoS profile of its interested service(s) that sidelink DRX is applied for the associated destination for NR sidelink groupcast or broadcast reception;","paragraph_zero_based":796},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:It is up to UE implementation to set the QoS profile in sl-RxInterestedQoS-InfoList for reception of NR sidelink discovery message or ProSe Direct Link Establishment Request message as described in TS 24.554 [72], or for reception of Direct Link Establishment Request message as described in TS 24.587 [57].","paragraph_zero_based":797},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>set sl-DestinationIdentity to the associated destination identity configured by upper layer for NR sidelink groupcast or broadcast reception;","paragraph_zero_based":798},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if configured by upper layers to perform NR sidelink transmission and configured with sl-ScheduledConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":799},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>include sl-TxResourceReqList and/or sl-TxResourceReqListCommRelay and set its fields (if needed) as follows for each destination for which it reports to network:","paragraph_zero_based":800},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>set sl-DRX-InfoFromRxList to include the sidelink DRX assistance information of the associated destination, if any, received from the associated peer UE;","paragraph_zero_based":801},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>if the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message includes the sl-DRX-ConfigReject:","paragraph_zero_based":802},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7>set sl-Failure as drxReject-v1710 for the associated destination for the NR sidelink communication transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":803},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>set sl-DRX-Indication to include the sidelink DRX on/off indication for the associated destination for NR sidelink groupcast transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":804},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE initiates the procedure while connected to an E-UTRA PCell:","paragraph_zero_based":805},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>submit the SidelinkUEInformationNR to lower layers via SRB1, embedded in E-UTRA RRC message ULInformationTransferIRAT as specified in TS 36.331 [10], clause 5.6.28;","paragraph_zero_based":806},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":807},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>submit the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to lower layers for transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":808},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.4Void","paragraph_zero_based":809},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.5Sidelink synchronisation information transmission for NR sidelink communication/discovery","paragraph_zero_based":810},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.5.1General","paragraph_zero_based":811},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":812},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.5.1-1: Synchronisation information transmission for NR sidelink communication/discovery, in (partial) coverage","paragraph_zero_based":813},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":814},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.5.1-2: Synchronisation information transmission for NR sidelink communication/discovery, out of coverage","paragraph_zero_based":815}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["00248aef8b52f484e6cd595c34b80f1328fa74c07fb52573866066bd8459f8c4","21359126701c42403b0743aaf293d29031169987e6bd8f6903063907428aa176","2f96b713a079b0622c3b9ea929f717fe507ac97c264605b352a475d4b979b2eb","3637da021c4ec46e61f0f93c81fd1ec9a573873078492613a664ed89ecf4ae6f","2d80a2a7a8d6563b97607a15cdcf5cac58077264304c6996e8de1a52ab4d7c6b","423672c6aed3e9892d0e32ef34d19b0e3c32ee436b7a8d6c9a142680e87c0a23","9efc82723d765dc59fab39f8c2039be099e717d51364ba6d6246ac4de3898dea","f97076e2fa63934996e90abea024837563dcaebb7fbb4e5c4daaf8fbe62f6124","826bded14fc18ed21a054c5ff5a9b673498a4f9437d377bca970f214d564b1f3","6fc52892b5f6dbcbbe6960b753a659010c6a4ab21ed4599eb9b84a5100f10339","876e5e5fb8eb285bdc189fa9ec28a98f28689f990245821b5661484c3137156b","1afebf0d4ef8b18a6c0b7ad72c61ff7a1469e879f59d950b2cf6fcb052f57552","9f50c7e83c098b6a0654fb9b75d3413d903331b4f6e52d697c84b08ecc99ba16","c067f08ee648795ede62e99cb9be7fbe01387a54eac54840827bd79b89c663ae","02ba2a99f01f889ba0b8928137db420391a7faba3f4e6508591efbb68ad9fdc2","2c7073abf311c5810fe1293ae172c8235ba23ecede2dfdb08b0eba1b0a5d7f8d","e56791bf9c7b750fb5a3d31321ca9464d6fe682afb2dab0f5ed8d50731b33bf7","98409b14e9fa13c40603743fa5bbecd347e5050258f84afd0fdb78566268ba4d","51bc21750cba5d658de54fbe42833b884e6d93f11898d6e8ddfdddfddf8578be","3e9880e7adb3c928bee11e794e1d8fad97518a10fd137de56973b926778d42b3","53219ec11cf8e8e0859e4d8bf238adbbb042905abab717098bd9945ce87e9e11","b8ac6fabed093b719888eb973f92456658eeadc4fd9d15bdacb23f12453f7f01","ec9c345a697032e5a7554d41be11b5c5f22c6d5ed36d0ea9ed56943929b628f3","9d97cae4401107f83460aba66783d854e1137a5eff59705b50f0517e613d6129"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[792,815],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p792"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to provide synchronisation information to a UE. This procedure also applies to NR sidelink discovery.","paragraph_zero_based":816},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.5.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":817},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink communication/discovery and SLSS/PSBCH transmission shall, when transmitting NR sidelink communication/discovery, and if the conditions for NR sidelink communication/discovery operation are met and when the following conditions are met:","paragraph_zero_based":818},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if in coverage on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery, as defined in TS 38.304 [20]; and has selected GNSS or the cell as synchronization reference as defined in 5.8.6.3; or","paragraph_zero_based":819},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if out of coverage on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery, and the frequency used to transmit NR sidelink communication/discovery is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message or included in sl-FreqInfoList within SIB12; and has selected GNSS or the cell as synchronization reference as defined in 5.8.6.3:","paragraph_zero_based":820},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if in RRC_CONNECTED; and if networkControlledSyncTx is configured and set to on; or","paragraph_zero_based":821},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if networkControlledSyncTx is not configured; and for the concerned frequency syncTxThreshIC is configured; and the RSRP measurement of the reference cell, selected as defined in 5.8.6.3, for NR sidelink communication/discovery transmission is below the value of syncTxThreshIC:","paragraph_zero_based":822},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>transmit sidelink SSB on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery in accordance with 5.8.5.3 and TS 38.211 [16], including the transmission of SLSS as specified in 5.8.5.3 and transmission of MasterInformationBlockSidelink as specified in 5.8.9.4.3;","paragraph_zero_based":823},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":824},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery, if syncTxThreshOoC is included in SidelinkPreconfigNR; and the UE is not directly synchronized to GNSS, and the UE has no selected SyncRef UE or the PSBCH-RSRP measurement result of the selected SyncRef UE is below the value of syncTxThreshOoC; or","paragraph_zero_based":825},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery, if the UE selects GNSS as the synchronization reference source:","paragraph_zero_based":826},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>transmit sidelink SSB on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery in accordance with TS 38.211 [16] , including the transmission of SLSS as specified in 5.8.5.3 and transmission of MasterInformationBlockSidelink as specified in 5.8.9.4.3;","paragraph_zero_based":827},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.5.3Transmission of SLSS","paragraph_zero_based":828},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall select the SLSSID and the slot in which to transmit SLSS as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":829},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if triggered by NR sidelink communication/discovery and in coverage on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery, as defined in TS 38.304 [20]; or","paragraph_zero_based":830},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if triggered by NR sidelink communication/discovery, and out of coverage on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery, and the concerned frequency is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message or included in sl-FreqInfoList within SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":831},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has selected GNSS as synchronization reference in accordance with 5.8.6.2:","paragraph_zero_based":832},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select SLSSID 0;","paragraph_zero_based":833},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>use sl-SSB-TimeAllocation1 included in the entry of configured sl-SyncConfigList corresponding to the concerned frequency, that includes txParameters and gnss-Sync;","paragraph_zero_based":834},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select the slot(s) indicated by sl-SSB-TimeAllocation1;","paragraph_zero_based":835},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has selected a cell as synchronization reference in accordance with 5.8.6.2:","paragraph_zero_based":836},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select the SLSSID included in the entry of configured sl-SyncConfigList corresponding to the concerned frequency, that includes txParameters and does not include gnss-Sync;","paragraph_zero_based":837},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select the slot(s) indicated by sl-SSB-TimeAllocation1;","paragraph_zero_based":838},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if triggered by NR sidelink communication/discovery and the UE has GNSS as the synchronization reference:","paragraph_zero_based":839}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["04c84769070a0fd1b2b5fe9d88397ae35650c9d10d37a0781ded942976866619","d9031db5b748568827f5fa709ddb7ccf5d2145744b8bbfb33e7649d63b9a0212","df953712e1cdb3eabbd286a8bde8903274c966300921f88b57b5ed158cd30139","31b3fa602fead4955121e585d79d8dd8975d7e3ed9c68afa321a98efa3d75acb","09162cf7eb503b8f333338a27a6e2455e4a49eb0d5d06ff07bce85a5ca38d03d","5810eb1f6fefdbeff727c286c7884becfcef18df676e9fc6a53ccc2605912a09","16a12df69ac7cb0d5576c00b063808d84fea6694eecd478938fe861445807247","e52ac1f8902590e64673e6a47c35294ad65a8ed99b32efcf64d0c70de6958c65","847ba3e17d0deaf816462e6327a3c9876f1a57c6c4eb47c16ea2ec08320b82c0","c07d610e5abbdb60b0139880e544396340af4fad2419009e4a9fa646e02054cd","ee85a38fb88f1f9c6bf17cef3df0a3dd8dce2c80b43aab9024607216e10a1a6e","9582ccf50278f7107fbcb717183186469964ae9820cb1b028317d133bcef0b22","aa02efb14a0247a3671794ce229d096b20b807cede44221da06a38950fc75e71","ec6a3dc079c204cf10d3b7da1d80908cc29a63a8ef5b2626717261898b3bfdf4","68146815d972134ca0fa7bb8ea239f0dc55b7f6a43a82ddb7483a9b1cd995386","978cbe6760ee9a73da381a86552e6325539874b072e981867767ef2feec268e5","a83a57b33fc5c99e55106e65139baa54fe313fb5cc419d633af276182b48551c","646fe16a4b7e5af3a4b423b45a3d829e442fc9d427b0cdfc88fa0cef25001a97","0f8c6f5bf2abebfbd004b991433b93b6656e21930dbd723f69f9971534212b14","682233e83cf3d58fd63fbaf0e3641983a01a37f2b81ea8bcce14fb06a368881e","a98948979eaf79caf47b6116a52ff7a9f8cba2126f62da052b79ac8fcb8d7bec","f021f700125af593ea1b0fceca55ccf504201dd08c68657208fb7063bab1a269","e47359231fafb40921aaa0624080504ebaada753f104e5b2acdb9838c624ba6e","f7f0ca488f70d8e5af09f0ea2d076aa68f564da4f7eef23862a651bd7839626c"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[816,839],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p816"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>select SLSSID 0;","paragraph_zero_based":840},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if sl-SSB-TimeAllocation3 is configured for the frequency used in SidelinkPreconfigNR:","paragraph_zero_based":841},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select the slot(s) indicated by sl-SSB-TimeAllocation3;","paragraph_zero_based":842},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":843},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select the slot(s) indicated by sl-SSB-TimeAllocation1;","paragraph_zero_based":844},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":845},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>select the synchronisation reference UE (i.e. SyncRef UE) as defined in 5.8.6;","paragraph_zero_based":846},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has a selected SyncRef UE and inCoverage in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE is set to true; or","paragraph_zero_based":847},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has a selected SyncRef UE and inCoverage in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE is set to false while the SLSS from this UE is part of the set defined for out of coverage, see TS 38.211 [16]:","paragraph_zero_based":848},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select the same SLSSID as the SLSSID of the selected SyncRef UE;","paragraph_zero_based":849},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select the slot in which to transmit the SLSS according to the sl-SSB-TimeAllocation1 or sl-SSB-TimeAllocation2 included in the preconfigured sidelink parameters corresponding to the concerned frequency, such that the timing is different from the SLSS of the selected SyncRef UE;","paragraph_zero_based":850},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the UE has a selected SyncRef UE and the SLSS from this UE was transmitted on the slot(s) indicated sl-SSB-TimeAllocation3, which is configured for the frequency used in SidelinkPreconfigNR:","paragraph_zero_based":851},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select SLSSID 337;","paragraph_zero_based":852},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select the slot(s) indicated by sl-SSB-TimeAllocation2;","paragraph_zero_based":853},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the UE has a selected SyncRef UE:","paragraph_zero_based":854},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select the SLSSID from the set defined for out of coverage having an index that is 336 more than the index of the SLSSID of the selected SyncRef UE, see TS 38.211 [16];","paragraph_zero_based":855},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>select the slot in which to transmit the SLSS according to sl-SSB-TimeAllocation1 or sl-SSB-TimeAllocation2 included in the preconfigured sidelink parameters corresponding to the concerned frequency, such that the timing is different from the SLSS of the selected SyncRef UE;","paragraph_zero_based":856},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else (i.e. no SyncRef UE selected):","paragraph_zero_based":857},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE has not randomly selected an SLSSID:","paragraph_zero_based":858},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>randomly select, using a uniform distribution, an SLSSID from the set of sequences defined for out of coverage except SLSSID 336 and 337, see TS 38.211 [16];","paragraph_zero_based":859},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>select the slot in which to transmit the SLSS according to the sl-SSB-TimeAllocation1 or sl-SSB-TimeAllocation2 (arbitrary selection between these) included in the preconfigured sidelink parameters in SidelinkPreconfigNR corresponding to the concerned frequency;","paragraph_zero_based":860},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.5aSidelink synchronisation information transmission for V2X sidelink communication","paragraph_zero_based":861},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.5a.1General","paragraph_zero_based":862},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":863}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["11bf6f61fcd2f8d6995ee7ce2582b61238b8dd943cde99394c16be17ed222917","54e4ef3010b983ec65b8793bd1c23d1da97e62ec993b44ce6a0be7359cdcf284","6482dc9982619aa8facef1b35b922a04be5b2e0758cbbbe8cbdff47c2e4e9c9a","0985b0622338d6ee3f02c4656a409ee102aed2253a6f09b2dc837f98f9303b0c","12da4c6aac49e2d815c4005a3d4379aa01097671192c2b4f1824a952ba63697f","b3d3eb0edfe484819845c01a07b6e3bb5740e26600758f15dd54b5ae5e918721","435881a003af9d8dbf4dc7555bbeb8437eee70ef6c04671823c9caba07ec63e6","9fe2ae6ae36970ad226e97e6e5d55ac1559e71c7acecceef9040fe7c051c9374","0980e1f9531d67cf18c06859fffe7a5cf176d7f4c5249a513b13ec0d9393b110","27d349ec1f96964a59439f5ae383881620a7d2556cc8918ad8852441076f0922","7634f5c068b53fa51c7de156df63f59473ce378dd03e48687745a990ba6099d7","4dfaf0a5ccbdf438d40e3aa803ffd0f72541280fb836694fbed4aa9142ac0cf8","0be15d3b6830fa8776ab716a8cd9ccece94b6260d780d2511f08d2638632dada","e303d7a2cf0dde8bac405cbfb3258e940019c95000e544faafd600b5e5991aab","c4e239bce0573c5d8f26b8a09b2c5a78dbf75ca7a93447782264d0edd44b1b91","5790adba352695843bba0b96f1eb4240f125af131569c571ae164de80215f2c8","1fc56b696d05bd08ef819e3d2eb9fec32c061daca2085f57f476e6fea84803af","22c3539744009539e272b709113b6cc04757dea13a4cb35dd9f1a5fe0a4f7647","f8a60a5fd921c1f281891ac106646dfd6f16f533e3777cf41d9f796718fc1dcd","e5fd99e1ddb94e3bb63f39ab755d9927ecd8e43cf712cd9e2156cc699de0ab78","2d7cf3d9d70848b761786bebfe7d9cf2c34923c9ff67c81b0996f1561db6ce3d","837d258ec4ef7d795b375b319104f8801c1c64ac9d667ba33e91dfaba31ce1ed","e4c532599d0b27db5a05e09cb109028cf4816805642ae2c3a3ebf37b4857b630","989d44a5c729a573e0627a03bcf8d162437545477949e85ba3712a53255b4b02"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[840,863],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p840"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.5a.1-1: Synchronisation information transmission for V2X sidelink communication, in (partial) coverage","paragraph_zero_based":864},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":865},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.5a.1-2: Synchronisation information transmission for V2X sidelink communication, out of coverage","paragraph_zero_based":866},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to provide synchronisation information to a UE.","paragraph_zero_based":867},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.5a.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":868},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of V2X sidelink communication initiates the transmission of SLSS and MasterInformationBlock-SL-V2X according to the conditions and the procedures specified for V2X sidelink communication in clause 5.10.7 of TS 36.331 [10].","paragraph_zero_based":869},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1: When applying the procedure in this clause, SIB13 and SIB14 correspond to SystemInformationBlockType21 and SystemInformationBlockType26 specified in TS 36.331 [10] respectively","paragraph_zero_based":870},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.6Sidelink synchronisation reference","paragraph_zero_based":871},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.6.1General","paragraph_zero_based":872},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to select a synchronisation reference and used when transmitting NR sidelink communication/discovery. This procedure also applies to NR sidelink discovery.","paragraph_zero_based":873},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.6.2Selection and reselection of synchronisation reference","paragraph_zero_based":874},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":875},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message or included in sl-ConfigCommonNR within SIB12, and sl-SyncPriority is configured for the concerned frequency and set to gnbEnb:","paragraph_zero_based":876},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>select a cell as the synchronization reference source as defined in 5.8.6.3:","paragraph_zero_based":877},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:When an out of coverage L2 U2N Remote UE receives SIB12 with sl-SyncPriority set to gnbEnb, the L2 U2N Remote UE continues using the current synchronization source until higher priority synchronization source is found or the current synchronization source becomes unreliable.","paragraph_zero_based":878},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message or included in sl-ConfigCommonNR within SIB12, and sl-SyncPriority for the concerned frequency is not configured or is set to gnss, and GNSS is reliable in accordance with TS 38.101-1 [15] and TS 38.133 [14]:","paragraph_zero_based":879},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>select GNSS as the synchronization reference source;","paragraph_zero_based":880},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if the frequency used for NR sidelink communication/discovery is included in SL-PreconfigurationNR, and sl-SyncPriority in SidelinkPreconfigNR is set to gnss and GNSS is reliable in accordance with TS 38.101-1 [15] and TS 38.133 [14]:","paragraph_zero_based":881},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>select GNSS as the synchronization reference source;","paragraph_zero_based":882},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":883},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform a full search (i.e. covering all subframes and all possible SLSSIDs) to detect candidate SLSS, in accordance with TS 38.133 [14]","paragraph_zero_based":884},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>when evaluating the one or more detected SLSSIDs, apply layer 3 filtering as specified in 5.5.3.2 using the preconfigured sl-filterCoefficient, before using the PSBCH-RSRP measurement results;","paragraph_zero_based":885},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has selected a SyncRef UE:","paragraph_zero_based":886},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the PSBCH-RSRP of the strongest candidate SyncRef UE exceeds the minimum requirement TS 38.133 [14] by sl-SyncRefMinHyst and the strongest candidate SyncRef UE belongs to the same priority group as the current SyncRef UE and the PSBCH-RSRP of the strongest candidate SyncRef UE exceeds the PSBCH-RSRP of the current SyncRef UE by syncRefDiffHyst; or","paragraph_zero_based":887}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e5d3ef74f43784d29c592c10dde5733456373df889a9131c643be9b9e69d7b4d","e662e9f6ff7915656f80430ef2c0d89d84d6ec746e75d9148b0023e53fbdfd18","f4a21dbf5c42598ff98d9abd19d595de8cf9e43f96f6281c19749bd95ee1573a","d48b77fb00c978c7798a906e0c72574a6058ac127d82e52870cbdf94a7241c63","8b930612f5c85797e2396c9528ba0d66b00090de70224889a62cec5ca357dd5a","b7b754364a4f3472ac55f0d8bdd8686717a891e31f6d49a7b5f626f3cabe5260","04f143fa284579c9c96eb0a1d05e42404c1195bc65c9ea0278c954dc7264cb69","25aaa94030a3286fe193661eec4af80b92f35ee9dd436f17dcd75072a86aa18a","17bd8e9776cf8914c3f3cbc84021f002c40b05fa613e57dd43f41ffa9349b111","1fd108c733f5c92fa9fa8daa760bc14f47df63ccf29801a5643e95fb645732c5","2d3f280b6c5ada79d29706dd18e48d130108c82ef3fc57f79bf97f68b4cdbc36","e1b7aece43d5dd932f58c19f9cb6080917ca546b6cd09fb070382e4e78dbf2d9","d391d1282f3c3d9ff7b8322e5e13ffce3729bfb70c308cba488ecea4fda588f9","5981a6ad5fc2bf67cfd631b2499c70377eada84cb7bccf2be7f0c020942907a2","d9ffcde59b5742958836b0936dfceee03beef1597f53edce18dcc24974ba31dd","36314dc3944e7b5cfb84c92cbfa9e691c0fadfda1578acf9f22f12086135b630","872b1bc25c855f44b03ea94c71ac7ec5d9579f057c2374c68106eee37b66b16b","466f6ea86e51c4f25e560e2142d48a6c3302168331ef691ebf9a65f95087427c","e0800bfdebdc0605a2dcdb0afb008a9cec6b7b607fa872fe1585cf0d963ab031","14c601a2343bdb1aee315875d85e79ab0f3ad65bfb16f2a7d0d79bc0af602cb4","c664bede87bedd5510dae866246bc816fcf947cf1e10cd09b5e5f3a935f457bf","a8a10e9d37b279bf2111a4a82b5acc6a61a6cb6df107568d0d74fc3c55392d47","29688a4559535e2f3cb34f5eb21ab62df228f88fb68746298e5e59e45147e480","94cb493c23eaacd3a1319b42caeb590e2da81128ff8f6bb0b9afc1f9a8e9ddab"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[864,887],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p864"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the PSBCH-RSRP of the candidate SyncRef UE exceeds the minimum requirement TS 38.133 [14] by sl-SyncRefMinHyst and the candidate SyncRef UE belongs to a higher priority group than the current SyncRef UE; or","paragraph_zero_based":888},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if GNSS becomes reliable in accordance with TS 38.101-1 [15] and TS 38.133 [14], and GNSS belongs to a higher priority group than the current SyncRef UE; or","paragraph_zero_based":889},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if a cell is detected and gNB/eNB (if sl-NbAsSync is set to true) belongs to a higher priority group than the current SyncRef UE; or","paragraph_zero_based":890},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the PSBCH-RSRP of the current SyncRef UE is less than the minimum requirement defined in TS 38.133 [14]:","paragraph_zero_based":891},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>consider no SyncRef UE to be selected;","paragraph_zero_based":892},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has selected GNSS as the synchronization reference for NR sidelink communication/discovery:","paragraph_zero_based":893},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the PSBCH-RSRP of the candidate SyncRef UE exceeds the minimum requirement defined in TS 38.133 [14] by sl-SyncRefMinHyst and the candidate SyncRef UE belongs to a higher priority group than GNSS; or","paragraph_zero_based":894},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if GNSS becomes not reliable in accordance with TS 38.101-1 [15] and TS 38.133 [14]:","paragraph_zero_based":895},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>consider GNSS not to be selected;","paragraph_zero_based":896},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has selected cell as the synchronization reference for NR sidelink communication/discovery:","paragraph_zero_based":897},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the PSBCH-RSRP of the candidate SyncRef UE exceeds the minimum requirement defined in TS 38.133 [14] by sl-SyncRefMinHyst and the candidate SyncRef UE belongs to a higher priority group than gNB/eNB; or","paragraph_zero_based":898},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the selected cell is not detected:","paragraph_zero_based":899},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>consider the cell not to be selected;","paragraph_zero_based":900},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE has not selected any synchronization reference:","paragraph_zero_based":901},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE detects one or more SLSSIDs for which the PSBCH-RSRP exceeds the minimum requirement defined in TS 38.133 [14] by sl-SyncRefMinHyst and for which the UE received the corresponding MasterInformationBlockSidelink message (candidate SyncRef UEs), or if the UE detects GNSS that is reliable in accordance with TS 38.101-1 [15] and TS 38.133 [14], or if the UE detects a cell, select a synchronization reference according to the following priority group order:","paragraph_zero_based":902},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if sl-SyncPriority corresponding to the concerned frequency is set to gnbEnb:","paragraph_zero_based":903},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UEs of which SLSSID is part of the set defined for in coverage, and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to true, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 1);","paragraph_zero_based":904},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UE of which SLSSID is part of the set defined for in coverage, and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to false, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 2);","paragraph_zero_based":905},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>GNSS that is reliable in accordance with TS 38.101-1 [15] and TS 38.133 [14] (priority group 3);","paragraph_zero_based":906},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UEs of which SLSSID is 0, and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to true, or of which SLSSID is 0 and SLSS is transmitted on slot(s) indicated by sl-SSB-TimeAllocation3, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 4);","paragraph_zero_based":907},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UEs of which SLSSID is 0 and SLSS is not transmitted on slot(s) indicated by sl-SSB-TimeAllocation3, and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to false, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 5);","paragraph_zero_based":908},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UEs of which SLSSID is 337 and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to false, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 5);","paragraph_zero_based":909},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>Other UEs, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 6);","paragraph_zero_based":910},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if sl-SyncPriority corresponding to the concerned frequency is set to gnss, and sl-NbAsSync is set to true:","paragraph_zero_based":911}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["3c97d0f1101db634fe2ceb30dea41299e2daeec5385a38a8af117662c11d6499","d964faa12d32465a7ca2fe7c436f02e22fa04f5a6cd56d605709655725aac3aa","16d49aada407c5a5ce957547f69d704fb0c1002404ad29f0aedde231059ee9b3","212b73561f7113e1ab6926f011b90839a53e9668e0bdcf3ea83c084cdc106838","70e8fde5670034ee1662ae8f683fa6861af9369af2a4eb17428fc6ee14fc94fb","c7d8b90f938984ce2d7a6f2dd90a5c459a022dc005c3dcabe0b873aabd038734","06d5fe4450fc88f93914ec8668a2189342f16052bbc9dc5f4de79229418c45c1","787308e14c16f12e9392aee9e814a51bd97674ba5b4cb30309921ce716314659","f609860d1fb78609c7772e67b7f4671231350762f0ce12c98f4b61c3eb5e93a6","d598c73a8eb1365dd8dcda12dea79e340fc1c52679b1ab3cf4326c514638de77","4cb31ad0d50fc9da804c62cf99663300d9e1a34017b24655a9e31a399d42476d","e3b42d0526d80609a7fea2568905fd942fa66f6ef0f114bbc5497ab1237533ff","9c95757a48c45dcee7057203cae3743bad14ee7cd6ed3e6a9b5e45fe2a3443a0","5b1b65460fa4c0883fa48f9a381d42861f186289292c6971e43a5243926492aa","d68d4d142afe4ceea7be5aea1d5bea11257c6647c315edc76138a1b563c17af6","c92de575c88477da46d31316415b0ab59c0fb34a56e5ac11a00b2011ad492631","bca101b3d66d9384363045dd203428f5972620900962a3427d000f4ead11c81a","27e91d5af71291c8103cfed71e438201ec41fb664fb9bbda157542fb68d95311","876314f34ea22d74339bd854bd07dfdde935a28f502dd35ec0f6024ecc4f0259","57edf13175b09d860e31566d1193b9b92dcdedf864f4309372b1220b8930f015","af2fd9c95fbf36131479a0db9a0f5bb84184da46a41844fd58e33bf98eb88d01","13a6b069a0a787389f39faa2c8e60b8363cd2039e13c41880ead4350dfb0341b","251f7b15aa232de701bd2ebf718763a64b6dce25ef6b0f9494779f299bcd8aa7","6058105465c09876d4927da245a7aa2a17414537c2a2ca51959c256c8a665fc0"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[888,911],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p888"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UEs of which SLSSID is 0, and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to true, or of which SLSSID is 0 and SLSS is transmitted on slot(s) indicated by sl-SSB-TimeAllocation3, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 1);","paragraph_zero_based":912},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UEs of which SLSSID is 0 and SLSS is not transmitted on slot(s) indicated by sl-SSB-TimeAllocation3, and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to false, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCHS-RSRP result (priority group 2);","paragraph_zero_based":913},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UEs of which SLSSID is 337 and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to false, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 2);","paragraph_zero_based":914},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>the cell detected by the UE as defined in 5.8.6.3 (priority group 3);","paragraph_zero_based":915},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UEs of which SLSSID is part of the set defined for in coverage, and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to true, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 4);","paragraph_zero_based":916},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UE of which SLSSID is part of the set defined for in coverage, and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to false, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 5);","paragraph_zero_based":917},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>Other UEs, starting with the UE with the highest S-RSRP result (priority group 6);","paragraph_zero_based":918},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if sl-SyncPriority corresponding to the concerned frequency is set to gnss, and sl-NbAsSync is set to false:","paragraph_zero_based":919},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UEs of which SLSSID is 0, and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to true, or of which SLSSID is 0 and SLSS is transmitted on slot(s) indicated by sl-SSB-TimeAllocation3, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 1);","paragraph_zero_based":920},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UEs of which SLSSID is 0 and SLSS is not transmitted on slot(s) indicated by sl-SSB-TimeAllocation3, and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to false, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCHS-RSRP result (priority group 2);","paragraph_zero_based":921},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>UEs of which SLSSID is 337 and inCoverage, included in the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message received from this UE, is set to false, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 2);","paragraph_zero_based":922},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>Other UEs, starting with the UE with the highest PSBCH-RSRP result (priority group 3);","paragraph_zero_based":923},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:How the UE achieves subframe boundary alignment between V2X sidelink communication and NR sidelink communication/discovery (if both are performed by the UE) is as specified in TS 38.213, clause 16.7.","paragraph_zero_based":924},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.6.3Sidelink communication transmission reference cell selection","paragraph_zero_based":925},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink communication/discovery that is configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink communication/discovery shall:","paragraph_zero_based":926},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for the frequency used to transmit NR sidelink communication/discovery, select a cell to be used as reference for synchronization in accordance with the following:","paragraph_zero_based":927},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the frequency concerns the primary frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":928},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>use the PCell or the serving cell as reference;","paragraph_zero_based":929},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the frequency concerns a secondary frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":930},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>use the concerned SCell as reference;","paragraph_zero_based":931},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the UE is in coverage of the concerned frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":932},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>use the DL frequency paired with the one used to transmit NR sidelink communication/discovery as reference;","paragraph_zero_based":933},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else (i.e., out of coverage on the concerned frequency):","paragraph_zero_based":934},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>use the PCell or the serving cell as reference, if needed;","paragraph_zero_based":935}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["d220bd38a9289f200e5617912b8411b307807e175be4902132da672e38edf73f","74577c534a2f94ed3d05ecb01144d031d58b04d180003a896faaf17a77072bc1","40894dceb5aa235979b0b205df0c3a5305b7e8e51ae344e25fa1bba7be3aa0d1","46c83e815ed3c30f69f20b2d3865635435eaa589a6c354905d180b65aa8def17","ea99b94b5f1fbe42baed9abce1b915ee449af9fd8b705f4fd5e46a00ba8e33ab","6d1460f5391d3b685e80c3ba3cbeea19d796e71c7bd6c7dbd4b6767997cde4a4","2dc97818a6261993fcf6a91110cf85fdc1638f09bee4bd256cdcb3b7d60180e4","a2f63d6d489de800b91286d586450b4ff4ffa9a4a1c901ba7292ea9308bc65ba","a0a618b00cd1dd4994cda4c813b64a638686c5702cff28cf60935d2db9bbda7c","abc6e8e33967d8a0aa4ef95bbc79124f73f299e1286946446e4d9c540d74ec5d","886409109d6b045a2ee86f880898b7da81df37ddcaf52746e15cf41c035cb293","5f2109393ad26be1ed0e002c347f8f4f9f4e0e2ea61f0f56133b8228a4e6ae0c","55d4780eb35e10fe24e95e236884aee29c701fc1edf4b40eb0a594712c8fb41f","102e43d7e75fa7a41f66b40bce37b3284f6cc6a1947c70bcfed58dd41c081613","8c40a391546a0b4de0a93ad0ff02cc4bb833d8171ac0583d590050d16ce069b9","0df3b4cf6e135ac96ec818a83fa84d4cff1970c6e8de9cfaac9f51729033aadc","2ae97358000889a244a5ec8a77f9838a60c3e7edc1192eba76ab9e7870c15705","6ef13a35fccc2e6bddc177c928d91d97b1270942fb70a68048610c673ef3a09b","cabc28ef6bb97ac01f811657f4eb2720713250d4b71737a9eca2436273923316","76fadec9ff8d17ffab22246e8cfebbddd4db29a87e7110d8fb0e9f2cf0542c85","0c4bacb11fdfca148e67297fe2af0626b6f7b32084bf310be80fad5e6c112298","f7bb9055c2c08b6e98b943feae689aea3fe7d523f693e4c49829bff4f6e24956","f5c2a92bd687e61844678a25abe39e9454de0dd110aacaa5b4dff26aad30ff8c","7361dffa361e68b622adfca71a490e346e63782628fe60e5b6e036359e609004"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[912,935],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p912"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.7Sidelink communication reception","paragraph_zero_based":936},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink communication that is configured by upper layers to receive NR sidelink communication shall:","paragraph_zero_based":937},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the conditions for NR sidelink communication operation as defined in 5.8.2 are met:","paragraph_zero_based":938},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the frequency used for NR sidelink communication is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in RRCReconfiguration message or sl-FreqInfoList included in SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":939},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is configured with sl-RxPool included in RRCReconfiguration message with reconfigurationWithSync (i.e. handover):","paragraph_zero_based":940},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>configure lower layers to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding data using the pool(s) of resources indicated by sl-RxPool;","paragraph_zero_based":941},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else if the cell chosen for NR sidelink communication provides SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":942},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>configure lower layers to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding data using the pool(s) of resources indicated by sl-RxPool in SIB12;","paragraph_zero_based":943},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":944},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>configure lower layers to monitor sidelink control information and the corresponding data using the pool(s) of resources that were preconfigured by sl-RxPool in SL-PreconfigurationNR, as defined in clause 9.3.","paragraph_zero_based":945},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.8Sidelink communication transmission","paragraph_zero_based":946},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE capable of NR sidelink communication that is configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink communication and has related data to be transmitted shall:","paragraph_zero_based":947},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the conditions for NR sidelink communication operation as defined in 5.8.2 are met:","paragraph_zero_based":948},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the frequency used for NR sidelink communication is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message or included in sl-ConfigCommonNR within SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":949},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is in RRC_CONNECTED and uses the frequency included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message:","paragraph_zero_based":950},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the UE is performing non-relay NR Sidelink Communication; or","paragraph_zero_based":951},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the UE is performing NR sidelink L3 U2N Relay communication; or","paragraph_zero_based":952},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the UE is performing NR Sidelink U2U Relay Communication; or","paragraph_zero_based":953},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the UE acting as U2U Relay UE is performing U2U Relay Communication with integrated Discovery as specified in TS 23.304[65] and sl-DiscConfig is included in RRCReconfiguration, and if the NR sidelink U2U Relay UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.X1.2 are met based on sl-RelayUE-ConfigU2U:","paragraph_zero_based":954},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE X: For U2U Relay UE, it can be up to UE implementation on cross-layer interaction for the AS layer condition check for Direct Communication Request message with integrated discovery forwarding.","paragraph_zero_based":955},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the UE is configured with sl-ScheduledConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":956},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>if T310 for MCG or T311 is running; and if sl-TxPoolExceptional is included in sl-FreqInfoList for the concerned frequency in SIB12 or included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR in RRCReconfiguration; or","paragraph_zero_based":957},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>if T301 is running and the cell on which the UE initiated RRC connection re-establishment provides SIB12 including sl-TxPoolExceptional for the concerned frequency; or","paragraph_zero_based":958},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>if T304 for MCG is running and the UE is configured with sl-TxPoolExceptional included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR for the concerned frequency in RRCReconfiguration:","paragraph_zero_based":959}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["6f0e3e91fb984abc63395520ff08b281849bc59adf5c4bb25a23bbec1c7e89ab","8f9ac67f70eacdad6c4bd9f54b70fafbfe5cbf0583baad7555f48b30d9cbee90","6fd893fe24a02acd400d44b85dc2d1415a0205a514c94bf0182935b8bc294450","c6c5aaab91bf100fa2665d3e48b6e70ec08741167c2e06b3d6ceccfa95297150","2cd451c11a55ea53cb658caca520f28468166c5f80da44bf324ce471ce6131a3","86c41172acb989b1448cc03cc80dacdbcc9a740e1624043485cfae2d5ed2b932","15027a5f2e3dab9f45786f6b98b3f92fd660252e04f080192152f6d9cc909217","2a1b7d5e07137d8b6176cb0f591e4f7fba647a7f88723cf0fb1cd759d2627fc5","e4ab02f2de7e6bca623ce9c69947c75c9c80322d4b3ab3e221fdce2b671808d8","290ed5ff5f556b95798d2b662310e1df7b8be8121bc5341ef9931efc8ffaff5c","0e60526c570b3e0ae8fa7e95a011dad11cb9aff05a34aad5932362950b2f4785","79b1ddb564ae1bec00614c86d98b9a7c34a3c016d37a4534acac962775473729","250c1dc5e9159db0629631650da2cd2fa878463a00173321116c00e2ec7df3a3","c5d62dc97fc57e6ea0ad4878e1712a674a9d781c17c6c79053ea28056867f6c5","e37d2d2f82a39569713462fa57a7ec87374e420dc8af8ca682fd6620a581cc4e","f9979d48841c8309d500fa8ec8d746b8f8014afc5a378d837130efaf9b02068a","956433b4cf3108c11607cc0473a63981af71fb4dc5e6066fe000fee7b22a2a57","814fd0d1940d4abbaa531081e291dcd13b106b5c1a152d156f6abad865edbc61","48865a66f448ed50592ba508a8f1e42f5bd8b30ec1ec6979e5d1b5ded4a99fe9","62231940a40fd57cea26ef78636749e338820b1780279e85256acd7156f39a86","5dbfc8c62ffe14b9ecfdc0563b4d09e97a78e5fcb7d2523ea07f7ff257a14b1e","1602f6c8a521f1a29fc187a3b824ca4358d73c2283cc2be77a198b06f4e64b6e","cb0056536b36301281d9cd7ba067490b1d85051c442c6e914bce19ade48247f8","44d74b1f0a3a149d594ce95add3a58be89c51bc0918d71ac1fd8743f25d8b7f9"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[936,959],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p936"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on random selection using the pool of resources indicated by sl-TxPoolExceptional as defined in TS 38.321 [3];","paragraph_zero_based":960},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>else:","paragraph_zero_based":961},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 1 for NR sidelink communication;","paragraph_zero_based":962},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>if T311 is running, configure the lower layers to release the resources indicated by rrc-ConfiguredSidelinkGrant (if any);","paragraph_zero_based":963},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the UE is configured with sl-UE-SelectedConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":964},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>if a result of full/partial sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration is not available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19];","paragraph_zero_based":965},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7>if sl-TxPoolExceptional for the concerned frequency is included in RRCReconfiguration; or","paragraph_zero_based":966},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7>if the PCell provides SIB12 including sl-TxPoolExceptional in sl-FreqInfoList for the concerned frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":967},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"8>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on random selection using the pool of resources indicated by sl-TxPoolExceptional as defined in TS 38.321 [3];","paragraph_zero_based":968},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>else, if the sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency is included in the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration:","paragraph_zero_based":969},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on resource selection operation according to sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig (as defined in TS 38.321 [3] and TS 38.214 [19]) using the pools of resources indicated by sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency;","paragraph_zero_based":970},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else:","paragraph_zero_based":971},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the cell chosen for NR sidelink communication transmission provides SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":972},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the UE is performing non-relay NR sidelink communication; or","paragraph_zero_based":973},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the UE is performing NR sidelink L3 U2N Relay communication; or","paragraph_zero_based":974},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the UE is performing NR sidelink U2U Relay communication; or","paragraph_zero_based":975},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the UE acting as U2U Relay UE is performing U2U Relay communication with integrated Discovery as specified in TS 23.304[65], and if the NR sidelink U2U Relay UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.X1.2 are met based on sl-RelayUE-ConfigCommonU2U in SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":976},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>if SIB12 includes sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency, and a result of full/partial sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in the sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal is available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19] or random selection, if allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, is selected:","paragraph_zero_based":977},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on resource selection operation according to sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig using the pools of resources indicated by sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency as defined in TS 38.321 [3];","paragraph_zero_based":978},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>else if SIB12 includes sl-TxPoolExceptional for the concerned frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":979},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7>from the moment the UE initiates RRC connection establishment or RRC connection resume, until receiving an RRCReconfiguration including sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, or receiving an RRCRelease or an RRCReject; or","paragraph_zero_based":980},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"7>if a result of full/partial sensing, if selected and is allowed by sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig, on the resources configured in sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency in SIB12 is not available in accordance with TS 38.214 [19]:","paragraph_zero_based":981},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"8>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on random selection (as defined in TS 38.321 [3]) using the pool of resources indicated by sl-TxPoolExceptional for the concerned frequency;","paragraph_zero_based":982},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":983}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["2694219a291624034fb14bde58d521fccc9df43f7e5c2a04d4e651947c70e65d","bd965c539d28d1856e14a9f890c9c2d4f2e587bc9828d1d910445d95cdde3ed2","ba45ee92bc30dde1ed6068ecdad5ddf3ba826e4a87e5753abb164c27da016eb1","838300fde186257adc5a6980137bc84c94c1ca8774f482eaab19a30b2d92def6","f6a513f82b40a921691388a31fb66bdd47c8b22914d4329c8b6240bdc1121a60","5ad1fef0f2ef4d5218c2f5aa9f6278c3dc688e33703d9d66db81a29da1d14387","ad88f596b7747d510d4af7dbd405e2ebdc63f22062a3bcb9f827fe6350c41094","a5192e36995f62b3384f996abb2045f1151e1af5623f6a47edd897d726056cd7","6b8a0b05dde1def48949c9f897349f0f968610ce677e72a57ede9a7d2eb98f98","4471aad9fac12cb6fcbe365c7a78c42f451854eb6d13c84c536883c2a8b6910f","6b7ac078326b1b59eb8acb624ac4fffa1910d2ebd323a26c9422a2b42b314ad4","9257fa725db577e5b3d28f3dd693b7381d08798c4689c99548458620cb17b04a","a3c44a96475b8e00fc3e1a117b10fe75fc93ffc5b35ea07f297e91c59698d2c6","e3f56b30064dd9fd5756893f2cdabb995f3ce02b577a19f702515ad66a9807bc","2ab0f3af813f18eee6ce60dd6ad5a7088e418e54da8e87a465cb39089c9bd133","80b4e7e31b0993c176781583e9a36cbd8a7915835a04a01d5bff9df094fa248d","7ae53f388f3d44ad480764c3a3c6613a3670149273b37c566d33cdf8071e319a","c841a98aed9887da33caacb26e79343f071f5d19bb65bbdb329a6e63b15ff15c","8658a2904c8d770350db187073d40c7987c996b405c012d297658a2096f1dee2","c37c20e6a2a1d8bf5b35f5d3039acebdfde7fd308e949606525d2659daa86f20","1761d9558b566cd58e74159f3c76375bd176ec3b7c8ae018a8780ac080ecf2f8","c4fe97cb7c7947f47f478f50c1a26e823a9480cf80c8ba42c7ce55a7f071267d","a4f96a69ce202813e4fe6e23f1fa36309397d7f3176126efb0ac23569988e7cf","efa8ae1082e2a12d01e1cf5d563c43137ee574c18ab969865fa90b01b92c0031"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[960,983],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p960"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is performing non-relay NR sidelink communication; or","paragraph_zero_based":984},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is performing NR sidelink L3 U2N Relay communication; or","paragraph_zero_based":985},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is performing NR sidelink U2U Relay communication; or","paragraph_zero_based":986},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE acting as U2U Relay UE is performing U2U Relay communication with integrated Discovery as specified in TS 23.304[65], and if the NR sidelink U2U Relay UE threshold conditions as specified in 5.8.X1.2 are met based on sl-RelayUE-PreconfigU2U in SidelinkPreconfigNR:","paragraph_zero_based":987},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>configure lower layers to perform the sidelink resource allocation mode 2 based on resource selection operation according to sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig (as defined in TS 38.321 [3] and TS 38.214 [19]) using the pools of resources indicated by sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal in SidelinkPreconfigNR for the concerned frequency.","paragraph_zero_based":988},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:The UE continues to use resources configured in rrc-ConfiguredSidelinkGrant (while T310 is running) until it is released (i.e. until T310 has expired). The UE does not use sidelink configured grant type 2 resources while T310 is running.","paragraph_zero_based":989},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:In case of RRC reconfiguration with sync, the UE uses resources configured in rrc-ConfiguredSidelinkGrant (while T304 on the MCG is running) if provided by the target cell.","paragraph_zero_based":990},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 3:It is up to UE implementation to determine, in accordance with TS 38.321[3], which resource pool to use if multiple resource pools are configured, and which resource allocation scheme is used in the AS based on UE capability (for a UE in RRC_IDLE/RRC_INACTIVE) and the allowed resource schemes sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig in the resource pool configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":991},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 4:In case that the network does not provide resource pools in SIB12, a UE which is out of coverage, will be unable to obtain sidelink resources to send the first UL RRC message.","paragraph_zero_based":992},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If configured to perform sidelink resource allocation mode 2, the UE capable of NR sidelink communication that is configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink communication shall perform resource selection operation according to sl-AllowedResourceSelectionConfig on all pools of resources which may be used for transmission of the sidelink control information and the corresponding data. The pools of resources are indicated by SidelinkPreconfigNR, sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, or sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal in SIB12 for the concerned frequency, as configured above.","paragraph_zero_based":993},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9Sidelink RRC procedure","paragraph_zero_based":994},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1Sidelink RRC reconfiguration","paragraph_zero_based":995},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1.1General","paragraph_zero_based":996},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":997},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":998},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.9.1.1-1: Sidelink RRC reconfiguration, successful","paragraph_zero_based":999},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":1000},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.9.1.1-2: Sidelink RRC reconfiguration, failure","paragraph_zero_based":1001},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to modify a PC5-RRC connection, e.g. to establish/modify/release sidelink DRBs or PC5 Relay RLC channels, to (re-)configure NR sidelink measurement and reporting, to (re-)configure sidelink CSI reference signal resources, to (re)configure CSI reporting latency bound, to (re)configure sidelink DRX, and to (re-)configure the latency bound of SL Inter-UE coordination report.","paragraph_zero_based":1002},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE may initiate the sidelink RRC reconfiguration procedure and perform the operation in clause 5.8.9.1.2 on the corresponding PC5-RRC connection in following cases:","paragraph_zero_based":1003},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the release of sidelink DRBs associated with the peer UE, as specified in clause 5.8.9.1a.1;","paragraph_zero_based":1004},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the establishment of sidelink DRBs associated with the peer UE, as specified in clause 5.8.9.1a.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1005},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the modification for the parameters included in SLRB-Config of sidelink DRBs associated with the peer UE, as specified in clause 5.8.9.1a.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1006},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the release of PC5 Relay RLC channels for L2 U2N/U2U Relay UE and Remote UE, as specified in clause 5.8.9.7.1;","paragraph_zero_based":1007}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c5261ee4925d98628fc5d62724b5f761b2c93d19922e0c22e59bfd22d3d8d554","6ec7dbe179a1634fc4e0dafbd8d0e9a76c32f4426b59fda857d62031c6604d3c","10e307774fd0bd647f022cdf75888339249dea9a9bda80ca1381c1c7b2a14d78","63c546dd256ee0e08c025e14247faf0089dc400df058f79ff9a2258411c5d984","e43883f7b91fc583fb82ee9906136f62aa167e183b89bad7af78e6578e4a3813","43bfdc63331dcffe8760a4a29a1844bc9f01a3e22712f018babf4dcd93fd4e49","03619ce51e5b639787bbefd9533d66ea8aff89fc71bfacfe844d3111908bbe75","08d8122454da9f54b0d5988ab406687f536a57bc20614fe9511bbe3c0978e3c0","8960104f191639fc73c1065ceac69c17b55729a68356ee5abd6cc6031cab36d7","3e6a0ac33b31a2cbf0619cba8840b64888cc978bccedd3394f913f614600bfcd","30fa8438efce0c6a707fe29059112e64621bfff55692109b5ec798fa823d3c79","828bec16736dd8b65d88a3df2eb117eaf5262222345c59d139f926cf3eaf0452","d916abf2960b801de036b7e0266d020c9ad52284ffdc1e86585a9cb2aa5c8310","4243c3799344cb22e04b931f6d08f7e15bf3a9323ddc167f6b6a7a6d81c22d24","ea203c659ea9579c7a0c0274a77609359dbfb2b9da7ac79a88e90941fdc42ff1","cb9165fa1abac535faaa0bccb8bcd7673bb65754773b3da097450773c13bc9e4","344026485555c6b0c7daa4221ce27128d5916a2d1a1d0dd78820a8a1bf336aa7","dfc966036649b0efa904333dc5402f48a241994ccfefbbef761affb48ccbfdfe","9aa0294e6cb0c3ddc9b3547d98b4af37ef3e39ddc0becce68e62e1f0e7e0685c","c2081f247578dff3b913ed9942fe9dab63c7d48a7dd322fd42db94b8608b6eab","ecf825af64d1592583d460a1f35f969440b2162b0738023c9bc85710443c90f1","fe5b6d2a4b30bf16ee42fa77bfba32f0621c96a23dfa1ad59a672496874ef7fe","e8f47a8a74d6f17e222be38728d3b1154e83c1822840f2a3e057c0b13b4149a6","1968fb76d52eeff2dd6823d0e3b5ac6849c85c4a179d91c0dfe179d4bbc6679e"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[984,1007],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p984"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the establishment of PC5 Relay RLC channels for L2 U2N/U2U Relay UE and Remote UE, as specified in clause 5.8.9.7.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1008},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the modification for the parameters included in SL-RLC-ChannelConfigPC5 of PC5 Relay RLC channels for L2 U2N/U2U Relay UE and Remote UE, as specified in clause 5.8.9.7.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1009},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the (re-)configuration of the peer UE to perform NR sidelink measurement and report.","paragraph_zero_based":1010},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the (re-)configuration of the sidelink CSI reference signal resources and CSI reporting latency bound;","paragraph_zero_based":1011},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the (re-)configuration of the peer UE to perform sidelink DRX;","paragraph_zero_based":1012},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the (re-)configuration of the latency bound of SL Inter-UE coordination report;","paragraph_zero_based":1013},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the (re-)configuration of the local UE ID and split QoS for L2 U2U Remote UEs by L2 U2U Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":1014},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In RRC_CONNECTED, the UE applies the NR sidelink communications parameters provided in RRCReconfiguration (if any). In RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE, the UE applies the NR sidelink communications parameters provided in system information (if any). For other cases, UEs apply the NR sidelink communications parameters provided in SidelinkPreconfigNR (if any). When UE performs state transition between above three cases, the UE applies the NR sidelink communications parameters provided in the new state, after acquisition of the new configurations. Before acquisition of the new configurations, UE continues applying the NR sidelink communications parameters provided in the old state.","paragraph_zero_based":1015},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Editor Note: It is FFS that the two conclusions on TX remote UE derivation for e2e SL-DRB do not exclude the involving information from gNB/preconfiguration/specified configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":1016},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Editor Note: It is FFS how the Relay UE derives second hop configuration for SL-DRB.","paragraph_zero_based":1017},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":1018},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1.2Actions related to transmission of RRCReconfigurationSidelink message","paragraph_zero_based":1019},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall set the contents of RRCReconfigurationSidelink message as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":1020},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sidelink DRB that is to be released, according to clause 5.8.9.1a.1.1, due to configuration by sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR or by upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":1021},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set the entry included in the slrb-ConfigToReleaseList corresponding to the sidelink DRB;","paragraph_zero_based":1022},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sidelink DRB that is to be established or modified, according to clause 5.8.9.1a.2.1, due to receiving sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12 or SidelinkPreconfigNR:","paragraph_zero_based":1023},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if a sidelink DRB is to be established:","paragraph_zero_based":1024},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>assign a new logical channel identity for the logical channel to be associated with the sidelink DRB and set sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfigPC5 in the SLRB-Config to include the new logical channel identity;","paragraph_zero_based":1025},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set the SLRB-Config included in the slrb-ConfigToAddModList, according to the received sl-RadioBearerConfig and sl-RLC-BearerConfig corresponding to the sidelink DRB;","paragraph_zero_based":1026},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>set the sl-MeasConfig as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":1027},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>If the frequency used for NR sidelink communication is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message or included in sl-ConfigCommonNR within SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":1028},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if UE is in RRC_CONNECTED:","paragraph_zero_based":1029},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set the sl-MeasConfig according to stored NR sidelink measurement configuration information for this destination;","paragraph_zero_based":1030},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if UE is in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE:","paragraph_zero_based":1031}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["66456e4e16674a8e5de86590784f98ecdcfba745c73992af088aea201b6c3d4d","2295ef1042b8a778e76f06c263376286b365f134350d18d035cd4403515cbee7","f59d4f0fc8235d6df984b71f004438476d642e7c8458e883e85b1bfc5388e567","a13594bf8a2f070188e0fcb2d512ded02740d0b3241ba729d4a05519040e6d6f","703eadffc9b0908e4b85c3e9205a0e7f5348c43e0d87e421cce96866b9a8d777","d9ca8d1a3d816dcbdadff1575aa215e3fb656ad0a18f726a86789cf90c9738a2","4eb841c013a02faddbc3738fa001394896104cb71d4903abcfc88834951a95c7","86002f779da5a809e8bdf430c81e1b45ec72ff49d257220ad9063234462d3d5e","174b17a2a36c6bca4d2ea841b7abd9a2963dc45d5a3739e2d4a876b925fb21e7","ff1875581b26c034122615a19dd53d4f18a5542b10ad66b8e6447ca0dd7fd531","3dd9d43cd4906b402b6d28171040564b38f0fcd9a9c956ed828dd49d5601ea74","60054bdc7b8a60e4412f8b1255db32dfd72aaf6c4af78808d485d196e18f3bae","01da49677c05fabbc23de728511e76c733e8eec16bd6a334b84970e075e85a80","4733d1135f97dfa5bb964bc5e44598becbca4729fd9a22451542702905ac9f74","c1bc22e9ef167ed250c0be6be27ff0b830b0df2d2e71d3ce473b2542a44d35bc","5f05156ce22878236d9913985430a69880ed177b1e19a923ff5ef25e2bf6be8c","8a4a67751b8d192a6cbcc9f98f8964fcde565af1b0a0d1cb74b5e115f7a936d4","668c0a471986ba6065ee2c1e8cd60598539c0cb003a8f373858f538aa99f4ee5","b6bdaf414ccab75336e165b3cd3c3315d16d3868538ea1ffafa18522435770ca","1cdb49be709786462b65488d0f5d8cf1f469fe2e32a7a867ca961b04828bb3b6","c7389d63f57756c3675109d62a2d2282a35269aefac6e257dc84cc84a3b9c6f1","ecf614b63dcc3bcd5141af61ef5748a6fc38d7e2273f13cafb79c103aaed6ff1","da7e381689cf87d50f46cd7b5e320187a87ac1748e58991475534c493c618215","44bab33c2014022624bacbfdbb79372c2863ef6dadaff28a23a875d6d2820c04"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1008,1031],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1008"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set the sl-MeasConfig according to stored NR sidelink measurement configuration received from SIB12;","paragraph_zero_based":1032},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":1033},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the sl-MeasConfig according to the sl-MeasPreconfig in SidelinkPreconfigNR;","paragraph_zero_based":1034},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>set the sl-LatencyBoundIUC-Report;","paragraph_zero_based":1035},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>start timer T400 for the destination;","paragraph_zero_based":1036},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>set the sl-CSI-RS-Config;","paragraph_zero_based":1037},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>set the sl-LatencyBoundCSI-Report;","paragraph_zero_based":1038},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>set the sl-ResetConfig;","paragraph_zero_based":1039},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:Whether/how to set the parameters included in sl-LatencyBoundIUC-Report, sl-CSI-RS-Config, sl-LatencyBoundCSI-Report and sl-ResetConfig is up to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":1040},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>set the sl-DRX-ConfigUC-PC5 as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":1041},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>If the frequency used for NR sidelink communication is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration message or included in sl-ConfigCommonNR within SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":1042},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if UE is in RRC_CONNECTED and if sl-ScheduledConfig is included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration:","paragraph_zero_based":1043},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set the sl-DRX-ConfigUC-PC5 according to stored NR sidelink DRX configuration information for this destination.","paragraph_zero_based":1044},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:If UE is in RRC_IDLE or in RRC_INACTIVE or out of coverage, or in RRC_CONNECTED and sl-UE-SelectedConfig is included in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration, it is up to UE implementation to set the sl-DRX-ConfigUC-PC5.","paragraph_zero_based":1045},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each PC5 Relay RLC channel that is to be released due to configuration by sl-ConfigDedicatedNR:","paragraph_zero_based":1046},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set the SL-RLC-ChannelID corresponding to the PC5 Relay RLC channel in the sl-RLC-ChannelToReleaseListPC5;","paragraph_zero_based":1047},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each PC5 Relay RLC channel that is to be established or modified due to receiving sl-ConfigDedicatedNR:","paragraph_zero_based":1048},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if a PC5 Relay RLC channel is to be established:","paragraph_zero_based":1049},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>assign a new logical channel identity for the logical channel to be associated with the PC5 Relay RLC channel and set sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfigPC5 in the SL-RLC-ChannelConfigPC5 to include the new logical channel identity;","paragraph_zero_based":1050},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set the SL-RLC-ChannelConfigPC5 included in the sl-RLC-ChannelToAddModListPC5 according to the received SL-RLC-ChannelConfig corresponding to the PC5 Relay RLC channel, including setting sl-RLC-ChannelID-PC5 to the same value of sl-RLC-ChannelID received in SL-RLC-ChannelConfig;","paragraph_zero_based":1051},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as L2 U2U Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":1052},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if both the PC5-RRC connection with L2 U2U Remote UE and the PC5-RRC connection with peer L2 U2U Remote UE are successfully established:","paragraph_zero_based":1053},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>assign a new local UE ID for L2 U2U Remote UE according to association between User Info and L2 ID as specified in TS 23.304 [65]. and set sl-RemoteUE-LocalIdentity-config in the SL-SRAP-ConfigPC5 to include the new local UE ID and L2 ID of L2 U2U Remote UE, if needed; ","paragraph_zero_based":1054},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>assign a new local UE ID for peer L2 U2U Remote UE according to association between User Info and L2 ID as specified in TS 23.304 [65] and set sl-RemoteUE-LocalIdentity-config in the SL-SRAP-ConfigPC5 to include the new local UE ID and L2 ID of peer L2 U2U Remote UE, if needed;","paragraph_zero_based":1055}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["a52bbd4d21921d5efccc0d0478112bb5a0965f4565f0e7bd79a78233ffe2645f","68e338ed3b32af1017d3d9e289bf5c9f3d1aea13e07b752677e1739a8ee25a30","2f7e7e93dd7cab44b61e12b983bcb6bc81460e863fcf4ccf64d161d2406e6861","2f81771ed479278e81ccdbf7f9fa301f05867ebef41cbf03bb656e0830bbd533","5ee1913de4fcc9902c663ea991f4709405c4a1428d862cabeb61be1e65c37d7f","6b59f379e2dece7617a66c0fbf045d8ec450ad5f9605f96e77e95428b030f862","8ac719493493a308c2421ef98918665b506dd9d7a558946b3d99d5aa8211ff71","9c06228b12f499f2cd7b1441840b7827f0282dd2c1d8f2dbe9a81be436394cc2","cc317568ac2c7b43c73e14cd58e5a271ddbf3f79dc5084f8bf2d329809ec6dda","b897760fc8cf6b78c06d0ebc48b9f5b6c4b24bb37f08ddb6e898c34a3ce6650f","2eb83a066f1f96b73546e5dac115594160eb04b186d4689bdb88bd5886cf4c49","25cd2623f48453a7ae201979d3b82199a01c9e6256d18c889c6387f317e081f1","82fc23f7064069ebcefdf219c046eed129cb7982f708a56fbe5cd4191937e4c9","505991796ca1ead76384d029668783ba25765afcd6a3ee9be2855cb83c0dc9fb","477d87871f078bc00fca7078f2859e6411e0377878bc530904d31cf0188b8de7","dab44d798d76c1d36520628cb1b176ee9917a610483a81b2816050ce5ca8be22","dbd4ed88da6597c234526f4e939659f40b4720a419bd04d246df2ba95a220419","2934f2c5160c57f8c72982374fe3287d40c92a5780aa6465609be1a36101c076","6ea4b2042dc8726ddcb0e6255c96b7f3bad54c2ba8c1315fe78d1e1b00b520d6","d32ee31c21cddc56e4a2ccb90cd9bce976975ca2c7de318beacc5383298f7328","cc22a1617d87f7051a874b55dff803e558b8cf4161f1851569da1651adb3c77d","29d71e691778ca9b37b91718fb2bf75768025d8ec8e283fb84c8c4e9fc4c25c1","813eaca0007ffc2337bb714974bf2f3391a600f6312cf4cd35ae11594fe31c29","07f10489d51e51aa0ab5f9a56cf2118a5c8a3fd14bae94e952ec53fcc9779aa9"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1032,1055],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1032"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>determine the submission of an RRCReconfigurationSidelink message to L2 U2U Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":1056},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>determine the submission of an RRCReconfigurationSidelink message to peer L2 U2U Remote UE; ","paragraph_zero_based":1057},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":1058},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Editor NOTE: WA: Carry L2 ID and Local ID in RRCReconfigurationSidelink message with the assumption that the association between User Info and L2 ID is done at ProSe layer.","paragraph_zero_based":1059},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if sl-QoS-InfoListPC5 is included in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message received from the Source L2 U2U Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":1060},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform QoS split based on the sl-QoS-InfoListPC5 for each QoS flow to decide the splitting QoS for each PC5 hop and set sl-SplitQoS-InfoListPC5 to include the splitting QoS Info on the second PC5 hop between L2 U2U Relay UE and the Target L2 U2U Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":1061},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>determine the submission of an RRCReconfigurationSidelink message to the Target L2 U2U Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":1062},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as the Source L2 U2U Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":1063},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set sl-QoS-InfoListPC5 to include the end-to-end QoS profile(s) of the sidelink QoS flow(s) of the Target L2 U2U Remote UE if configured by the upper layer;","paragraph_zero_based":1064},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set sl-DestinationIdentity to include the associated destination for the Target L2 U2U Remote UE if configured by the upper layer;","paragraph_zero_based":1065},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>determine the submission of an RRCReconfigurationSidelink message to L2 U2U Relay UE;","paragraph_zero_based":1066},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall submit the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message to lower layers for transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":1067},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1.3Reception of an RRCReconfigurationSidelink by the UE","paragraph_zero_based":1068},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall perform the following actions upon reception of the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":1069},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfigurationSidelink includes the sl-ResetConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":1070},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink reset configuration procedure as specified in 5.8.9.1.10;","paragraph_zero_based":1071},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfigurationSidelink includes the slrb-ConfigToReleaseList:","paragraph_zero_based":1072},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each entry value included in the slrb-ConfigToReleaseList that is part of the current UE sidelink configuration;","paragraph_zero_based":1073},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the sidelink DRB release procedure, according to clause 5.8.9.1a.1;","paragraph_zero_based":1074},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfigurationSidelink includes the slrb-ConfigToAddModList:","paragraph_zero_based":1075},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each slrb-PC5-ConfigIndex value included in the slrb-ConfigToAddModList that is not part of the current UE sidelink configuration:","paragraph_zero_based":1076},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if sl-MappedQoS-FlowsToAddList is included:","paragraph_zero_based":1077},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>apply the SL-PQFI included in sl-MappedQoS-FlowsToAddList;","paragraph_zero_based":1078},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the sidelink DRB addition procedure, according to clause 5.8.9.1a.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1079}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["abf95229d9daa357376c982416023380a1c6b1f2217ab55a76cece15c56e9a6e","fd639f91f24ee494c7f7333f325c43ea96fa72578d3cc4af5d9ced5346c54965","401dc7aca1e393b693d1f77c759bfa908eaaae238dbef2a3805a20213ac9060f","6e88e3898597ca3e3b9e863ba185c89777c08d49765bb54b0efd712b0d478ab1","9522c78757b76e8fbb383915f99d4cac229e2c6445e34ec36a60bd8fd8f78116","cb624b827438e25ec4255fad43ff76f6caee00d346bcaa5ed219741002033bdf","9c6df29b34d1845f6088805f8be747d4a33c2288faf5682ead316f02bdbde14d","eb30e1b78b51547ad43eb41e5d44d84c9c041625d8f35fa1da44686c995fc1bf","91413e6846ca26a9ee7339b223805d0497e0ddffcc7076d03a2e908914c8c376","3674ef638d373742d658704cd0db00102d3143ea89d66d68f660cf1687e1c343","f222c76e9b145d421e05b1bb6aaa1017cec2b693b2fb19a1060cd901c615b18b","ade4c629d3eba3fa31420d27ee831e175d8c94b8faa76c73b51480e48c44f1a3","7afe32ea51ded958288ac575a47afb5ada60b0df5c16fab584889fc85d6bdcb0","849271d244ec24861c89f7f65b931cc076d6aee07e075f1f51ca2fc3d20f9097","fe123f8c238136b7647bf62bf7190867a1436dfaad44090990dd0c7cbfd38192","5bca48d29e8bda42b29a16c77f884738537fe0e6f59bb67d98ab8e233dc1d1be","9253436f0d1e594fc907ffe5b57b4845db4fafd45807466a07f13e4abcf17522","19343d8fee20d3de5d027215ab4ce41bbfd1c1fd2a9ee8b0c61490d0b3dd1ba4","31c08530828ce7bd9194afa8d06635ad29dc1d148307b907fd89576c4f863718","543f1895e2d2146a359cece3538f7be6239b703916d94237dc53477a9c399032","10166cad0c495369d1e9640ef42d63dccd61f9afd5de9784646d7aa338b1a869","8af2add0ab826538b3c0a6c1ed2b3579847d64252cb903cc47c10d41e636a70d","2bd492b8794a01c1224513e003b300eba85303523d00939cb634439e9c6a23a4","323bf9af57d6b3459e258a6b85cd8437b4bca08aa7acfb3502b2d4ba9c335759"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1056,1079],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1056"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each slrb-PC5-ConfigIndex value included in the slrb-ConfigToAddModList that is part of the current UE sidelink configuration:","paragraph_zero_based":1080},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if sl-MappedQoS-FlowsToAddList is included:","paragraph_zero_based":1081},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>add the SL-PQFI included in sl-MappedQoS-FlowsToAddList to the corresponding sidelink DRB;","paragraph_zero_based":1082},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if sl-MappedQoS-FlowsToReleaseList is included:","paragraph_zero_based":1083},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>remove the SL-PQFI included in sl-MappedQoS-FlowsToReleaseList from the corresponding sidelink DRB;","paragraph_zero_based":1084},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the sidelink DRB release conditions as described in clause 5.8.9.1a.1.1 are met:","paragraph_zero_based":1085},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>perform the sidelink DRB release procedure according to clause 5.8.9.1a.1.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1086},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else if the sidelink DRB modification conditions as described in clause 5.8.9.1a.2.1 are met:","paragraph_zero_based":1087},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>perform the sidelink DRB modification procedure according to clause 5.8.9.1a.2.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1088},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message includes the sl-MeasConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":1089},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink measurement configuration procedure as specified in 5.8.10;","paragraph_zero_based":1090},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message includes the sl-CSI-RS-Config:","paragraph_zero_based":1091},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>apply the sidelink CSI-RS configuration;","paragraph_zero_based":1092},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message includes the sl-LatencyBoundCSI-Report:","paragraph_zero_based":1093},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>apply the configured sidelink CSI report latency bound;","paragraph_zero_based":1094},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfigurationSidelink includes the sl-RLC-ChannelToReleaseListPC5:","paragraph_zero_based":1095},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each SL-RLC-ChannelID value included in the sl-RLC-ChannelToReleaseListPC5 that is part of the current UE sidelink configuration;","paragraph_zero_based":1096},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the PC5 Relay RLC channel release procedure, according to clause 5.8.9.7.1;","paragraph_zero_based":1097},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfigurationSidelink includes the sl-RLC-ChannelToAddModListPC5:","paragraph_zero_based":1098},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each sl-RLC-ChannelID-PC5 value included in the sl-RLC-ChannelToAddModListPC5 that is not part of the current UE sidelink configuration:","paragraph_zero_based":1099},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the PC5 Relay RLC channel addition procedure, according to clause 5.8.9.7.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1100},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each sl-RLC-ChannelID-PC5 value included in the sl-RLC-ChannelToAddModListPC5 that is part of the current UE sidelink configuration:","paragraph_zero_based":1101},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the PC5 Relay RLC channel modification procedure according to clause 5.8.9.7.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1102},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message includes the sl-DRX-ConfigUC-PC5, and","paragraph_zero_based":1103}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c2eed3b3b9a20c982652a8928750bf12029a433ddb23b0d91733863637f95033","73118c7506eb409978fb8dbb2956a72f2b1a93cdb58b1e49e6804873cd52dae0","905e4e1eb418a6b818acdc8111cb132ca248ed7e6905123c0a3b7092a9d02481","e6a5f6c525d9686ebed9988228126b6c44ca2173bd4b1565e21f6309bfbf1ce2","3de7eda2bfa0ed441d623bb2ed0d0ade24507521bbe47cbfaf1a13ce7f4daacb","9b81691a4cf2b5f2a19ed65aa33defbdc661e43cb86ffa7ef559a9837e28e912","a16211a15c3f1ee5dce3aadc59349eba8fc6952f87233ea38b0a5215ffcd38ee","e4df8070cdd1eb4d1f6a1fc0ca947747f42f672e7afb19384554cd2d5c35f9f0","41a9e3835b5eac0ff0945460ec588a2562cff97301cf2d75f7a67d165b71afd3","5743edbb89f0ac93b05e085c66c6bc00e619840e45fac04a2554140d6542f291","4742ecf07d8b42bf65004419331a7ab25009b80ed0edea324837bb0c7b2d4799","d10d7f8ad5ea7c8d4d6e559ad9506c941575dc078bf0c19ddfe9d2e0abb57509","a62763bfb2693f0a6d375d99969e819a428c17ded23ac7f9647574843fa4c25e","136106869f48b6f3eb12c9b9a5e192fe8a4cfd79b5938e310fe3664d9bc000bc","b51d667c28c3efa9ee333db0773fa24dfb9d2cdb971ab2f6987882f734b4f654","483019f98bcb70e2a3a12e9d2694cd1b2f508ed8ae5a7d93e99c76c97cb6392e","ac25cc156407fdef52d4c3ab0c9810d05f668ee37ec86ff9d409f8ea96de952a","9e99ae547c84cef7dffda69542eed2430c0fff58b586c82edfcb8cc978788720","f390fbed198f97aa8e5a1687de81daccea94690d52352498e338105425283609","ddcbda0b2e97091ebd7ba9ef05d0699ec55fa1e4011b6b3d206a0588478c6965","15c8c8c453fc79f5f9d6283aa650efc430c623e2099706dd01337b8f498027f0","bddad9401bfe3d5fd4729e606ecd334d8510edea48e49fa138945277a4e2e3ec","247078af6def820cb5ef9a9fb363b6f7ed1029ddf627bd253f6532f06cfec50a","dbefa78e0d582b842c87e10e3044964ca158596fbf9b6b76e0a6cb7827d0375f"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1080,1103],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1080"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE accepts the sl-DRX-ConfigUC-PC5:","paragraph_zero_based":1104},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>configure lower layers to perform sidelink DRX operation according to sl-DRX-ConfigUC-PC5 for the associated destination as defined in TS 38.321 [3];","paragraph_zero_based":1105},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message includes the sl-LatencyBoundIUC-Report:","paragraph_zero_based":1106},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>apply the configured sidelink IUC report latency bound;","paragraph_zero_based":1107},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message includes the sl-RemoteUE-LocalIdentity-config and sl-PeerRemoteUE-LocalIdentity-Config:","paragraph_zero_based":1108},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>configure lower layers to perform NR sidelink U2U Relay operation according to sl-RemoteUE-LocalIdentity-config for L2 U2U Remote UE and sl-PeerRemoteUE-LocalIdentity-config for peer L2 U2U Remote UE as defined in TS 38.351 [65];","paragraph_zero_based":1109},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfigurationSidelink includes the sl-QoS-InfoListPC5:","paragraph_zero_based":1110},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform actions related to transmission of RRCReconfigurationSidelink as specified in 5.8.9.1.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1111},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is unable to comply with (part of) the configuration included in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink (i.e. sidelink RRC reconfiguration failure):","paragraph_zero_based":1112},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>continue using the configuration used prior to the reception of the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message;","paragraph_zero_based":1113},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set the content of the RRCReconfigurationFailureSidelink message;","paragraph_zero_based":1114},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>submit the RRCReconfigurationFailureSidelink message to lower layers for transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":1115},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":1116},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set the content of the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message;","paragraph_zero_based":1117},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE rejects the sidelink DRX configuration sl-DRX-ConfigUC-PC5 received from the peer UE:","paragraph_zero_based":1118},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>include the sl-DRX-ConfigReject in the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message;","paragraph_zero_based":1119},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>consider no sidelink DRX to be applied for the corresponding sidelink unicast communication;","paragraph_zero_based":1120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if sl-SplitQoS-InfoListPC5 is included in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message received from L2 U2U Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":1121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set sl-AcceptQoS-InfoListPC5 to include the accepted QoS Info on the second PC5 hop between L2 U2U Relay UE and the Target L2 U2U Remote UE, with considering the received sl-SplitQoS-InfoListPC5;","paragraph_zero_based":1122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>determine the submission of of RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message to L2 U2U Relay UE;","paragraph_zero_based":1123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":1124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>submit the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message to lower layers for transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":1125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:When the same logical channel is configured with different RLC mode by another UE, the UE handles the case as sidelink RRC reconfiguration failure.","paragraph_zero_based":1126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2: It is up to the UE implementation whether or not to indicate the rejection to the peer UE for a received sidelink DRX configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":1127}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["9dcc371bc38b26eb68cd62e7ab3ff3b48ac391e1c5bfe18b93d98a50640d7201","4e54bf446b625c50ff4e37df5da9380e031857151ad8c925845202d596d146b2","5854cdc3fd3b6c7eb4e3a0faa7b0f6fd87021b50fb735d037297e18ad4dedb01","9d4957add6efa2910d1e4c391d8813bebd232a5c705ee8e73599bd13d43b0286","6dea0bf3c633ff19470291389869c008b4778cee293a7323e1204a3f01d6b4d2","0348cc16d5bbef7152e45dca3c853316ba72fb9316569be7c681d0a3592b2e58","9b09ecb92844b26ea7590d8b65b83dadda60df0abd78effaf4f02cb125cb5b3e","ce168f71a4741270f97337d247a7f66376789a0192849bf98d5cf2e31da8f265","7d5b5f28d91f8f8b3c9fc7a8ab0e8fa70205c182f779456cafee454e66314f14","4221bd12ace26679bf2e0e5e4efe3f143deb9416b097eb379e43e647e5a1cbda","48fc75223e6948a0d8c3a25501f23ce2511fd9dca71b97b887d8b745afceba60","f3d03cd46c301c99775d3398d7db9412db9c688f39a305b63d7f87e3013c9689","cd21ea881353f516692448d0c9d77706955dba6d4605f60945e97584e9bc390c","945b6c5a92d848fb71475d514fdd4ddea75bdc1c79b5098bf85b06a12fe2b625","944e3a77fc7b698af4187bcbaf8692ea5260e1a9270b973a8c5bcfedf87c3666","618cdf6ed500c70201b2ebb8a5f7d4c80e0557a39e141d4b87a2dac95f0047ef","8de7504f2ebd0565393a31200746469fac4a7d56444c87ba431041dd82cff253","71d047e3d3781afe974ff5617e2f852b78e74b8a090371e892f3d762a3dad45f","b1de5e62ddbaf1ea9066b31f843ab9a49e3f19a9bd8904b6996713b192c9ca23","2dca960e69185a01b23b855897ba606502b6e22c6f11891359dc4ed61a0c8e01","d3a84a6d4fa41e64c735ec677a028d102865fc9fea9f7edd3318223aba1e208e","ebb854d936397af279b1c294782a350fbab78913dd20faaa043a1e9cc7e90f2a","ad83c21b66d88be369a290f449b36f3f28a9da16a8e7578c635909442edbbb64","4cec707d32d6164178b8edb7bca7fa023c2236ee296ce06073fe8789b01a7b2c"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1104,1127],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1104"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1.4Void","paragraph_zero_based":1128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1.5Void","paragraph_zero_based":1129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1.6Void","paragraph_zero_based":1130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1.7Void","paragraph_zero_based":1131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1.8Reception of an RRCReconfigurationFailureSidelink by the UE","paragraph_zero_based":1132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall perform the following actions upon reception of the RRCReconfigurationFailureSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":1133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>stop timer T400 for the destination, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":1134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>continue using the configuration used prior to corresponding RRCReconfigurationSidelink message;","paragraph_zero_based":1135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if UE is in RRC_CONNECTED:","paragraph_zero_based":1136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink UE information for NR sidelink communication procedure, as specified in 5.8.3.3 or clause 5.10.15 in TS 36.331 [10];","paragraph_zero_based":1137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1.9Reception of an RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink by the UE","paragraph_zero_based":1138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall perform the following actions upon reception of the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":1139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>stop timer T400 for the destination, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":1140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>consider the configurations in the corresponding RRCReconfigurationSidelink message to be applied.","paragraph_zero_based":1141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message includes the sl-DRX-ConfigReject:","paragraph_zero_based":1142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>consider no sidelink DRX to be applied for the corresponding sidelink unicast communication;","paragraph_zero_based":1143},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message received from the Target L2 U2U Remote UE includes the sl-AcceptQoS-InfoListPC5:","paragraph_zero_based":1144},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the content of the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message:","paragraph_zero_based":1145},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set sl-SplitQoS-InfoListPC5 to include the splitting QoS Info on the first PC5 hop between the Source L2 U2U Remote UE and the L2 U2U Relay UE, with considering the received sl-AcceptQoS-InfoListPC5;","paragraph_zero_based":1146},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set set sl-DestinationIdentity to include the associated destination for the Target L2 U2U Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":1147},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>determine the sumbmission of RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message to the Source L2 U2U Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":1148},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>submit the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message to lower layers for transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":1149},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":1150},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1.10Sidelink reset configuration","paragraph_zero_based":1151}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c46f0ddcdaaf0dd56bf0061bb6336ff8876ff6868d93291a59bfd91c33607e9c","b4708affd801bb25eaa50be695c84998e07a0bd512bf29717c62b7aece842457","ac196d5072489409c2507c07b72b99e9bffeb00d0a1a406694b36b7ae3ef23c8","c6c403dba752f7dcf75d71ff86fdf4a1e62504f7e1a8a8713b365afa7ea759a0","ce2729dd6b95a707610d29df2c3c46bae26358c313f47ee2b858d33b75386f0b","680b5295228c09358986fe50afa73c99066d7be1a50e9b216b81fd2e07f72936","4796253aac4cc6d81754bb994f4a4b8d443cac044153ece7bd130002fefe14c3","031bac2b77a390b49a0e86c96e541c6320256a1a56038a7b7da8b40b72d47538","531b19f3307a8741e3c5a2ca6b83a62dd9f7dad95315914222558140dbeeab84","a9181af733c52ca926ffec3a7fdc0ba2c84c83938979a2948ebff3da003b9839","f6c645263c7c293521d5a09cbd5e0f0b0dcf721e10d21240c9ec753d0e843b9e","7f77631576868c7082ceb10848f4f7d56cca65cd1ba62180ec3f2583837b81ad","b320ef59bac6c87702da3bdafc1c797caa37fbbff5f97974eb1c3548133a38b0","9a4634b636f47cfe6a3f01ace95393d0ce7e8f53d179fd66848b72a1edf81f31","c4cd509eb19f9fd63ec56e8b90c3876125875cd2ee2bd651c92552303aa02928","502c979bef47e9a4aef8fa246ed2ac661b78a89f90ac33bb1b7d96f591ce1713","dee305749386b2adcf9001a8d1b35c663e57a3209b0c2adc703b3713b5fb2afb","ec4147beeedf8e615a3893345dae2242b301bc12f03684a03e7542ce80e16e5d","2bfa3c2e9b3ed02ee63a60cb568ce18d7e6232bc18ca907106ba9f882ee979a2","a35278f453e49b766625a8dcc59e60b0b0a46357897d856f997e6e7e220e14a1","81e130a08b0dc1fc7e3e216d19febdf5dd0f47ebebd33f347babedf1046f06e9","aa96baa7c742fab33b21bc2006fecda13872aafc98fee61cec22af743a5e97cf","27e27d16065fdf1fea5042f5103f2ca456226b30776140d8df15582a2e362b01","ad06d905a4f90a66fe6a3cd62a8b2968d0d277e6dea685931d8f6366d3d53fb8"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1128,1151],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1128"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release/clear current sidelink radio configuration of this destination received in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink;","paragraph_zero_based":1153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>release the sidelink DRBs of this destination, in according to clause 5.8.9.1a.1;","paragraph_zero_based":1154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>reset the sidelink specific MAC of this destination.","paragraph_zero_based":1155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:Sidelink radio configuration is not just the resource configuration but may include other configurations included in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message except the sidelink DRBs of this destination.","paragraph_zero_based":1156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:After the sidelink DRB release procedure, UE may perform the sidelink DRB addition according to the current sidelink configuration of this destination, received in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12 and SidelinkPreconfigNR, according to clause 5.8.9.1a.2.","paragraph_zero_based":1157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1aSidelink radio bearer management","paragraph_zero_based":1158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1a.1Sidelink DRB release","paragraph_zero_based":1159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1a.1.1Sidelink DRB release conditions","paragraph_zero_based":1160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For NR sidelink communication, a sidelink DRB release is initiated in the following cases:","paragraph_zero_based":1161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for groupcast, broadcast and unicast, if slrb-Uu-ConfigIndex (if any) of the sidelink DRB is included in sl-RadioBearerToReleaseList in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR; or","paragraph_zero_based":1162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for groupcast and broadcast, if no sidelink QoS flow with data indicated by upper layers is mapped to the sidelink DRB for transmission, which is (re)configured by receiving SIB12 or SidelinkPreconfigNR; or","paragraph_zero_based":1163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for groupcast, broadcast and unicast, if SL-RLC-BearerConfigIndex (if any) of the sidelink DRB is included in sl-RLC-BearerToReleaseList in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR; or","paragraph_zero_based":1164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, if no sidelink QoS flow with data indicated by upper layers is mapped to the sidelink DRB for transmission, which is (re)configured by receiving SIB12 or SidelinkPreconfigNR, and if no sidelink QoS flow mapped to the sidelink DRB, which is (re)configured by receiving RRCReconfigurationSidelink, has data; or","paragraph_zero_based":1165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, if SLRB-PC5-ConfigIndex (if any) of the sidelink DRB is included in slrb-ConfigToReleaseList in RRCReconfigurationSidelink or if sl-ResetConfig is included in RRCReconfigurationSidelink; or","paragraph_zero_based":1166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, when the corresponding PC5-RRC connection is released due to sidelink RLF being detected, according to clause 5.8.9.3; or","paragraph_zero_based":1167},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, when the corresponding PC5-RRC connection is released due to upper layer request according to clause 5.8.9.5.","paragraph_zero_based":1168},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1a.1.2Sidelink DRB release operations","paragraph_zero_based":1169},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For each sidelink DRB, whose sidelink DRB release conditions are met as in clause 5.8.9.1a.1.1, the UE capable of NR sidelink communication that is configured by upper layers to perform NR sidelink communication shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1170},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for groupcast and broadcast; or","paragraph_zero_based":1171},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, if the sidelink DRB release was triggered after the reception of the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message; or","paragraph_zero_based":1172},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, after receiving the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message, if the sidelink DRB release was triggered due to the configuration received within the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR or indicated by upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":1173},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the PDCP entity for NR sidelink communication associated with the sidelink DRB;","paragraph_zero_based":1174},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if SDAP entity for NR sidelink communication associated with this sidelink DRB is configured:","paragraph_zero_based":1175}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ed260facc392e347df973e7ae36b6a4b06dde5e19eaddedc4edae2b12fcb8712","9979592a79a8f6715ea9435e3a3bfa379d4df9a0d3e8c39c22bf4cde37796f19","b48e2d18c5196330e6c6085854b69015b5fc5ad2181f7f4843360a11372f60c4","cf16eb35ceeb796f57744806914a0ad4b3bde4c0e496245cd0c6c99d59732907","4f42367f345ab8304907994d69bebe541b244a7199f2bb6b5fbe99eef9ab9ff3","f1cb8164fa2695c7b5ef9e3b0b3d615b2ae4907bc10b1be4a9d8c95d6145c84d","ae18c09d5c1fff0789ebeb816f3b18b423c86115103adb39fc108288e19cf4d9","f83a2a77f2048a16b2427a03455c4f9fa014c9b4e0a63ef2c8f89a266b33f63f","d520d4555f9abf7de392fe0c948403387529a2990ba86660099f31f044822f56","e4848a1d890fcf2f378b9be28e14e076d0db60dace0704aa10544a1c85808e0b","8a04aabc14c9453afee206eee7d09c108ff581943cefa9adf51db45d62866d33","a1c6d998b1ef1369f3bc2dbb4d080360a1c641090e5c40b9fe5cb45370ea989e","aa9354844786dd863f25d8fd9d8498401f2804f610f23d9b8473e9a70b2efdc8","c62372adf9b22217e72ef9f908237b277fd0a5fc3549225b96eed5737e1a7d6f","5cd15bd47c34374ab2974f7ab4ac1f771c693456875c359522ad335536999807","31da815a8aebb9c8ad677f6262ecdfee5bf6c36dd0739f29d7a368b8d44c6e8b","48b0ee760e871067f6e820a3a210e28f830f07c7c1924af3b7ab6a0b645c6244","0847d06378eea5c8aaacfa5f0e02d81edd06b8bb3431de6b467eddd56cbed151","560eb0b2b6d5969df3f4dbfbb15416463d46f8b9c5a2a12e641aad4dc126a121","53473c6484bf7059d7169a64004ed60567750cea78c65d836b548bc313b3eeb0","0fd293ed212e95efa80ca37eac5ef939cdaffae4688785da60c8589cc5948667","c588b6b4cdd8360a3b1019bbddd1a215a1ce89a63bb511516f8603743d5a374e","412143c897751285bab63104bd7fbe729fedfd7fb87df72682de42c843fd26bc","2696179319609e4b69a6bb147cef0a757ff0e358d7e71d34c4dd6026789361f2"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1152,1175],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1152"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>indicate the release of the sidelink DRB to the SDAP entity associated with this sidelink DRB (TS 37.324 [24], clause 5.3.3);","paragraph_zero_based":1176},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release SDAP entities for NR sidelink communication, if any, that have no associated sidelink DRB as specified in TS 37.324 [24] clause 5.1.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1177},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for groupcast and broadcast; or","paragraph_zero_based":1178},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, after receiving the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message, if the sidelink DRB release was triggered due to the configuration received within the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR:","paragraph_zero_based":1179},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each sl-RLC-BearerConfigIndex included in the received sl-RLC-BearerToReleaseList that is part of the current UE sidelink configuration:","paragraph_zero_based":1180},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>release the RLC entity and the corresponding logical channel for NR sidelink communication, associated with the sl-RLC-BearerConfigIndex.","paragraph_zero_based":1181},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, if the sidelink DRB release was triggered due to the reception of the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message; or","paragraph_zero_based":1182},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, after receiving the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message, if the sidelink DRB release was triggered due to the configuration received within the SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR or indicated by upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":1183},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the RLC entity and the corresponding logical channel for NR sidelink communication associated with the sidelink DRB;","paragraph_zero_based":1184},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink UE information procedure in clause 5.8.3 for unicast if needed.","paragraph_zero_based":1185},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the sidelink radio link failure is detected for a specific destination:","paragraph_zero_based":1186},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the PDCP entity, RLC entity and the logical channel of the sidelink DRB for the specific destination.","paragraph_zero_based":1187},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Editor Note: FFS on how to release SL DRB on E2E and hop configuration for U2U relay.","paragraph_zero_based":1188},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1a.2Sidelink DRB addition/modification","paragraph_zero_based":1189},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1a.2.1Sidelink DRB addition/modification conditions","paragraph_zero_based":1190},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For NR sidelink communication, a sidelink DRB addition is initiated only in the following cases:","paragraph_zero_based":1191},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if any sidelink QoS flow is (re)configured by sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR and is to be mapped to one sidelink DRB, which is not established; or","paragraph_zero_based":1192},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if any sidelink QoS flow is (re)configured by RRCReconfigurationSidelink and is to be mapped to a sidelink DRB, which is not established;","paragraph_zero_based":1193},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For NR sidelink communication, a sidelink DRB modification is initiated only in the following cases:","paragraph_zero_based":1194},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if any of the sidelink DRB related parameters is changed by sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR or RRCReconfigurationSidelink for one sidelink DRB, which is established;","paragraph_zero_based":1195},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1a.2.2Sidelink DRB addition/modification operations","paragraph_zero_based":1196},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For the sidelink DRB, whose sidelink DRB addition conditions are met as in clause 5.8.9.1a.2.1, the UE capable of NR sidelink communication that is configured by upper layers to perform NR sidelink communication shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1197},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for groupcast and broadcast; or","paragraph_zero_based":1198},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, if the sidelink DRB addition was triggered due to the reception of the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message; or","paragraph_zero_based":1199}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["19a883d0b36434ed92f5da8ae4c38a15fd838fb84839766033aae83b3d0f04fa","2f6d74779ecdf949c515c34f6dfd449b794fa45072a048be699468cc98233c05","4fa8142f1845fdebfbf7623b299c493286ac191c676d9a9f457bfbc4fe231843","9b16e73707874b5fdbe6604b947082616b6a14365a7559f1435425eb4a42a3c9","bbb7be1351b30c44eab586954db1a38b1d776140313405b986f419e1b861442b","76756a2f7bfd4f683a5d7f41d19e6b1bd77229d6c4fce85be47f4bb0fce88c92","76884888ec708b4e04a49b003fe30b39d1c9e1b2f14f1624e77cd1b380cc78d7","47a5594e6fa9173df127ede0d3f64b613fd59392f5009756e4382f8a929dae4d","48a5e1f29eb02d6fc4c779f6d3c5543838be2742c2cdd6cc1666da0e5879c42b","4232b8dca0868f2d2a790bc6b161060225f6dde926251886617761f842a2d922","92657545ad4a2b91840cebda36949072945d7da2daecc8452ea78cb4e59220b3","de504989207ede4313f65bbb083c2ead6a70a2b6494914552934caa9a6a9c611","2f36fa78be2e5f4b8394e8a8c708f74c0f268d45a443e131990667795329a142","702321a362992707b0ab93bb2492cac6e17e2a7c7a46ccaee9258fefbf341f29","ef25d8ac154e5b58686b93f12371fcc114e16f67a2678e0a0a9e238fe8d5e77b","af705456d079d83905d468657beab21c6d090945d9bd3a3abe47fda545705e41","21584c3b9e8615a29aef8f2589e17a1bcc8cfadaecdfc31a287bc5cfd97a6dfc","49e1bc22c6129b2f54c94e4b2e9df7f6a51945d7a6a53a6ab3281ea6e45aecae","222a039771af525c575f9de5a8732e9d3d01ab9af4343b97e37f6f87bf75c564","fc9ecb748b2aede6f2a46af28a8acabfc373ff6ef397331d19ecebc76052bf29","edf0d7f4dd2824785f68519a903e93c204023a702b9968894f2ff10f9a163d5d","57e9226bc0f5485c07857c71ae0f0446987d592a247758f8636e06f29d3ba575","365da6ecf6cbd388170672633dfcf39f0a12e463b9c88f15c9fbf76b0ba3fbc0","bea4671676a583ba587f7880a8c632808c085066538f0cfcf1c0968a1f6f1a7d"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1176,1199],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1176"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, after receiving the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message, if the sidelink DRB addition was triggered due to the configuration received within the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR or indicated by upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":1200},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if an SDAP entity for NR sidelink communication associated with the destination and the cast type of the sidelink DRB does not exist:","paragraph_zero_based":1201},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>establish an SDAP entity for NR sidelink communication as specified in TS 37.324 [24] clause 5.1.1;","paragraph_zero_based":1202},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>(re)configure the SDAP entity in accordance with the sl-SDAP-ConfigPC5 received in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink or sl-SDAP-Config received in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR, associated with the sidelink DRB;","paragraph_zero_based":1203},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>establish a PDCP entity for NR sidelink communication and configure it in accordance with the sl-PDCP-ConfigPC5 received in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink or sl-PDCP-Config received in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR, associated with the sidelink DRB;","paragraph_zero_based":1204},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>establish a RLC entity for NR sidelink communication and configure it in accordance with the sl-RLC-ConfigPC5 received in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink or sl-RLC-Config received in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR, associated with sidelink DRB;","paragraph_zero_based":1205},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if this procedure was due to the reception of a RRCReconfigurationSidelink message:","paragraph_zero_based":1206},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>configure the MAC entity with a logical channel in accordance with the sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfigPC5 received in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink associated with the sidelink DRB, and perform the sidelink UE information procedure in clause 5.8.3 for unicast if need;","paragraph_zero_based":1207},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if this procedure was due to the reception of a RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message:","paragraph_zero_based":1208},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>configure the MAC entity with a logical channel associated with the sidelink DRB, in accordance with the sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfig received in the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR;","paragraph_zero_based":1209},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else (i.e. for groupcast/broadcast):","paragraph_zero_based":1210},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>configure the MAC entity with a logical channel associated with the sidelink DRB, in accordance with the sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfig received in the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR and assign a new LCID to this logical channel.","paragraph_zero_based":1211},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:When a sidelink DRB addition is due to the configuration by RRCReconfigurationSidelink, it is up to UE implementation to select the sidelink DRB configuration as necessary transmitting parameters for the sidelink DRB, from the received sl-ConfigDedicatedNR (if in RRC_CONNECTED), SIB12 (if in RRC_IDLE/INACTIVE), SidelinkPreconfigNR (if out of coverage) with the same RLC mode as the one configured in RRCReconfigurationSidelink.","paragraph_zero_based":1212},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For the sidelink DRB, whose sidelink DRB modification conditions are met as in clause 5.8.9.1a.2.1, the UE capable of NR sidelink communication that is configured by upper layers to perform NR sidelink communication shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1213},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for groupcast and broadcast; or","paragraph_zero_based":1214},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, if the sidelink DRB modification was triggered due to the reception of the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message; or","paragraph_zero_based":1215},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for unicast, after receiving the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message, if the sidelink DRB modification was triggered due to the configuration received within the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12 or SidelinkPreconfigNR:","paragraph_zero_based":1216},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>reconfigure the SDAP entity of the sidelink DRB, in accordance with the sl-SDAP-ConfigPC5 received in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink or sl-SDAP-Config received in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR, if included;","paragraph_zero_based":1217},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>reconfigure the PDCP entity of the sidelink DRB, in accordance with the sl-PDCP-ConfigPC5 received in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink or sl-PDCP-Config received in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR, if included;","paragraph_zero_based":1218},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>reconfigure the RLC entity of the sidelink DRB, in accordance with the sl-RLC-ConfigPC5 received in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink or sl-RLC-Config received in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR, if included;","paragraph_zero_based":1219},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>reconfigure the logical channel of the sidelink DRB, in accordance with the sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfigPC5 received in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink or sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfig received in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR, SIB12, SidelinkPreconfigNR, if included.","paragraph_zero_based":1220},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1a.3Sidelink SRB release","paragraph_zero_based":1221},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1222},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if a PC5-RRC connection release for a specific destination is requested by upper layers or AS layer; or","paragraph_zero_based":1223}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["93b453d87e92e6311c81ce142dbf89a57710ed40d8d8eb41b86ee3f5170a16bc","5cb518977c0c20cf7647df61d5909ea97cddfdb425430dbc7f92cba41b89872f","be3fa4e0e77405a745a7f45223b2caf0ac66fd5c77b2e2dbc1b5bc654cbf512d","d342df24490a2eb66f4bdbde2ca1de3088872e9dc29fa58e6880a2a15f4a49d4","a3c4fc00f7afa3089ccceefa8a2143da987ef315c1be46b13bc70b22e570715d","888ad30642bb28d8062e9b67bdeec8301f9f2fe30df2ee6a1560c63cf5cd56f8","7bc704eb07c2707732847b82cdd6ecbf72d1cf5d6d73641c88fb585be63c97fc","091a5bacfa7aec8dd80b83610a21e750fab5de9e2aa52e502df5dae2bb113cce","6a0f5a9dc9101292af60aafd08f9ac96b6969fb9f9d658470c92193051a08e60","f85aed9109c10c6984e686d1ccf8455b3d55ca83b16c05bef926ece51cf33ca0","89f6d5d7996d173f0ed41a4d16613167de29dfc1dcefaf5152256cd4c8fe89b9","b451f8426e4069602e97e13c2d87ad2a5c23f03b4bb8a8fc770331221cbd4094","221d31a84d4a3fbc53898d39354fbad7b67812c1ab078ff2a6bb0b7a2b5ace7b","fe7d51d44e9863e6b5b4869e8d9aa186d78c9993d88160481a884be5850788ee","c17ed567be5a9215a0a4f1789dee44dc3199cf1b85669444d3ba1d841c6cd8c8","9df5ec30fa23add69503f50ef3948277d040b8b4ed9a17d01e57d3ea31e2e015","2a989436a38bec0007f5c10824e5f7646509ad94f7f286213ca189c2e3897c6d","c4ac322bfb55ec9186da2d5e149e1af2552e4c50bdb145d8f7a35a011487a990","c1db1c757fc40f2fe56dd9e505f32caee5362fdfdf50c2108ff38b06b0586df6","248602b15ce5387b32687e8b6ea24f56af0a2628f3597cc56ffeb691e19b4daa","902539f37ea54930875d42fa20d84df6e17712a08e1f89bac80c1b92fcf194e4","5dc093cc04febe71c7b77624e93d971dd31be6b5d80c3c826651235542fe23bd","cf8a6c0072477e2f1c61ecf3d76a2be9a2e6f4cc9e0d9d326062de184146bff3","0f37510ee300574f813746c8cf9db8dafdc6383c6290109f46f5fe7666d84bef"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1200,1223],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1200"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the sidelink radio link failure is detected for a specific destination:","paragraph_zero_based":1224},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the PDCP entity, RLC entity and the logical channel of the sidelink SRB for PC5-RRC message of the specific destination;","paragraph_zero_based":1225},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>consider the PC5-RRC connection is released for the destination.","paragraph_zero_based":1226},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if PC5-S transmission for a specific destination is terminated in upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":1227},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the PDCP entity, RLC entity and the logical channel of the sidelink SRB(s) for PC5-S message of the specific destination;","paragraph_zero_based":1228},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if discovery transmission for a specific destination is terminated in upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":1229},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the PDCP entity, RLC entity and the logical channel of the sidelink SRB4 for discovery message of the specific destination;","paragraph_zero_based":1230},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Editor Note: FFS on how to release SL SRB on E2E and hop configuration for U2U relay.","paragraph_zero_based":1231},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":1232},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.1a.4Sidelink SRB addition","paragraph_zero_based":1233},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1234},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if transmission of PC5-S message for a specific destination is requested by upper layers for sidelink SRB:","paragraph_zero_based":1235},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>establish PDCP entity, RLC entity and the logical channel of a sidelink SRB for PC5-S message, as specified in clause 9.1.1.4;","paragraph_zero_based":1236},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if transmission of discovery message for a specific destination is requested by upper layers for sidelink SRB:","paragraph_zero_based":1237},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>establish PDCP entity, RLC entity and the logical channel of a sidelink SRB4 for discovery message, as specified in clause 9.1.1.4;","paragraph_zero_based":1238},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if a PC5-RRC connection establishment for a specific destination is indicated by upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":1239},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>establish PDCP entity, RLC entity and the logical channel of a sidelink SRB for PC5-RRC message of the specific destination, as specified in clause 9.1.1.4;","paragraph_zero_based":1240},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>consider the PC5-RRC connection is established for the destination.","paragraph_zero_based":1241},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.2Sidelink UE capability transfer","paragraph_zero_based":1242},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.2.1General","paragraph_zero_based":1243},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This clause describes how the UE compiles and transfers its sidelink UE capability information for unicast to the initiating UE.","paragraph_zero_based":1244},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":1245},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.9.2.1-1: Sidelink UE capability transfer","paragraph_zero_based":1246},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.2.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":1247}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["b084f4319f009d3545f74fd6e4437463922ffa8d85850b92200300edfb543e29","1f67dd116e369031b2e5afe3506cd57d2233275c2d1a198cceec665dcac28c04","767468aeb4e86ee7a7af2f5a28b94664bcb557230daad55b2f61b9406dd69014","64a1ff7e187ec2925201ac026596c15458eff6b65eb1770613b0487aabea51d6","c96d27a336f36498635ec826d112ca5fda7380343056c73c33c9a0e9f4f55bf5","06c5fca666bd4829c9ce705bef11076851fdf89a4dfde5d323feaf846aeaf70d","6e9ea6f8aa80a45ab6023dff5e2b71e5a5305caf2947df39d25ae9c601be4402","4707de3b359a504fc6337fa77d315faca0317a255f64e22d269b10124282f7d1","ac109be729424714374457f8e308c98a67a903311a19dbd36af868ca45dde502","02fd54fd28e224e802faad6d7a92ecf88606f3bfcd8a996fa9cf2af7848b3129","78e0e43976b80f31fd542936768133145e99d3542e860e144c8ff29ae47d6954","8ab8034a6737435ab82a33ca27a9f3c7d7013729be1f492c222ff1d2e5f9dd96","c0267547b22f9f063746cc07bce21b25917b80a6fa37c43331edff2de86ebbee","bc58b7b4bc9cbfcc7ef18fd6068ae8b085764f9d76d9e5692ef531b9c2ec7cbb","1ffc54e459dfb7802db51e3690d74ddee5c4bd6d3bc5ba6d64eecc5363dc1420","1a77faa5930fe8aa5d2c0c288870321848676013befd59756aab00a04f809974","929895ab50b17103172d03a073783e2e015e717db98551d0a54311c1816dc1a0","eaeb4ac31fdd25d0461a6ad3490a3dd980518c94cd27645364ef613bd88574d8","51fc896850cff87a14824c44f25cccb4ac9b39fc2c8a44f736995edb43d2f88d","2673daec86fd62535d8876e45991f16b35f43480375c1253d12b7a1a4a8025d0","f981208b8785dc95d4ede82586243499701ab549979c948f40386c21e2476626","e56e60c6476954c05fe9854d793f492e2f09ebf6658680f39efa9d1e3191e499","1c7934c84a41f9e9aad4d1ab8510c687c7a88e52815304ff7490093ca0c0fb77","6278490c5cc58dc0909aee2d4784f2b0d9db527861e94b85363848f1ab5896cc"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1224,1247],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1224"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE may initiate the sidelink UE capability transfer procedure upon indication from upper layer when it needs (additional) UE radio access capability information.","paragraph_zero_based":1248},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.2.3Actions related to transmission of the UECapabilityEnquirySidelink by the UE","paragraph_zero_based":1249},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The initiating UE shall set the contents of UECapabilityEnquirySidelink message as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":1250},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>include in UE radio access capabilities for sidelink within ue-CapabilityInformationSidelink, if needed;","paragraph_zero_based":1251},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:It is up to initiating UE to decide whether ue-CapabilityInformationSidelink should be included.","paragraph_zero_based":1252},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>set frequencyBandListFilterSidelink to include frequency bands for which the peer UE is requested to provide supported bands and band combinations;","paragraph_zero_based":1253},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:The initiating UE is not allowed to send the UECapabilityEnquirySidelink message without including the field frequencyBandListFilterSidelink.","paragraph_zero_based":1254},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>submit the UECapabilityEnquirySidelink message to lower layers for transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":1255},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.2.4Actions related to reception of the UECapabilityEnquirySidelink by the UE","paragraph_zero_based":1256},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The peer UE shall set the contents of UECapabilityInformationSidelink message as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":1257},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>include UE radio access capabilities for sidelink within ue-CapabilityInformationSidelink;","paragraph_zero_based":1258},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>compile a list of \"candidate band combinations\" only consisting of bands included in frequencyBandListFilterSidelink, and prioritized in the order of frequencyBandListFilterSidelink (i.e. first include band combinations containing the first-listed band, then include remaining band combinations containing the second-listed band, and so on).","paragraph_zero_based":1259},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>include into supportedBandCombinationListSidelinkNR as many band combinations as possible from the list of \"candidate band combinations\", starting from the first entry;","paragraph_zero_based":1260},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>include the received frequencyBandListFilterSidelink in the field appliedFreqBandListFilter of the requested UE capability;","paragraph_zero_based":1261},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>submit the UECapabilityInformationSidelink message to lower layers for transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":1262},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:If the UE cannot include all band combinations due to message size or list size constraints, it is up to UE implementation which band combinations it prioritizes.","paragraph_zero_based":1263},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.3Sidelink radio link failure related actions","paragraph_zero_based":1264},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1265},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>upon indication from sidelink RLC entity that the maximum number of retransmissions for a specific destination has been reached; or","paragraph_zero_based":1266},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>upon T400 expiry for a specific destination; or","paragraph_zero_based":1267},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>upon indication from MAC entity that the maximum number of consecutive HARQ DTX for a specific destination has been reached; or","paragraph_zero_based":1268},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>upon integrity check failure indication from sidelink PDCP entity concerning SL-SRB2 or SL-SRB3 for a specific destination:","paragraph_zero_based":1269},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>consider sidelink radio link failure to be detected for this destination;","paragraph_zero_based":1270},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the DRBs of this destination, according to clause 5.8.9.1a.1;","paragraph_zero_based":1271}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["e2964393ab68c5706a5b7fc5150dd4372d955521345baa02b8006f1fa6abaa04","794dea14f0a4c65916bb0733e07cd2f1d4d109aaec30559cd41976c6c6502b67","76d2924762e17be150348e1ce396e4a9c5a3801d13c5e506111717022a42ff91","e50e58c2e943401734ce574a10615b70cc03f7a1013b67a5368a652a5676cfb0","6f5bc96acd225ba123585204df1c303d2dbed8b624c1fb3287823b757639491e","a0d3bb56ebb3b2c8de20153efd7fc5c700b0e793c81565b19717c7c24a330a12","1b480a7699a0d72048af97cdc2c0eb620bf295ae240d1e67890810648fb1366b","de0e8ae70090f312add6f9ce7359b69bb6fcfac2777281460d1b84ed33a81b5e","d0523f58930eb0e57092dd023912694f1cb3b935a9b82f73b03f0ff2d0006975","4c3fd7f95adf486f426c5b6b8dfbeebf6abf0ea54f77e1fd5680d5171a84f662","4ac703f076976e8bd73bd5a967cc526b3b3ee6d3a7d6a7cd3cd9830a8b1e76aa","3e91728efb4d5fe6a722d676ae7d59b5c14f4ee9a2f9883a44a0ce5a3f165ade","e23b9797501d815337411cc2f3f5b25b202d70a8bec90e40bd8fe00c496b3095","ccf9dd6e9f2996d6614ff11f1634b86dc76b4bc07676789f23b9a8e878ee479f","cf82ba07886ec3c1567120fac8def7d11cfc390310102c0135ee9c166e85412f","0cf376124511ba3d8393d97ea5869472e02721320baa74c21720007d5434711b","1174209adcea4084fa17ce50ba72fbea223c1563700c7476ea191607c32892bd","1975f0fd61707d8983e4e02231f05fd2d17fa87caefc40ef319970f928330177","d5ccc73065948445d0ec4cb42af18d2e8d167ff9fa5ed989fa93a91e2230f44a","e700488e8f5399dea4c1777ebf29c2bf65a776bcdc9112a2e7c6d7a3af088895","1d0504e553b33a5dcb1ae8dfe44a53de4ced22ad824f48630d0f827bd86658c4","609db438ef79880cb18c89e68bfffe67c435acd4555c62e0da132dd3a2811d6a","6e843a72b170aabccced65d746a800962c002b776cb703721a0181df3741687c","fda9beed4ecf92cfff74d42e187bd680c248ee21a953a794af5688b2da67b28a"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1248,1271],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1248"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the SRBs of this destination, according to clause 5.8.9.1a.3;","paragraph_zero_based":1272},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the PC5 Relay RLC channels of this destination if configured, in according to clause 5.8.9.7.1;","paragraph_zero_based":1273},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>discard the NR sidelink communication related configuration of this destination;","paragraph_zero_based":1274},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>reset the sidelink specific MAC of this destination;","paragraph_zero_based":1275},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>consider the PC5-RRC connection is released for the destination;","paragraph_zero_based":1276},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>indicate the release of the PC5-RRC connection to the upper layers for this destination (i.e. PC5 is unavailable);","paragraph_zero_based":1277},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if UE is in RRC_CONNECTED:","paragraph_zero_based":1278},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is acting as L2 U2N Remote UE for the destination:","paragraph_zero_based":1279},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate the RRC connection re-establishment procedure as specified in 5.3.7.","paragraph_zero_based":1280},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else:","paragraph_zero_based":1281},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>perform the sidelink UE information for NR sidelink communication procedure, as specified in 5.8.3.3;","paragraph_zero_based":1282},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Editor Note:FFS whether additional procedure for L2 U2U PC5 RLF initiation.","paragraph_zero_based":1283},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Editor Note: FFS on how to handle E2E PC5 connection and hop PC5 connection.","paragraph_zero_based":1284},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:It is up to UE implementation on whether and how to indicate to upper layers to maintain the keep-alive procedure [55].","paragraph_zero_based":1285},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.4Sidelink common control information","paragraph_zero_based":1286},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.4.1General","paragraph_zero_based":1287},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The sidelink common control information is carried by MasterInformationBlockSidelink. The sidelink common control information may change at any transmission, i.e. neither a modification period nor a change notification mechanism is used. This procedure also applies to NR sidelink discovery.","paragraph_zero_based":1288},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A UE configured to receive or transmit NR sidelink communication/discovery shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1289},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE has a selected SyncRef UE, as specified in 5.8.6:","paragraph_zero_based":1290},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>ensure having a valid version of the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message of that SyncRef UE;","paragraph_zero_based":1291},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.4.2Actions related to reception of MasterInformationBlockSidelink message","paragraph_zero_based":1292},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon receiving MasterInformationBlockSidelink, the UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1293},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>apply the values included in the received MasterInformationBlockSidelink message.","paragraph_zero_based":1294},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.4.3Transmission of MasterInformationBlockSidelink message","paragraph_zero_based":1295}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["1501dc7d31abfdc63b167550502b5ba9bb25a07207b2940bfc133fca1f3fe6d4","2852c9d9d288d9daae62a06819298827c489659a8b23ff53b5f85d8f04faaeb8","20033bb6a486cace52e63aadb34d37a046962e0788e0a5396aafefe9fc9782d9","e39af981b5c427e0831bdcbd69ebce94a712fe56669bfaa14b99eb15b0e0c645","65007d6563ea379e70cabd0bc7a2655490585d8a7174cbb8ac2fb0d2683981d8","d1e533c9d237ee9caec1ce85a60a1f24d52f21f8fe962cb2d2f9cff97d0a2ed8","1f7c4e079afc4d96876c298a17da939449efa74d2a9f4b0f997bb7ebf8bf6fc5","9b195ba5f92effe988dfb932ed595f6cc40c38d8ac4ee977f1dce4d1329aa6d9","4924e5dc35e345489a51a9b00670ab47c782d4dac74fb97de04010e57112232d","c21d16fe6bfb016a633e0557660165a075688e85854f6d6d672714fdde35be90","4edc50b39b274685ee38808016464b9dc9d7f04f8a8bef063c3cc7352c47bffd","5d6ead2495e34065ca5ee1204e46d637534d4f25a5c3adb0008115b83bc93ff7","2238e8d32ab69cdb10c6c5741c4168cea4d99d0c8a72ec937b6909d737a3aecf","023c7e880b58457dba3df3b9786a5f8ecc4739d7b8f888232cf014b40db32cf8","6ca3830afccd86fda462a877424aa8fa521f95388a17d472585124cb87f3ca5e","6c28d0687e4b60d19f6bae9db46a1ceb26841f52adb8fb2b37df7fe41ac09f7f","0d6f731d55d791bd2da45967837c6a372acf6ef2048904e6fa6ae6cd0f92e568","8c3be16fcf4b0de02363180d3fc6346e466ad65df99975781e6a4109e6fb48a7","ecad7fec0f4abf1aed0fa81ceaa45edb1da823706a54d31aabdcb268f7b3fb9b","eb1fe7ea454b55acc19d33cf53468e3ae93fe2d15a17235f467ac1662854dffe","f637143d84b8a86fd7e8e37b2a6cf97ec678cb81e41b57e02a9af0f06468afa1","859d12f054e0c876de367fcce354c722e1e25c97c34d780a16f3cf859909abf1","730b6a8b634739013ba7ee298ed44a13c57e36b7e1cd09224d8b3a4cd0602b39","444cd73779e2b37b4e6825e0a420ebb90a9a43de8b2274970fd8f073ec044cbe"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1272,1295],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1272"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall set the contents of the MasterInformationBlockSidelink message as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":1296},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if in coverage on the frequency used for the NR sidelink communication as defined in TS 38.304 [20].","paragraph_zero_based":1297},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set inCoverage to true;","paragraph_zero_based":1298},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if tdd-UL-DL-ConfigurationCommon is included in the received SIB1:","paragraph_zero_based":1299},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set sl-TDD-Config to the value representing the same meaning as that is included in tdd-UL-DL-ConfigurationCommon, as described in TS 38.213, clause 16.1 [13];","paragraph_zero_based":1300},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":1301},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set sl-TDD-Config to the value as specified in TS 38.213 [13], clause 16.1;","paragraph_zero_based":1302},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if syncInfoReserved is included in an entry of configured sl-SyncConfigList corresponding to the concerned frequency from the received SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":1303},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set reservedBits to the value of syncInfoReserved in the received SIB12;","paragraph_zero_based":1304},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":1305},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set all bits in reservedBits to 0;","paragraph_zero_based":1306},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if out of coverage on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication as defined in TS 38.304 [20]; and the concerned frequency is included in sl-FreqInfoToAddModList in RRCReconfiguration or in sl-FreqInfoList within SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":1307},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set inCoverage to true;","paragraph_zero_based":1308},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set reservedBits to the value of the corresponding field included in the preconfigured sidelink parameters (i.e. sl-PreconfigGeneral in SidelinkPreconfigNR defined in 9.3);","paragraph_zero_based":1309},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set sl-TDD-Config to the value representing the same meaning as that is included in the corresponding field included in the preconfigured sidelink parameters (i.e. sl-PreconfigGeneral in SL-PreconfigurationNR defined in 9.3) as described in TS 38.213, clause 16.1 [13];","paragraph_zero_based":1310},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if out of coverage on the frequency used for NR sidelink communication as defined in TS 38.304 [20]; and the UE selects GNSS as the synchronization reference and sl-SSB-TimeAllocation3 is not configured for the frequency used in SidelinkPreconfigNR:","paragraph_zero_based":1311},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set inCoverage to true;","paragraph_zero_based":1312},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set reservedBits to the value of the corresponding field included in the preconfigured sidelink parameters (i.e. sl-PreconfigGeneral in SidelinkPreconfigNR defined in 9.3);","paragraph_zero_based":1313},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set sl-TDD-Config to the value representing the same meaning as that is included in the corresponding field included in the preconfigured sidelink parameters (i.e. sl-PreconfigGeneral in SL-PreconfigurationNR defined in 9.3) as described in TS 38.213, clause 16.1 [13];","paragraph_zero_based":1314},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else if the UE has a selected SyncRef UE (as defined in 5.8.6):","paragraph_zero_based":1315},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set inCoverage to false;","paragraph_zero_based":1316},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set sl-TDD-Config and reservedBits to the value of the corresponding field included in the received MasterInformationBlockSidelink;","paragraph_zero_based":1317},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":1318},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set inCoverage to false;","paragraph_zero_based":1319}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["d6ca41e33f935d82338a2c54e4247f397834df85461ecf4702a55d6aab3fe4f3","ac8a8c2fa231443eea93e9d0bfb48d989503e5a3eff3311a9407f3cd311c941f","b6ceffb32a71c018488d549963b4bc859f6ed4e0202174df52b9d81817a12e56","27b9f1921176be0b73545bc8900e83b818ebcacb1fac7d02ac8577be9e01df1a","beef634db094f88991222cb95c3668516e55b7fc17a8c1b4f1921ee79b03c7e8","08134b4df0be8385b98ccfa94ac631f6e55625c0da3b338ee31d059ffde0e9f8","076d56afe8f19c32d03b6e3ba57e830ca15c4e9b77871440e9c57d69401d5bf0","4fa1dd1284819fcbe2912e0ac03dba5eb589be296b8a8882e93e915d070ed232","a31050aba3a5f97624a4d3d1209c3848cecb4800b0c2c80f773cc97962fbeee2","80e05eeaab649e704b05b7576f4e19b5cad7201d406d228256d5a2dee8cb06b7","80d26075d9d61a7a5913c8f5dbf303fd17f72b2d0ee32bd3656cbe3d828c4ebf","484c530a591cc5c338836b547160f8b6feff077cbf395d18dfb142c06bf39c56","85ffd3df7c899a2580387b67210150a99b1510adce4f1ccdb10440dc995a3235","1906418851ed21994c54deadc037f284ddff0e601f9183ac73d802050d83f1b3","2cdfa980f659060451fe17a6d1365d19f5ffe5486022f6916814838785fc7097","67d07fdda8820069769e04a71991c084794dc61c49103c079a304395f0ba4809","25d09109f62ed21ff795922b7d1d00a66a9778c36390e172a72d580c4765f0e0","a5f732ac852f45c822297b54176d38d0199722ec2a409738534545f6f118d60d","e1ae49c168313ed348cda13a184fe39665355da8e0d1bb0fa0dfa0ab00a43ded","7ea9110545707fa4570511e59673e4c43347c71d875fd49e6b16d47dd55953b6","fa844561c2acfdac282edd728748a555a99be5900a3747d8274f0a162c0669cd","22e2a983b118d2bca137b151ace4c36c793a6adfaade276140dd1e060fb31f83","c267814105cfd841e74f64b763332a0116f8f614c78360af7e7e0fab8bfd2f82","6de9c0ff2eda1d44df9ac53f8daad94d249c7dc1c4c00bfbc749e60344eb3694"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1296,1319],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1296"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>set reservedBits to the value of the corresponding field included in the preconfigured sidelink parameters (i.e. sl-PreconfigGeneral in SidelinkPreconfigNR defined in 9.3);","paragraph_zero_based":1320},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2> set sl-TDD-Config to the value representing the same meaning as that is included in the corresponding field included in the preconfigured sidelink parameters (i.e. sl-PreconfigGeneral in SL-PreconfigurationNR defined in 9.3) as described in TS 38.213, clause 16.1 [13];","paragraph_zero_based":1321},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>set directFrameNumber and slotIndex according to the slot used to transmit the SLSS, as specified in 5.8.5.3;","paragraph_zero_based":1322},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>submit the MasterInformationBlockSidelink to lower layers for transmission upon which the procedure ends;","paragraph_zero_based":1323},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.5Actions related to PC5-RRC connection release requested by upper layers","paragraph_zero_based":1324},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE initiates the procedure when upper layers request the release of the PC5-RRC connection as specified in TS 24.587 [57] or TS 24.554 [72]. The UE shall not initiate the procedure for power saving purposes.","paragraph_zero_based":1325},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1326},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the PC5-RRC connection release for the specific destination is requested by upper layers:","paragraph_zero_based":1327},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>discard the NR sidelink communication related configuration of this destination;","paragraph_zero_based":1328},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the DRBs of this destination if configured, in according to clause 5.8.9.1a.1;","paragraph_zero_based":1329},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the SRBs of this destination, in according to clause 5.8.9.1a.3;","paragraph_zero_based":1330},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the PC5 Relay RLC channels if configured, in according to clause 5.8.9.7.1;","paragraph_zero_based":1331},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>reset the sidelink specific MAC of this destination.","paragraph_zero_based":1332},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>consider the PC5-RRC connection is released for the destination;","paragraph_zero_based":1333},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.6Sidelink UE assistance information","paragraph_zero_based":1334},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.6.1General","paragraph_zero_based":1335},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":1336},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.9.6.1-1: Sidelink UE assistance information","paragraph_zero_based":1337},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is for a UE to inform its peer UE of the sidelink DRX assistance information used to determine the sidelink DRX configuration for unicast communication.","paragraph_zero_based":1338},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For sidelink unicast, a UE may include its desired sidelink DRX configurations in the UEAssistanceInformationSidelink as the sidelink DRX assistance information which is transmitted to its peer UE.","paragraph_zero_based":1339},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:It is up to UE implementation to determine its desired sidelink DRX configurations for unicast communication.","paragraph_zero_based":1340},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.6.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":1341},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For sidelink unicast, if both a RX UE and its peer TX UE for a direction of sidelink communication are capable of sidelink DRX, the RX UE that is interested in sending the sidelink DRX assistance information may send the UEAssistanceInformationSidelink as the sidelink DRX assistance information to its peer UE when the sidelink DRX assistance information has not been sent previously or when the previously transmitted sidelink DRX assistance information has changed.","paragraph_zero_based":1342},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.6.3Actions related to reception of UEAssistanceInformationSidelink message","paragraph_zero_based":1343}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["562bdd96426d130d55715a4c63c4b44f619aa63e1a5ada60898dd8bfe4f2b1be","b627ca0b7f8803ddaba823914860c04d21d7b3baaebd2631f788b8ea692215e8","568b5b1bd24132a11221f8cbaff36ce8bfb6524ce221d088bf2fbc1db0768710","585233b301c3a11f450bd3977418608f5c4570ff4969a4ad4fd000fd4da2a8b9","bc3c4edd0469f5b97e5164eaeddede102574dcdd71146ea20348260b06c54b22","06278311462e84b4ea7a09c13291979539767bc917550c151bd6bdc80b3cf64f","05c41081c1758be7a94e62740e9137901a254f5f757c1b94a1f9b5801fcb44c4","ce4eac772bf8c17bd9f438a2ae359f0751528f78389a237356bd87278dd19d62","b7822ff03ea51a203b61af2a1c3e3097aa58a162d560458c33938fe21277bde5","c974aa14858e1f69d1bb15d183743ee7e4551b7209a6cce0ba887446a5a508a5","5acd1ab8444cea38887dabe4911e8c86642a415166c75b2e3cb5aa5bd1b89564","5c5bdcdc0367fb7c790e31e38314530ee3f6a49933cad50e54e4a4af1f9133ad","44694525b85a3fc7bd8b55cb4f0f35c29564d8671dd6174f55f59ead3ab1299f","36fee90e6b0f786c37b8de319daba2090fe5cab7d2ea1f9d73cae77673b7ef6d","85fb66573a3e615821950df72c836f7a7ea83e5ca8668d2318cf6b2f19272b18","c75d9c20e7ffc8803f44555d5c7e327f0760456badec0dc380ecf8dcc030b399","deeff1e28d6ba538dbb3af7e6742760e9c9933f7ede693f4e3dbadb0a7680173","47c2f2169389e5c571e510e3deb4a68470271158ffe75a828085a6f7e7b43b91","fd5d39947f1a6e9028e3f75f22ef9d86229cbcc117f9daf0103d25d675f48d58","8c3107db5a6fb7d95c65153e5517ca56f4327cbc4fde82fd36835c29fd544066","ee2b8e5158d6aeab7837e9a32ae81e0e5e8f9ca5f71ade314b26d92aca204d64","c70394c5985562ed3d3746b0342489a689e90e746633b1bc2ac6180f393414e6","8e0dc5a7ae5c34ebcadd11f23d5c97b3a37c70de054cf1733e39aeafc2dc0e59","eebb3b2c136e708f1e1ff76ce18e086ebf2e405c45101c00efddd466f1596162"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1320,1343],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1320"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For sidelink unicast, when a UE is in RRC_CONNECTED and is performing sidelink operation with resource allocation mode 1, it may report the sidelink DRX assistance information received within the UEAssistanceInformationSidelink from its peer UE to the network as specified in 5.8.3. For sidelink unicast, when a UE is in RRC_CONNECTED and is performing sidelink operation with resource allocation mode 2 or is in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE or out of coverage, regardless of whether the UE has obtained the sidelink DRX assistance information from the UEAssistanceInformationSidelink transmitted from its peer UE or not, it may determine the sidelink DRX configuration SL-DRX-ConfigUC for its peer UE.","paragraph_zero_based":1344},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:When UE determines the sidelink DRX configuration for its peer UE, it may take the sidelink DRX assistance information received from its peer UE into account.","paragraph_zero_based":1345},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.7PC5 Relay RLC channel management for L2 U2N relay","paragraph_zero_based":1346},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.7.1PC5 Relay RLC channel release","paragraph_zero_based":1347},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1348},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the PC5 Relay RLC channel release was triggered after the reception of the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message; or","paragraph_zero_based":1349},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>after receiving the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message, if the PC5 Relay RLC channel release was triggered due to the configuration received within the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR:","paragraph_zero_based":1350},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each SL-RLC-ChannelID in sl-RLC-ChannelToReleaseList received in sl-ConfigDedicatedNR within RRCReconfiguration or for each SL-RLC-ChannelID included in the received sl-RLC-ChannelToReleaseListPC5 that is part of the current UE sidelink configuration:","paragraph_zero_based":1351},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>release the RLC entity and the corresponding logical channel associated with the SL-RLC-ChannelID;","paragraph_zero_based":1352},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the PC5 Relay RLC channel release was triggered for a specific destination by upper layers as specified in 5.8.9.5 or due to sidelink RLF as specified in 5.8.9.3:","paragraph_zero_based":1353},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the RLC entity and the corresponding logical channel associated with the SL-RLC-ChannelID of the specific destination;","paragraph_zero_based":1354},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.7.2PC5 Relay RLC channel addition/modification","paragraph_zero_based":1355},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon PC5-RRC connection establishment between the L2 U2N Relay UE and L2 U2N Remote UE, the L2 U2N Relay UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1356},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>establish a SRAP entity as specified in TS 38.351 [66], if no SRAP entity has been established;","paragraph_zero_based":1357},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>apply RLC specified configuration of SL-RLC0 as specified in clause 9.1.1.4:","paragraph_zero_based":1358},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>apply RLC default configuration of SL-RLC1 as defined in clause 9.2.4 if the L2 U2N Relay UE is in RRC_IDLE/INACTIVE state;","paragraph_zero_based":1359},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1360},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the PC5 Relay RLC channel addition/modification was triggered due to the reception of the RRCReconfigurationSidelink message; or","paragraph_zero_based":1361},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>after receiving the RRCReconfigurationCompleteSidelink message, if the PC5 Relay RLC channel addition/modification was triggered due to the configuration received within the sl-ConfigDedicatedNR:","paragraph_zero_based":1362},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the current configuration contains a PC5 Relay RLC channel with the received sl-RLC-ChannelID or sl-RLC-ChannelID-PC5:","paragraph_zero_based":1363},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>reconfigure the sidelink RLC entity in accordance with the received sl-RLC-Config or sl-RLC-ConfigPC5;","paragraph_zero_based":1364},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>reconfigure the sidelink MAC entity with a logical channel in accordance with the received sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfig or sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfigPC5;","paragraph_zero_based":1365},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else (a PC5 Relay RLC channel with the received sl-RLC-ChannelID or sl-RLC-ChannelID-PC5 was not configured before):","paragraph_zero_based":1366},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>establish a sidelink RLC entity in accordance with the received sl-RLC-Config or sl-RLC-ConfigPC5;","paragraph_zero_based":1367}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["0aed2b9918ba4c9d20f0d5a146a6153d8b0e317b38cbaf6408dccd8b12c97e19","043ba4e7e40ea123461a9ef8c1a64e95c96243c45876d4ecb32fcb7ce2d132e1","977526b77053859192eed37dab6bd3f426393922d3811133e87f2938b4768754","a7cc9cbe5c60aa1369d1feb0ec513cb292411b322939c63f5a52aa5f9ae14475","7dfa15fce52607989fe12f52c996c1fa05deceeaffdd83ba9ab0008fcd26851d","be499da6cf91ac17942db6f615167c6dcef129614acd20cc47e8b9802d6052ad","c2cf3641bb0ec8d8f70f620df8f219fd855631ae90d050b4488558f4ddbf8cc2","5e612ea47b17b610ea0a24c27cf1aa35cb9561a4f3706b83b339a245bb66e582","791f94a92eb8f8267603317fed807de899f589ea3f924c5cba5088cd2a9ab4d8","27d9e2b9d3d0c94618286c83bf2c271098668ff01b95f5014b4d4dc6930b578e","bdb0abeb1631227bc061b83ba4f13c8475a7187f47f98fc8d506ae3da71767eb","47a6a8a616d9535a9b1a968b08aa450da7d5ae6accd63e13d2601f0664c11b0f","ea1faa4ef328fc12213948cdf28b5efd570489631abe5b66c36f77fd9d2a6750","e6bed6e9a3a67dc2b75a912094f44fa331a44ca5d5192cfa51f152dafdb40329","5883fa1f12742b00b07f7b22ac2624ed63df247862642ff6a96bee315b00ae6f","53af1cd6dec05b6948243e60d85917ccd40fa87e8ad72b24ec63efc9a2a886f6","14556ef7108f51ac1562e22cf46c6a87d83dbfe6a71de5908f10e6f1ab66b2dd","61187e459181258bd53788bd68baa4a8e7ce40fc3d53fea9faf47857bf60c09c","b9ff5ec109c75e5ec57cfdb538564b2d6df4c0410340c19323bb2490243bb1bb","ddfb317f8367fac035dfc033868ddf0c5037dec8c5c0a708a9990740051f58b5","a6041383239961d201c6b1ba4966d01bdeda78401bf071e29bf22d2af9c6fc01","3d0a30b905426270399b9ebd28c36115f35247d9ffece95099ca1773957b864a","e2e190f17016735ffc92e1bc2006a107ff5ac05ba01f6e88c7a6d1fa4f3a16f3","ff927cee8c5666d27bc3dec9b8c514610d602447ffbd1f04bd60ac9f39ceb118"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1344,1367],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1344"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>configure the sidelink MAC entity with a logical channel in accordance with the received sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfig or sl-MAC-LogicalChannelConfigPC5.","paragraph_zero_based":1368},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.8Remote UE information","paragraph_zero_based":1369},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.8.1General","paragraph_zero_based":1370},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":1371},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.9.8.1-1: Remote UE information","paragraph_zero_based":1372},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This procedure is used by the L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE/RRC_INACTIVE to inform about the required SIB(s) and provide Paging related information to the connected L2 U2N Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":1373},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:MIB is not required by a L2 U2N Remote UE.","paragraph_zero_based":1374},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.8.2Actions related to transmission of RemoteUEInformationSidelink message","paragraph_zero_based":1375},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When entering RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE, or upon change in any of the information in the RemoteUEInformationSidelink while in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE, the L2 U2N Remote UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1376},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE has not stored a valid version of a SIB, in accordance with clause 5.2.2.2.1, of one or several required SIB(s) in accordance with clause 5.2.2.1 and the requested SIB has not been indicated in RemoteUEInformationSidelink message to the L2 U2N Relay UE before:","paragraph_zero_based":1377},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>include sl-RequestedSIB-List in the RemoteUEInformationSidelink to indicate the requested SIB(s);","paragraph_zero_based":1378},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE has not sent sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE in the RemoteUEInformationSidelink message to the L2 U2N Relay UE before, set sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":1379},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the L2 U2N Remote UE is in RRC_IDLE:","paragraph_zero_based":1380},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>include ng-5G-S-TMSI in the sl-PagingIdentityRemoteUE;","paragraph_zero_based":1381},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE specific DRX cycle is configured by upper layer, set sl-PagingCycleRemoteUE to the value of UE specific Uu DRX cycle configured by upper layer;","paragraph_zero_based":1382},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the L2 U2N Remote UE is in RRC_INACTIVE:","paragraph_zero_based":1383},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>include ng-5G-S-TMSI and fullI-RNTI in the sl-PagingIdentityRemoteUE;","paragraph_zero_based":1384},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE specific DRX cycle is configured by upper layer,","paragraph_zero_based":1385},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set sl-PagingCycleRemoteUE to the minimum value of UE specific Uu DRX cycles (configured by upper layer and configured by RRC);","paragraph_zero_based":1386},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else:","paragraph_zero_based":1387},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>set sl-PagingCycleRemoteUE to the value of UE specific DRX cycle configured by RRC;","paragraph_zero_based":1388},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>submit the RemoteUEInformationSidelink message to lower layers for transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":1389},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When entering RRC_CONNECTED, if L2 U2N remote UE had sent sl-RequestedSIB-List and/or sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE, the L2 U2N Remote UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1390},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>set the sl-RequestedSIB-List to the value release if requested before;","paragraph_zero_based":1391}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["fb92b20cefd630ab6ddcef9f9f1f1e56676d204691d95b1724464b628ceb5b3d","c52527775ea4875856d480cdd3e9dc40e5ddf0f29de53ff2f8e08ca55cc17e1e","8e6695bd5a2d8f8f01b9af4800dc4de5a8fe41d1fbdd5455e4ee8268223e02a6","8476c3503d695d2e3b87711045ac0b0a232699ea2add58a84affcedf0a97d0a5","f3c80b376dd27cbdcfbdf2495b329897dfc8a205225cc5539d927b5df1d22d1f","50c868aab6210a75e0c3f04b942b4c17434d683d6956a49f8a10071062c99778","ea1557bd8b3bbe437461ef649a7ccf19963157f7af51d2b279079328cad54c72","423a90aba5f945676db4e5c95ac3fde4d5497b65428cd9e1da62e4eaf9512ff7","2a9c6873d156a24e19201181d4dd5433e2198d943979694b9aca8dc952be03ce","6805b66c79e1da9beeecbdaf849d7196a3b77d0cc1b8c0542615f69ed20cb9c1","8cb036225b6a90b6d91ed69809a4c5361280ed3c03afb423d91c41e823e11cbb","6b085fac8f6b1c31d48c481a5ee45eafaa01d4b2d8783482e861e75db19102a0","900ea05e348d0c3929955b8a05fa8876fc8b979da220da8fa6bade0095aeac20","e63ce2e465d4159b6066ee9a7e75bcb6f3bcf807043e6c4e212acb38dbe4cde1","3b9df8b4ea4ab637b97acaa8e5e8dc58784eef338884c00f2089ed21fcf1cba8","24e59351cab3968b70854889d1be7e49e4ad67414cf6333d5c559959e82a1c37","8165bd32205986ca0debb5958fed37af32e5949469741c9bb66b18c589730cd8","58ac9290987d55df335595b58135fcaa1e8a6b6c4f68df8eef0207ce410c2ede","5a02e4b9fa3e63b06d5f23e7128bd1ff93ace7dd4782cc3f4249159bf2dc8fc8","94627380032159a4d247de6e4020bd0ae9cee5bdd4957f25fe05e6d56ea522ed","49f9e77dc9814b8b89d4f0ac19b5a715cb60f1f6c248951ba9778268695196c9","ab464f648682b82c8d1f7aa57267154397225efd421706724cbbb0fbcaa69e5b","dc0148fad2294b81575a9d368744a07675d53e8e90464a79f73ff6a024dacecd","385915325a3db2f6b02ce94a26f99b9bc86b8c3c91c7890b7951f624bf5b7405"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1368,1391],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1368"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>set the sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE to the value release if sent before;","paragraph_zero_based":1392},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>submit the RemoteUEInformationSidelink message to lower layers for transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":1393},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.8.3Reception of RemoteUEInformationSidelink message by the L2 U2N Relay UE","paragraph_zero_based":1394},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The L2 U2N Relay UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1395},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RemoteUEInformationSidelink includes the sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE:","paragraph_zero_based":1396},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is in RRC_CONNECTED on an active BWP with common search space configured including pagingSearchSpace; or","paragraph_zero_based":1397},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE:","paragraph_zero_based":1398},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE is set to setup:","paragraph_zero_based":1399},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>monitor the Paging message at the L2 U2N Remote UE's paging occasion calculated according to sl-PagingIdentityRemoteUE and sl-PagingCycleRemoteUE included in sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE;","paragraph_zero_based":1400},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else (the sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE is set to release):","paragraph_zero_based":1401},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>stop monitoring the Paging message at the L2 U2N Remote UE's paging occasion;","paragraph_zero_based":1402},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>release the received paging information in sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE;","paragraph_zero_based":1403},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else (the UE is in RRC_CONNECTED on an active BWP without pagingSearchSpace configured):","paragraph_zero_based":1404},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE is set to setup:","paragraph_zero_based":1405},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>include the received sl-PagingIdentityRemoteUE in SidelinkUEInformationNR message and perform Sidelink UE information transmission in accordance with 5.8.3;","paragraph_zero_based":1406},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else (the sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE is set to release):","paragraph_zero_based":1407},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>initiate transmission of the SidelinkUEInformationNR message to release the sl-PagingIdentityRemoteUE in SidelinkUEInformationNR message in accordance with 5.8.3;","paragraph_zero_based":1408},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>release the received paging information in sl-PagingInfo-RemoteUE;","paragraph_zero_based":1409},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RemoteUEInformationSidelink includes the sl-RequestedSIB-List:","paragraph_zero_based":1410},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-RequestedSIB-List is set to setup:","paragraph_zero_based":1411},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3> if the L2 U2N Relay UE has not stored a valid version of SIB(s) indicated in sl-RequestedSIB-List:","paragraph_zero_based":1412},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>perform acquisition of the system information indicated in sl-RequestedSIB-List in accordance with 5.2.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1413},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the Uu message transfer procedure in accordance with 5.8.9.9;","paragraph_zero_based":1414},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the sl-RequestedSIB-List is set to release:","paragraph_zero_based":1415}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["87d6d6fc149d9dcfb1de3fa3b99e95b690d40721483d799992169d4c628825e3","9096258843b8704b4c6d43729854e21b147940df1f1860a582872449b8daf23a","fc6ef7016d4a10529a798e34be48cb4f3d79977d5bb3c70f9a74cf8b7581185a","955d460585eb6a6e63204ecd43b62901fe8181db80eb93c3144f8cc53a8f378e","041781042c31b2b2fbf15dd9ad6bd99cf8dc68ae103b32600eb1ddc688195243","d7d6e950bea9d85e9812d9cc8b5d3aa7a7ff885c7172a51a6cbc50ca044f463d","6e8c0061d8b08e19b10e0bc343029f8b0e05080db5d17c1fc2422b19d7681caa","81804f98deb572a6aefaac440ebce1bc85103e8f0953e103edda9eb3e026f9ff","acdccb54f7d10323f26dca2cf2e1a5098e6d32f9e7bf265fecbf6acbcfea54a3","cd1eec66711e348b6b9bf60d0241ff9e4587a936c9c87e20f08b81950af52f56","4023f8d116339c24a4aba919a06323aec4136a37d84cd62d1a695c7e8fd90e3d","2c48699bf18364f0e406dd732bbb44b7857fbc3da013a257c3772dbf47cd8043","c1f0194c72542b6db96db136213d4d630ee91755230e7a3f0dafb1a8e1252c78","1b6d8278b4e995232946bf3080b60ebbe98bb74bc2ad78b9d6b68dc1c65b4602","57334da092946d0cca2b8555cda86eb116e22086d8c3c04ec5ebf589754556f4","bf29282fe77ab7da7ece9b1e29c1e4fefee7eb0516ee4994b6abe708ac64ef1d","fdd2a8287c73a14cc93c7581953a1ca84949f72129f6653b5c53a953cf436627","e5eb5c116288a71761506ee82bffd7797502eb5d653b69260467d0783031e27a","aec561223d763216add2cb02d983de0641dcece1c5e55fb5d927afc290ff8c40","71d4352590f89c0ec7eb26475f0b3813289cf59973839c4d4f77cab8b9d72d91","bc4529f07c6fe86966632c8cb8ba61b466b6f003f7dafe84f82dbbcada87dae0","8f39c8398887fe8231c056cb5028599228f77a1fe2b71cba5083f62b62f313cf","30bdb326971877f83a3b7f30e020c741d939784568d5a24a2ad15b1b745a5d1c","46a49cefd328727240a9fa2aeafdb48ad5e7ba2c4f2909ed82cab55d6ef2492c"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1392,1415],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1392"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>release received SIB request in sl-RequestedSIB-List.","paragraph_zero_based":1416},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.9Uu message transfer in sidelink","paragraph_zero_based":1417},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.9.1General","paragraph_zero_based":1418},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":1419},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.9.9.1-1: Uu message transfer in sidelink","paragraph_zero_based":1420},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The purpose of this procedure is to transfer Paging message and System Information from the L2 U2N Relay UE to the L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE/RRC_INACTIVE.","paragraph_zero_based":1421},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.9.2Actions related to transmission of UuMessageTransferSidelink message","paragraph_zero_based":1422},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The L2 U2N Relay UE initiates the Uu message transfer procedure when at least one of the following conditions is met:","paragraph_zero_based":1423},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>upon receiving Paging message related to the connected L2 U2N Remote UE from network (including Paging message within RRCReconfiguration message);","paragraph_zero_based":1424},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>upon acquisition of the SIB(s) requested by the connected L2 U2N Remote UE (as indicated in sl-RequestedSIB-List in the RemoteUEInformationSidelink) or upon receiving the updated SIB(s) from network which has been requested by the connected L2 U2N Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":1425},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>upon unsolicited SIB1 forwarding to the connected L2 U2N Remote UE or upon receiving the updated SIB1 from network;","paragraph_zero_based":1426},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For each associated L2 U2N Remote UE, the L2 U2N Relay UE shall set the contents of UuMessageTransferSidelink message as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":1427},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>include sl-PagingDelivery if the Paging message received from network containing the ue-Identity of the L2 U2N Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":1428},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>include sl-SIB1-Delivery if any of the conditions for initiating Uu message transfer procedure related to SIB1 are met;","paragraph_zero_based":1429},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>include sl-SystemInformationDelivery if any of the conditions for initiating Uu message transfer procedure related to System Information are met;","paragraph_zero_based":1430},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>submit the UuMessageTransferSidelink message to lower layers for transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":1431},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:The L2 U2N Relay UE may perform unsolicited forwarding of SIB1 to the L2 U2N Remote UE based on UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":1432},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.9.3Reception of the UuMessageTransferSidelink","paragraph_zero_based":1433},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon receiving the UuMessageTransferSidelink message, the L2 U2N Remote UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1434},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if sl-PagingDelivery is included:","paragraph_zero_based":1435},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the paging reception procedure as specified in clause 5.3.2.3;","paragraph_zero_based":1436},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if sl-SystemInformationDelivery and/or sl-SIB1-Delivery is included:","paragraph_zero_based":1437},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the actions specified in clause 5.2.2.4.","paragraph_zero_based":1438},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.10Notification Message","paragraph_zero_based":1439}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["5b7c34b75fda30b368ede57e0eb2b525341a27ca94aeb69be315dfd04e1c0bcc","b2e2ac0499806d4ac9518674daaf19efbdac74d62ac1a4d929233cb199505407","25e4585c0228e61e72f3c6041fa196aa6bb7fa6a7edc6ebe4d6247ac454ba174","52079153e8b7ab454bae75237adb5a96cd7ad1626bdba0263093d9ad258e52ba","de90eb248b7e632ad646551a45e2002db8957b9cc23217e9765d0b5fcac01ee5","9a75d57faec83a60fad851cf22e63aed26a54d3c482ba6f1b3e90b02799d55db","9b6f6b6f14973bc538a37691d2c00c59920ef78e1bd2afc6bd8857f2ffe7cd1c","b59893806f7abef56d0ab8b794801d01267e7b8f713b839fc24b84e6138cae23","daaa45bc86add4e28fff38b00bdd7eba96f5dbc23ff2826cfbc532e62947522c","d2d997466736e5d07c0ef86ce7b608489eb369300d653aee510e93ba0d3ea8d3","ccee3a74ba11963706e1e3ec7967be55a4fb096ca8fdf669097f59be07eaa2d9","2d9ae0c342d8de00fdf78438a04bf0ab048f3de93b6d0ea1566020f1ad3b591b","13f42508cef10c42aa6cf532bc4ae258a781943b46f44af7c6373f7fa537fd60","66812aea88f33510ff105cedf582bf5f84cb3f8400b26781a6395e1d1811644d","43b747525b7a5ad6cc1091a33a2b60773270409e5401a2bf16c4bb7f1b8ce286","e69ba542d24f2a9753a94fbdc31231bb258e14a0cd7c7d8cadf015c03faa4287","bd368109dd4c0eee59633234ea1a28e513bff407e247fab273983f0531862e2e","e0793114bd88fc1ecba35de67484be17261f8d0f61100ba2bf2d4d3b24e928d4","9ae3d1d515bbda91826d1fe73113571f04cfe350d7e51d6a488d2b0f66971db8","92ce781f61af3df38e9570082197ac67b3c11e632062b2c3d72f3c4de8b8cfc7","95a15c7d9407343684db2dd9d11ac91ece1fde9a8134dc228bb2e47d4d44e306","a5bdcb0eb2a384a9d097bd5a9d32b1213caac5caa64cf37526f5a6254edd217c","cb13167b40a1bbbe82cd2a29caea6861dd379dc9b2d5453ac18ec79761067ecb","5a410cdb1e35c9d1f9307f4ba9296ce94de5cda0a0e090ffb011705f33a99907"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1416,1439],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1416"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.10.1General","paragraph_zero_based":1440},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":1441},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Figure 5.8.9.8.1-1: Notification message in sidelink","paragraph_zero_based":1442},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This procedure is used by a U2N Relay UE to send notification to the connected U2N Remote UE, or used by a U2U Relay UE to send notification to the peer connected U2U Remote UE when condition(s) as specified in 5.8.9.10.2 is met with the connected U2U Remote UE.","paragraph_zero_based":1443},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.10.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":1444},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The Relay UE may initiate the procedure when one of the following conditions is met:","paragraph_zero_based":1445},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as U2N Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":1446},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>upon Uu RLF as specified in 5.3.10;","paragraph_zero_based":1447},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>upon reception of an RRCReconfiguration including the reconfigurationWithSync;","paragraph_zero_based":1448},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>upon cell reselection;","paragraph_zero_based":1449},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>upon L2 U2N Relay UE's RRC connection failure including RRC connection reject as specified in 5.3.3.5 and 5.3.13.10, and T300 expiry as specified in 5.3.3.7, and RRC resume failure as specified in 5.3.13.5;","paragraph_zero_based":1450},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as L2 U2U Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":1451},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>upon detection of PC5 RLF with L2 U2U Remote UE as specified in 5.8.9.3;","paragraph_zero_based":1452},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Editor Note: FFS the previous agreement “When the remote UE receives PC5-RLF indication from the U2U relay UE, it would inform upper layers and rely on upper layers to trigger relay reselection (or not).” applies to L3 U2U relay or not, including whether there is a need for the PC5-RLF indication in this case.","paragraph_zero_based":1453},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.10.3Actions related to transmission of NotificationMessageSidelink message","paragraph_zero_based":1454},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The Relay UE shall set the indication type as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":1455},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as U2N Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":1456},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE initiates transmission of the NotificationMessageSidelink message due to Uu RLF:","paragraph_zero_based":1457},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the indicationType as relayUE-Uu-RLF;","paragraph_zero_based":1458},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the UE initiates transmission of the NotificationMessageSidelink message due to reconfiguration with sync:","paragraph_zero_based":1459},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the indicationType as relayUE-HO;","paragraph_zero_based":1460},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else if the UE initiates transmission of the NotificationMessageSidelink message due to cell reselection:","paragraph_zero_based":1461},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the indicationType as relayUE-CellReselection;","paragraph_zero_based":1462},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE initiates transmission of the NotificationMessageSidelink message due to Uu RRC connection establishment/Resume failure:","paragraph_zero_based":1463}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["a50b7380d1af080a914789dba502c452b2a73a3967c906cea44f2b4b4aa042fc","bffe411c6d8fb7270dbfe613fe032a29712adf8442238034881dfde238ece824","eb429ba8bed3637d8eeda49e0ce52bcca747377dea1e9b76d583456ce96fabb8","ede875730fdd808815d2d580ecc665b143f410e706e1f51efabf9893000446da","c1a34ef6f2fe9e3d74c8511be0f46dd0a8eee70fd9fa42b3972c7ae378d5215f","67efa38d95df7f41fc45ed191d05caa2d143a08869ab4f0b8401a4550e8be5dc","3d99830cc00c94569e82de5ce813b6c21c89bb080473bd3105f76cdb2693212f","cab2f2cd1f4ad4a9d077de37c29da2631fcabf70b6a658a070622d4e2134df2f","d632d68f8000fdffad551c155f416e3991f2141ae53115a29e2786b1c6f27313","d7a27928bcba00730a92fb5197b891de00f0ffd81a04ce01aa8f5126212a15b3","3e1950d0ef682d9cc8d96c0d4061511ae9bb8354749330e52cb6840961481dad","1023a196187ce723ed9f0ba9d2ac3d4c3d45db70d4389bf5902e63930618b7de","4367161434a2a1b55d6fe0b4cb807c5383b2b3d91bdf22dea94aa7fbcb3e15dc","85c0e0b9370bb7268453eab8ad6c4bfda9d1081fb4ab0d913a7793b3879b50ab","5b9452727a564478d248dfe42f4a41e3158e4991b85380181ed1e4383572265c","3c3870760c34c136a13a98b1cbe7fccac9676f4ae8acc71fb6f11cf0895b67ca","c12b083399cf151a6ab1500fc6331024c6471343679e1e343a80664c9c94c278","08ac3779eb2e19f110707bc518f836eb8c1fa384cf2611b27954026afa91c578","f889843dd87acca3f4ccae7f8d94ecd59eeca29a4735d869221ae20fad48cbb0","9ab84a29b5a8ab542c960b6c22d805efcef486be166880bc78c3ad4316fe406f","e1d9fe3229098802c5e13e675a1988b38f07c67efb5161fa7cdbbaf039e8688d","bc933e87cc1c8df83647702ce18b5da8759311469b5dbba601685209b0dfbd2a","d287e8f80f9de4d3b9cad9470ead8ec154f819dd31e782f68c1add39eeb4707e","569546bb7516d7166b22a508e5c445222433fb9ccd24212566e6aa30bac90f4e"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1440,1463],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1440"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the indicationType as relayUE-Uu-RRC-Failure;","paragraph_zero_based":1464},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>submit the NotificationMessageSidelink message to lower layers for transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":1465},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as L2 U2U Relay UE:","paragraph_zero_based":1466},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE initiates transmission of the NotificationMessageSidelink message due to PC5 RLF with L2 U2U Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":1467},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the sl-IndicationType as relayUE-PC5-RLF;","paragraph_zero_based":1468},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>set the sl-DestinationIdentity as the associated destination for L2 U2U Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":1469},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>determine the submission of the NotificationMessageSidelink message to peer L2 U2U Remote UE;","paragraph_zero_based":1470},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>submit the NotificationMessageSidelink message to lower layers for transmission;","paragraph_zero_based":1471},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":1472},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.9.10.4Actions related to reception of NotificationMessageSidelink message","paragraph_zero_based":1473},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Upon receiving the NotificationMessageSidelink, the Remote UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1474},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as U2N Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":1475},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the indicationType is included:","paragraph_zero_based":1476},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the UE is L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_CONNECTED:","paragraph_zero_based":1477},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if T301 is not running, initiate the RRC connection re-establishment procedure as specified in 5.3.7;","paragraph_zero_based":1478},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>else (the UE is L3 U2N Remote UE, or L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE):","paragraph_zero_based":1479},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>if the PC5-RRC connection with the U2N Relay UE is determined to be released:","paragraph_zero_based":1480},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>indicate upper layers to trigger PC5 unicast link release;","paragraph_zero_based":1481},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>else (i.e., maintain the PC5 RRC connection):","paragraph_zero_based":1482},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5>if the UE is L2 U2N Remote UE and the indicationType is relayUE-HO or relayUE-CellReselection:","paragraph_zero_based":1483},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"6>consider cell re-selection occurs;","paragraph_zero_based":1484},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:For L3 U2N Remote UE, or L2 U2N Remote UE in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE, it is up to Remote UE implementation whether to release or keep the PC5 unicast link.","paragraph_zero_based":1485},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 2:The L2 U2N Remote UE may ignore the NotificationMessageSidelink if it does not release the PC5 unicast link in source side yet during an indirect-to-direct path switch, i.e. T304 is running.","paragraph_zero_based":1486},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the UE is acting as L2 U2U Remote UE:","paragraph_zero_based":1487}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["503e7d8f0d3fbed8e19a1aca89993288049f8ec6ad106800cd541e4c209f4672","c66b2b497127d9c2ccc947ef86f07a183c4269769ad381dd2cbc719d5a751847","e68be6000f9222e5d2dd79c85b8e3bcf8221c9fa08b22eb7a497d2af8e81d2e8","952c51e8ceda0412016e4ec2498dfdff78dc7ba75fb754507a1306e248e68575","57351c414bd00ca83abec858587e4103292e8c7e228bcd735c509ebb716542b6","3fff5cf139677e45a74ce2b025a0da5dfa7028a19c3a555ed262e31d5f09265c","cd6027d043f9992bf863fd85d17e5626b66051b645a48bfd1ae848a8ac260c57","f4f993fbdee1d8a0a60afd76b8e7b12b78a703cb7d842ce498cca8c75c264e0c","1533726694040f1b00f160159119c589be82d8ddf0a5cef91cc01083065f8689","dfcea5fae9941cad73a48973af0cc8568a40c618839f6455247ab7ff1d7d147e","369c088fa5425e3fc1615871faab2e26483938fd70c71fb18f7fc6e4121365c1","5a6cb23bb41da60a4c7b5f00b4e79842cdba232b9096474443535fdc88a09f84","50846db86654cd303d0d312b3821721126b651ca8420d58dd3879e153e762288","b33ceceb92697f0be243165591fed872d1f930623703cf0cc59ec8451049e822","c319f1e0fb7209777df29dc6855edaea1dc5ae9ff8fcdae3fc05deeaa519abca","37405f5afa78fd292cfa37cba7ef651d146b8ff94c10c39a67647f14e8ccc62f","33d35fb6b97fb1780345c8b4ac95f9592b8b33d173e16797818917c936e79447","8b92bda62ef27c62d98304f4f073745953655637bf5adf30ff71ec2b7776d642","3e8382be0ebbb4e373c30efaf8d8af09df6e07520984ae3108e70c2170380d40","0da8ea1283432d2157bd834435b39ea6534e412ac950581fdf2f8fc93a326875","9b7dd448e26acbccc28840d91c1a3e4274bf27f4974966f65c7967014339f943","9ca266137d555822e616c4cca36ee7e415523da789ae41a29284c46338893b8e","b5f125ae56dec9ba69078bcb5a589c05d049007c19f5c50fe8fd1019deb82d4a","215c72e61020280ec70329d5f61b86bb3061d8c1ffefc2f9bb6c35bb20804221"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1464,1487],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1464"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if sl-IndicationType is relayUE-PC5-RLF:","paragraph_zero_based":1488},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>indicate PC5 RLF received from U2U Relay UE to the upper layers for the indicated L2 U2N Remote UE based on the received sl-DestinationIdentity;","paragraph_zero_based":1489},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE X:It is up to the upper layers on whether to trigger U2U Relay reselection after the PC5 RLF indication received from U2U Relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":1490},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Editor Note:FFS if there would be any constraints on the Remote UE implementation behaviour to keep or release the PC5 link with the relay UE.","paragraph_zero_based":1491},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10Sidelink measurement","paragraph_zero_based":1492},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.1Introduction","paragraph_zero_based":1493},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE may configure the associated peer UE to perform NR sidelink measurement and report on the corresponding PC5-RRC connection in accordance with the NR sidelink measurement configuration for unicast by RRCReconfigurationSidelink message.","paragraph_zero_based":1494},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The NR sidelink measurement configuration includes the following parameters for a PC5-RRC connection:","paragraph_zero_based":1495},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1.NR sidelink measurement objects: Object(s) on which the associated peer UE shall perform the NR sidelink measurements.","paragraph_zero_based":1496},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For NR sidelink measurement, a NR sidelink measurement object indicates the NR sidelink frequency of reference signals to be measured.","paragraph_zero_based":1497},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2.NR sidelink reporting configurations: NR sidelink measurement reporting configuration(s) where there can be one or multiple NR sidelink reporting configurations per NR sidelink measurement object. Each NR sidelink reporting configuration consists of the following:","paragraph_zero_based":1498},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Reporting criterion: The criterion that triggers the UE to send a NR sidelink measurement report. This can either be periodical or a single event description.","paragraph_zero_based":1499},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-RS type: The RS that the UE uses for NR sidelink measurement results. In this release, only DMRS is supported for NR sidelink measurement.","paragraph_zero_based":1500},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Reporting format: The quantities that the UE includes in the measurement report. In this release, only RSRP measurement is supported.","paragraph_zero_based":1501},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3.NR sidelink measurement identities: A list of NR sidelink measurement identities where each NR sidelink measurement identity links one NR sidelink measurement object with one NR sidelink reporting configuration. By configuring multiple NR sidelink measurement identities, it is possible to link more than one NR sidelink measurement object to the same NR sidelink reporting configuration, as well as to link more than one NR sidelink reporting configuration to the same NR sidelink measurement object. The NR sidelink measurement identity is also included in the NR sidelink measurement report that triggered the reporting, serving as a reference to the network.","paragraph_zero_based":1502},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.NR sidelink quantity configurations: The NR sidelink quantity configuration defines the NR sidelink measurement filtering configuration used for all event evaluation and related reporting, and for periodical reporting of that NR sidelink measurement. In each configuration, different filter coefficients can be configured for different NR sidelink measurement quantities.","paragraph_zero_based":1503},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Both UEs of the PC5-RRC connection maintains a NR sidelink measurement object list, a NR sidelink reporting configuration list, and a NR sidelink measurement identities list according to signalling and procedures in this specification.","paragraph_zero_based":1504},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2Sidelink measurement configuration","paragraph_zero_based":1505},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2.1General","paragraph_zero_based":1506},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1507},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-MeasObjectToRemoveList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":1508},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink measurement object removal procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.4;","paragraph_zero_based":1509},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-MeasObjectToAddModList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":1510},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink measurement object addition/modification procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.5;","paragraph_zero_based":1511}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_sha256":"470fa87ca234afd3cdd6813f454487933839ab990f95bcfa5c1735fcd90b61bf","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["853191f07bebd4abd45bd1f75f74045a1512b665b11434844e24cae51192b3c7","0fddc7b253fcf7acb9b1de1db848e141c2545f56e0200435af81ce43e480f7af","2eae61c71859ccd13a445837317df0957b04baa36a26d5fa6c4cb755e18b9312","c1388ece25fc646a3badb78d1035837931e10defd84caa09b9ef464974b246bb","b17b3ddaf62ab334fdf2d77fd45fd22e6212da2ba3242d4c01c78fbb4ae4ba28","bc70a0298ad54ca22ec22e5a769566b60f1f56095f64c26d8119f9ed4e4e1cdb","133e3fed9d31abd2cd176a2b92337fbb2e66023fc1db52223f819ee36041fd42","3c7afd37b3a6f705995b879ad2b329dcf65c11429a2b9e8082cc703ee450558a","dcd695bd087c343ea8ac995156d2bf12b4b694c0e385e69488a1244b79563ab7","e9c9e21546e3698b24531ee05500b0d33bd394542d956d0e5e271613a5bf8054","e4cc0a666f856e36e6e4131d6b40ab178c2f63d407aebdb7cc8ed042d530277b","c7843afc9eb10e668e9452bfd64d6bbfc4729f2aac462cb716e6dee7f3e87dc9","f564955794f9357a33db4d0b911d5ca1bc10248cb8604c63aeb6d360e5e08c7f","a42c00013cc38229724718077cfc5e394dee9e2a269242c41eb480a42c88745b","bfd25bf5fc3fb7c90b3ee28f2392e837f84d80022308181470d40bf7edcadd6f","0925a1f72d4f302e1faac4a75f5dbfb7efbaaafc6b9479e65f932f9836a4b612","c51088db48ff973688be3691afc70562f023ba27e4783e29af88c1c3dd4749e7","7fd89b3fdc53bfed188f5f29fe0463f6c583e931b8fc9631197f26228e210711","5f56bc693990865b6dbabfb2b03e11ac4a1379ae472e129ea61ae700ab28fadd","edac91cc4ed9525a58b1cfce13542fa7eac3ea6bcdc2a5d8f7a4357637abad46","8fef06a2b97b60c111babfbfd75caaee137d400a5800659dea1d54ec242a739d","804ccdd1cfca2d04cfb88015c8791532ae57ad27ba2a8bd9351848ca4475994a","239f26bd6f7fcf6a88c09e5bb55be111e3568b944c98dc9e5a9ba4dddf154659","0ea45d283303d112bc7b8cf136376f8ebff3acd495cbf137be9a30f8dd968e25"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[1488,1511],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx:p1488"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311934.zip::R2-2311934_Introduction of NR sidelink U2U relay.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-ReportConfigToRemoveList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":1512},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink reporting configuration removal procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.6;","paragraph_zero_based":1513},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-ReportConfigToAddModList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":1514},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink reporting configuration addition/modification procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.7;","paragraph_zero_based":1515},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-QuantityConfig in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":1516},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink quantity configuration procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.8;","paragraph_zero_based":1517},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-MeasIdToRemoveList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":1518},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink measurement identity removal procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.2;","paragraph_zero_based":1519},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the received sl-MeasConfig includes the sl-MeasIdToAddModList in the RRCReconfigurationSidelink:","paragraph_zero_based":1520},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the sidelink measurement identity addition/modification procedure as specified in 5.8.10.2.3;","paragraph_zero_based":1521},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2.2Sidelink measurement identity removal","paragraph_zero_based":1522},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1523},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-MeasId included in the received sl-MeasIdToRemoveList that is part of the current UE configuration in VarMeasConfigSL:","paragraph_zero_based":1524},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>remove the entry with the matching sl-MeasId from the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL;","paragraph_zero_based":1525},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>remove the NR sidelink measurement reporting entry for this sl-MeasId from the VarMeasReportListSL, if included;","paragraph_zero_based":1526},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>stop the periodical reporting timer and reset the associated information (e.g. sl-TimeToTrigger) for this sl-MeasId.","paragraph_zero_based":1527},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:The UE does not consider the message as erroneous if the sl-MeasIdToRemoveList includes any sl-MeasId value that is not part of the current UE configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":1528},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.8.10.2.3Sidelink measurement identity addition/modification","paragraph_zero_based":1529},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall:","paragraph_zero_based":1530},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>for each sl-MeasId included in the received sl-MeasIdToAddModList:","paragraph_zero_based":1531},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if an entry with the matching sl-MeasId exists in the sl-MeasIdList within the VarMeasConfigSL:","paragraph_zero_based":1532},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>replace the entry with the value received for this sl-MeasId;","paragraph_zero_based":1533},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else:","paragraph_zero_based":1534},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>add a new entry for this sl-MeasId within the VarMeasConfigSL;","paragraph_zero_based":1535}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"ffe6aa9e169eee2e55d5910307b90f1a0088b587d5b1b62ff44829994c9db517","original_member_