tion of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx:p24"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"B","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-18","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-16(Release 16)Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)Rel-19(Release 19)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This CR is to introduce the support of Rel-18 Multi-path and capture RAN2 agreements into the RRC specification.","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In 3.1, the definitions of Multi-path, MP remote UE, MP relay UE, N3C indirect path, SL indirect path are added for MP. In addition, Split DRB which is missing from legacy releases.","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In 3.2, the abbreviations of MP, N3C are added.","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In 4.2.2, the clarification on split SRB to accommodate MP is added.","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In 4.4, path management is added for MP.","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In 5.3.3.1a, the condition of remote UE bringing idle relay UE to connected state by PC5-RRC message is added.","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In 5.3.5.2, path management is added for MP.","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In 5.3.5.3, handling indirect path related to MP in RRCReconfiguration message, as well as the stop behaviour of T4xx when successfully sending RRCReconfigurationComplete message via SL indirect path (i.e., PC5 RLC acknowledgement is received from target L2 U2N Relay UE) are added.","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"cfd1aef054dea290a9770e5c2de1b12f4cc7358b773882ae43663cec7a0c7249","original_member_sha256":"eb486990e07cad7e16d78b726e76051d7652abe5c7bb2e34c237c431cbcb3180","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["aece9f43dc861aa2d41b1a72eaa0f2829fcd73ed55c9ddcce31f1d854aabe4b4","02769b912084b058d113cf92c4831b4ff89903847a3cef8ebd5585fd9c951ba8","0659c2a851f13f5705a7326ce5857d5d5d1b7f07c402171063d5242ec4c8ea37","ea30732bd1c2e330ae7ac458b16a61b6c46a2b2b176d46f0d2124120e458061e","2768af24b429f7788b00d7ca27583cdcd8bf7f7ca0ed1e76be1be16e589de298","51868a5b040384c722da2f454ea25a31d1999dc06dbb518a4b052ac49d3fbf23","70f0408f0bfbe07114a8e1bad232f8a2635b995efa9561658283d4262da2f098","484bf60bde0d60a30b710861e4ef3acc4626428474f42fedc45335eeeb3fa49d","496c2f12b957e7f2a752a00629ea121774dbb93561fd