{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRAPSidelink Relay Adaptation Protocol","paragraph_zero_based":336},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRBSignalling Radio Bearer","paragraph_zero_based":337},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRSSounding Reference Signal","paragraph_zero_based":338},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SSBSynchronization Signal Block","paragraph_zero_based":339},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TAGTiming Advance Group","paragraph_zero_based":340},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TDDTime Division Duplex","paragraph_zero_based":341},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TEGTiming Error Group","paragraph_zero_based":342},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TMTransparent Mode","paragraph_zero_based":343},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TMGITemporary Mobile Group Identity","paragraph_zero_based":344},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"U2NUE-to-Network","paragraph_zero_based":345},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UDCUplink Data Compression","paragraph_zero_based":346},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UEUser Equipment","paragraph_zero_based":347},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ULUplink","paragraph_zero_based":348},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UMUnacknowledged Mode","paragraph_zero_based":349},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UPUser Plane","paragraph_zero_based":350},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"VRVirtual Reality","paragraph_zero_based":351},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":352},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In the ASN.1, lower case may be used for some (parts) of the above abbreviations e.g. c-RNTI.","paragraph_zero_based":353},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":354},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NEXT CHANGE","paragraph_zero_based":355},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":356},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.2.2Signalling radio bearers","paragraph_zero_based":357},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"\"Signalling Radio Bearers\" (SRBs) are defined as Radio Bearers (RBs) that are used only for the transmission of RRC and NAS messages. More specifically, the following SRBs are defined:","paragraph_zero_based":358},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SRB0 is for RRC messages using the CCCH logical channel;","paragraph_zero_based":359}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"cfd1aef054dea290a9770e5c2de1b12f4cc7358b773882ae43663cec7a0c7249","original_member_sha256":"eb486990e07cad7e16d78b726e76051d7652abe5c7bb2e34c237c431cbcb3180","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["9ebf9acdc498bdb9354f8530d3bbe536d171e8e27f9472c944898a7cf6aee839","d2b110e251d050bb132158f46fa6a19a94cd15542fb8c056e89db16718e57e0b","e81d198665b74f720952b9580c13b78a7cfe827e712986d2451964b2afb3a5ef","709755b89eac6a39faf81b19338c39ca13305cf8dc9ee37f3e1fa30ffa99799a","c7dfe83054ffbae7c79f4c51ce90bdbacea79e2ecc83c5d80c922b0bf3dc50b3","7e330b4d8a00634b187a6865aaba102710794fb2dd6448085b07770f8bc3829f","1ac56c63dfaff43ac329f7a4286cf3e5177fb7c941bbd740a260bd23c1d7140a","8036b1ae2e98f5975ac0bcd0e4798a2b0696d6984c3520bc446082624ece7852","eadfda4a3e40820d72f4f2fffdebc5d14d8a07554d0fd6161d9ee59381aac776","508dae3d527045ff7f4d030373219950a74b19be291b401ad2f0f200730a6e62","78b5392428a5e0c1979332bc4846b81a2b9b146a6487103ff0a625b6394a7a98","c632b12a51d4b4ba8ef63a411bacab30a46ac00863b8855dab58e9fa13c24cfd","b2a3d4aa0a700d0874b7ebfed94b08c465da2e83dfbe186578d19f5872d82a2c","0505ef6c3912de9da16bd87c6eeb0f317979209691f0d498b5219d7cccc98ddd","d31ffae152d0f400735ce945649e0790a559b16daf5f02cd491eef3db2d752ea","bb0bb7b64956f74ba36978954d9f99c8a7bf7db5d8b0dd85bb49563970c141d8","4370d57692d17abe3b1d5ce7f3d5c7f58f4a64ec2e9bee9715df942b3815ffcb","f95cb58abccf314c26f354be4d96ec95d8e9aae53502b6b58a3ead7acb1c8dcb","6bc74232088e3c219ed1d8dbca3bacc4ad4eff6061797121c94075bb18b0d024","040b9cbd34aa85f040c03f4531c5b0d43c454fb60b9c92d44e6dd8dba1f93142","b6e3cc714d5465b0b43a134e7df4d529568cacfda75173612e0361e58adc6d48","72618896d14d85084999ed63cc3bcc1679e69c29707578cd8ebd0f6b354b5734","5a4749fbe76d76582113d05df6653564fba2dce6ed08640e472c42d69a9e5b15","93d634bc924e157c1c5176c7a86f6c6e600757a7ec30d2a7c9e673414c7349d8"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[336,359],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx:p336"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SRB1 is for RRC messages (which may include a piggybacked NAS message) as well as for NAS messages prior to the establishment of SRB2, all using DCCH logical channel;","paragraph_zero_based":360},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SRB2 is for NAS messages and for RRC messages which include logged measurement information, all using DCCH logical channel. SRB2 has a lower priority than SRB1 and may be configured by the network after AS security activation;","paragraph_zero_based":361},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SRB3 is for specific RRC messages when UE is in (NG)EN-DC or NR-DC, all using DCCH logical channel;","paragraph_zero_based":362},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-SRB4 is for RRC messages which include application layer measurement report information, all using DCCH logical channel. SRB4 has a lower priority than SRB1 and can only be configured by the network after AS security activation.","paragraph_zero_based":363},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In downlink, piggybacking of NAS messages is used only for one dependant (i.e. with joint success/failure) procedure: bearer establishment/modification/release. In uplink piggybacking of NAS message is used only for transferring the initial NAS message during connection setup and connection resume.","paragraph_zero_based":364},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:The NAS messages transferred via SRB2 are also contained in RRC messages, which however do not include any RRC protocol control information.","paragraph_zero_based":365},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Once AS security is activated, all RRC messages on SRB1, SRB2, SRB3 and SRB4, including those containing NAS messages, are integrity protected and ciphered by PDCP. NAS independently applies integrity protection and ciphering to the NAS messages, see TS 24.501 [23].","paragraph_zero_based":366},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Split SRB is supported for all the MR-DC options as well as MP in both SRB1 and SRB2 (split SRB is not supported for SRB0, SRB3 and SRB4).","paragraph_zero_based":367},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For operation with shared spectrum channel access in FR1, SRB0, SRB1 and SRB3 are assigned with the highest priority Channel Access Priority Class (CAPC), (i.e. CAPC = 1) while CAPC for SRB2 is configurable.","paragraph_zero_based":368},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":369},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NEXT CHANGE","paragraph_zero_based":370},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4.4Functions","paragraph_zero_based":371},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The RRC protocol includes the following main functions:","paragraph_zero_based":372},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Broadcast of system information:","paragraph_zero_based":373},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Including NAS common information;","paragraph_zero_based":374},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Information applicable for UEs in RRC_IDLE and RRC_INACTIVE (e.g. cell (re-)selection parameters, neighbouring cell information) and information (also) applicable for UEs in RRC_CONNECTED (e.g. common channel configuration information);","paragraph_zero_based":375},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Including ETWS notification, CMAS notification;","paragraph_zero_based":376},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Including positioning assistance data.","paragraph_zero_based":377},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-RRC connection control:","paragraph_zero_based":378},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Paging;","paragraph_zero_based":379},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Establishment/modification/suspension/resumption/release of RRC connection, including e.g. assignment/modification of UE identity (C-RNTI, fullI-RNTI, etc.), establishment/modification/suspension/resumption/release of SRBs (except for SRB0);","paragraph_zero_based":380},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Access barring;","paragraph_zero_based":381},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Initial AS security activation, i.e. initial configuration of AS integrity protection (SRBs, DRBs) and AS ciphering (SRBs, DRBs);","paragraph_zero_based":382},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-RRC connection mobility including e.g. intra-frequency and inter-frequency handover, path switch from a PCell to a target L2 U2N Relay UE or from a L2 U2N Relay UE to a target PCell, associated AS security handling, i.e. key/algorithm change, specification of RRC context information transferred between network nodes;","paragraph_zero_based":383}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"cfd1aef054dea290a9770e5c2de1b12f4cc7358b773882ae43663cec7a0c7249","original_member_sha256":"eb486990e07cad7e16d78b726e76051d7652abe5c7bb2e34c237c431cbcb3180","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["18ff31367334b440707f53a69496e20121d6e0b0c70db9c861a5548122c6d72a","c0522b9c844c816cbcc1aa8add58813028ffdbc16d07ddecdab69e878929848b","5ccde223db97b7e7ae115941d5854e639a63030ccd08559ee236db9b3b4f8786","3674ca9450360f4418ef1faaf8147a43837214f8de3987aa786a87fda2c17a8c","ee7cfa14c794a3676aae8811d5a95704f2fd674465b60eff5e74bd7715ae3181","7811a8d2194e9780259627849eb578cc0a4490d864a44ea38d8c388abfd2d654","6c92074d9d06fe3e0b97827dc1ff9489640a037e6b7f8cfb073d281f2666dfa4","921debc2b11a76a0cf3b0b06142118cf17adc05a16fbdba7cabeae6a856dcf2f","f05a5d1a80bfdb553bf3cb0c2e322b0772640ba559075ca4448f7fad106562ad","6bc74232088e3c219ed1d8dbca3bacc4ad4eff6061797121c94075bb18b0d024","040b9cbd34aa85f040c03f4531c5b0d43c454fb60b9c92d44e6dd8dba1f93142","9e685ac3b06aa15fda1db5e859fd17435b80f8b9be192e4cef9ab352802c6c5a","6898f4ea6a47a0d3bde756f454361e4fba67138726abe25a80b6c4f61fd0e257","7025d18787738355bc5edb764cdc7f53b224991829d239e69bae2a372c368cdc","3ea9668c1d50298ef45c5fa4a6ed81a828d281863f627e0f87e4a01885f8a996","7c43fa03132ebb32107c2c49c0ebb94d06bcf5ee53e308b5ed9eb432acc8b6ab","90e809bb1ed0edcddbc14f7a3f939e76dcf1a82f01ebfb99625dbfa4c2e5b080","9a3c4ee6a4d594a87a8c91fd8c1b040210d538a195fa52f04202151f269b3282","72d483ea81fc9b704aa096194991d9cde1288162e6a1888762e618408a0c62ef","302a8837804f7c2117dc66fc9e2dd66899439783370eb42abdc22797ba90b135","d708f805171de53637c50b5a6640550ffafcf86acff0f1ac42171fa51245fbf0","d891aeace9ba5d73b82b3a0fe53e4b6b75935e8c159deb026528f515e36a006e","d32f8858b3dd90a1e2a33b5f1cd5f67c42161eaf7654578764e41993fd9e1a97","60b2fd3531828fa7815160500a81e60be6f9f2633fa20fa3d5e73b3e32bd0d8f"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[360,383],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx:p360"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Establishment/modification/suspension/resumption/release of RBs carrying user data (DRBs/MRBs);","paragraph_zero_based":384},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Radio configuration control including e.g. assignment/modification of ARQ configuration, HARQ configuration, DRX configuration;","paragraph_zero_based":385},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-In case of DC, cell management including e.g. change of PSCell, addition/modification/release of SCG cell(s);","paragraph_zero_based":386},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-In case of CA, cell management including e.g. addition/modification/release of SCell(s);","paragraph_zero_based":387},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-In case of MP, path management including e.g. indirect path addition/modification/release; ","paragraph_zero_based":388},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-QoS control including assignment/ modification of semi-persistent scheduling (SPS) configuration and configured grant configuration for DL and UL respectively, assignment/ modification of parameters for UL rate control in the UE, i.e. allocation of a priority and a prioritised bit rate (PBR) for each RB of UE and logical channel of IAB-MT.","paragraph_zero_based":389},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Recovery from radio link failure.","paragraph_zero_based":390},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Inter-RAT mobility including e.g. AS security activation, transfer of RRC context information;","paragraph_zero_based":391},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Measurement configuration and reporting:","paragraph_zero_based":392},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Establishment/modification/release of measurement configuration (e.g. intra-frequency, inter-frequency and inter- RAT measurements);","paragraph_zero_based":393},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Setup and release of measurement gaps;","paragraph_zero_based":394},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Measurement reporting.","paragraph_zero_based":395},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Configuration of BAP entity and BH RLC channels for the support of IAB-node.","paragraph_zero_based":396},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Configuration of SRAP entity and Uu/PC5 Relay RLC channels for the support of L2 U2N relay.","paragraph_zero_based":397},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Other functions including e.g. generic protocol error handling, transfer of dedicated NAS information, transfer of UE radio access capability information.","paragraph_zero_based":398},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Support of self-configuration and self-optimisation.","paragraph_zero_based":399},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Support of measurement logging and reporting for network performance optimisation, as specified in TS 37.320 [61];","paragraph_zero_based":400},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-Support of transfer of application layer measurement configuration and reporting.","paragraph_zero_based":401},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":402},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NEXT CHANGE","paragraph_zero_based":403},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":404},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.3.1aConditions for establishing RRC Connection for NR sidelink communication/discovery/V2X sidelink communication","paragraph_zero_based":405},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For NR sidelink communication/discovery, an RRC connection establishment is initiated only in the following cases:","paragraph_zero_based":406},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink communication and related data is available for transmission:","paragraph_zero_based":407}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"cfd1aef054dea290a9770e5c2de1b12f4cc7358b773882ae43663cec7a0c7249","original_member_sha256":"eb486990e07cad7e16d78b726e76051d7652abe5c7bb2e34c237c431cbcb3180","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["00a31c9290c66b07ce3d147944a011b1094fd6bf70f7d22914b83a80c5138f67","23456eabea3ac7996d56550a4b9e63ea8fe47571881b9fb0f19e67ca13c494a3","323502e2c6cd5cc08acb490b286b6a9bcdf12d5d236a3d39c7d998758cb5d224","881ca8ab88f6d0900a3b4937c6f6a45fe11176ef95a3f78377d8b2f1d4061440","eec5183af644ad5e3117e379e9ffd1c937b9b764a80eb0e7bb90452cbc62ba51","16392f633031c66aa213edec53d13cac50ca89537167924aa909d53436fa20b4","b172349d7a214e8fa318105461e2d11a1ba85bcce46a924b2c6351b6d5312f43","6b74cef11d5604ba34b8ffcf8192607ecb6b8db579ceb3e308fae5ef7fc86985","c558601533dc5cdd93c01ccf164f8971317ca3b9b3df9fd4c6bb4004dc023b29","44651b26890b809c91bad040bbf7eea5d1f79cf0f924153d6685de863cdc6208","4bed6f2655aef547160275c6f4313bd3c827520c052a03c49e1045d49917b590","8a9becc8e0606656fcefb43e645bf6294dfac0c6fcdd170f930e5a5544142213","749983283547dd1b77aa9e33443a7a4b66e646bf326dadb47edfa2cdf409381b","8d34245adc54821223fec1298732afd10c8453ea898a69896258aaeb31a25f75","f401ed5345706a1667cbad92d13e9ed29ebc775e2d285195a16475c9718c1cb6","b42abf9c2022efeafd4ee82a8fa59c039f6408c29338fe09ac30e428e0cd80da","ee9abcd46a7ba01d53dc4699f96b051a01d15e8a1879881adfa8211064f13ed2","440e321a76f82833a1154a456d944f00c4d92876277e6a86d84d0628be2a59a6","94676ff3ad221721391c2caafe42b175657ff418bc552d71bcba67378a39a42d","040b9cbd34aa85f040c03f4531c5b0d43c454fb60b9c92d44e6dd8dba1f93142","94676ff3ad221721391c2caafe42b175657ff418bc552d71bcba67378a39a42d","ba95f3f85950a1bb7923713cf9abffcb483a600ba74737d0b2b7a0d626e7e105","a1fd015f2ae98f89b823790568015e9765e8d7d50f8f72749ae7436ea50044b2","802df1017076810e32df529a960de70b89e831846e4e384f02f5e4ffc0a1e81c"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[384,407],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx:p384"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the frequency on which the UE is configured to transmit NR sidelink communication is included in sl-FreqInfoList within SIB12 provided by the cell on which the UE camps; and if the valid version of SIB12 does not include sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency;","paragraph_zero_based":408},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink discovery and related data is available for transmission:","paragraph_zero_based":409},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink L2 U2N relay discovery messages and sl-L2U2N-Relay is included in SIB12; or","paragraph_zero_based":410},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink L3 U2N relay discovery messages and sl-L3U2N-RelayDiscovery is included in SIB12; or","paragraph_zero_based":411},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the UE is configured by upper layers to transmit NR sidelink non-relay discovery messages and sl-NonRelayDiscovery is included in SIB12:","paragraph_zero_based":412},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the frequency on which the UE is configured to transmit NR sidelink discovery is included in sl-FreqInfoList within SIB12 provided by the cell on which the UE camps; and if the valid version of SIB12 includes neither sl-DiscTxPoolSelected nor sl-TxPoolSelectedNormal for the concerned frequency;","paragraph_zero_based":413},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For L2 U2N Relay UE in RRC_IDLE, an RRC connection establishment is initiated in the following cases:","paragraph_zero_based":414},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if any message is received from a L2 U2N Remote UE via SL-RLC0 as specified in 9.1.1.4 or SL-RLC1 as specified in 9.2.4; or","paragraph_zero_based":415},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if RemoteUEInformationSidelink containing the connectionForMP is received from a L2 U2N Remote UE as specified in 5.8.9.8.3;","paragraph_zero_based":416},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For V2X sidelink communication, an RRC connection is initiated only when the conditions specified for V2X sidelink communication in clause 5.3.3.1a of TS 36.331 [10] are met.","paragraph_zero_based":417},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE:Upper layers initiate an RRC connection (except if the RRC connection is initiated at the L2 U2N Relay UE upon reception of a message from a L2 U2N Remote UE via SL-RLC0 or SL-RLC1). The interaction with NAS is left to UE implementation.","paragraph_zero_based":418},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":419},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NEXT CHANGE","paragraph_zero_based":420},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.5.2Initiation","paragraph_zero_based":421},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The Network may initiate the RRC reconfiguration procedure to a UE in RRC_CONNECTED. The Network applies the procedure as follows:","paragraph_zero_based":422},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the establishment of RBs (other than SRB1, that is established during RRC connection establishment) is performed only when AS security has been activated;","paragraph_zero_based":423},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the establishment of BH RLC Channels for IAB is performed only when AS security has been activated;","paragraph_zero_based":424},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the establishment of Uu Relay RLC channels and PC5 Relay RLC channels (other than SL-RLC0 and SL-RLC1) for L2 U2N Relay UE is performed only when AS security has been activated, and the establishment of PC5 Relay RLC channels for L2 U2N Remote UE (other than SL-RLC0 and SL-RLC1) is performed only when AS security has been activated;","paragraph_zero_based":425},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the addition of Secondary Cell Group and SCells is performed only when AS security has been activated;","paragraph_zero_based":426},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the reconfigurationWithSync is included in secondaryCellGroup only when at least one RLC bearer or BH RLC channel is setup in SCG;","paragraph_zero_based":427},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the reconfigurationWithSync is included in masterCellGroup only when AS security has been activated, and SRB2 with at least one DRB or multicast MRB or, for IAB, SRB2, are setup and not suspended;","paragraph_zero_based":428},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the conditionalReconfiguration for CPC is included only when at least one RLC bearer is setup in SCG;","paragraph_zero_based":429},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the conditionalReconfiguration for CHO or CPA is included only when AS security has been activated, and SRB2 with at least one DRB or multicast MRB or, for IAB, SRB2, are setup and not suspended;","paragraph_zero_based":430},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-the addition of indirect path for MP is performed only when AS security has been activated.","paragraph_zero_based":431}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"cfd1aef054dea290a9770e5c2de1b12f4cc7358b773882ae43663cec7a0c7249","original_member_sha256":"eb486990e07cad7e16d78b726e76051d7652abe5c7bb2e34c237c431cbcb3180","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c34fb6d7cf5f65ae60e22fe9283aca49a10047ec2fc5d3a9ec5152ac0ff90b06","389c81c41007961bccc35284e34d0643269f03e8d35256bc438c3d5896404959","f156c98f53cca556fc2ed789518e5faff135466f311043072833e2f12c10a87f","41af37a93af5ea1c9f3eba12cc8176b157c0c7e1f6c60f5c9e26e20a86b8b7ad","e1d7a463bbf0a4b84502d5597db6949b8513dd1946a267f464caaf42959817ff","0f598d0a5a3fe1704861f712b9404421da8b6dee98a23e38873afd1f68385bf9","b78cb48eb6fb8b0f761dfbf557b5eaa3570ed07eda8a1822b61437f5b8a56feb","5336ba08de2ae823cc7e5cab74b8253770a1301add2b83a5a05c2e85b3221288","d3a20be52bf07a057646b626385bcbc8df2aa261859944436e9b40a31ce9ac18","3edbc3100805bad4805e750d274a0f60c705b8a65f564846401412f6da4cceb3","669e6e3086c38383e16c2a5a40df8ee93dab77f4724d544cafef089fba516212","94676ff3ad221721391c2caafe42b175657ff418bc552d71bcba67378a39a42d","040b9cbd34aa85f040c03f4531c5b0d43c454fb60b9c92d44e6dd8dba1f93142","4809bfa0e7513ec8f9cfcf121edcd051d6c485b00eae7504edb6803eb96e31c1","d7756f6a09a0f7701a33de772a43f1f157c0693dc8c97fe7e6227f8e99b787f1","b92dbef1c86e55a4db353032ce6abff69975e139fff73e609cfb2ea84983ac5f","212c56c27c39a12b2a906f6da6e6e7a294c72fc160933b64a3aa0127cb310013","a946aab265599937c28c3ae6d526650735a6a855a2fb2102e9ee2abdec254a05","b4c87121f8d588bd7da7020aa07ddd634254e33705ca977534e9128b321fabdb","04f5d80e10e99b4f5731739bf18c5f04fe0bdd033fa16855cbf483509be65630","f5cfcab34b7d311a055fa0de927553f384ad7a43240573daeb37249c6b7a1d08","279b05037c5db84beac06085323894338639822e15058304864eb054315488cb","30cede37bbe0e3d46fa5388a4c2e6a3fad525b63a47a5208b3808534d8a6e490","4ccd062aa68a9c5671c9d256a99881958ebf44b59bd4f0abf8d8d75a9676cb8f"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[408,431],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx:p408"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":432},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NEXT CHANGE","paragraph_zero_based":433},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"5.3.5.3Reception of an RRCReconfiguration by the UE","paragraph_zero_based":434},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE shall perform the following actions upon reception of the RRCReconfiguration, or upon execution of the conditional reconfiguration (CHO, CPA or CPC):","paragraph_zero_based":435},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration is applied due to a conditional reconfiguration execution upon cell selection performed while timer T311 was running, as defined in 5.3.7.3:","paragraph_zero_based":436},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>remove all the entries within the MCG and the SCG VarConditionalReconfig, if any;","paragraph_zero_based":437},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration includes the daps-SourceRelease:","paragraph_zero_based":438},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>reset the source MAC and release the source MAC configuration;","paragraph_zero_based":439},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each DAPS bearer:","paragraph_zero_based":440},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>release the RLC entity or entities as specified in TS 38.322 [4], clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell;","paragraph_zero_based":441},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>reconfigure the PDCP entity to release DAPS as specified in TS 38.323 [5];","paragraph_zero_based":442},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>for each SRB:","paragraph_zero_based":443},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>release the PDCP entity for the source SpCell;","paragraph_zero_based":444},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>release the RLC entity as specified in TS 38.322 [4], clause 5.1.3, and the associated logical channel for the source SpCell;","paragraph_zero_based":445},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>release the physical channel configuration for the source SpCell;","paragraph_zero_based":446},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>discard the keys used in the source SpCell (the KgNB key, the KRRCenc key, the KRRCint key, the KUPint key and the KUPenc key), if any;","paragraph_zero_based":447},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration is received via other RAT (i.e., inter-RAT handover to NR):","paragraph_zero_based":448},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the RRCReconfiguration does not include the fullConfig and the UE is connected to 5GC (i.e., delta signalling during intra 5GC handover):","paragraph_zero_based":449},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>re-use the source RAT SDAP and PDCP configurations if available (i.e., current SDAP/PDCP configurations for all RBs from source E-UTRA RAT prior to the reception of the inter-RAT HO RRCReconfiguration message);","paragraph_zero_based":450},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>else:","paragraph_zero_based":451},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the RRCReconfiguration includes the fullConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":452},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform the full configuration procedure as specified in 5.3.5.11;","paragraph_zero_based":453},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration includes the masterCellGroup:","paragraph_zero_based":454},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the cell group configuration for the received masterCellGroup according to 5.3.5.5;","paragraph_zero_based":455}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"cfd1aef054dea290a9770e5c2de1b12f4cc7358b773882ae43663cec7a0c7249","original_member_sha256":"eb486990e07cad7e16d78b726e76051d7652abe5c7bb2e34c237c431cbcb3180","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["94676ff3ad221721391c2caafe42b175657ff418bc552d71bcba67378a39a42d","040b9cbd34aa85f040c03f4531c5b0d43c454fb60b9c92d44e6dd8dba1f93142","fd0ceec8d217da9799e0453cd7c151849af9aec8816764665240beadb7be5418","19ac4956b34bef2d7ed3e1d3eec87e7c396ae77305b365147160963ba53bd935","dbc1b52296c04b330e8dbee586a36139e8f3e03991974a117460eeee9f731e12","0f2c5f1cd67c393dc0879eb4ed9ba2f41b2edf4fbd42500874993c3dcad36a71","f04dc5c4e2f00119c78b4ea65afdc6720adec07162676a16eea7da7e41ccce80","8d11c6103bbf975182ce76fa484af314e39fcb1eb53841fc4c058667d58211d4","515e7100bc61bdcbebaa24a2e26de58b2f415338a558a0b4dbc75e312ee84492","92dfaae3d41d5b3f8ca48251e4d2442b487469a923aa8085d5f7a657cdd1b01b","ac0ab020dfed385b8e684fa0f878790ed79676077e5d2449aa710263f42ff95b","bf7c53b4d5d73dd9bb67c68ef8604e539f438c523eb8fb39626f0efc4bb3b2c6","b432d90f0b168d2f7a9e44ad97ef24e03930ee8b57ebb7a0f100681ce48aa52c","2eb4d4351e140f2c49a7eabfd53bc9bc9a2d8f8af0f1cd796b9480112d44e6c9","dc1d27361f225c9c6c5379b64dab552492bff46ba9171d876c857e574de0f7d7","fa1d154b8ba679f4882068936e416e703fa609a70e5db9fc23f24615c0fcf3f4","4e11bcf9a5ba3a1d6d40143c14961a2acd641ce29ddedfdef3561973e547122f","15fcf7dad1e13bb9e9d756b1ed6437cba1df3d43f530a8a1ef7aefb014ea6e67","484f12b23dffa844ca2e3fbc6cd317641e036f55dfd7f8e1a1700d4faae269d7","fb4e786357ec2a707b7644275113ae3c66f3679613369702cddc921d2c4f11fa","5734668f6ae07af0e644e4abd53dbc94219054d6b953a0826bf3b95e12a7badc","b4369715d71fce37c67023ff8df0b9fbc87f73f930b501806e71c8aae736bd3e","e76ab57bb4a14b2dd9c087bc0ca201a647beeda85076600828ef9218a1bbfdfa","76ba71b06d19e7938c5cd3032008d9f591d914ad3037e455b5eab720fba5e1f7"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[432,455],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx:p432"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration includes the masterKeyUpdate:","paragraph_zero_based":456},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform AS security key update procedure as specified in 5.3.5.7;","paragraph_zero_based":457},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration includes the sk-Counter:","paragraph_zero_based":458},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform security key update procedure as specified in 5.3.5.7;","paragraph_zero_based":459},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration includes the secondaryCellGroup:","paragraph_zero_based":460},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the cell group configuration for the SCG according to 5.3.5.5;","paragraph_zero_based":461},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration includes the mrdc-SecondaryCellGroupConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":462},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if the mrdc-SecondaryCellGroupConfig is set to setup:","paragraph_zero_based":463},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the mrdc-SecondaryCellGroupConfig includes mrdc-ReleaseAndAdd:","paragraph_zero_based":464},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>perform MR-DC release as specified in clause 5.3.5.10;","paragraph_zero_based":465},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the received mrdc-SecondaryCellGroup is set to nr-SCG:","paragraph_zero_based":466},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>perform the RRC reconfiguration according to 5.3.5.3 for the RRCReconfiguration message included in nr-SCG;","paragraph_zero_based":467},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>if the received mrdc-SecondaryCellGroup is set to eutra-SCG:","paragraph_zero_based":468},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"4>perform the RRC connection reconfiguration as specified in TS 36.331 [10], clause 5.3.5.3 for the RRCConnectionReconfiguration message included in eutra-SCG;","paragraph_zero_based":469},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>else (mrdc-SecondaryCellGroupConfig is set to release):","paragraph_zero_based":470},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform MR-DC release as specified in clause 5.3.5.10;","paragraph_zero_based":471},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the radioBearerConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":472},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the radio bearer configuration according to 5.3.5.6;","paragraph_zero_based":473},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the radioBearerConfig2:","paragraph_zero_based":474},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the radio bearer configuration according to 5.3.5.6;","paragraph_zero_based":475},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the measConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":476},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the measurement configuration procedure as specified in 5.5.2;","paragraph_zero_based":477},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the dedicatedNAS-MessageList:","paragraph_zero_based":478},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>forward each element of the dedicatedNAS-MessageList to upper layers in the same order as listed;","paragraph_zero_based":479}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"cfd1aef054dea290a9770e5c2de1b12f4cc7358b773882ae43663cec7a0c7249","original_member_sha256":"eb486990e07cad7e16d78b726e76051d7652abe5c7bb2e34c237c431cbcb3180","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["7d90c610b5f633494979b5a01688e199f4857aab91985d4aed55bf6a076d2006","502888a8cb51eb855f749ecc866adc07c3045673cdb1871e6bd56467c81b0b0d","5634ac1f17829eff066981f5219d5bde35c50f4203151e99faffc9b84e4aae8a","20b937336bcddaafa47f28580deea6c72198c47678690b30c4aa5f2883a7b023","7e12cef914dbfa8dc5b37b3245d802137971c0754f4a94e999c57c2256714cd8","9a0d82c3d5956a75a60d683fc631ecf30cb9ff344e2698a04a0dffed94a0a6a7","e980923b7740bd634c44786e664841b1514151995d82847fada00b5cfd85e762","8012289efed076ef25051d4d75c925b628363d4c7c0df97d43a49c617f76e972","2fb64ff524d5598d2b1201d8cdb75a9f899f37225b64355d046bda18c642dc0e","57ada6f83185c3995153f96e5fc4ef9cccce2aece73139fda239b775942fd836","000d64b4274c01c6ce2f90db030bafdb6e8614da5e37daed5eae71166e204add","c937e8c94cc2e73bdbb555ccc83f50630221ca27424ba722eb749b974638597b","51fde9922bae8613a9049f1f091734e0152d7b0ffdd6a97782ff1c74136113df","f69fcc0abe675508455971be956c3e2c4bc9dbe5aa0de26d873b41c0d02c9927","34b9f757d3431f7d89b2b0d342837ef14aa941732507351f306fd33a6b3f471a","808d52e931b533def47793bbff126cc7b1e2c4de21b9b10df410d07c87479d46","eb6f3103c2563cf1751d1248d4b5fe3a2c489c7b48f042758ec7c1741a2afa99","f788ca5d608738b5ec9cc3ab94e35eb6ae4dd9e479ab91465d3a490dfef78b93","d149f5cd092e973dd1aef05140c452540a1c4584ef6925f78ce9d7f41a7c7036","f788ca5d608738b5ec9cc3ab94e35eb6ae4dd9e479ab91465d3a490dfef78b93","41112c6f40042c460ff70dc93ad1c4b9c700dd491bb435b016c15c0c112b1e84","e7524c85c29f9a9be4083789fc0df5b8d9a7cceb5bba7e1242ae5689168b4d63","6fd47721fa5d9dcb8d928607a7d849e1ea4b9c5eeb1dd1101f4c0557c2992abb","e3b3eb322b26d38e8553739e065f094208ee75627bbeee93a85ed46b98b6bd21"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[456,479],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx:p456"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2311970.zip::R2-2311970 Introduction of Rel-18 Multi-path.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the dedicatedSIB1-Delivery:","paragraph_zero_based":480},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the action upon reception of SIB1 as specified in 5.2.2.4.2;","paragraph_zero_based":481},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 0:If this RRCReconfiguration is associated to the MCG and includes reconfigurationWithSync in spCellConfig and dedicatedSIB1-Delivery, the UE initiates (if needed) the request to acquire required SIBs, according to clause 5.2.2.3.5, only after the random access procedure towards the target SpCell is completed.","paragraph_zero_based":482},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the dedicatedSystemInformationDelivery:","paragraph_zero_based":483},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the action upon reception of System Information as specified in 5.2.2.4;","paragraph_zero_based":484},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if all the SIB(s) and/or posSIB(s) requested in DedicatedSIBRequest message have been acquired:","paragraph_zero_based":485},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>stop timer T350, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":486},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the dedicatedPosSysInfoDelivery:","paragraph_zero_based":487},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the action upon reception of the contained posSIB(s), as specified in clause 5.2.2.4.16;","paragraph_zero_based":488},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if all the SIB(s) and/or posSIB(s) requested in DedicatedSIBRequest message have been acquired:","paragraph_zero_based":489},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>stop timer T350, if running;","paragraph_zero_based":490},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the otherConfig:","paragraph_zero_based":491},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the other configuration procedure as specified in 5.3.5.9;","paragraph_zero_based":492},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the bap-Config:","paragraph_zero_based":493},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform the BAP configuration procedure as specified in 5.3.5.12;","paragraph_zero_based":494},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the iab-IP-AddressConfigurationList:","paragraph_zero_based":495},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if iab-IP-AddressToReleaseList is included:","paragraph_zero_based":496},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform release of IP address as specified in 5.3.5.12a.1.1;","paragraph_zero_based":497},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if iab-IP-AddressToAddModList is included:","paragraph_zero_based":498},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3>perform IAB IP address addition/update as specified in 5.3.5.12a.1.2;","paragraph_zero_based":499},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the conditionalReconfiguration:","paragraph_zero_based":500},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>perform conditional reconfiguration as specified in 5.3.5.13;","paragraph_zero_based":501},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"1>if the RRCReconfiguration message includes the needForGapsConfigNR:","paragraph_zero_based":502},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"2>if needForGapsConfigNR is set to setup:","paragraph_zero_based":503}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"cfd1aef054dea290a9770e5c2de1b12f4cc7358b773882ae43663cec7a0c7249","original_member_sha256":"eb486990e07cad7e16d78b726e76051d7652abe5c7bb2e34c237c431cbcb3180","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c02856dbe459d52b6b1729c803701b010b71537eb130c00107e20d74d78bb4fc","3d6f0858270faae6230621baf