{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312192.zip::R2-2312192 38323 CR0128 Introduction of XR Enhancements.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-References are either specific (identified by date of publication, edition number, version number, etc.) or nonspecific.","paragraph_zero_based":120},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For a specific reference, subsequent revisions do not apply.","paragraph_zero_based":121},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-For a non-specific reference, the latest version applies. In the case of a reference to a 3GPP document (including a GSM document), a non-specific reference implicitly refers to the latest version of that document in the same Release as the present document.","paragraph_zero_based":122},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[1]3GPP TR 21.905: \"Vocabulary for 3GPP Specifications\".","paragraph_zero_based":123},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[2]3GPP TS 38.300: \"NG Radio Access Network; Overall description\".","paragraph_zero_based":124},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[3]3GPP TS 38.331: \"NR Radio Resource Control (RRC); Protocol Specification\".","paragraph_zero_based":125},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[4]3GPP TS 38.321: \"NR Medium Access Control (MAC) protocol specification\".","paragraph_zero_based":126},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[5]3GPP TS 38.322: \"NR Radio Link Control (RLC) protocol specification\".","paragraph_zero_based":127},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[6]3GPP TS 33.501: \"Security Architecture and Procedures for 5G System \".","paragraph_zero_based":128},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[7]IETF RFC 5795: \"The RObust Header Compression (ROHC) Framework\".","paragraph_zero_based":129},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[8]IETF RFC 3095: \"RObust Header Compression (ROHC): Framework and four profiles: RTP, UDP, ESP and uncompressed\".","paragraph_zero_based":130},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[9]IETF RFC 4815: \"RObust Header Compression (ROHC): Corrections and Clarifications to RFC 3095\".","paragraph_zero_based":131},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[10]IETF RFC 6846: \"RObust Header Compression (ROHC): A Profile for TCP/IP (ROHC-TCP)\".","paragraph_zero_based":132},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[11]IETF RFC 5225: \"RObust Header Compression (ROHC) Version 2: Profiles for RTP, UDP, IP, ESP and UDP Lite\".","paragraph_zero_based":133},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[12]3GPP TS 36.321: \"Evolved Universal Terrestrial Radio Access (E-UTRA) Medium Access Control (MAC) protocol specification\".","paragraph_zero_based":134},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[13]3GPP TS 23.287: \"Architecture enhancements for 5G System (5GS) to support Vehicle-to-Everything (V2X) services\".","paragraph_zero_based":135},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[14]3GPP TS 33.536: \"Security Aspect of 3GPP Support for Advanced V2X Services\".","paragraph_zero_based":136},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[15]IEEE Standard 802.3™-2018: \"Ethernet\".","paragraph_zero_based":137},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[16]3GPP TS 24.587: \"Vehicle-to-Everything (V2X) services in 5G System (5GS), Stage 3\".","paragraph_zero_based":138},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[17]3GPP TS 33.401: \"3GPP System Architecture Evolution (SAE); Security Architecture\".","paragraph_zero_based":139},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[18]3GPP TS 23.304: \"Proximity based Services (ProSe) in the 5G System (5GS)\".","paragraph_zero_based":140},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[19]IETF RFC 1951: \"DEFLATE Compressed Data Format Specification version 1.3\".","paragraph_zero_based":141},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[20]IETF RFC 3485: \"The Session Initiation Protocol (SIP) and Session Description Protocol (SDP) Static Dictionary for Signaling Compression (SigComp)\".","paragraph_zero_based":142},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[21]IETF RFC 1979: \"PPP Deflate Protocol\".","paragraph_zero_based":143}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"10e5cb38b37b0dfb8f12c0c9cfbbe0bf8e332eae9de43cc451d00082f067088b","original_member_sha256":"eb546e95813d17061e2f2e29046594609d54b33f198e181aef2aa863719d00e5","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["06d000fc472828706f7ddb7fb92104709e4880d959d9b94e17432369d0dc675d","746d0dd7c8f84962bcf71ece6ac8e32b051fa57409e008b93690ffb9e3856caa","d23926b8d017f876ab4e04104c8cbc02bc04c06a437ff9acc2b3eef333debb2e","5773f9d29f3a5dd2e13de6d05a151c2b73c55726b390bc12696831fb96c098d1","f7bc1c8c62c3a3092ac5e87f39a8222f1967954599f5afcea72879fd109337fe","95b0eeda196b33c1e5c33560cd8b9c96c58dd067bc6f96d0ffb1a785a0ae1ced","b8f608956d3dde28cd17a1d06f3e37772755b408d07caab1f5e51e486891a2ff","2f6c695eb756fda81aa9c95a8d84857e12565ca7641618ada77293dc3e9c0556","179c2a989009edb32a93473e2405b92f73442d04652048714a6caa5ed1247c51","1cd2ca205a52168b31ffa5eff414cc9e08d3a91361b5006bf35f1fe582a944b8","31f21257ce12c3cd8a61914bb6916d9146d84b90f24bc82813682b4090709781","31c69122718528ddc8d685129f138a2059fd133368280fa4e92948e4d0b2f69f","0ac74c59abc628d5262ae3a45e5d6999fbb9ad3762ebbb204870c4b6947c25d4","4d6022bca03e9e6916d65f01b037fd73d88e4de1721e29fb41c42c99b03f3fce","8020a95c94719646d88293988618f34b1317dd421dea53687db73249ddc6dced","f5ff9a10b8579421aab7b5c8c8cc975fd28dbb2e1605197e27c048f0a5f32bf4","fb3c32ff6219d815c4b23e16698e2b59210fe8057504d771d7b3ac8878bbcea7","2ba521cacc02ea292f7260374a19d1fc8c243db5c6a7a21b259369185de90d3d","d8f4db292fe851d7d281153849e6952d20ce4ad1e337171da95aec8dfbc2d211","db4d38c74ab8cb94f533e765707642c7b8798a312d75c03ff6652d9a756b5358","470143108ad054f8899a85d785b54e91926177644c7ce066b458b147fa3e6c04","b06d3182b0e613a782d716fbbd3e99d574870641d973e702c1c20d86f67f5316","cee93a99cf0d913af01982503bcf5de3dd5ff91bd745db79fa8c744b30367d87","bfaf46b7a2b3bd9d8ada6c0c28f026b531a555e226e710e6f0980ab788a79530"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[120,143],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312192.zip::R2-2312192 38323 CR0128 Introduction of XR Enhancements.docx:p120"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312192.zip::R2-2312192 38323 CR0128 Introduction of XR Enhancements.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[22]3GPP TS 38.351: \"NR; Sidelink Relay Adaptation Protocol (SRAP) Specification\".","paragraph_zero_based":144},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"[xx]3GPP TS 23.501: \"System Architecture for the 5G System; Stage 2\".","paragraph_zero_based":145},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":146},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3.1Definitions","paragraph_zero_based":147},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"For the purposes of the present document, the terms and definitions given in TR 21.905 [1] and the following apply. A term defined in the present document takes precedence over the definition of the same term, if any, in TR 21.905 [1].","paragraph_zero_based":148},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"AM DRB: a data radio bearer which utilizes RLC AM.","paragraph_zero_based":149},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"AM MRB: an MRB associated with at least one AM RLC bearer for PTP transmission.","paragraph_zero_based":150},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Broadcast MRB: a radio bearer configured for MBS broadcast delivery.","paragraph_zero_based":151},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DAPS bearer: a bearer whose radio protocols are located in both the source gNB and the target gNB during DAPS handover to use both source gNB and target gNB resources.MBS Radio Bearer: a radio bearer that is configured for MBS delivery.","paragraph_zero_based":152},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Delay-critical PDCP SDU: the PDCP SDU for which the remaining time till discardTimer expiry is less than a [threshold].","paragraph_zero_based":153},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Delay-critical PDU Set: the PDU Set to which the delay-critical PDCP SDU belongs.","paragraph_zero_based":154},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Multicast MRB: a radio bearer configured for MBS multicast delivery.","paragraph_zero_based":155},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Non-split bearer: a bearer whose radio protocols are located in either the MgNB or the SgNB to use MgNB or SgNB resource, respectively.","paragraph_zero_based":156},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR sidelink communication: AS functionality enabling at least V2X communication as defined in TS 23.287 [13] and ProSe communication (including ProSe non-Relay and UE-to-Network Relay communication) as defined in TS 23.304 [18], between two or more nearby UEs, using NR technology but not traversing any network node.","paragraph_zero_based":157},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR sidelink discovery: AS functionality enabling ProSe non-Relay Discovery and ProSe UE-to-Network Relay discovery for Proximity based Services as defined in TS 23.304 [18] between two or more nearby UEs, using NR technology but not traversing any network node.","paragraph_zero_based":158},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NR sidelink transmission: any NR Sidelink-based transmission, including both transmission for NR sidelink discovery and transmission for NR sidelink communication.","paragraph_zero_based":159},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDCP data volume: the amount of data available for transmission in a PDCP entity.","paragraph_zero_based":160},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDU Set: one or more PDUs carrying the payload of one unit of information generated at the application level (e.g. frame(s) or video slice(s) etc for XR Services), as defined in TS 23.501 [xx]. A PDU in the PDU Set corresponds to a PDCP SDU.","paragraph_zero_based":161},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Split bearer: in dual connectivity, a bearer whose radio protocols are located in both the MgNB and the SgNB to use both MgNB and SgNB resources.","paragraph_zero_based":162},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Split secondary RLC entity: in dual connectivity, the RLC entity other than the primary RLC entity which is responsible for split bearer operation. If the PDCP entity is associated with two RLC entities, the split secondary RLC entity is the RLC entity other than the primary RLC entity. If the PDCP entity is associated with more than two RLC entities, the split secondary RLC entity is configured by upper layers.","paragraph_zero_based":163},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UM DRB: a data radio bearer which utilizes RLC UM.","paragraph_zero_based":164},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UM MRB: an MRB associated with only RLC UM.","paragraph_zero_based":165},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":166},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"3.2Abbreviations","paragraph_zero_based":167}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"10e5cb38b37b0dfb8f12c0c9cfbbe0bf8e332eae9de43cc451d00082f067088b","original_member_sha256":"eb546e95813d17061e2f2e29046594609d54b33f198e181aef2aa863719d00e5","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["29e34beb22cd5eb80a4b9a6d6a47c6c4daa6e2df8ef598f21e13d89cbb31be5d","5f6176f931e869466bc3c357a34b90039d776b5357cfd33f68910ce0a9ce91c2","2e8079eabeb773185b1256330e0fca06a7522a2be5236900ea972e299ce8f922","d063b52b286a5eab49afc19d06602e758501040aa282895b0774fde5d23d346c","36da681f90dad7f6a1a232f9889106b023068d07130c46a850fb38edb963a126","f0c31c6d69098db2f4a21312e8029fab23b6fc3023cb55c83913e1c03161862e","85ca65247f2d50abcd6f6d338f97531549f2c56b3daac5429b1ed189a25610e3","3a5db33e956e6085dfab6c4072b0ca8bfcfc50aab1387739173e037afc361506","638b1023d3ad292c406ae0ff8054488a836ee55af5848f81c51bd58ffc5c439f","d103d9aa0c54fee0daadbdea0f22b910d1774f9e638d54a01191aae8a97a94f9","3370d3afb61773f86113b00fe68ef51e610ac512aa8306b3a2096a53ff1a55e1","f90aaa26dd3370a6849930959dfb9ff409ad88d6e89faae887c6dbe096cee65a","08b98816d5477ee3051327af40a0f836ca4b7480e8f269ad0a9f31d724967386","a44266a2a7d7e1d0bdccb04b63d0efdc7ad55f750f19183ac4548118f483e653","164e85391ee7d926bc3d7740365a204f