{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of references to NZP CSI-RS resources used for beam measurement and reporting in a CSI-RS resource set.","paragraph_zero_based":17472},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If resourceType is set to 'aperiodic', the network configures up to maxNrofNZP-CSI-RS-ResourceSetsPerConfig resource sets. If resourceType is is set to 'periodic' or 'semiPersistent' and groupBasedBeamReporting-v1710 is not configured in IE CSI-ReportConfig, the network configures 1 resource set. If resourceType is set to 'periodic' or 'semiPersistent' and groupBasedBeamReporting-v1710 is configured, the network configures 2 resource sets, which may be two NZP CSI-RS resource sets (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.2.1.2 and 5.2.1.4.2). In this case, in TS 38.212 [17] Table 6.3.1.1.2-8B, the first resource set is indicated by a resource set indicator set to 0 and the second resource set by a resource set indicator set to 1.","paragraph_zero_based":17473},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"resourceType","paragraph_zero_based":17474},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Time domain behavior of resource configuration (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.2.1.2). It does not apply to resources provided in the csi-SSB-ResourceSetList.","paragraph_zero_based":17475},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":17476},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–CSI-ResourceConfigId","paragraph_zero_based":17477},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE CSI-ResourceConfigId is used to identify a CSI-ResourceConfig.","paragraph_zero_based":17478},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-ResourceConfigId information element","paragraph_zero_based":17479},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":17480},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CSI-RESOURCECONFIGID-START","paragraph_zero_based":17481},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":17482},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-ResourceConfigId ::=            INTEGER (0..maxNrofCSI-ResourceConfigurations-1)","paragraph_zero_based":17483},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":17484},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CSI-RESOURCECONFIGID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":17485},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":17486},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":17487},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–CSI-ResourcePeriodicityAndOffset","paragraph_zero_based":17488},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE CSI-ResourcePeriodicityAndOffset is used to configure a periodicity and a corresponding offset for periodic and semi-persistent CSI resources, and for periodic and semi-persistent reporting on PUCCH. both, the periodicity and the offset are given in number of slots. The periodicity value slots4 corresponds to 4 slots, value slots5 corresponds to 5 slots, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":17489},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-ResourcePeriodicityAndOffset information element","paragraph_zero_based":17490},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":17491},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-CSI-RESOURCEPERIODICITYANDOFFSET-START","paragraph_zero_based":17492},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":17493},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CSI-ResourcePeriodicityAndOffset ::=    CHOICE {","paragraph_zero_based":17494},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    slots4                                  INTEGER (0..3),","paragraph_zero_based":17495}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717a8289e1b579d","paragraph_ElementTree