{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Provides the frequency band indicator and a list of additionalPmax and additionalSpectrumEmission values for aerial UE as defined in TS 38.101-1 [15], table TBD, TS 38.101-2 [39], table TBD, and TS 38.101-5 [75], table TBD. If the field is present, the aerial UE shall apply the first listed band which it supports in the frequencyBandListAerial field. If the field is absent, frequencyBandList applies.","paragraph_zero_based":18792},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"frequencyShift7p5khz","paragraph_zero_based":18793},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Enable the NR UL transmission with a 7.5 kHz shift to the LTE raster. If the field is absent, the frequency shift is disabled.","paragraph_zero_based":18794},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"p-Max","paragraph_zero_based":18795},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in dBm applicable for the cell. If absent the UE applies the maximum power according to TS 38.101-1 [15] in case of an FR1 cell, TS 38.101-2 [39] in case of an FR2 cell or TS 38.101-5 [75] in case of an NTN cell. In this release of the specification, if p-Max is present on a carrier frequency in FR2, the UE shall ignore the field and applies the maximum power according to TS 38.101-2 [39]. This field is ignored by IAB-MT, the IAB-MT applies output power and emissions requirements, as specified in TS 38.174 [63].","paragraph_zero_based":18796},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"scs-SpecificCarrierList","paragraph_zero_based":18797},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A set of carriers for different subcarrier spacings (numerologies). Defined in relation to Point A (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 5.3). The network configures this for all SCSs that are used in UL BWPs configured in this serving cell.","paragraph_zero_based":18798},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":18799},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Conditional Presence","paragraph_zero_based":18800},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Explanation","paragraph_zero_based":18801},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FDD-OrSUL","paragraph_zero_based":18802},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is mandatory present if this FrequencyInfoUL-SIB is for the paired UL for a DL (defined in a FrequencyInfoDL-SIB) or if this FrequencyInfoUL-SIB is for a supplementary uplink (SUL). It is absent otherwise (if this FrequencyInfoUL-SIB is for an unpaired UL (TDD).","paragraph_zero_based":18803},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FDD-TDD-OrSUL-Optional","paragraph_zero_based":18804},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field is optionally present, Need R, if this FrequencyInfoUL-SIB is for the paired UL for a DL (defined in a FrequencyInfoDL-SIB), or if this FrequencyInfoUL-SIB is for an unpaired UL (TDD) in certain bands (as defined in clause 5.4.2.1 of TS 38.101-1 and in clause 5.4.2.1 of TS 38.104 [12]), or if this FrequencyInfoUL-SIB is for a supplementary uplink (SUL). It is absent otherwise.","paragraph_zero_based":18805},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":18806},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–GapPriority","paragraph_zero_based":18807},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE GapPriority is used to identify the priority of a gap configuration.","paragraph_zero_based":18808},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GapPriority information element","paragraph_zero_based":18809},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":18810},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-GAPPRIORITY-START","paragraph_zero_based":18811},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":18812},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"GapPriority-r17 ::=                       INTEGER (1..maxNrOfGapPri-r17)","paragraph_zero_based":18813},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":18814},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-GAPPRIORITY-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":18815}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717a8289e1b579d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["f4e39a38e502597542b5068431bcf75ae8c22cfef47066afc742117dc80329a9","353099e91c60ce07ced1f1aa2d6602b89ffa1d2c39539d1c2ab50d36a450a7f7","62083ffe365e55c111d22968bbf0d4e346cf108b07917a25007240eda74b7e45","65aacdd081f56a2ee6f3865d22c5d79c07290fcfca4c0b3098f97f27ab6b70a3","10caf18342d69f46aca37cf9d08766407c7751465e36c2f6278e017cb192ec36","12e8bc5922e802393e5eb67745f1d09338409aebbc6468adfa90e22c4b06403a","b4d3f4182c331c2d446e1d2a3c23c3086238814e8a313318f435edb53bc17289","e73e9fd44b1a881d53a4a28238687c286c6b6196f447cf7f6dc2869ad62d264d","cc755bdc03abdefd66520f76b9e4c79d5c55e18b4644007435fcf484ef40f66b","15d452cd74dfdf42a17e6c2c266f31424844228ad0b2ed950c18ab32bc92dddc","0f01761f772ce2252f9ded05380964a75d8d5d525711d3812e400632f17ea0ad","e210369c3b4ca28accb8a5c70857f207156ed71b126529b074e98b79fb5fa8f6","68c17ec53225461e60be6afba24c0ba0c9b6d83e11db2407e43600f4d49f4fd2","da496f5a619118b3823eaa47c5229f93b8fcb9c73a3e272183ce1ca4801fd7df","0e20d1eb8bfac8bbd50d2198cd7b9fed01206aad6a511fb8d2deeea7fe3739f9","5b89aa61c6c65380059a852ff7260dd9fb7249d8ea76aa44d9fc0d62fe030809","f76d40943fad079c7c3e45dcc24cc11fb763e8b0007d8a5f6423a33638a5dd88","e50f865a52eb98ec92829578a7da7b7f234b6ae64fa9ab671f81184748553309","c82fe252ee0638724add333e45af5f6e57034226a3c794462122a082a1c1f918","bfaa031c11c0f6c43450c91c972673c780f70dfb51d2be8112433132a04c0dce","0d77165825425e0e2cd29b77be7c7e63b3beba99a9eb032826cc3f3ea7124751","8e1332aa00f2c7cd90b446d9c55fcf665f56fe6d8bcdee34680a35caa7c6ea55","aaab4edf3571a141708ebc63ea7178642022373a59abc319e6dc5083783ab0c1","b2069265d4db2b3a7d43b3587c78134bba5c5873e091b3ebe7ecb0d721983b58"