{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"physicalCellIdRange","paragraph_zero_based":19872},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Physical cell identity or a range of physical cell identities.","paragraph_zero_based":19873},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":19874},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRAN-Cell field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":19875},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"physicalCellId","paragraph_zero_based":19876},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Physical cell identity of a cell in the cell list.","paragraph_zero_based":19877},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellIndividualOffset","paragraph_zero_based":19878},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Cell individual offset applicable to a specific cell. Value dB-24 corresponds to -24 dB, dB-22 corresponds to -22 dB and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":19879},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":19880},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MeasObjectEUTRA field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":19881},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"allowedMeasBandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":19882},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The maximum allowed measurement bandwidth on a carrier frequency as defined by the parameter Transmission Bandwidth Configuration \"NRB\" TS 36.104 [33].","paragraph_zero_based":19883},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"associatedMeasGap","paragraph_zero_based":19884},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the associated measurement gap for measuring this EUTRA frequency. If this field is absent, the associated meaurment gap is the gap configured via gapFR1 or gapUE.","paragraph_zero_based":19885},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"carrierFreq","paragraph_zero_based":19886},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Identifies EUTRA carrier frequency for which this configuration is valid. Network does not configure more than one MeasObjectEUTRA for the same physical frequency, regardless of the E-ARFCN used to indicate this.","paragraph_zero_based":19887},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellsToAddModListEUTRAN","paragraph_zero_based":19888},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of cells to add/ modify in the cell list.","paragraph_zero_based":19889},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellsToRemoveListEUTRAN","paragraph_zero_based":19890},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of cells to remove from the cell list.","paragraph_zero_based":19891},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"eutra-PresenceAntennaPort1","paragraph_zero_based":19892},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When set to true, the UE may assume that at least two cell-specific antenna ports are used in all neighbouring cells.","paragraph_zero_based":19893},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"eutra-Q-OffsetRange","paragraph_zero_based":19894},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Used to indicate a cell, or frequency specific offset to be applied when evaluating triggering conditions for measurement reporting. The value is in dB. Value dB-24 corresponds to -24 dB, value dB-22 corresponds to -22 dB and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":19895}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717a8289e1b579d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["760aba60afc7da42b795464f24eaae11ac080dfa69391166115d10cf706d928b","88045c26ca57f5dbb3b106725a6fdfc2038f86cf611e2b17f5da1d8c6d037ef8","2bff1103b9bc94692e2deaf480d0c9aa2e594dd766e7ab66abf3bfa8b4e1db97","03e32a7c69f5682d82e26a5b039367badfacfae39430b15b214716e938225e6b","61e81edb5c6e48ff3079a57d65b6dc5e10098406160e3cb72c5ecc7b540deb8f","2bc7219ff9476c44a9d7a0036f876594d61c2411ffaf8d87842fc1a2b1e885ca","0628fadc9b3f8d354124b465effef5afc068