{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PCI-RangeIndex","paragraph_zero_based":22032},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PCI-RangeIndex identifies a physical cell id range, which may be used for different purposes.","paragraph_zero_based":22033},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PCI-RangeIndex information element","paragraph_zero_based":22034},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":22035},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PCI-RANGEINDEX-START","paragraph_zero_based":22036},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22037},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PCI-RangeIndex ::=                  INTEGER (1..maxNrofPCI-Ranges)","paragraph_zero_based":22038},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22039},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PCI-RANGEINDEX-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":22040},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":22041},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22042},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PCI-RangeIndexList","paragraph_zero_based":22043},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PCI-RangeIndexList concerns a list of indexes of physical cell id ranges, which may be used for different purposes.","paragraph_zero_based":22044},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PCI-RangeIndexList information element","paragraph_zero_based":22045},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":22046},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PCI-RANGEINDEXLIST-START","paragraph_zero_based":22047},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22048},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PCI-RangeIndexList ::=              SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofPCI-Ranges)) OF PCI-RangeIndex","paragraph_zero_based":22049},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22050},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PCI-RANGEINDEXLIST-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":22051},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":22052},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22053},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PDCCH-Config","paragraph_zero_based":22054},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PDCCH-Config is used to configure UE specific PDCCH parameters or MBS multicast PDCCH parameters such as control resource sets (CORESET), search spaces and additional parameters for acquiring the PDCCH. If this IE is used for the scheduled SCell in case of cross carrier scheduling, the fields other than searchSpacesToAddModList and searchSpacesToReleaseList are absent. If the IE is used for a dormant BWP, the fields other than controlResourceSetToAddModList and controlResourceSetToReleaseList are absent. If this IE is used for MBS CFR, the field downlinkPreemptiom,tpc-PUSCH, tpc-SRS, uplinkCancellation, monitoringCapabilityConfig, and searchSpaceSwitchConfig are absent.","paragraph_zero_based":22055}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717a8289e1b579d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["7f6293b91cf74fb3e6afc426c8cbc76ac103d672871ff8698712ad6cad691ba2","341437063d0b340b55645a5ba0933018695c3836ca780cd56f7f90368010e0ef","dcfe6dbe4600b8ca85d5d1f47aed74648f7de7404f4626ed7ae51e01b762f86e","8ad4f42f6cb961be8392582c676e00e0f093e6c621587bcf0f10eea5ef1d14da","58993d23181f304f6f8a72646be4d1ada6ddfc7850dc4fdccfde982325d4b1f3","a4954775e5f44c0edc86b886bf7d7fb47526c52ffc5411fa7a0ef09bf675ea1b","acef97eeef309d2811e72eb998cf98e85fd19f49ed6274a3929aff7a73b6e02d","8ed3c0307852a68f928615bf248786717721a273de8b28f0ea2af6ceb6b36546","f92eb02a83e11533e03cf7f7667bb