{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"phr-ProhibitTimer","paragraph_zero_based":22968},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in number of subframes for PHR reporting as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. Value sf0 corresponds to 0 subframe, value sf10 corresponds to 10 subframes, value sf20 corresponds to 20 subframes, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":22969},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"phr-Tx-PowerFactorChange","paragraph_zero_based":22970},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Value in dB for PHR reporting as specified in TS 38.321 [3]. Value dB1 corresponds to 1 dB, dB3 corresponds to 3 dB and so on. The same value applies for each serving cell (although the associated functionality is performed independently for each cell).","paragraph_zero_based":22971},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"phr-Type2OtherCell","paragraph_zero_based":22972},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If set to true, the UE shall report a PHR type 2 for the SpCell of the other MAC entity. See TS 38.321 [3], clause 5.4.6. Network sets this field to false if the UE is not configured with an E-UTRA MAC entity.","paragraph_zero_based":22973},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"twoPHRMode","paragraph_zero_based":22974},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates if the power headroom shall be reported as two PHRs (each PHR associated with a SRS resource set) is enabled or not.","paragraph_zero_based":22975},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22976},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PhysCellId","paragraph_zero_based":22977},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The PhysCellId identifies the physical cell identity (PCI).","paragraph_zero_based":22978},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PhysCellId information element","paragraph_zero_based":22979},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":22980},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PHYSCELLID-START","paragraph_zero_based":22981},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22982},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PhysCellId ::=                      INTEGER (0..1007)","paragraph_zero_based":22983},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22984},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PHYSCELLID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":22985},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":22986},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":22987},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PhysicalCellGroupConfig","paragraph_zero_based":22988},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PhysicalCellGroupConfig is used to configure cell-group specific L1 parameters.","paragraph_zero_based":22989},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PhysicalCellGroupConfig information element","paragraph_zero_based":22990},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":22991}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717a8289e1b579d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ebeed509e1852c2a7e504f4b205e29751833da05ec444cfaed0766b68fa396a5","bd48bc7e53106c34c54422e9ad4bce34a7b1629ffefb2a84fcbf40158b8da176","73bf9b21546775eec5a5ce8c27c9c750fd75cea1859236399586b65f63b7afd1","84c4ff1dddc2dd96d92fbfd1ed57084b8efd62e02e8cdb8eb17b022677a44113","ead19f3fc69374c78ecce3aeec1da11179b8ed83a1b1a92fc6f043606f18f96f","ec479a8bf6e2ebeb75e857cc990a7008ec4faab6c8641238753285c76fb56c1c","a434113338c5d82bfaf68f90fc509d218ea00227b262b4e082d02e5d847063d9","ca7d263ae1968646bb1311613779a5235a20fad7f6ed587855d87cc0a2016c39","1c6c3ae4339ff5994c32ff5fc8375be9f725d391af271eee60e69fd157329ae4","70e7806a413ff2e8eaaccc2e1a86aba94122a1aa468e69dfabc7ebd1cd