of Scheduling Request configurations to add or modify. If schedulingRequestToAddModListExt is configured, it contains the same number of entries, and in the same order, as schedulingRequestToAddModList.","paragraph_zero_based":26967},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"schedulingRequestToReleaseList","paragraph_zero_based":26968},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of Scheduling Request configurations to release.","paragraph_zero_based":26969},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":26970},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SchedulingRequestToAddMod field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":26971},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"schedulingRequestId","paragraph_zero_based":26972},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Used to modify a SR configuration and to indicate, in LogicalChannelConfig, the SR configuration to which a logical channel is mapped and to indicate, in SchedulingRequestresourceConfig, the SR configuration for which a scheduling request resource is used.","paragraph_zero_based":26973},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sr-ProhibitTimer","paragraph_zero_based":26974},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Timer for SR transmission on PUCCH in TS 38.321 [3]. Value is in ms. Value ms1 corresponds to 1ms, value ms2 corresponds to 2ms, and so on. If sr-ProhibitTimer-v1700 is configured, UE shall ignore sr-ProhibitTimer (without suffix). If both sr-ProhibitTimer (without suffix) and sr-ProhibitTimer-v1700 are absent, the UE applies the value 0.","paragraph_zero_based":26975}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717a8289e1b579d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["675ad0f510e65ecb5901261b6390994455b9bd69d243b2e743e3184b21364d65","064a292f93b20cc695db4c31207833eddf53fd85b5a05b8301f244af0d3da39e","