{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CRS-InterfMitigation-r17 ::=        SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":32424},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    -- R4 24-1 CRS-IM (Interference Mitigation) in DSS scenario","paragraph_zero_based":32425},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    crs-IM-DSS-15kHzSCS-r17             ENUMERATED {supported}                                                  OPTIONAL,","paragraph_zero_based":32426},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    -- R4 24-2 CRS-IM in non-DSS and 15 kHz NR SCS scenario, without the assistance of network signaling on LTE channel bandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":32427},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    crs-IM-nonDSS-15kHzSCS-r17          ENUMERATED {supported}                                                  OPTIONAL,","paragraph_zero_based":32428},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    -- R4 24-3 CRS-IM in non-DSS and 15 kHz NR SCS scenario, with the assistance of network signaling on LTE channel bandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":32429},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    crs-IM-nonDSS-NWA-15kHzSCS-r17      ENUMERATED {supported}                                                  OPTIONAL,","paragraph_zero_based":32430},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    -- R4 24-4 CRS-IM in non-DSS and 30 kHz NR SCS scenario, without the assistance of network signaling on LTE channel bandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":32431},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    crs-IM-nonDSS-30kHzSCS-r17          ENUMERATED {supported}                                                  OPTIONAL,","paragraph_zero_based":32432},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    -- R4 24-5 CRS-IM in non-DSS and 30 kHz NR SCS scenario, with the assistance of network signaling on LTE channel bandwidth","paragraph_zero_based":32433},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    crs-IM-nonDSS-NWA-30kHzSCS-r17      ENUMERATED {supported}                                                  OPTIONAL","paragraph_zero_based":32434},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":32435},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32436},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-FEATURESETDOWNLINKPERCC-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":32437},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":32438},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32439},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC-Id","paragraph_zero_based":32440},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC-Id identifies a set of features applicable to one carrier of a feature set. The FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC-Id of a FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC is the index position of the FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC in the featureSetsDownlinkPerCC. The first element in the list is referred to by FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC-Id = 1, and so on.","paragraph_zero_based":32441},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC-Id information element","paragraph_zero_based":32442},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":32443},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-FEATURESETDOWNLINKPERCC-ID-START","paragraph_zero_based":32444},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32445},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FeatureSetDownlinkPerCC-Id ::=      INTEGER (1..maxPerCC-FeatureSets)","paragraph_zero_based":32446},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32447}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717a8289e1b579d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c77a03da1bd892d8648c6d8173a2bed4c3c3065bb332d541aaa7f1ad2a547029","4cdcd70de1f04219d13b41c4bfcc1e3fce1d