eparationClassUL-v1620 ::= ENUMERATED {mhz1000}","paragraph_zero_based":32920},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32921},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-FREQSEPARATIONCLASS-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":32922},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":32923},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":32924},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–FreqSeparationClassDL-Only","paragraph_zero_based":32925},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE FreqSeparationClassDL-Only is used to indicate the frequency separation between lower edge of lowest CC and upper edge of highest CC of DL only frequency spectrum in a frequency band.","paragraph_zero_based":32926},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FreqSeparationClassDL-Only information element","paragraph_zero_based":32927}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717a8289e1b579d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["61aa600591d1ea021b08a5b09a8d515fb564aa673217091aa54ebe4140f5ba55","45f4bf504b0d07e394a10fdac258b5cf2f3653d71f2fce0f25115860d2109f14","4f08f337c2d5add620ef3627af3c0ce248d15453ddcb246df1f4febbc59e0a30","a9445c3318f82521ee7f5d4f74012a89599572712ee5bf82262801565037d4fe","aabaee919e768ce50d936525f857cdae4965c0b94efe9724043cb2ece7d9ba55","1e7f16e441fe68bcf0f15aed1ac3a49db34ae908ebe9a91fc29d7583c4640865","30543399244f8dfc2f6e15b5a5448cd188487a2a872d96700fc150fddfe2ef9c","7e24377eed694881daf4365f90f3dd8dfbdf94a28a49e986ec97b4f123d8206d","f91ff548a9db224207822a260518fb4be3444ec25edb2f83c173a4c4eb519c7f","3eed6ea4150ecf5f71f7b80f4523425f372fc25e732fb7fd3536d0b7b95525de","7e83e686a2605f572a80755dcc5d96674799b347e579343cab24a9f4e23df1b1","a933c9a6ff3649a1c0af39bb7d6496473ec81e8d36647f3c15447d826fdbf70d","4f9