{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-NS-PMAXLIST-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36792},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36793},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36794},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–EUTRA-PhysCellId","paragraph_zero_based":36795},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE EUTRA-PhysCellId is used to indicate the physical layer identity of the cell, as defined in TS 36.211 [31].","paragraph_zero_based":36796},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PhysCellId information element","paragraph_zero_based":36797},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":36798},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PHYSCELLID-START","paragraph_zero_based":36799},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36800},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PhysCellId ::=                        INTEGER (0..503)","paragraph_zero_based":36801},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36802},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PHYSCELLID-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36803},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36804},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36805},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange","paragraph_zero_based":36806},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange is used to encode either a single or a range of physical cell identities. The range is encoded by using a start value and by indicating the number of consecutive physical cell identities (including start) in the range. For fields comprising multiple occurrences of EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange, NW may configure overlapping ranges of physical cell identities.","paragraph_zero_based":36807},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange information element","paragraph_zero_based":36808},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":36809},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PHYSCELLIDRANGE-START","paragraph_zero_based":36810},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36811},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PhysCellIdRange ::=       SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":36812},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    start                           EUTRA-PhysCellId,","paragraph_zero_based":36813},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    range                           ENUMERATED {n4, n8, n12, n16, n24, n32, n48, n64, n84, n96,","paragraph_zero_based":36814},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"                                                n128, n168, n252, n504, spare2, spare1}                         OPTIONAL    -- Need N","paragraph_zero_based":36815}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717a8289e1b579d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["2a781f54d284364af246a68def1652cd695b75de793038496aa9979fb54c5590","e85c16d3cc87094473dd699bfe817a32cc25a436d69471b7e39af78c0cb0c73b","3915d9e3b63ac651c56541b9b588a08bff51219f6b725f1da55590e6e469bda3","cde309f2472549fe5c665a7a6d3ad086fd91bf016c88e469ec88ae9d45771180","63dd3a2b61abbb8a509c052a6588e2e2e88adb7ca358c0bc123b8db09738a6c8","e4292b7e12f6e71e4b741c8364973d4c37943a54d3a0d624ae7a22b8894bfe65","72ac3a6c0adf63d29c4f3dcbf7bb5539da5523e91c7abd8257d37cc0d1b5fbc7","745669bdff1a373a24251c5d47e61413a1efb1f41383d773b79175602c43f977","5996845f75e5c40f39e7aef808c59e276a495eb3bad01209e80ddcb255313a21","8da492e7461762e87405629295f7bebc4ffdaf290548ff784cffb8ae2d03edd2","f1f6aedb8e5ac823cd073bc152c211c2dc75fed04202da247ea53b55971f9921","d3f7282d929c12327fdcaf7827c6078a5c53689bb904a1ac6ab9eb5c37b2878d","ea2d346a2679dc55964271db69bd1b602fd0cd07ad7e20efa8aedeb8b0041d03","3efc3a3adfa2da2f2b06beacc95cc6b04b1b25fcc71c8946ec4a4764ede7587e","516b6d9fc35eeee2ee0ac68683cc30c9a9551a9eab4e019c5e3eb38d0ca5f808","1dc2972ec99e62dc36190b1838ae1b4c00bf1a271763ca695f757d6e12916100","0ca94f42b4855220a824e7cc0f42c4c577e2996f2b96d8a69fe71f24c8bdb5aa","0b1212075952b56c6b1bf3a8e7c5cb7a0a541f280a73655473adbda2f47fc8cd","55d07549ffc283bbaa624f94661af205cca4872092634bfc85c3dfddb34d0346","56f54c326ba920fdee33ccde8ff46c4a4bc9191a7f04202c64e216c6ea652ba4","b7e66a32f5a8b732333cb217f0e352cad718d07b69cdc1faac83f145aab8d226","4505bea5dbdf91a9a3d7e43ebec537d6e6866975cff00fad2ff4491c7170d1aa","aa69d71caddfb5bdc949e5b8ac1bc983dbf7dc03f376cce6b5b5904f2476096d","17928123006a12721b6a39a2bcbb26f655e3458bb4010cd4f590af350fe19c1f"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[36792,36815],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx:p36792"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":36816},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36817},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PHYSCELLIDRANGE-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36818},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36819},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36820},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–EUTRA-PresenceAntennaPort1","paragraph_zero_based":36821},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE EUTRA-PresenceAntennaPort1 is used to indicate whether all the neighbouring cells use Antenna Port 1. When set to true, the UE may assume that at least two cell-specific antenna ports are used in all neighbouring cells.","paragraph_zero_based":36822},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PresenceAntennaPort1 information element","paragraph_zero_based":36823},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":36824},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PRESENCEANTENNAPORT1-START","paragraph_zero_based":36825},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36826},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"EUTRA-PresenceAntennaPort1 ::=              BOOLEAN","paragraph_zero_based":36827},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36828},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-EUTRA-PRESENCEANTENNAPORT1-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36829},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":36830},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":36831},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–EUTRA-Q-OffsetRange","paragraph_zero_based":36832},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE EUTRA-Q-OffsetRange is used to indicate a cell, or frequency specific offset to be applied when evaluating triggering conditions for measurement reporting. The val