{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-BWP-PoolConfigCommon field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":37632},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"sl-TxPoolExceptional","paragraph_zero_based":37633},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the resources by which the UE is allowed to perform NR sidelink transmission in exceptional conditions on the configured BWP. For the PSFCH related configuration, if configured, will be used for PSFCH transmission/reception. This field is not present when SL-BWP-PoolConfigCommon is included in SidelinkPreconfigNR.","paragraph_zero_based":37634},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37635},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–SL-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":37636},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE SL-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList indicates the mapping between PSSCH transmission parameter (such as MCS, PRB number, retransmission number, CR limit) sets by using the indexes of the configurations provided in sl-CBR-PSSCH-TxConfigList, CBR ranges by an index to the entry of the CBR range configuration in sl-CBR-RangeConfigList, and priority ranges. It also indicates the default PSSCH transmission parameters to be used when CBR measurement results are not available, and MCS range for the MCS tables used in the resource pool.","paragraph_zero_based":37637},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList information element","paragraph_zero_based":37638},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":37639},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-SL-CBR-PRIORITYTXCONFIGLIST-START","paragraph_zero_based":37640},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37641},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList-r16 ::= SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..8)) OF SL-PriorityTxConfigIndex-r16","paragraph_zero_based":37642},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37643},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-CBR-PriorityTxConfigList-v1650 ::= SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..8)) OF SL-PriorityTxConfigIndex-v1650","paragraph_zero_based":37644},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37645},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-PriorityTxConfigIndex-r16 ::=    SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":37646},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-PriorityThreshold-r16             INTEGER (1..8)                                                   OPTIONAL,    -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":37647},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-DefaultTxConfigIndex-r16          INTEGER (0..maxCBR-Level-1-r16)                                  OPTIONAL,    -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":37648},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-CBR-ConfigIndex-r16               INTEGER (0..maxCBR-Config-1-r16)                                 OPTIONAL,    -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":37649},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-Tx-ConfigIndexList-r16            SEQUENCE (SIZE (1.. maxCBR-Level-r16)) OF SL-TxConfigIndex-r16   OPTIONAL     -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":37650},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":37651},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":37652},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SL-PriorityTxConfigIndex-v1650 ::=  SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":37653},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    sl-MCS-RangeList-r16                SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxCBR-Level-r16)) OF SL-MinMaxMCS-List-r16    OPTIONAL     -- Need M","paragraph_zero_based":37654},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":37655}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717