{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowList-r17 ::= SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofMTCH-SSB-MappingWindow-r17)) OF MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowCycleOffset-r17","paragraph_zero_based":40008},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":40009},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowCycleOffset-r17 ::= CHOICE {","paragraph_zero_based":40010},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ms10                                      INTEGER(0..9),","paragraph_zero_based":40011},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ms20                                      INTEGER(0..19),","paragraph_zero_based":40012},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ms32                                      INTEGER(0..31),","paragraph_zero_based":40013},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ms64                                      INTEGER(0..63),","paragraph_zero_based":40014},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ms128                                     INTEGER(0..127),","paragraph_zero_based":40015},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    ms256                                     INTEGER(0..255)","paragraph_zero_based":40016},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":40017},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":40018},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-MTCH-SSB-MAPPINGWINDOWLIST-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":40019},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":40020},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":40021},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowList field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":40022},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MTCH-SSB-MappingWindowCycleOffset","paragraph_zero_based":40023},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the cycle and offset for MTCH PDCCH ocassions to SSB mapping. Values in unit of ms. ms10 corresponds to cycle of 10 ms with corresponding offset between 0 and 9 ms, value ms20 corresponds to cycle of 20 ms with corresponding offset between 0 and 19 ms, and so on. The mapping window starts at a subframe in a SFN where [(SFN number × 10) + subframe number] modulo (cycle) = offset.","paragraph_zero_based":40024},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDCCH monitoring occasions for MTCH in a mapping window which are not overlapping with UL symbols (determined according to tdd-UL-DL-ConfigurationCommon) are sequentially numbered starting from 1 in the maping window. The [x×N+K]th PDCCH monitoring occasion for MTCH in this mapping window corresponds to the Kth transmitted SSB, where x = 0, 1, ...X-1, K = 1, 2, …N, N is the number of actual transmitted SSBs determined according to ssb-PositionsInBurst in SIB1 and X is equal to CEIL(number of PDCCH monitoring occasions in MTCH to SSB mapping transmission window/N). The actual transmitted SSBs are sequentially numbered from one in ascending order of their SSB indexes.","paragraph_zero_based":40025},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":40026},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–PDSCH-ConfigBroadcast","paragraph_zero_based":40027},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE PDSCH-ConfigBroadcast is used to configure parameters for acquiring the PDSCH for MCCH and MTCH.","paragraph_zero_based":40028},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDSCH-ConfigBroadcast information element","paragraph_zero_based":40029},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":40030},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PDSCH-CONFIGBROADCAST-START","paragraph_zero_based":40031}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717a8289e1b579d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["156f49e91279c6f06e2116de15e144e248fe8e37c7c52b23ea293d57c1e98342","a37d079b23c741c5d98befd954d65747c5bbadfd4eaeff9c874f2c293fc12396","313e073c366d369175303cd9271605956bcdb73eba3c85632ea6dbfc0447704d","8b8cf96ed7cf8d80833d69eb8338de84f9817f9b8b8ba9cda67cd802e71f3d07","3ed52978cd7221398524c30f070499e1283794a8ab23e6147d7b7ddac815c41c","a037fccdf02b4ada4dce0ca652953540353f55a0fa0e91abd72a634a0fe8b241","02bd8b7bc55b693d702ab24d392f5f856c976c625c8fcfcc6a54d683bd4012aa","8244624985918eb3e166dad567e3ee7a6c82f2ee6d5bdf2dd816c56a150c55ff","5f802dc9e6cace9b7550b6522730ea67501df5fcd9fbf4f70e47d0f42f5146a2","313b73e5a53c250b363c2a7f6fddfd2c464b58ae739f36bbcb0b16242bbb592a","6319b5e343b51d8bbf670806732a12977853271046c5bde7550a1cdeae311194","61cd47f8a5c670a9a24f89d74d81ead0f8928822d6bf98d66313e1040bd1bc6f","25d855e4d1c8cb18da1072c76d1b61f7577b0aa925369e2e116a6a747ef8a783","0d7d43bb2a33bfee866325ec3a3652adabaee8d0d2f11b9e357b75753e12106e","89a1226d8414b93c4d0078bcd4138fb48ed3c90670e23d0027e9f1191bd98d40","e4e2121819b09a1ce525327b9bc228ada9f5f849dbeb00ce1eafe65cc947cac4","770737b7ab3a7d574772938a21049872668183f9400423ffde0cef2bd7f41640","5bcc931f36e3f141743eda1aa83b73bc4bbc8e8f383d2a3ed8698433d22a0406","3317ecc3219092a08e4abd310affcdc46cef4c6c5fdc64e98a372f22c03fd95f","d5f01f63ddbe058f3fcb33caa21d5330d485e9b506b343f11bebd45c15ff5d30","cc21b85b3242ad9c61ad2e0632be6773b5fa8bf23a2fb56742fbd266f40471f0","a01af85b167df1f9d45b8eecdefd7b4166c0b3239b1315d73f244e2a94c8cfc6","62ec43186741811cc5bedd5b094ab3998772c7721ab394d0caa73e6d7ba0dc90","8cbb196dc165a44ce37681fadea8cd717723b102cc6be179addbbaee25dafb7d"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[40008,40031],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx:p40008"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":40032},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDSCH-ConfigBroadcast-r17 ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":40033},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    pdschConfigList-r17                    SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofPDSCH-ConfigPTM-r17) ) OF PDSCH-ConfigPTM-r17,","paragraph_zero_based":40034},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    pdsch-TimeDomainAllocationList-r17     PDSCH-TimeDomainResourceAllocationList-r16                          OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":40035},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    rateMatchPatternToAddModList-r17       SEQUENCE (SIZE (1..maxNrofRateMatchPatterns)) OF RateMatchPattern   OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":40036},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    lte-CRS-ToMatchAround-r17              RateMatchPatternLTE-CRS                                             OPTIONAL,   -- Need R","paragraph_zero_based":40037},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    mcs-Table-r17                          ENUMERATED {qam256, qam64LowSE}                                     OPTIONAL,   -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":40038},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    xOverhead-r17                          ENUMERATED {xOh6, xOh12, xOh18}                                     OPTIONAL    -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":40039},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":40040},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":40041},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDSCH-ConfigPTM-r17 ::= SEQUENCE {","paragraph_zero_based":40042},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    dataScramblingIdentityPDSCH-r17        INTEGER (0..1023)         OPTIONAL,   -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":40043},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    dmrs-ScramblingID0-r17                 INTEGER (0..65535)        OPTIONAL,   -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":40044},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"    pdsch-AggregationFactor-r17            ENUMERATED {n2, n4, n8}   OPTIONAL    -- Need S","paragraph_zero_based":40045},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"}","paragraph_zero_based":40046},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":40047},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-PDSCH-CONFIGBROADCAST-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":40048},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":40049},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":40050},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDSCH-ConfigBroadcast field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":40051},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"lte-CRS-ToMatchAround","paragraph_zero_based":40052},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Parameters to determine an LTE CRS pattern that the UE shall rate match around.","paragraph_zero_based":40053},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pdschConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":40054},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of PDSCH parameters which can be configured per G-RNTI. Only one entity is allowed to be configured if included in SIB20.","paragraph_zero_based":40055}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717a8289e1b579d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["2d2866ee9b207f00565fd8a541c28c5d24ece3d3fa97d444b4b26f95632e05a1","6dca65c0e9dbf79f523a9809425e34b9b377b127c93fc3b20b0954801325cd51","69553e25005be9b4eeeaba8b1f37a86e271596fa93bfd841fe946372594b88fc","203f989c6594786c623990c169628f320da44b34709814a6756da9c3273a6a63","f0119ee174c44681e9b4458da30aa93dbbfbee72d2400afdd1063cb626ef2149","3171592cf690a65b413a7dab03e2cbe547894b922e0742acfccb2ad63afd8774","955637f1d7adc6178d0b1e654b2acf14496b2bcc73c3e0031c76644d30d5f450","bb5a9acbbc2a686f70ac2756312afb9fd154032f901136ac8826ddb66df86352","987a527587e1452bfd086afd8f3bf086baa123889f2ff565c15fdaf551724118","45be716e683eb0578a18f4c90e1eeaf61ad4fcb4032a098549561c66aea526ae","74aade262636afd4ea508bb620229dbf8f3ce3589ed511565af5ec4a5b9873cd","5f50f0c21adb5bf2e7d1bf52548a37876dc6930e23345ab966c2b60be7f404e1","4253c3a8f9650fe7060657c3480500e8619f1386d98426d6f28a14070b5b82a0","85426f104b347dc135eee599012a7bb970e5d1bbd1b36c7a165c856ce5d53dc5","678be4e5c6f8d8f8496e7cbbbe03b5952c2b74187d8fac1be92ab6141510b915","74f2ae6160d77fc23b46e34d19c5d85542345aad9ccd9f592b91abc8d7399356","b4745b09ff5cf39625fa63e6c2e3c391d96c96399ba5227c40adcef4248950e9","496279849c096bbc7797a6835724faa4dcb1c715261b158a517a11c3193db3df","97a3a4a325052a980f29767b070aa3c2c494b1c56f6bb28f14f235b27fe5591d","f838607850ba453cf11293ea93555c82b252455f4d3085513972115936d07991","dd8308853c603c0c883b69c1435c9b62dbd0967646b08916e755ca650e8d0959","864e481ac79e85f7709d965220689835a1cbb39880e187c2b9dae2026e3170dc","6c9149d901c599aa7fa2bcb8631013dbe76c407e5e0d0bd5fb02346af2c74150","98b2d2b17bc74a958173b0572204ca9529d6f7434386d1f1e53ba633302268ce"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[40032,40055],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx:p40032"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312230.zip::R2-2312230-UAV-RRC-CR-Update-v07-rapp-cl.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pdsch-TimeDomainAllocationList","paragraph_zero_based":40056},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"List of time-domain configurations for timing of DL assignment to DL data.","paragraph_zero_based":40057},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field pdsch-TimeDomainAllocationList applies to DCI format 4_0 (see table 5.1.2.1.1-1 in TS 38.214 [19]). When the field is absent, the UE follows PDSCH time domain resource allocation determination rule as specified in TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.2.1.1.","paragraph_zero_based":40058},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"rateMatchPatternToAddModList","paragraph_zero_based":40059},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Resources patterns which the UE should rate match PDSCH around. The UE rate matches around the union of all resources indicated in the rate match patterns (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.4.1).","paragraph_zero_based":40060},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mcs-Table","paragraph_zero_based":40061},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates which MCS table the UE shall use for PDSCH. If the field is absent the UE applies the value 64QAM. The field mcs-Table applies to DCI format 4_0 with CRC scrambled by MCCH-RNTI/G-RNTI (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.3.1).","paragraph_zero_based":40062},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"xOverhead","paragraph_zero_based":40063},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Accounts for an overhead from CSI-RS, CORESET, etc. If the field is absent, the UE applies value xOh0 (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.3.2).","paragraph_zero_based":40064},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":40065},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PDSCH-ConfigPTM field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":40066},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dataScramblingIdentityPDSCH","paragraph_zero_based":40067},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Identifier(s) used to initialize data scrambling (c_init) for PDSCH as specified in TS 38.211 [16], clause 7.3.1.1. When the field is absent the UE applies the value physCellId configured for this serving cell.","paragraph_zero_based":40068},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"dmrs-ScramblingID0","paragraph_zero_based":40069},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DL DMRS scrambling initialization (see TS 38.211 [16], clause 7.4.1.1.1). When the field is absent the UE applies the value physCellId configured for this serving cell.","paragraph_zero_based":40070},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"pdsch-AggregationFactor","paragraph_zero_based":40071},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Number of repetitions for dynamic scheduling of MBS broadcast data for MTCH PDSCH (see TS 38.214 [19], clause 5.1.2.1). When the field is absent the UE applies the value 1.","paragraph_zero_based":40072},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":40073},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–TMGI","paragraph_zero_based":40074},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The IE TMGI is used to identify the MBS session.","paragraph_zero_based":40075},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TMGI information element","paragraph_zero_based":40076},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1START","paragraph_zero_based":40077},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-TMGI-START","paragraph_zero_based":40078},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":40079}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"88ac48b8abb8e582293899eb6fcf429cfe666bf19f2b5195cc18f96b95e0fc00","original_member_sha256":"b9eae4c3bdf5a2993a73f949e5986a1204cf998aea465f31f717a8289e1b579d","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ad0ef26dac2ac6d65ad57ba63332e1b3f24e06b1a86f87c9141a155bad16ad3c","98fb66cf352be18a50b33ca5c92475ae95e78df900bd411cdd8306cbed19262c","f1226951c8dfcd4d2d30c2e44345a38f433c6c6f01ef9c0e