{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312518.zip::R2-2312518 - 38321_CR1706_Rel-18_Introduction of Cross-RRH TCI state switch indication for high speed train.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":48},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Category:","paragraph_zero_based":49},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"B","paragraph_zero_based":50},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":51},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Release:","paragraph_zero_based":52},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-18","paragraph_zero_based":53},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":54},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following categories:F  (correction)A  (mirror corresponding to a change in an earlier release)B  (addition of feature), C  (functional modification of feature)D  (editorial modification)","paragraph_zero_based":55},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Detailed explanations of the above categories canbe found in 3GPP TR 21.900.","paragraph_zero_based":56},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Use one of the following releases:Rel-8(Release 8)Rel-9(Release 9)Rel-10(Release 10)Rel-11(Release 11)…Rel-16(Release 16)Rel-17(Release 17)Rel-18(Release 18)Rel-19(Release 19)","paragraph_zero_based":57},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":58},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":59},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Reason for change:","paragraph_zero_based":60},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Introduction of the new MAC CE indicated in RAN4 LS R4-2306399 ","paragraph_zero_based":61},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RAN4 is working on the Release 18 NR_HST_FR2_enh WI on enhanced support for HST scenario in FR2. One of the objectives of the Release 18 WI [WID, RP-220985] is to ","paragraph_zero_based":62},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Specify UL timing adjustment solution, including explicit NW signalling assistance, for FR2 HST scenario with large UL/DL propagation delay difference from different RRHs/TRPs to UE [RAN4, RAN2].","paragraph_zero_based":63},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RAN4 has concluded that NW signalling assistance is needed to indicate when the UE shall apply one-shot large uplink timing adjustment at TCI state switch. The following was agreed at RAN4#106bis-e:","paragraph_zero_based":64},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Introduce MAC-CE based solution with 1bit indication to inform UE on the TCI state switch across RRHs","paragraph_zero_based":65},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RAN4 respectfully asks RAN2 to introduce MAC-CE 1bit indication to inform UE on the TCI state switch across non-collocated RRHs. ","paragraph_zero_based":66},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"As further indicated in LS response R4-2314299, RAN4 only intends affects the MAC CE intended for indicating target TCI state for PDCCH in 6.1.3.15 in TS 38.321, i.e., TCI State Indication for UE-specific PDCCH MAC CE.","paragraph_zero_based":67},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UE procedure on handling reception of a new MAC CE needs to be captured in the MAC spec","paragraph_zero_based":68},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"As indicated in LS response R4-2314299, the intended UE behavior up reception of a new MAC CE is","paragraph_zero_based":69},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":70},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MAC-CE indicates “1”:","paragraph_zero_based":71}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"7ecc7295152ab004fee6c5fe5b51922f6b04fc31c69bc0c2a87740df08932928","original_member_sha256":"5ac2a6eb195866185c7c6c25a8e6bde44e85ab5aebfb9dafb46d77b16a9bd085","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["07b37f9382cb4563a76e06a3091184f1a25d93efb1d4a7ce6b1912cf5e0344c5","49757793c301e1b42ce3a2f5fe6de1d778711cbd77defe5a9880549543d950b9","0cfe81740ce728997e6f2bbc4f5530e7bf436dc75943e4538f987eebd4a483eb","337ea18d1cbe73cd23af973173806423cc975a8a8ed020d665da422d8a237198","99f7497d345193f94321fc78259eb1ee9d8374103ccda1740fdba9df311d1159","4237421dc4a192fb02084f80f4a2eae907e64525a5e3649dc54fafd8a06aa5f0","5b47f45d49e536de3b6d5e631981f66afc7f1da2e37d6a6a473a2e92e01fcbbc","8bd151c2b6bd30b02395cf315d3840e70074a5c9b7b771d52833ee373298c178","9ee8004cb88a34162bb5eb46c0c18bb0bf1eb58264f6a683d54e41efb29c2c15","4150cbaaabf1e132d6a7c803a37dae13ee904d3b14e33890e023ff2e9aba3f25","2278383fedc6ace6f8f0a92516943d5e75aa7f14ca403617a07b6ffe0a5d4ddb","d64d21a445eb6d60b7cdeb423c7ebff1e9b9d6d8e68fa04c8c9b014923795d8b","0f286b194b59e9918e17b804b443b11d843c7c26e43dda1f0ed905456b089bae","82ac05c0f62a0022e691328731b1c1ae0cb14f58f20908d9596f8359bba24085","0eac66b9a64c17e4d69427d16e3a30c38523246bcd4fe8a22c02bce8ee0ff294","1203f2e7aef4ed1c6990f9ec22df1c7ee1fd80a1aa8a59732a92eb37639ad7df","5a81a7ba665b3263524a01d070318aa479989c850532c2db737bb119818c34bd","f7c61650da4812bfa35b442b32eef99e1f199ecf1dbdbb99ea5789f365e2b4ef","5c424bc6319776e7d9a55f002e4e86ed7440d97d2df817ba0deebe8e076d5ca0","880bc9e542d8e079edfe60ca1b7002257fc6151934748ba5f174e74517666771","29c55c25c54f99d845bdee303138b254ca10e349e42469c29ab611e3c6ecb476","a30a6b143e0d0b78eb91548f613b6e3a4baefb1ad1ca7766f9d74c657de3c681","c75e618b864160060106b411589d5c65dc87cc69f1d5ae947cccf14499caa0ed","16ba3d7e130671db39b8d0d1bb5bc41b04918c711130e1b266ae6671f16d66ee"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[48,71],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312518.zip::R2-2312518 - 38321_CR1706_Rel-18_Introduction of Cross-RRH TCI state switch indication for high speed train.docx:p48"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312518.zip::R2-2312518 - 38321_CR1706_Rel-18_Introduction of Cross-RRH TCI state switch indication for high speed train.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Rel-17 TCI state switching delay requirements in HST FR2 scenarios from TS 38.133, Clause 8.10.3A are followed without changes.","paragraph_zero_based":72},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"When highSpeedLargeOneStepUL-TimingFR2-r17 is enabled for HST PC 6 UE supporting [largeOneStepUL-timingFR2-r17] capability, UE shall apply the one shot large timing adjustment specified in Clause 7.1.2.3 in TS 38.133 on the first UL transmission after TCI state switch without checking the DL timing difference threshold.","paragraph_zero_based":73},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MAC-CE indicates “0”:","paragraph_zero_based":74},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UE follows the Rel-15 TCI state switching requirements as described in TS 38.133 Clause 8.10.3","paragraph_zero_based":75},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Gradual timing adjustment requirements in Clause 7.1.2.1 in TS 38.133 apply to the first UL transmission after TCI state switch, i.e., one shot large UL timing adjustment is not applied.","paragraph_zero_based":76},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"UE timing adjustment behavior does not depend on the existing Rel-17 RRC parameter highSpeedDeploymentTypeFR2.","paragraph_zero_based":77},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"No new PC6 UE behaviour is expected in comparison to Rel-17 when Rel-18 enhanced MAC CE indication is not signaled or UE does not support [highSpeedTCISwitchEnhMAC-CE-FR2-r18] capability.","paragraph_zero_based":78},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The UE procedure on handling reception of a new MAC CE needs to be captured in the MAC spec.","paragraph_zero_based":79},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":80},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":81},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Summary of change:","paragraph_zero_based":82},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"in clause 3.2, define the abbreviation RRH","paragraph_zero_based":83},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"in clause 5.18.1, add the Cross-RRH TCI State Indication for UE-specific PDCCH MAC CE","paragraph_zero_based":84},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In clause 5.18.5, define the MAC procedure when the MAC entity receives a Cross-RRH TCI State Indication for UE-specific PDCCH MAC CE on a Serving Cell.","paragraph_zero_based":85},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In clause 6.1.3.15, add texts on the Cross-RRH TCI State Indication for UE-specific PDCCH MAC CE","paragraph_zero_based":86},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"In clause 6.2.1, introduce the LCID for for the Cross-RRH TCI State Indication for UE-specific PDCCH MAC CE","paragraph_zero_based":87},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":88},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":89},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":90},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":91},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Consequences if not approved:","paragraph_zero_based":92},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If the change is not approved, the network cannot support MAC-CE based solution with 1bit indication to inform UE on the TCI state switch across RRHs.","paragraph_zero_based":93},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":94},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":95}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"7ecc7295152ab004fee6c5fe5b51922f6b04fc31c69bc0c2a87740df08932928","original_member_sha256":"5ac2a6eb195866185c7c6c25a8e6bde44e85ab5aebfb9dafb46d77b16a9bd085","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["32a39e0cfa73d3fc17635422173a2ad7e70fa9059d1e7c23619e8b7e2f288ee8","8905742eea7a11f5c1024e5b1e6ce7