{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- TAG-MOBILITYFROMNRCOMMAND-STOP","paragraph_zero_based":9480},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"-- ASN1STOP","paragraph_zero_based":9481},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":9482},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"MobilityFromNRCommand-IEs field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":9483},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"nas-SecurityParamFromNR","paragraph_zero_based":9484},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"If targetRAT-Type is eutra, this field is used to deliver the key synchronisation and Key freshness for the NR to LTE/EPC handovers and a part of the downlink NAS COUNT as specified in TS 33.501 [11] and the content of the parameter is defined in TS 24.501 [23]. If targetRAT-Type is utra-fdd, this field is used to deliver the key synchronisation and Key freshness for the NR to FDD UTRAN handover and a part of the downlink NAS COUNT as specified in TS 33.501 [11] and the content of the parameter is defined in TS 24.501 [23].","paragraph_zero_based":9485},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"targetRAT-MessageContainer","paragraph_zero_based":9486},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The field contains a message specified in another standard, as indicated by the targetRAT-Type, and carries information about the target cell identifier(s) and radio parameters relevant for the target radio access technology. A complete message is included, as specified in the other standard. See NOTE 1","paragraph_zero_based":9487},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"targetRAT-Type","paragraph_zero_based":9488},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the target RAT type.","paragraph_zero_based":9489},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"voiceFallbackIndication","paragraph_zero_based":9490},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the handover is triggered by EPS fallback for IMS voice as specified in TS 23.502 [43].","paragraph_zero_based":9491},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":9492},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"NOTE 1:The correspondence between the value of the targetRAT-Type, the standard to apply, and the message contained within the targetRAT-MessageContainer is shown in the table below:","paragraph_zero_based":9493},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"targetRAT-Type","paragraph_zero_based":9494},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Standard to apply","paragraph_zero_based":9495},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"targetRAT-MessageContainer","paragraph_zero_based":9496},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"eutra","paragraph_zero_based":9497},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TS 36.331 [10] (clause 5.4.2)","paragraph_zero_based":9498},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"DL-DCCH-Message including the RRCConnectionReconfiguration","paragraph_zero_based":9499},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"utra-fdd","paragraph_zero_based":9500},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"TS 25.331 [45] (clause 10.2.16a)","paragraph_zero_based":9501},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Handover TO UTRAN command","paragraph_zero_based":9502},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":9503}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["c4866f80f6ddcec0d66922d4a048303a1de1549f3a54eddcbba05a6c88839c0f","2b6e05c594be1054909299f092c044723f19c4042e91e6a92346c253ea63bf62","a2c6c316f5e4b5c702a208a28e5c63bde4ea20438b399fee381863685f034b09","43aa5a0c34eb002cb8a8b07deeda807cdd69861169ba5c65cadcc6afb8d3ed54","7f8257b512a42f990f8110a72b79b8cac5d4d6b68299768af3939c9da73c227c","4a5af469ccf4b022abd3d1a43772951310520955bfdc9072cbe25ea40be603fa","301006c