{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"deprioritisationReq","paragraph_zero_based":10272},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether the current frequency or RAT is to be de-prioritised.","paragraph_zero_based":10273},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"deprioritisationTimer","paragraph_zero_based":10274},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the period for which either the current carrier frequency or NR is deprioritised. Value minN corresponds to N minutes.","paragraph_zero_based":10275},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"measIdleConfig","paragraph_zero_based":10276},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates measurement configuration to be stored and used by the UE while in RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE.","paragraph_zero_based":10277},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mpsPriorityIndication","paragraph_zero_based":10278},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the UE can set the establishment cause to mps-PriorityAccess for a new connection following a redirect to NR or set the resume cause to mps-PriorityAccess for a resume following a redirect to NR. If the target RAT is E-UTRA, see TS 36.331 [10]. The gNB sets the indication only for UEs authorized to receive MPS treatment as indicated by ARP and/or QoS characteristics at the gNB, and it is applicable only for this instance of release with redirection to carrier/RAT included in the redirectedCarrierInfo field in the RRCRelease message.","paragraph_zero_based":10279},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"noLastCellUpdate","paragraph_zero_based":10280},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Presence of the field indicates that the last used cell for PEI shall not be updated. When the field is absent, the PEI-capable UE shall update its last used cell with the current cell. The UE shall not update its last used cell with the current cell if the AS security is not activated.","paragraph_zero_based":10281},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"srs-PosRRC-InactiveConfig","paragraph_zero_based":10282},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"SRS for positioning configuration during RRC_INACTIVE state.","paragraph_zero_based":10283},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"suspendConfig","paragraph_zero_based":10284},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates configuration for the RRC_INACTIVE state. The network does not configure suspendConfig when the network redirect the UE to an inter-RAT carrier frequency or if the UE is configured with a DAPS bearer.","paragraph_zero_based":10285},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"redirectedCarrierInfo","paragraph_zero_based":10286},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates a carrier frequency (downlink for FDD) and is used to redirect the UE to an NR or an inter-RAT carrier frequency, by means of cell selection at transition to RRC_IDLE or RRC_INACTIVE as specified in TS 38.304 [20]. Based on UE capability, the network may include redirectedCarrierInfo in RRCRelease message with suspendConfig if this message is sent in response to an RRCResumeRequest or an RRCResumeRequest1 which is triggered by the NAS layer (see 5.3.1.4 in TS 24.501 [23]).","paragraph_zero_based":10287},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"voiceFallbackIndication","paragraph_zero_based":10288},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the RRC release is triggered by EPS fallback for IMS voice as specified in TS 23.502 [43].","paragraph_zero_based":10289},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10290},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"CarrierInfoNR field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":10291},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"carrierFreq","paragraph_zero_based":10292},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates the redirected NR frequency.","paragraph_zero_based":10293},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ssbSubcarrierSpacing","paragraph_zero_based":10294},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Subcarrier spacing of SSB in the redirected SSB frequency.","paragraph_zero_based":10295}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["ed681ed94c59fce0aadfe8a4b4da23054b49b458a58a799fa17e01a8e9c3dbb3","fe8d96b73516f51d9fc254bbf70e8403e562762db22596e8af27b958e9249349","d3ab4d648f750df1088978f0b860ed01d43fbd5e5386e33935224c435d62f1b8","2fa8c0d7a0d697fd848e8c8c67c428e538d95271a95d50c490edc07bbdc17e7e","5d26170bfff1013b276182d91cfb8d34315d9ea92409e59859d57e77ed5084f1","d1fc9fa85f2790c92c78834985957c5d2d6df8646a436ccd351f698da33a7252","0fbae1fcd78ffd9f698bf8d49b5948ce41b94c197a9536200a7c2273d8f62429","e89ecefff550d04c036464a903ae149c471efdf07d3516cc9bf96501f5d3a7fe","7e34cd6e36470d08e9f00844040b005f935808f5e9b3cff8a15e0214d7567731","a640be81624f378c6b9f0dbbcbd5b6cd81218d0c4678433decef4dced59303c0","18c0b6e38c7a965bb700f8bc6e5fb5b8cca0825cbb1121adbf2cad9d9395afb8","8ae2563f97b6b2b970fcd09f3f1e9d0631ca264e45f2a7daa13b0a44f2ba776d","fd8c68471d19a16a72b3b9fdb537e67130680b99deac01d60c8c696ea83cc2df","b94e977e8f5d3e13e4fdc6983f7ed5706ce8873c7dde4ddbd0e15963fd611d0c","94b09422311cb48902b9ce428a6ba3e89b2178ac1ab2f7b072ac52ffdc7e2bf3","61343d471cc2f2032562c40a78d48e4da7f1b1dce7404c196340da2be11b056b","3cb1771a64987eff2ff887a51484dc1e32bdb22b4b298ae1a26827a526deeabe","a92b0eb3d01cf2c43f57df43eef4ff2a3a07e493572d64cfb5c9ae7ecc276d14","dbc545bf039702400a517fb35b52816e3baedc279ffa746a6994f1e37c7b5496","57f2931b11c84bf097ed13a7df23888a88220225d439849da5332b9e0a5775a8","60ee2f04176e85f493643799a9e0f15d0adf1df96f08b6d69858dba598137efa","868f418f09a068d512e54016dd574fec74410d602f9e9f848d0bbfd216b8bdf9","131689d75e1d5910349cc779eb365ac2b0e000959cd1cac1073e3d5a3fae4cb2","60855815f363a59c4fbd1ab852e8fcd499f0daed99fc8cd4b3d6766f197a175c"],"paragraph_range_zero_based":[10272,10295],"projection":"All w:t and m:t including tracked insertion/deletion runs; not a final-edit-state interpretation or answer annotation."},"source_row":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx:p10272"}
{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Only the following values are applicable depending on the used frequency:","paragraph_zero_based":10296},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR1:    15 or 30 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":10297},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-1:  120 or 240 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":10298},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"FR2-2:  120, 480, or 960 kHz","paragraph_zero_based":10299},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"smtc","paragraph_zero_based":10300},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The SSB periodicity/offset/duration configuration for the redirected SSB frequency. It is based on timing reference of PCell. If the field is absent, the UE uses the SMTC configured in the measObjectNR having the same SSB frequency and subcarrier spacing.","paragraph_zero_based":10301},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10302},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RAN-NotificationAreaInfo field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":10303},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"cellList","paragraph_zero_based":10304},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A list of cells configured as RAN area.","paragraph_zero_based":10305},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ran-AreaConfigList","paragraph_zero_based":10306},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"A list of RAN area codes or RA code(s) as RAN area.","paragraph_zero_based":10307},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10308},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PLMN-RAN-AreaConfig field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":10309},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"plmn-Identity","paragraph_zero_based":10310},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PLMN Identity to which the cells in ran-Area belong. If the field is absent the UE not in SNPN access mode uses the ID of the registered PLMN. This field is not included for UE in SNPN access mode (for UE in SNPN access mode the ran-Area always belongs to the registered SNPN).","paragraph_zero_based":10311},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ran-AreaCodeList","paragraph_zero_based":10312},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The total number of RAN-AreaCodes of all PLMNs does not exceed 32.","paragraph_zero_based":10313},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ran-Area","paragraph_zero_based":10314},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indicates whether TA code(s) or RAN area code(s) are used for the RAN notification area. The network uses only TA code(s) or both TA code(s) and RAN area code(s) to configure a UE. The total number of TACs across all PLMNs does not exceed 16.","paragraph_zero_based":10315},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10316},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PLMN-RAN-AreaCell field descriptions","paragraph_zero_based":10317},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"plmn-Identity","paragraph_zero_based":10318},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"PLMN Identity to which the cells in ran-AreaCells belong. If the field is absent the UE not in SNPN access mode uses the ID of the registered PLMN. This field is not included for UE in SNPN access mode (for UE in SNPN access mode the ran-AreaCells always belongs to the registered SNPN).","paragraph_zero_based":10319}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["2d3b6b4929873bf630bfed2fe195c31369f72712896cb04ec8e0ed51cfc76ada","ef31fecfd8bff6841877c7b5c5c2ad54e5b740d0676ec145ec0f4090b4c246fa","cc467ab3883a977a0feadf6a5ef6871f6176dc07631b2d90c59f378db842f790","8031c729da0b7be4a0b21fdbecb5026bc8465b2acc222e31a4b494b13614cc2b","29694f74aba2522d5f54fa4467aeb4d7b54de661eefd85b646000e74627fdece","989a01a2e0432c7a1d32a4b