{"fields":{"filename":"R2-2312910.zip::R2-2312910 38331-h60 NES merged CR.docx","origin":"original_author_document_complete_unfiltered_paragraph_projection","paragraphs":[{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"iab-NodeIndication","paragraph_zero_based":10752},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is used to indicate that the connection is being established by an IAB-node as specified in TS 38.300 [2].","paragraph_zero_based":10753},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"idleMeasAvailable","paragraph_zero_based":10754},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Indication that the UE has idle/inactive measurement report available.","paragraph_zero_based":10755},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"mobilityState","paragraph_zero_based":10756},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the UE mobility state (as defined in TS 38.304 [20], clause 5.2.4.3) just prior to UE going into RRC_CONNECTED state. The UE indicates the value of medium and high when being in Medium-mobility and High-mobility states respectively. Otherwise the UE indicates the value normal.","paragraph_zero_based":10757},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ng-5G-S-TMSI-Part2","paragraph_zero_based":10758},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The leftmost 9 bits of 5G-S-TMSI.","paragraph_zero_based":10759},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"onboardingRequest","paragraph_zero_based":10760},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates that the connection is being established for UE onboarding in the selected onboarding SNPN, see TS 23.501 [32].","paragraph_zero_based":10761},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"registeredAMF","paragraph_zero_based":10762},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field is used to transfer the GUAMI of the AMF where the UE is registered, as provided by upper layers, see TS 23.003 [21].","paragraph_zero_based":10763},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"selectedPLMN-Identity","paragraph_zero_based":10764},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Index of the PLMN or SNPN selected by the UE from the plmn-IdentityInfoList or npn-IdentityInfoList fields included in SIB1.","paragraph_zero_based":10765},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"ul-RRC-Segmentation","paragraph_zero_based":10766},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"This field indicates the UE supports uplink RRC segmentation of UECapabilityInformation.","paragraph_zero_based":10767},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"","paragraph_zero_based":10768},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"–RRCSetupRequest","paragraph_zero_based":10769},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"The RRCSetupRequest message is used to request the establishment of an RRC connection.","paragraph_zero_based":10770},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Signalling radio bearer: SRB0","paragraph_zero_based":10771},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RLC-SAP: TM","paragraph_zero_based":10772},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Logical channel: CCCH","paragraph_zero_based":10773},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"Direction: UE to Network","paragraph_zero_based":10774},{"literal_text_all_w_t_and_m_t":"RRCSetupRequest message","paragraph_zero_based":10775}],"source":"Whole authentic original CR source member; all unfiltered body and nested table paragraphs"},"source_cell_coordinates":{"document_XML_sha256":"e6da965682bd316cba86572597901ea384f59f1fc16f9cae6cc2322c6ca66446","original_member_sha256":"98ba9f2b5573fe46d64ecaac42249cc03885c5438afddaea698dae3590b59c3c","paragraph_ElementTree_utf8_XML_sha256":["4823373556572de795dcda0b3bfe060810b7e491b6a63a60c01b058b4a2085bc","af6d7009e09e4a22acc43de5cffaf834bcd424e1f73bea73bb462c32def64df1","eec6e08efb1affaee29679eab75455c24d0459f150e31b69cf347d9465d1a6dd","c28963226d9840d4af35e6eb687a31358be5b2fc4b0b9b2a69b9ef6adb03f301","4ddee34201cc0c65764296a9d875b21eeddfa8ab93eb4f4294222bdb4edc4cad","3ce3a4d4c5ff02070d37625409be3e3f0fa25afdf040fc5af508b644cf43a32a","3e37ff91b1a25ed0dc6ff0be99c928fe5b131a132eb92dcdde0ea95aa2bdd306","32e3e956cc4adc35e058974fa9523053d01e5eb0de4aba8247eee660c334a94e","2e19e0e57593a42cdc1e0a92385eb1382c025b77148